2 CONT An échanson (also known as a cupbearer) was an officer in a medieval court responsible for serving drinks, particularly wine, to a king, prince, or high-ranking noble. This was a position of great trust and responsibility, as the 
2 CONC échanson would often taste the drinks before the sovereign consumed them to protect against poisoning attempts. This practice highlights the prevalence of intrigue and suspicion in medieval courts. 
