1 NOTE {geni:about_me} AMEY BE FALLETANS, Squire, second son of RENAUD, Lord of Falletans, Knight, settled in Salins. He alienated, in 1317, in favor of Amey de Montagu, Canon of Besançon, a quarter and a half of Muire which he collected
2 CONC  from the saltworks, and had married a Lady named Marguerite, who remarried with Gérard de Paloufet, of Salins. Widowed by both her husbands, she made her will on the Thursday after All Saints' Day in 1341, chose her burial in the
2 CONC  Church of Saint-Maurice de Salins, and designated her children as her heirs, in half of her estate.
2 CONT
2 CONT Genealogical History of the Lords of Salins in the County of Burgundy, by J.B. GUILLAUME, Volume 1, 1758.
2 CONT He settled in Salins and in 1317 sold a quarter and a half of a muire he collected from the salt marshes to Amey de MONTAGU, canon of Besançon. His wife, Marguerite, married Gérard PALOUSET de Salins, after being widowed. Once wid
2 CONC owed by her two husbands, she made her will on the Thursday after All Saints' Day in 1341, by which she chose to be buried in the church of Saint Maurice de Salins. She appointed as heirs to half of her property, Humbert de FALETA
2 CONC NS, Guillemette de FALETANS, wife of Étienne dit Ferroillat, Gérarde de FALETANS, wife of Jean VAUCHARD and Isabelle de FALETANS, widow of Jacques de l'AULE, her children and to the other half Renaud PALOUSET, her son.
2 CONT
2 CONT *Muire: Salt water drawn from wells to make salt.
2 CONT
2 CONT https://gw.geneanet.org/jykempf?lang=en&pz=christiane&nz=peter&p=marguerite&n=&oc=5
