1 NAME Barthélémi /Du Drac/
2 GIVN Barthélémi
2 _MARNM Du Drac
1 SEX M
1 BURI
2 ADDR
3 CITY Paris
3 STAE Île-de-France
3 CTRY France
1 BIRT
2 DATE ABT 1315
1 DEAT
2 DATE 23 MAY 1363
2 ADDR
3 CITY Paris
3 STAE Île-de-France
3 CTRY France
1 OCCU Trésorier des guerres de Charles V
1 NOTE {geni:about_me} https://fr.wikipedia.org/wiki/Barth%C3%A9lemy_du_Drac
2 CONT
2 CONT Barthélémy du Drac, or Drach according to the spelling of the time, was born in Picardy in 1320 and died in Paris in 1365. Son of Armand du Drac dit Drac de Châteauneuf, he is however considered the founder of the family of the Dr
2 CONC ac, whose arms are: "Or, to the dragon of Vert crowned and langued Gules" 1.
2 CONT
2 CONT Biography
2 CONT
2 CONT He wore the titles of knight and chamberlain of King Philippe de Valois. He then became treasurer of the king's wars with the title of "lieutenant of the king on the borders of Flanders and Hainaut" 2 or that of "captain for the k
2 CONC ing in the parts of Picardy, Boulogne and Calais". In 1340, he performed the same function at the Bovines, and in 1350 he continued to work under Jean le Bon1.
2 CONT
2 CONT The details of his accounts that have come down to us have been used by many historians such as Charles du Fresne, 4 Father Anselme, in his monumental Genealogical and chronological history of the royal house of France to justify 
2 CONC the nobility of certain families, or by others to establish historical facts: "In the accounts of Jean the Mire, Barthélemy of Drach, Jean de Cange, Jean le Mercier, Etienne de Bracque and other treasurers of the wars, we find the
2 CONC se squires Bannerets at Royal service with their suite5. ".
2 CONT
2 CONT It is in one of his accounts that we note, in 1338, the first trace of the use of gunpowder in France at the headquarters of Puy-Guillaume: "To Henri de Faumechont, to have powders and other things necessary to the guns which were
2 CONC  before Puy-Guillaume6, 7. "
2 CONT
2 CONT Barthelemy du Drac died in Paris on May 12, 1365. He was buried in the church of the Holy Sepulcher of Paris. His epitaph was: "Cyistist noble man Barthelemy of Drac, treasurer of the wars of the king, who trespassed the year of g
2 CONC race MCCCLXV, the twelfth day of May9. "
2 CONT
2 CONT Wife and offspring
2 CONT
2 CONT Married to Jeanne Odde, whom he had:
2 CONT
2 CONT     Jean du Drac, lord chatelain of the Baillie-les-Amiens and Champagne-sur-Oise, died 04/01/1413, first advise in the year 1391, then president of the parliament of Paris (April 11, 1410) , married to Jacqueline, vicomtesse d'Aÿ
2 CONC , died on June 8, 1404 at Paris1.
2 CONT     Berthelot du Drac (who was on trial with his brother Jean, Berthelot attacked him with the dagger, and Jean answered with the knife.)
