2 CONT 2.   '''      ISABELLE de Meulan''' (-after Nov 1281?).  "Almaricus de Meullento dominus de Cauda, Guillelmus de Essartis dominus de Ambleinvilla, Gobertus de Argus dominus de Guitebuef, Albertus de Longavalle dominus de Croissiac
2 CONC o milites, Ysabellis predicti Guillelmi, Yda dicti Goberti, et Anna dicti Alberti uxores" confirmed rights of pasture to Notre-Dame de Gournay by charter dated Apr 1274, with another charter dated Nov 1274 relating to the same mat
2 CONC ter[2055].  Jean de Châtillon Comte de Blois approved the division of "la forest de Roissy" agreed by “monseingnor Amaurri de Meulant, Guobert d’Argis et Yde sa fame, Guillaume des Essarz et Ysabel sa fame, Aubert de Longueval et 
2 CONC Anne sa fame, chevaliers et dames” by charter dated Mar 1276 (O.S.)[2056].  The reversing of the name order of Guillaume des Essarts/Gobert de Dargies in this document (as well as the Nov 1281 document) compared with the Apr 1274 
2 CONC charter has not been explained.  "Almauricus de Meulento dominus de Cauda et de Gornayo armiger, dominus Gobertus de Argiis et dominus Guillelmus de Amblevilla milites" authorised the opening of two roads through “nemorum nostroru
2 CONC m de Roissiaco in Bria” by charter dated Nov 1281[2057].  The presence of her husband in this document suggests that Isabelle may still have been alive.  
2 CONT
