2 CONT i)          AMAURY de Montfort (-[1213]).  A charter dated Feb 1199 recalls a donation to the leprosery of Grand-Beaulieu near Chartres by "Amauricus de Monteforti", with the consent of "Amauricus parvus filius eiusdem Amaurici, q
2 CONC ui erat sub custodia Amaurici de Mestenon"[2650].  He succeeded his father in 1182 as Comte d'Evreux.  Earl of Gloucester.  m firstly (before [1194/96]) AGNES d'Amboise, daughter of HUGUES [II] Seigneur d'Amboise & his wife Mathil
2 CONC de de Vendôme (-after 20 Mar [1202/03]).  "Sulpicius dominus Ambaziæ et Matildis mater mea et omnes fratres et sorores Hugo…et Johannes, Helisabeth et Agnes atque Dionisia" donated property to the abbey of Fontaines-les-Blanches b
