2 CONT b)         SIMON [IV] de Montfort (-1187 or before, bur Abbaye de Haute-Bruyère).  Robert of Torigny records the death in 1182 of "Simon comes Ebroicensis" and the succession "in comitatu Ebroicensis in Normannia" of "Amalricus fi
2 CONC lius eius" and "in comitatu de Rocha et in terra Francie" of "Simon alter filius eius"[2658].  He succeeded his father in 1181 as Seigneur de Montfort-l'Amaury.  -        see below.
