2 CONC d to [1048/61], witnessed by “...Amalricus de Sparnoto, Simon et Mainerius filii eius...”[462].  "Amalricus miles" founded the priory of Saint-Thomas d’Epernon, with the consent of "conjugis mee…Bertredis…et filiorum meorum…Simoni
2 CONC s…atque Mainerii", by charter dated [11 Apr 1052/Jul 1053][463].  He succeeded his father as Seigneur de Montfort and completed the construction of the castle known as Montfort-l'Amaury which was started by his father[464].  "…Sim
2 CONC on de Monte forti…" witnessed the charter dated 29 May 1067 under which Philippe I King of France confirmed the possessions of Saint-Martin-des-Champs[465].  Orderic Vitalis records the death of “Simon de Monteforti, gener Ricardi
2 CONC  comitis Ebroicensium”, dated to 1087 from the context[466].  "Mainerium, fratrem Symonis de Monte Forti" donated property, with the consent of "Simone fratre eius comiteque Belli Montis Ivonis", by charter dated to before 1091, w
2 CONC hich also names "domnus Simon, filio suo Amalrico"[467]. 
