2 CONT 4.         RICHARD de Montfort (-killed in battle [Nov 1092], bur Epernon).  Orderic Vitalis records that “Ricardus frater eius” succeeded after the death of “Almaricus de Monteforti qui Fortis” and relentlessly took vengeance aga
2 CONC inst Guillaume de Breteuil for the death of his brother, dated to 1089[480].  He succeeded his brother as Seigneur de Montfort-l’Amaury.  Orderic Vitalis records the bitter dispute between “Helvisa...comitissa” [wife of Guillaume 
2 CONC Comte d’Evreux] and “Isabelem de Conchis”  [wife of Raoul [III] de Tosny] and the war between their husbands which followed, during the course of which “nepotes eius...Guillelmus de Bretolio et Ricardus de Monteforti” supported “G
2 CONC uillelmus comes” and Richard was killed, being buried “Asparlone in cimiterio sancti Thomæ apostoli”, dated to [1090][481]. 
