2 CONT
2 CONT Amaury III of Montfort
2 CONT
2 CONT From Wikipedia, the free encyclopedia
2 CONT
2 CONT Amaury III de Montfort (died 1137) was seigneur de Montfort l'Amaury from 1101 to 1137 and comte d'Évreux from 1118 to 1137. He was the son of Simon I, seigneur de Montfort, and his wife Agnès d'Évreux.[1]
2 CONT
2 CONT [edit]Life
2 CONT
2 CONT [edit]Marriages and children
2 CONT
2 CONT Around 1115 he married his first wife, Richilde de Hainaut, daughter of Baudouin II, comte de Hainaut and of Ide de Louvain, but they separated in 1118 on grounds of consanguinity.
2 CONT
2 CONT In 1118 he remarried, to Agnès de Garlande, daughter of Anseau de Garlande, seigneur de Rochefort-en-Yvelines, and of Béatrice or Agnès de Rochefort. Their children were :
2 CONT
2 CONT Agnès († 1181), in 1141 married Waleran IV de Meulan (1104 † 1166), count of Meulan
2 CONT
2 CONT Simon III († 1181), count of Évreux, then seigneur de Montfort
2 CONT
2 CONT Amaury IV († 1140), seigneur de Montfort
2 CONT
2 CONT Robert de Montfort
2 CONT
