2 CONT
2 CONT     CHARLEMAGNE, Holy Roman EMPEROR is the 8th great-grandfather of Roger DeBEAUMONT Count.
2 CONT
2 CONT     Roger de Beaumont; Seigneur (feudal Lord) of Beaumont, Pontaudemer,Brionne and Vatteville, Normandy; married Adeline, sister of Hugh Countof Meulan and daughter by his 1st wife of Waleran Count ofMeulan.[Burke's Peerage]
2 CONT
2 CONT     <nowiki>---------------------------------------</nowiki>
2 CONT
2 CONT     The well-known Roger de Beaumont held Sturminster Marshal, Dorset, in1086; it descended to the counts of Meulan through Roger's eldest son,Robert count of Meulan. That Roger took his name from Beaumont is a partofthe general h
2 CONC istory of Normandy. It follows that Roger's descendants,the counts of Meulan, the Earls of Leicester, and the Earls of Warwick,all derive from Beaumont-le-Roger. [The Origins of Some Anglo-NormanFamilies]
2 CONT
2 CONT     Roger was one of the most powerful noblemen of his era. He furnishedsixty warships for William the Conqueror's invasion fleet, but remainedbehind to govern Normandy in William's absence. In later life, he becamea monk.
2 CONT --------------------
