1 OCCU Comtesse de Meulan
1 NOTE {geni:about_me} Adeine married Roger de Beaumont circa 1048 or earlier. Adeline of Meulan (ca. 1014-1020 - 1081), daughter of Waleran III, Count de Meulan and Oda de Conteville, and sister and heiress of a childless Count of Meula
2 CONC n. Meulan eventually passed to their elder son who became Count of Meulan in 1081. 
2 CONT
2 CONT Their surviving children were:
2 CONT
2 CONT 1. Robert de Beaumont, 1st Earl of Leicester, Count of Meulan (b ca 1049 - 1118) who succeeded his father in the major part of his lands, and who fought in his first battle at Hastings.
2 CONT
2 CONT 2. Henry de Beaumont, 1st Earl of Warwick, overshadowed by his elder brother, but who established a more enduring line of Beaumont earls at Warwick Castle.
2 CONT
2 CONT 3. William de Beaumont (not mentioned in most sources).
2 CONT
2 CONT 4. Alberee de Beaumont, Abbess of Eton.
2 CONT
2 CONT --------------------
2 CONT
2 CONT http://www.thepeerage.com/p382.htm#i3811
2 CONT
2 CONT Adeline de Meulan
2 CONT
2 CONT F, #3811, d. circa 8 April 1081
2 CONT
2 CONT Last Edited=12 Jun 2009
2 CONT
2 CONT Adeline de Meulan was the daughter of Waleran III de Meulan, Comte de Meulan. She died circa 8 April 1081.
2 CONT
2 CONT Children of Adeline de Meulan and Roger de Beaumont, Seigneur de Portaudemer
2 CONT
2 CONT Henry de Newburgh, 1st Earl of Warwick+1 d. 1123
2 CONT
2 CONT Robert de Meulan, 1st Earl of Leicester+ b. c 1046, d. 5 Jun 1118
2 CONT
2 CONT Citations
2 CONT
2 CONT [S22] Sir Bernard Burke, C.B. LL.D., A Genealogical History of the Dormant, Abeyant, Forfeited, and Extinct Peerages of the British Empire, new edition (1883; reprint, Baltimore, Maryland: Genealogical Publishing Company, 1978), p
2 CONC age 399. Hereinafter cited as Burkes Extinct Peerage.
2 CONT
2 CONT --------------------
2 CONT
2 CONT Roger de Beaumont
2 CONT
2 CONT From Wikipedia, the free encyclopedia
2 CONT
2 CONT Family and children
2 CONT
2 CONT He married circa 1048 or earlier Adeline of Meulan (ca. 1014-1020 - 1081), daughter of Waleran III, Count de Meulan and Oda de Conteville, and sister and heiress of a childless Count of Meulan. Meulan eventually passed to their el
2 CONC der son who became Count of Meulan in 1081. Their surviving children were:
2 CONT
2 CONT Robert de Beaumont, 1st Earl of Leicester, Count of Meulan (b ca 1049 - 1118) who succeeded his father in the major part of his lands, and who fought in his first battle at Hastings.
2 CONT
2 CONT Henry de Beaumont, 1st Earl of Warwick, overshadowed by his elder brother, but who established a more enduring line of Beaumont earls at Warwick Castle.
2 CONT
2 CONT William de Beaumont (not mentioned in most sources).
2 CONT
2 CONT Alberee de Beaumont, Abbess of Eton.
2 CONT
2 CONT --------------------
2 CONT
2 CONT It is known that Adeline is the daughter of the Comte Valeran (Galeran) III de Meulan and Oda de Conteville, but it is not known if she is the sister of Marie de Meulan, our family's ancestor.
2 CONT
2 CONT According to Lazarus Long's ancestry:
2 CONT
2 CONT http://freepages.genealogy.rootsweb.com/~lzrslong/b1286.htm#P4942
2 CONT
2 CONT Count Of Meulan Waleran DE MEULAN 7,37,45,70,102,105,115,117,262,377,378,838 was born in 990 in Mellent, Normandy, France.377,709 [NEED TO DEFINE SENTENCE: Alt. Death]262 
2 CONT
2 CONT He died on 8 Dec 1069.377 
2 CONT
2 CONT He was also known as Beaumont. OCCU Count of Meulan ... 
2 CONT
2 CONT SOUR Royalty for Commoners, Roderick W. Stuart, p. 140; 
2 CONT
2 CONT HAWKINS.GED; www.teleport.com/ddonahue/donahue ; 
2 CONT
2 CONT gendex.com/users/daver/ri gney/D0001 
2 CONT
2 CONT SOUR Royalty for Commoners, Roderick W. Stuart, p. 140; HAWKINS.GED & gendex.com/users/daver/rigney/D0001 say 1069; 
2 CONT
2 CONT www.teleport.com/ddonahue/donahue says 1069; 
2 CONT
2 CONT Galeran III, of Mellant, Normandy - Royalty for Commoners, Roderick W. Stuart, 
2 CONT
2 CONT p. 140; www.teleport.com/ddonahue/donahue says parents are Robert, Count of Meulan and Alix de Vexin - NPH 
2 CONT
2 CONT DATE 22 JUN 2000 
2 CONT
2 CONT Parents: Cmte Robert (Count Of Meulan) BEAUMONT and Adela DE VEXIN. Parents: Robert MEULAN and Alix De VEXIN.
2 CONT
2 CONT Spouse: Oda DE CONTEVILLE. 
2 CONT
2 CONT Count Of Meulan Waleran DE MEULAN and Oda DE CONTEVILLE were married about 1017 in Of Ponteaudemer, Normandy, France.377 
2 CONT
2 CONT Children were: Countess Of Meulent Adeline DE MEULAN, Hugh BEAUMONT, Marie DE MEULAN.
2 CONT
2 CONT Spouse: Alis. 
2 CONT
2 CONT Children were: Waleran DE MEULAN, Waleran De MEULAN, Fulk DE MEULAN, Fulk De MEULAN
2 CONT
2 CONT According to French Wikipedia's page on Adeline's husband, Roger de Beaumont:
2 CONT
2 CONT http://fr.wikipedia.org/wiki/Adeline_de_Meulan (redirected)
2 CONT
2 CONT Famille et descendance
2 CONT
2 CONT Il épousa, entre 1045 et 1050, Adeline de Meulan († 8 avril 1081), fille de Galéran III, comte de Meulan. Elle-même devint comtesse de Meulan lorsque son frère Hugues III entra dans les ordres à l'abbaye du Bec en 1077. Ils eurent
2 CONC  pour enfants, entre autres :
2 CONT
2 CONT Robert Ier de Beaumont, comte de Meulan (1081) et de Leicester (1090).
2 CONT
2 CONT Henri de Beaumont († 1119), 1er comte de Warwick.
2 CONT
2 CONT Guillaume de Beaumont.
2 CONT
2 CONT Alberée (ou Aubrée) de Beaumont, abbesse d'Eton.
2 CONT
2 CONT In English:
2 CONT
2 CONT Roger de Beaumont married Adeline de Meulan (d. 8 April 1081), daughter of Galeran III, Comte de Meulan, between 1045 and 1050. She became herself the Comtesse de Meulan when her brother, Hugh III, took his orders in the Abbey de 
2 CONC Bec in 1077. The couple had four children, among others:
2 CONT
2 CONT 1. Roger I de Beaumont, Comte Meulan (1081) and Leicester (1090).
2 CONT
2 CONT 2. Hugh de Beaumont (d. 1119), first Earl of Warwick.
2 CONT
2 CONT 3. William de Beaumont.
2 CONT
2 CONT 4. Alberee (or Aubree) de Beaumont, Abbess of Eaton.
2 CONT --------------------
2 CONT ADELINE DE MEULLANT born 1014 of Pontaudemer, Normandy, France and daughter of and eventually sole heiress of Waleran, Comte de Meullant, a great feudal nobleman of France. Adeline died in 1081. 
2 CONT
2 CONT Children: Abbot William, Abbess Albrede, Earl Robert, Earl Henry (c.1045) 
2 CONT --------------------
2 CONT Adeine married Roger de Beaumont circa 1048 or earlier. Adeline of Meulan (ca. 1014-1020 - 1081), daughter of Waleran III, Count de Meulan and Oda de Conteville, and sister and heiress of a childless Count of Meulan. Meulan eventu
2 CONC ally passed to their elder son who became Count of Meulan in 1081.
2 CONT
2 CONT Their surviving children were:
2 CONT
2 CONT 1. Robert de Beaumont, 1st Earl of Leicester, Count of Meulan (b ca 1049 - 1118) who succeeded his father in the major part of his lands, and who fought in his first battle at Hastings. 2. Henry de Beaumont, 1st Earl of Warwick, o
2 CONC vershadowed by his elder brother, but who established a more enduring line of Beaumont earls at Warwick Castle. 3. William de Beaumont (not mentioned in most sources). 4. Alberee de Beaumont, Abbess of Eton.
2 CONT --------------------
2 CONT
2 CONT http://www.thepeerage.com/p382.htm#i3811
2 CONT
2 CONT Adeline de Meulan
2 CONT
2 CONT F, #3811, d. circa 8 April 1081
2 CONT
2 CONT Last Edited=12 Jun 2009
2 CONT
2 CONT Adeline de Meulan was the daughter of Waleran III de Meulan, Comte de Meulan. She died circa 8 April 1081. Children of Adeline de Meulan and Roger de Beaumont, Seigneur de Portaudemer
2 CONT
2 CONT Henry de Newburgh, 1st Earl of Warwick+1 d. 1123
2 CONT
2 CONT Robert de Meulan, 1st Earl of Leicester+ b. c 1046, d. 5 Jun 1118
