2 CONC ontium 1062, MGH SS XXIII, p. 793.  [155] Hugonis Floriacensis, Liber qui Modernorum Regum Francorum continet Actus 11, MGH SS IX, p. 390.  [156] Orderic Vitalis, Vol. III, Book  V, p. 117.  ~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~ Probab
2 CONC ly more likely to be: http://fmg.ac/Projects/MedLands/CENTRAL%20FRANCE.htm#AgnesBaugencyMEnguerrandIICoucy
2 CONT
2 CONT AGNES de Baugency .  The De Genere Comitum Flandrensium, Notæ Parisienses records "Agnes uxor domini Ingelranni de Cociaco" as daughter of "domina de Baugenciaco primogenita [comitis Hugonis li Maines]"[1432].  A more explicit ref
2 CONC erence which confirms her parentage has not yet been identified.  m (1132) ENGUERRAND [II] de Coucy, son of THOMAS Seigneur de Coucy & his third wife Mélisende de Crècy (-[1131/47]).  
2 CONT
