1 NOTE Hugh I de Vermandois
2 CONT http://trees.ancestry.com/rd?f=document&guid=f182d66d-864c-4ab6-9bf6-710cca8bc374&tid=10145763&pid=-681535689
1 NOTE He was Duke of France and Burgundy, Marquis of Orleans, Count of Amiens, Clermont, Parish, Valois and Vermandois. He was a Crusader, a leader of the 1st Crusade.
1 NOTE BIOGRAPHY
2 CONT Hugues was born in 1057, the son of Henri I, king of France, and Anna of Kiev. He was the younger brother of King Philippe I. After 1067 he married Adelaide, comtesse de Vermandois et de Valois, only child of Heribert IV, comte de
2 CONC  Vermandois et de Valois and Adèle, comtesse de Valois. Hugues and Adelaide had five children of whom four would have progeny.
2 CONT
2 CONT In early 1096 Hugues and Philippe began discussing the First Crusade after news of the Council of Clermont reached them in Paris. Although Philippe could not participate, as he had been excommunicated, Hugues was said to have been
2 CONC  influenced to join the Crusade after an eclipse of the moon on 11 February 1096.
2 CONT
2 CONT That summer Hugues' army left France for Italy, where they would cross the Adriatic Sea into territory of the Byzantine empire, unlike the other Crusader armies which were travelling by land. On the way, many of the soldiers led b
2 CONC y fellow Crusader Emicho von Leiningen joined Hugues' army after Emicho was defeated by the Hungarians, whose land he had been pillaging. Hugues crossed the Adriatic from Bari in Southern Italy, but many of his ships were destroye
2 CONC d in a storm off the Byzantine port of Dyrrhachium.
2 CONT
2 CONT Hugues and most of his army were rescued and escorted to Constantinople, where they arrived in November 1096. Prior to his arrival, Hugues sent an arrogant, insulting letter to the Eastern Roman Emperor Alexius I Comnenos, accordi
2 CONC ng to the emperor's biography by his daughter (the _Alexiad_), demanding that Alexius meet with him.
2 CONT
2 CONT 'Know, O King, that I am King of Kings, and superior to all who are under the sky. You are now permitted to greet me, on my arrival, and to receive me with magnificence, as befits my nobility.'
2 CONT
2 CONT Alexius was already weary of the armies about to arrive, after the unruly mob led by Peter the Hermit had passed through earlier in the year. Alexius kept Hugues in custody in a monastery until Hugues swore an oath of vassalage to
2 CONC  him.
2 CONT
2 CONT After the Crusaders had successfully made their way across Seljuk territory and, in 1098, captured Antioch, Hugues was sent back to Constantinople to appeal for reinforcements from Alexius. Alexius was uninterested, however, and H
2 CONC ugues, instead of returning to Antioch to help plan the siege of Jerusalem, went back to France. There he was scorned for not having fulfilled his vow as a crusader to complete a pilgrimage to Jerusalem, and Pope Paschal II threat
2 CONC ened to excommunicate him. He joined the minor Crusade of 1101, but was wounded in battle with the Turks in Asia Minor about 5 September, and died of his wounds on 18 October in Tarsus.
2 CONT
2 CONT In 1103 his widow Adelaide married Renaud, comte de Clermont-en-Beauvaisis, and they had two children. Adelaide died on 28 September 1120 or 1124.
