2 CONT Simon I de Montfort
2 CONT
2 CONT From Wikipedia, the free encyclopedia
2 CONT
2 CONT Simon I de Montfort born about 1025 in Montfort l'Amaury, Ile de France, France and died 1087. He is buried in Epernon, Normandy, France. He was the son of Amaury de Montfort (c 1000-1031) and Bertrade de Gometz.
2 CONT
2 CONT [edit]Progeny
2 CONT
2 CONT Simon I first married Isabel de Broyles (b. 1034, Broyes, Marne, France), daughter of Hugh Bardoul. Their children were:
2 CONT
2 CONT Amauri de Montfort (c. 1056-1089)
2 CONT
2 CONT Isabel (Elizabeth) de Montfort (b. 1057), who married Raoul II de Tosny.[1]
2 CONT
2 CONT Simon I's second marriage was to Agnes d'Evreux (b. 1030), daughter of Richard d'Evreux of Rouen, Normandy. Their children were:
2 CONT
2 CONT Bertrade de Montfort (c. 1059-1117), became Queen of France.
2 CONT
2 CONT Richard de Montfort (c. 1066-1092), slain in attack on abbey at Conches.
2 CONT
2 CONT Simon II de Montfort (c. 1068-1101)
2 CONT
2 CONT Amaury III of Montfort(c. 1070-1137), married Richude (Richilde) de Hainault and Agnes de Garland.
2 CONT
2 CONT Guillaume de Montfort (c. 1073-1101)
2 CONT
2 CONT Adeliza de Montfort (b. 1075)[2]
2 CONT
