2 CONT
2 CONT --------------------
2 CONT
2 CONT Simon I, seigneur de Montfort, married Isabeau de Broyes, dame de Nogent, daughter of Hugh Bardoul, seigneur de Brozes, circa 1055. Later he married our ancestor Agnes d' Évereux, daughter of Richard, 2nd comte d' Évereux and Adel
2 CONC aide de Barcelona.
2 CONT
2 CONT Simon attested a charter of King Henry I to St. Germain-des-Près as "Sig. Simonis de Monteforti" in 1058.
2 CONT
2 CONT Simon took a leading part in persuading Duke William to recall Ralph de Tosny of Flamstead and Hugh de Grandmesnil from exile in 1063.
2 CONT
2 CONT Simon was attested an Act for the Abbey of Coulombs while with Duke William and his court on 13 April 1066 at Fécamp, Normandy. He confirmed with his wife, unnamed, a gift by Richard Fitz-Herluin of certain lands in "villa sancti 
2 CONC Hilari" to the same abbey (of Coulombs), the said lands being part of the inheritance of Simon's wife at Muelan, Normandy.
2 CONT
2 CONT Simon witnessed a charter of Philip I to St. Martin-des-Champs as "Simon de Monteforti" in 1067 in Paris. In 1072 he confirmed the gift of Philip to St. Magloire by "quidam miles de castro qui Montefortis vocatur Symon nomine" of 
2 CONC the churches of St. Peter and St. Laurence situate "in eodem castro" as "S. Simonis de castro Montefortis ... S. Almarici Simonis filii."
2 CONT
2 CONT Simon died in 1087 at or shortly before at age 62 years.
2 CONT
2 CONT Simon was our ancestor through two distinct descent lines--through his daughter Isabel and through his son Amauri III, each of whom was independently our ancestor.
2 CONT
2 CONT See "My Lines"
2 CONT
2 CONT ( http://homepages.rootsweb.ancestry.com/~cousin/html/p352.htm#i5258 )
2 CONT
