1 NOTE 1  BIRT 2  DATE ABT. 1025
1 NOTE Simon de Montfort, Earl of Leicester, who was married to the King's sister (Henry III). It was Simon who masterminded 'The Mad Parliament', where armed nobility made the king govern a representative Council of State, balancing the
2 CONC  royal needs and the national interests. 
2 CONT
2 CONT Henry called the knights of the shire to Windsor, and thus ensued two years of civil war, where Montfort eventually captured Henry and his heir, Edward. Montfort call the first ever type of Parliament in 1265, where all nobility a
2 CONC nd people of prominence met. 
2 CONT
2 CONT Edward escaped from prison and fought and killed Simon de Montfort at the Battle of Evesham. 
