2 CONT '''From Medlands:'''
2 CONT
2 CONT From http://fmg.ac/Projects/MedLands/NORMAN%20NOBILITY.htm#RotrouIdied1144B
2 CONT
2 CONT '''MARGUERITE du Perche''' (-27 Aug after 1156).  She is named and her parentage given in Orderic Vitalis, who also names her husband and, in a later passage, her father and two older sons[2364].  The Genealogiæ Scriptoris Fusniac
2 CONC ensis names " Rotaldum eiusdem loci comitem et Iulainam de Aquila matrem regine Navarrensis, et Margaretam uxorem Gisleberti de Novo-burgo" as children, incorrectly, of "Rotaldo comiti de Pertica" & his wife Beatrix de Roucy, spec
2 CONC ifying that Marguerite had children "Rotaldum Ebrodiensem episcopum cum aliis liberis utriusque sexus"[2365].  “Henricus…Warwicense consul et Margareta uxor mea et Rogerus noster filius” donated property to Warwick St Mary by unda
2 CONC ted charter[2366].  The 1130 Pipe Roll records "comitisse de Warwic" in Wiltshire[2367].  1156.  The necrology of the church of Evreux records the death "27 Aug" of "Margarita mater Rotrodi episcopi"[2368].  m HENRI de Beaumont Ea
2 CONC rl of Warwick, son of ROGER Seigneur de Beaumont-le-Roger & his wife Adeline de Meulan ([1048]-[20 Jun] 1119, bur Préaux).  
2 CONT
2 CONT ~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~
2 CONT
2 CONT http://www.thepeerage.com/p36859.htm#i368589
2 CONT
2 CONT Margaret de Perche1
2 CONT
2 CONT F, #368589
2 CONT
2 CONT Last Edited=12 Jun 2009
2 CONT
2 CONT      Margaret de Perche is the daughter of Geoffrey II de Perche, Comte de Perche et Mortagne.1 She married Henry de Newburgh, 1st Earl of Warwick, son of Roger de Beaumont, Seigneur de Portaudemer and Adeline de Meulan.1
2 CONT
2 CONT Child of Margaret de Perche and Henry de Newburgh, 1st Earl of Warwick
2 CONT
2 CONT Roger de Newburgh, 2nd Earl of Warwick+1 d. 12 Jun 1153
2 CONT
2 CONT Citations
