1 NOTE {geni:about_me} Bertram de Verdun and Ernée de Verdun appear in 1076 in a chart of [https://www.geni.com/people/Guillaume-fitzGuimond-d-Avranches/6000000003649718942 William d'Avranches, son of Wimund].
2 CONT
2 CONT « ''Notum sit omnibus presentibus & futuris quod ego Guillelmus Guimondi filius jure hereditario patris mei tenent & possident totam decimam omnium vavassorum meorum de Luot absq; Contradictione cujus libet quod inde mihi placebat
2 CONC  faciebam. Diuturno autem tempore me sic illam tenente tandem gradi cor meum illustrante quae cujus vult miserantur & quem vult indurat metu eterne gehenne cepi expavescere & amore future grante flagrare consilio & exhortatione re
2 CONC verentissimi presulis Michaelis abrincatensis dedit atque cor umdam canonicorum amicorum meorum Gauslini videlicet, Johannis magister scolarum, '''Erneisi de Verduno''' atque omni capitulo sancti Andree laudante & concedente do & 
2 CONC concedo do & sancto Michaeli archangelo ejusque monachis totam hanc decimam de Luot videlicet duos manipulos omnium vavassorum meorum quos in proprio domino retinebam premedio anime mee meique patris & matris atque pro salute uxor
2 CONC is mee Mathildis eo tenore atque condictione quod ubicumque morbitus evenerit in Normannia monachisci Michaelis me ad Montem deferent & sicut fratrem suum honestissime & honorifice me repelient atque me tumulabunt. Actum est hoc a
2 CONC nno ab incarnatione domini M°L°x…°vi residente Michaele episcopo sede pontificali qui hoc donum confirmatur & Rannulfo abbate in ecclesia sancti Michaelis istis videntibus & audientibus. S† Guillelmi, S† Mathildis uxoris ejus, S† 
2 CONC '''Bertranni de Verduno''', S† Gaufredi de Cavinne, S† Radulfi de sancto Johanne, S† Radulfi de Musca'' ».
2 CONT
2 CONT Mont-Saint-Michel abbey cartulary, folios 83v et 84 (Bibliothèque d'Avranches, Manuscrit 210) : https://www.unicaen.fr/bvmsm/img-server/IMG/Avranches_BM/MSS/Avranches_BM_210/Avranches_BM_210_vue183_f83v.jpg?r=0 https://www.unicaen
2 CONC .fr/bvmsm/img-server/IMG/Avranches_BM/MSS/Avranches_BM_210/Avranches_BM_210_vue184_f84r.jpg?r=0
2 CONT
2 CONT Most probably he is the Bertram de Verdun who held [https://opendomesday.org/place/SU9683/farnham-royal/ Farnham Royal] in Domesday Book, 1086 : https://opendomesday.org/name/bertram-of-verdun/
2 CONT
2 CONT « ''xxxviii. '''Terra Bertranni de Verdun'''. In Stoches Hundret. '''Bertranus de Verdun''' tenet Ferneham […] In dominio […] silva […] in tempore regis Eduardi hoc tenuit Goda comtassa. De hoc tenet Godffrid de Maneville dimidiam
2 CONC  hide in Elmodesham de qua desaisivit praedictum '''Bertrannii''' duc est transmare in servicio regis. Hoc attestatur Hundret. Radulf Tailgebosc fecit supra terra '''Bertranni''' unu molin qui non fuit ibi tempore regis Eduardi, u
2 CONC t Hundret testatur'' ». 
2 CONT
2 CONT Bertram's wife's name is unknown, but his son and heir was Bertram II de Verdun (? – c. 1129/30). His son continued to amass land in England, and by 1128 also had been granted land in Staffordshire and Leicestershire. Hagger sugge
2 CONC sts that he also had assumed an administrative position for Henry I, and was possibly sheriff of Yorkshire in 1100.
2 CONT
2 CONT source:http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Bertram_de_Verdun
