1 NOTE {geni:about_me} ====FMG: Paris Region: [http://fmg.ac/Projects/MedLands/PARIS%20REGION%20NOBILITY.htm#MathieuIBeaumontdied1155B Beaumont, Beauvais]
2 CONT * '''MATHIEU''' [I] '''de Beaumont''', son of IVES [II] Comte de Beaumont & his second wife Adelais --- ([1070/73]-1 Jan 1155)....'''m''' (before 1101) '''BEATRIX de Clermont''', daughter of HUGUES de Clermont-en-Beauvaisis & his 
2 CONC wife Marguerite de Roucy (-after 1110)....'''Mathieu [I] & his wife had [four or more] children:'''...
2 CONT ** 3. '''HUGUES''' [I] de Beaumont (-1 May 1180 or after). The priory of Saint-Martin-des-Champs, Paris donated property to the church of Saint-Léonor de Beaumont by charter dated 6 Jul 1151 which names “''Matheus comes, filius Yv
2 CONC onis comitis''” and is witnessed by “''Matheus comes, Hugo frater eius''”[72]. "''Mattheus comes Belli montis''" exempted Saint-Leu d’Esserent from duties, with the consent of "''Matheo comite patre meo et Hugone fratre meo et Mat
2 CONC hilde comitissa uxore mea''", by charter dated 1154[73]. “''Mathei comitis, Mathei majoris et Mathei junioris et Philippi filiorum eius, Hugonis fratris eiusdem, Aelidis comitisse''...” witnessed the charter dated [25 Mar 1170/25 
2 CONC Mar 1171] which records that “''Ancoult d’Hénonville ecommunié''” restored “la dîme de Nointel” to the monks of Nointel[74]. '''Seigneur de Persan.''' The ''Necrologium Bellimontense'' records the death “''Kal Mai''” of ''“Hugo vi
2 CONC cecomes frater comitis Bellimontis''”[75].  
2 CONT ** '''m BEATRIX''', daughter of —–. ''The primary source which confirms her marriage has not been identified.'' '''Hugues [I] & his first wife had six children:''' 
2 CONT *** a) HUGUES [II] de Beaumont (-after 1203)....
2 CONT *** b) IVES de Beaumont (-before 1223)....
2 CONT *** c) GUILLAUME de Beaumont (-before 1224)....
2 CONT *** d) HEUDEBORGE de Beaumont (-after 1203)....
2 CONT *** e) BEATRIX de Beaumont (-before 1223)....
2 CONT *** f) MARIE de Beaumont (-before 1223)....
2 CONT
2 CONT A Google Books Search limited to "Hugues de Beaumont-sur-Oise" brings up only one book showing "-sur-Oise" tagged to the name, which Medlands does not. It does so very briefly in a passing mention. From ''Bulletin archéologique, h
2 CONC istorique et scientifique''; [https://www.google.com/books/edition/Bulletin_arch%C3%A9ologique_historique_et_sc/U3Y4AAAAMAAJ?hl=en&gbpv=1&dq=%22Hugues+de+Beaumont-sur-Oise%22&pg=PA59&printsec=frontcover '''p. 59''']:—
2 CONT >"...On l'attribue à Gérard d'Auchy, descendant ce Guy de Beaumanoir, à qui Hugues Capt avait donné ce demaine en 1029. Il avait pour propriétaire, au XIIe siècle, '''Béatrix, fille d'Hugues de Beaumont-sur-Oise''', qui la porta d
2 CONC ans la maison de Thorotte, par son marriage avec Guy de Thorotte...."
2 CONT
2 CONT '''On 22 Mar 2026,''' Our Royal Titled Noble and Commoner Ancestors and Cousins for [https://our-royal-titled-noble-and-commoner-ancestors.com/p3663.htm#i110017 Hugues de Beaumont-sur-Oise, Seigneur de Persan] only cited trees:—
2 CONT * Généalogie Famille de Carné. – aka unsourced [https://gw.geneanet.org/adecarne?lang=fr&p=hugues&n=de+beaumont+sur+oise gw.Geneanet.org]
2 CONT * ''Europaische Stammtafeln'', by Wilhelm Karl, Prinz zu Isenburg, Vol. III, Tafel 644.
