2 CONT Basic information and justifications:
2 CONT *Birth: 990/995 (French Wikipedia) - may presume Meulan, but not specified by source.
2 CONT *Death: 8 December 1069 (FMG, Wikipedia) - may presume Meulan, but not specified by source.
2 CONT *Wedding: He married Oda around 1015, Adelais - unknown.
2 CONT *Burial: Unknown.
2 CONT *Occupation: Comte de Meulan (1005-1069)
2 CONT *Alternate names: Waleran, Gualeran, Valeran.
2 CONT
2 CONT --------------------
2 CONT
2 CONT From the Foundation for Medieval Genealogy page on Normandy Nobility (relating to his birth family):
2 CONT
2 CONT http://fmg.ac/Projects/MedLands/NORMANDY%20NOBILITY.htm#Walerandied1166B
2 CONT
2 CONT HUGUES [I] de Meulan (-after 25 Aug 1005).  
2 CONT *"…Hugo filius Waleranni comitis" are named as present in the charter dated 1035 under which "Willelmus adhuc puerulus…Roberti comitis filius" donated "Turstini villa" to the abbey of Préaux[1891].  
2 CONT *Comte de Meulan 998.  
2 CONT
2 CONT m --- de Valois, daughter of GAUTHIER [II] "le Blanc" Comte d'Amiens, de Mantes, de Valois et du Vexin & his wife Adela ---.  
2 CONT *The Chronicle of Alberic de Trois-Fontaines refers to the mother of "Waleranni comitis [Mellentini]" as daughter of "Gauterus Albus de Albamarla"[1892].  Yves de Chartres names "Gualterius Albus" as father of "matrem Gualeranni c
2 CONC omitis"[1893].  
2 CONT
2 CONT Hugues & his wife had three children (Galeran being the only one listed): 
2 CONT
2 CONT (a)   GALERAN [III] de Meulan (-8 Dec 1069).  
2 CONT *The Chronicle of Alberic de Trois-Fontaines names "Waleranni comitis [Mellentini]" as son of "filia Gauterus Albus de Albamarla"[1894].  
2 CONT *Comte de Meulan. 
2 CONT
2 CONT References:
2 CONT *[1892] Chronica Albrici Monachi Trium Fontium 1062, MGH SS XXIII, p. 793. 
2 CONT *[1893] Yves de Chartres, Epistola 45, Patrologia Latina, Tome 162, col. 57. 
2 CONT *[1894] Chronica Albrici Monachi Trium Fontium 1062, MGH SS XXIII, p. 793. 
2 CONT
2 CONT ----------------------
2 CONT
2 CONT From the Foundation for Medieval Genealogy page on Normandy Nobility (relating to his married family):
2 CONT
2 CONT http://fmg.ac/Projects/MedLands/NORMANDY%20NOBILITY.htm#Walerandied1166B
2 CONT
2 CONT GALERAN [III] de Meulan, son of HUGUES [I] Comte de Meulan & his wife --- de Valois (-8 Dec 1069).  
2 CONT *The Chronicle of Alberic de Trois-Fontaines names "Waleranni comitis [Mellentini]" as son of "filia Gauterus Albus de Albamarla"[1895].  Yves de Chartres names "Gualterius Albus" as father of "matrem Gualeranni comitis"[1896].  
2 CONT *Comte de Meulan.  William of Jumièges recounts that "Hugues du Mans et Galeran de Meulan" were among those who joined the army of Eudes Comte de Blois in attempting to capture the château de Tillières {Verneuil, Eure} from Richar
2 CONC d II Duke of Normandy, an event dated to the early 1000s[1897].  
2 CONT *"Gualerannus, Mellentis castri comes" donated a family of servants to "Sancti Petri Gisecii…Carnotensis", by undated charter, signed by "Gualeranni comitis, Hugonis primogeniti, coniugis Adelidis, Gualeranni filii, Fulcoisi filii
2 CONC , Teduini vicecomitis…"[1898].  “…Walterius comes Pontisariensis, Willelmus comes Corboilensis, Ivo comes Bellomontensis, Walerannus comes Melledensis” are named among those present at the opening of the reliquary of Saint-Denis, 
2 CONC dated 9 Jun 1053[1899].  
2 CONT
2 CONT ---
2 CONT
2 CONT m firstly (before 1015) ODA, daughter of ---.  
2 CONT *“Hugo comes Mellenti” founded the monastery of St Cosmus and St Damian, for the souls of “conjugis…Adelidis…genitoris mei comitis Galeranni atque Odæ genetricis meæ”, by charter dated 1067[1900].  1030.  
2 CONT
2 CONT ---
2 CONT
2 CONT m secondly ADELAIS, daughter of --- (-31 May <nowiki>----</nowiki>).  
2 CONT *She had previously been his concubine.  "Vualeranni comitis, Hugonis filii eius, Adilais uxoris eius" subscribed a charter dated to before 1031 recording a donation to Jumièges[1901].  1031/36, 1066.  "Gualerannus, Mellentis cast
2 CONC ri comes" donated a family of servants to "Sancti Petri Gisecii…Carnotensis", by undated charter, signed by "Gualeranni comitis, Hugonis primogeniti, coniugis Adelidis, Gualeranni filii, Fulcoisi filii, Teduini vicecomitis…"[1902]
2 CONC .  
2 CONT
2 CONT ---
2 CONT
2 CONT Galéran [III] & his first wife had two children:  
2 CONT
2 CONT 1.  HUGUES [III] de Meulan (-15 Oct 1081).  
2 CONT *"Vualeranni comitis, Hugonis filii eius, Adilais uxoris eius" subscribed a charter dated to before 1031 recording a donation to Jumièges[1903].  He is named as the brother-in-law of Roger de Beaumont by Orderic Vitalis[1904].  "G
2 CONC ualerannus, Mellentis castri comes" donated a family of servants to "Sancti Petri Gisecii…Carnotensis", by undated charter, signed by "Gualeranni comitis, Hugonis primogeniti, coniugis Adelidis, Gualeranni filii, Fulcoisi filii, T
2 CONC eduini vicecomitis…"[1905].  
2 CONT *Comte de Meulan.  The charter dated Oct 1056 under which "Mellendis castelli comes Hugo natus patre Waleranno" donated property to the abbey of Jumièges[1906] shows that he succeeded as comte well before his father's death, assum
2 CONC ing that this charter is correctly dated and that Waléran's date of death is as shown above.  “Hugo comes Mellenti” founded the monastery of St Cosmus and St Damian, for the souls of “conjugis…Adelidis…genitoris mei comitis Galera
2 CONC nni atque Odæ genetricis meæ”, by charter dated 1067[1907].  Guillaume de Jumièges names "Hugues oncle maternel" of Robert son of "Roger de Beaumont" & his wife[1908].  He became a monk at Bec before 1081.  
2 CONT *The necrology of Saint-Nicaise de Meulan records the death "Id Oct" of "Hugo comes Mellenti"[1909].  
2 CONT *m ADELAIS, daughter of ---.  “Hugo comes Mellenti” founded the monastery of St Cosmus and St Damian, for the souls of “conjugis…Adelidis…genitoris mei comitis Galeranni atque Odæ genetricis meæ”, by charter dated 1067[1910]. 
2 CONT
2 CONT 2. ADELINE de Meulan (-8 Apr 1081, bur Abbaye du Bec).  
2 CONT *Guillaume de Jumièges names "Adeline fille de Galeran comte de Meulan" as wife of "Roger de Beaumont"[1911].  The Chronicle of Alberic de Trois-Fontaines refers to "matrem Roberti comitis Mellentini" as daughter of "Waleranni com
2 CONC itis [Mellentini]"[1912].  Yves de Chartres names "Gualterius Albus" as father of "matrem Gualeranni comitis" and adds that the latter was the father of "matrem Roberti comitis"[1913].  
2 CONT *She was heiress of Meulan after the death of her brother Hugues Comte de Meulan.  Orderic Vitalis names Adeline as wife of Roger, and in another place states her father's name[1914].  Robert count of Mellent donated property to S
2 CONC t Pierre, Préaux for the souls of his parents Roger de Bellomonte and Adelina his wife, by charter dated to [1099][1915].  
2 CONT *m ROGER de Beaumont-le-Roger Seigneur de Beaumont et de Pont-Audemer, son of HONFROI de Vieilles & his wife Aubreye --- (-29 Nov 1094, bur Préaux, monastery of Saint-Pierre).  He contributed 60 ships to the fleet of Guillaume II 
2 CONC Duke of Normandy which invaded England in 1066[1916]. 
2 CONT *Galéran [III] & his [first/second] wife had one child.
2 CONT
2 CONT 3. DODA de Meulan .  
2 CONT *Her father is named by Orderic Vitalis, who also refers to her marriage[1917].  
2 CONT *m as his second wife, GUILLAUME de Moulins-la-Marche, son of GAUTHIER de Falaise & his wife --- (-19 Oct <nowiki>----</nowiki>, bur Saint-Evroul[1918]). Galéran [III] & his second wife had two children.
2 CONT
2 CONT 4. GALERAN de Meulan .  
2 CONT *"Gualerannus, Mellentis castri comes" donated a family of servants to "Sancti Petri Gisecii…Carnotensis", by undated charter, signed by "Gualeranni comitis, Hugonis primogeniti, coniugis Adelidis, Gualeranni filii, Fulcoisi filii
2 CONC , Teduini vicecomitis…"[1919].  1066.  
2 CONT *He left descendants, extinct in the male line in 13th century[1920]. 
2 CONT
2 CONT 5. FOULQUES de Meulan .  
2 CONT *"Gualerannus, Mellentis castri comes" donated a family of servants to "Sancti Petri Gisecii…Carnotensis", by undated charter, signed by "Gualeranni comitis, Hugonis primogeniti, coniugis Adelidis, Gualeranni filii, Fulcoisi filii
2 CONC , Teduini vicecomitis…"[1921]. 
2 CONT
