2 CONC oire des ducs de Normandie, par Guillaume de Jumiège (Paris), VII.3, p. 171. [1909] Obituaires de Sens Tome II, Prieuré de Saint-Nicaise de Meulan, p. 241. [1910] Veterum Scriptorum I, col. 471. [1911] Guizot, M. (ed.) (1826) Hist
2 CONC oire des ducs de Normandie, par Guillaume de Jumiège (Paris), VII.3, p. 170. [1912] Chronica Albrici Monachi Trium Fontium 1062, MGH SS XXIII, p. 793. [1913] Yves de Chartres, Epistola 45, Patrologia Latina, Tome 162, col. 57. [19
2 CONC 14] Orderic Vitalis, Vol. III, Book VI, p. 241, and Vol. IV, Book VIII, p. 205, respectively. [1915] Round (1899) 326, p. 111. [1916] Ship List of William the Conqueror, Houts (2000), p. 130. [1917] Orderic Vitalis, Vol. III, Book
2 CONC  V, p. 133. [1918] Orderic Vitalis, Vol. III, Book V, p. 135. [1919] Chartres Saint-Père I, Liber Septimus, Cap. XLIV, p. 171. [1920] See ES III 729 A. [1921] Chartres Saint-Père I, Liber Septimus, Cap. XLIV, p. 171.
2 CONT -----------------------
2 CONT
2 CONT Ben M. Angel notes, regarding Galeran's first wife:
2 CONT
2 CONT On the question of Oda vs. Alix, French Wikipedia supports Oda de Vexin. Alix de Vexin appears to be supported only by numerous GEDCOM files that do not appear to have a reliable source (I welcome a correction on this, if a reliab
2 CONC le source, other than "someone else's GEDCOM or online family tree" does exist - "The Plantagenet Ancestry" by W.H. Turton provides no primary sources, see below). My best guess as to why Alix has appeared and proliferated on unso
2 CONC urced GEDCOM files is confusion with Alix/Alys de Vexin, who was born to King Robert VII of France a century and a half later:
2 CONT
2 CONT http://familypedia.wikia.com/wiki/Alix_de_Vexin_(c1170-c1220)
2 CONT
2 CONT http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Alys,_Countess_of_the_Vexin
2 CONT
2 CONT ------------
2 CONT
2 CONT The Plantagenet Ancestry is cited as listing Alix de Vexin as husband of Hugues I (the online sample does not carry the page showing this, unfortunately). Although a fascinating collection of charts of 7,000 names showing what app
2 CONC ears to be researched relationships of the ancestry of the Plantagenets, the source material backing Alix de Vexin is not included within the online sample:
2 CONT
2 CONT http://books.google.cl/books?id=jcxwxO1723cC&pg=PT168&lpg=PT168&dq=%22The+Plantagenet+Ancestry%22+Turton&source=bl&ots=-HfaAYkDlb&sig=J9vmD2TXBOkEIyjEwLKQqmKb7jk#v=onepage&q&f=false
2 CONT
2 CONT --------------------------------
2 CONT
2 CONT From the Celtic Casimir online family tree:
2 CONT
2 CONT http://www.celtic-casimir.com/webtree/5/5840.htm
2 CONT
2 CONT Cte Valeran (Waleran) III DE MEULAN 1560,2071
2 CONT
2 CONT Born: 990, Meulan, Yvelines, Ile-de-France, France Married: Abt 1017, France Died: 8 Oct 1069 Ancestral File Number: FNMC-PW. Marriage Information:
2 CONT
2 CONT Valeran married Oda (Ode) DE CONTEVILLE, daughter of Earl Jean DE CONTEVILLE vicomte de Comyn and Unnamed Dame de Meullant, about 1017 in France. (Oda (Ode) DE CONTEVILLE was born about 990 in Conteville, Eure, Normandy, France an
2 CONC d died after 1022.) References:
2 CONT
2 CONT 1560. Jim Weber <jim.weber at nwint1.com>, WorldConnect at Rootsweb, http://worldconnect.rootsweb.com/cgi-bin/igm.cgi?op=PED&db=jweber&id=I00345&style=TABLE 2071. (Outdated link): http://perso.orange.fr/emmanuel.hamel/dat112.htm#1
2 CONC 68
2 CONT ------------------------------
2 CONT
2 CONT From the French Wikipedia page on Comte Galeran III de Meulan:
2 CONT
2 CONT http://fr.wikipedia.org/wiki/Gal%C3%A9ran_III_de_Meulan
2 CONT
2 CONT Galéran III ou Valéran III fut vicomte de Meulan à partir de 1005, puis s'intitula comte de Meulan peu avant 1015. Il était fils d'Hugues Ier, vicomte de Meulan, et d'Oda du Vexin.
2 CONT
2 CONT L'année de sa naissance n'est pas connue. L'on peut cependant l'estimer à 990/95, car son père est né aux alentours de 965, et Galéran est suffisamment puissant en 1015 pour prendre le titre de comte.
2 CONT
2 CONT En 1013, allié au comte Eudes II de Blois, il combat le duc Richard II de Normandie, puis le roi Robert II de France. C'est une lettre de l'évêque Fulbert de Chartres, datée de 1015, qui le qualifie de comte, qui l'incite à change
2 CONC r d'alliance et à se ranger aux côtés du roi de France. Il s'allie également au duc de Normandie et accorde en 1023 des exemptions de péage aux moines de Fécamp. Entre 1027 et 1031, un différent l'oppose à l'abbaye de Jumièges à p
2 CONC ropos de la terre de Bouafle.
2 CONT
2 CONT En 1041, avec son cousin Raoul IV de Vexin, il se révolte contre le roi Henri Ier, mais est vaincu, et ne conserve ses terres que par le soutien du duc de Normandie.[réf. nécessaire]
2 CONT
2 CONT Galéran III mourut le 8 décembre 1069, et son fils Hugues III lui succéda.
2 CONT
2 CONT Mariages et enfants
2 CONT
2 CONT Il épousa avant 1015 Ode (encore vivante en 1030), qui donna naissance à :
2 CONT
2 CONT 1. Hugues III († 1080), comte de Meulan 2. Adeline († 1081), comtesse de Meulan, mariée à Roger le Barbu (v. 1015 † 1094), seigneur de Beaumont. Il épousa en secondes noces Aelis[1], qui donna naissance à :
2 CONT
2 CONT 1. Galéran de Meulan, cité en 1066, et tige d'une branche qui se perpétua jusqu'au XIIIe siècle 2. Foulques de Meulan, cité en 1069. On ne sait pas pourquoi Galéran de Meulan ne succéda pas à son frère Hugues III.
2 CONT
2 CONT Une autre fille est connue, sans que l'on sache de quelle union elle était issue :
2 CONT
2 CONT 1. Duda, mariée à Guillaume de Moulins-la-Marche, fils de Gautier de Falaise. Notes et références
2 CONT
2 CONT 1.↑ Tout ceci est mentionné par une charte de Saint-Père de Chartres de qui porte les signatures suivantes, dans l'ordre et très littéralement: "Galéran comte, Hugues fils aîné, Aélis épouse, Galéran fils, Foulques fils" (éd. Guér
2 CONC ard, p. 117-118[précision nécessaire])
2 CONT
2 CONT ----
2 CONT
2 CONT English summary:
2 CONT
2 CONT Galeran or Valeran III became the Viscount (Vicomte) Meulan in 1005. He called himself Count (Comte) shortly before 1015. He was the son of Hugh Vicomte Meulan and Oda du Vexin.
2 CONT
2 CONT The year he was born is uncertain, but it is estimated to be between 990 and 995 as his father was born in 965, and he was sufficiently powerful to take the title of Count in 1015.
2 CONT
2 CONT In 1013, he became an ally of the Comte Eudes II of Blois. He fought Duke Richard II of Normandy and King Robert II of France.
2 CONT
2 CONT In a letter from the Bishop Fulbert of Chartres dated in 1015, he is addressed as Comte, and is encouraged to switch allegiances and side with the King of France. He also sides with the Duke of Normandy in 1023, and excludes from 
2 CONC taxes the monks of Fecamp. Between 1027 and 1031, he opposes the Abbey Jumieges over the land of Bouafle.
2 CONT
2 CONT In 1041, with his cousin Raoul Vexin IV, he rebels against King Henry I, but is defeated. He retains his lands with the support of the Duke of Normandy.
2 CONT
2 CONT Galeran III dies on December 8, 1069, and his son Hugh III succeeds him.
2 CONT
2 CONT He married Ode before 1015 (she was still alive in 1030), who gave birth to Hugh III (d. 1080), Comte Meulan, and Adeline (d. 1081), Comtesse de Meulan, who married Henry the Bearded (c. 1015 - d. 1094) Lord (or Seigneur) of Beaum
2 CONC ont.
2 CONT
2 CONT His second wife was Aelis, who gave birth to two other children: Galeran (cited in 1066 and whose branch continues until the 13th century) and Fulke (cited in 1069). There is no reason given why Galeran did not succeed his brother
2 CONC  Hugh III on his death.
2 CONT
2 CONT Another girl is known, although by whom she was born is not:
2 CONT
2 CONT Duda, married to William de Moulins-la-Marche, son of Walter of Falaise.
2 CONT
2 CONT (Marie is not listed.)
2 CONT
