2 CONT From Darryl Lundy's Peerage page on Anne of Kiev:
2 CONT
2 CONT http://www.thepeerage.com/p10318.htm#i103174
2 CONT
2 CONT Anne of Kiev[1]
2 CONT
2 CONT F, #103174, b. circa 1024, d. circa 1075
2 CONT
2 CONT Last Edited=7 Mar 2007
2 CONT
2 CONT Anne of Kiev was born circa 1024. She was the daughter of Jarislaus I, Grand Duke of Kiev and Ingegarde of Sweden.[1],[2]
2 CONT
2 CONT She married Raoul Crepi.[3]
2 CONT
2 CONT She married Henri I, Roi de France, son of Robert II, Roi de France and Constance d'Arles, on 29 January 1044.[1]
2 CONT
2 CONT She died circa 1075.
2 CONT
2 CONT Children of Anne of Kiev and Henri I, Roi de France
2 CONT
2 CONT 1. Philippe I, Roi de France+1 b. c 1052, d. 29 Jul 1108
2 CONT
2 CONT 2. Hugh de Crépi, Comte de Vermandois et de Valois
2 CONT
2 CONT +3 b. 1057, d. 18 Oct 1102
2 CONT
2 CONT Citations
2 CONT
2 CONT 1. [S45] Marcellus Donald R. von Redlich, Pedigrees of Some of the Emperor Charlemagne's Descendants, volume I (1941; reprint, Baltimore, Maryland, U.S.A.: Genealogical Publishing Company, 2002), page 63. Hereinafter cited as Pedi
2 CONC grees of Emperor Charlemagne, I.
2 CONT
