2 CONT     (3) Also AFN 8HJ7D0
1 NOTE Anne of Kiev
2 CONT Born in 1024
2 CONT Died after 1075
2 CONT
2 CONT Anne married on January 20, 1044 to Henry I Capet, King of France andthey had the following sons:
2 CONT
2 CONT Philip I the Fair Capet, King of France, born in 1052
2 CONT
2 CONT Anna Agnesa Yaroslavna Rurikide, Grand Duchess of Kiev and Queen ofFrance "Anne de Kiev" was born 1024 in Kiev, Ukraine and married 1051.She died circa 1076 in France and was buried in Villiers Abbey, LaFerte-Alais, Essonne, Franc
2 CONC e.
2 CONT
2 CONT BIOGRAPHY: Anne of Kiev was the wife of Henry I of France and thedaughter of Jaroslav I. She married Henry at the cathedral of Reims, May19, 1051 and had three sons: Philippe I, King of France, Hugues("Magnus"), and Robert. For si
2 CONC x years after his death in 1060, she servedas regent for their son, Philip, who was 7 at the time of his father'sdeath. She was the first queen of France to serve as regent. A year afterthe King's death, Anne, acting as Regent, to
2 CONC ok a passionate fancy forRaoul II (III?) de Péronne, Count of Crépy, of Valois and of the Vexin, aman whose political ambition encouraged him to repudiate his wife tomarry Anne in 1062. Accused of adultery, Raoul's wife appealed t
2 CONC o PopeAlexander II, who excommunicated Raoul and Anne. The young king Philippeforgave his mother, which was just as well, since he was to find himselfin a very similar predicament in the 1090s. Raoul died in September 1071.This in
2 CONC formation was taken fromhttp://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Anne_of_Kiev.
1 NOTE Anna Yaruslavna van Kiev, geb. 1036 in Kiev, ovl. 1076/89, begraven in abdij Villiers bij La-Ferté-Alais, ref. nr. 20.03.2005 ES II-11 /-128, GOFFp72.10,[56]                         Regentesse van Frankrijk 1060/67, sticht het klo
2 CONC oster St.-Martin-des-Champs te Parijs en St. Vincent te Senlis. Trouwt (2) 1061 Raoul II de Crépi, graaf van Valois, van Crépy en van Vitry. Uit het huwelijk van Henri met Anna blijkt, dat de banden tussen het Christelijk Europa e
2 CONC n de Orthodoxe Slavische wereld niet geheel verbroken waren (Le Goff).
1 NOTE Line 3121 from GEDCOM File not recognizable or too long:
2 CONT   NAME Anastasiya Agmunda Yaroslavna Princess Of /KIEV/
1 NOTE BIOGRAPHY
2 CONT Daughter of Jaroslav, grand duke of Kiev and Ingegerd of Sweden, Anna was born in 1036. On 19 May 1051 in Reims she married Henri I, king of France, son of Robert II 'le Pieux' and Constance de Provence. They had three sons of who
2 CONC m two would have progeny. Henri died in 1060 and about a year later she married Raoul de Crépy, count of Valois but he was excommunicated as he was related to the late king in a forbidden degree.
2 CONT
2 CONT Anna introduced the Christian name Philippe to France, giving it to her eldest son from her first marriage, who was to reign as Philippe I. Anna died after 1076.
