2 CONT '' Chapter 2.    ROCHEFORT
2 CONT '' A.      COMTES de ROCHEFORT (SEIGNEURS de MONTLHERY)
2 CONT '' https://fmg.ac/Projects/MedLands/parcorroc.htm#GuyIIMontlheryRochefortdied1108B
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT ''GUY [II] le Rouge" de Montlhéry'', son of GUY [I] Seigneur de Montlhéry & his wife Hodierne de Gometz-la-Ferté (-1108).  .. ... .... 
2 CONT
2 CONT '''m''' firstly ''' ELISABETH, daughter of ---'''.  The primary source which confirms her marriage has not been identified.   1059/1067.  Père Anselme reverses the order of Guy [II]’s wives, naming “Adelais” as his first wife and 
2 CONC “Elizabeth dame de Crecy, veuve de Bouchard II Comte de Corbeil” as his second, noting that “Adelais” founded the priory of Notre-Dame de Gournay-sur-Marne with her husband[528]. 
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT '''m''' secondly ( after [1071/80] ) as her second husband, [https://www.geni.com/people/Adelaide-Corbeil-Montlhery/6000000022080557312 ''ADELAIS de Crécy''],  widow of BOUCHARD [II] Comte de Corbeil, daughter of --- (-[24 Sep or 
2 CONC 12 Oct] after 1104). 
2 CONT
2 CONT Guy [II] & his [first] wife had [three] children: 
2 CONT *1.         GUY [III] (-[19 Nov] [1115]).  Comte de Rochefort.  "Guido comes Rocheforti" donated property to the abbey of Sainte-Trinité de Tiron by charter dated [1114] witnessed by "Rotrocus comes Perticensis, Beatrix comitissa 
2 CONC mater eiusdem"[534].  "Guido, Guidoni filius, de Rupe Forti" consented to a donation to Notre-Dame de Longpont by charter dated to [1115/18][535].  A charter dated to [1119/30] records that “Guido comes de Rupeforti” donated “in v
2 CONC illa...Ermentarvilla” to Saint-Jean-en-Vallée before he died, with the consent of “Beatrix soror eius”, witnessed by “...Hugo de Creci monacus”[536].  The necrology of Longpont records the death "IX Kal Aug" of "Guido institutor h
2 CONC ujus loci. Guido vicecomes; Adalaidis comitissa, uxor; Wido filius eius"[537].  [The necrology of Longpont also records the death "XIII Kal Dec" of "Guido de Rocaforti"[538].  The absence of the comital title in this entry suggest
2 CONC s that it may not refer to the comital family.  If it does, it is uncertain whether Guy [II] or Guy [III] is intended.]  m ---.  The name of Guy's wife is not known.  Guy [III] & his wife had [one child]:  …
2 CONT * 2.         [daughter .  The primary source which confirms her parentage and marriage has not been identified.   Père Anselme records that an unnamed daughter of Guy [II] married “Anseau de Garlande senechal de France” but indica
2 CONC tes no primary source on which the statement is based[540].  It may be speculative designed to explain the transmission of Rochefort to her daughter.  m ANSEAU de Garlande, son of GUILLAUME [I] Seigneur de Garlande & his wife Havo
2 CONC ise --- (-1118).  Seneschal of France 1107/18.] 
2 CONT *3.         [BIOTE de Montlhéry .  Her parentage and marriage are confirmed only by a document written in 1630 which names "Fédéric vicomte de Gastinois, fils de Guy…fils d’un autre Guy…vicomte de Gastinois nay de Biote de Rochefo
2 CONC rt, sœur de Guy II comte de Rochefort et de Hugues de Crécy"[541].  If this is correct, the chronology suggests that she was born from her father’s first marriage.  m (before 1098) FOULQUES Vicomte de Château-Landon, son of LETAUD
2 CONC  [II] & his wife --- (-after 1122).] 
2 CONT
2 CONT -------------
2 CONT
2 CONT Elizabeth, dame de Crécy, married Guy "le Rouge" de Montlhéry, senechal de France, son of Guy I, seigneur de Montlhéry and Hodierne de Gommets, before 1075.
2 CONT
2 CONT Elizabeth died after 1104.
2 CONT
2 CONT See "My Lines" 
