2 CONT The following information was supplied by Curt Hofemann, curt_hofemann@yaoo.com. I added Guy's 2nd wife, who appeared to be his mother-in-law. Guy 'le Rouge' de Montlhery, Comte de Rochefort-en-Yveline, Seigneur de Gournay et Gome
2 CONC z Count of Rochefort, Seigneur of Gournay & Gomez [Ref: Moriarty p63] Seigneur de Rochefort-en-Yveline & Montmorency [Ref: ES II:11] called "the Red," Sire de Montlhery, Count of Rochefort-en-Yvelines, Lord of Chateaufort, Senesch
2 CONC al of France, Seigneur of Fornay (sic) & Gomez [Ref: Royalty for Commoners 5:31] b: 1037 (Of Montlhery) [Ref: McBride] parents: [Ref: Moriarty Plantagenet p63 & 265] m1: Elise de Corbeil m2: Adelaide de Crecy as 2nd wife [Ref: ES 
2 CONC III:624] 2nd husband [Ref: ES II:79] d: 1108 [Ref:ES III:624] Regards, Curt
2 CONT --------------------
2 CONT Guy was also called Guy de Rochefort (Guy of Rochefort).
2 CONT
2 CONT Guy "le Rouge" de Montlhéry, senechal de France, married Elizabeth, dame de Crécy, before 1075. 
2 CONT
2 CONT Guy was the 8th senechal of France in 1093. 
2 CONT
2 CONT He was on Crusade in 1101.
2 CONT
2 CONT See "My Lines" 
