2 CONT
2 CONT The Seigneurs de Montfort-l'Amaury were vassals of the Comtes de Beaumont[sur-Oise], as shown by the charter dated to before 1091 under which "Mainerium, fratrem Symonis de Monte Forti" donated property, with the consent of "…comi
2 CONC teque Belli Montis Ivonis"[120].  The primary sources which confirm the parentage and marriages of the members of the following family have not yet been identified, unless otherwise stated below. 
2 CONT
2 CONT '''AMAURY de Montfort''', son of --- (-after Apr 1052).  “Comes Ivo de Bello monte, Ebo miles, Guarinus miles Parisius, Almaricus miles de Monteforte” witnessed the charter dated 1022 under which Robert II King of France confirmed
2 CONC  the possessions of the abbey of Saint-Mesmin de Micy[121].  “…Almarici de Monteforti…” witnessed the charter dated 1028 under which Robert II King of France confirmed the possessions of the abbey of Saint-Mesmin de Micy[122].  Ro
2 CONC bert II King of France confirmed the donation of "Manasses comes" to Chartres Notre-Dame by charter dated 4 Feb 1031, signed by "…Manasses comitis, Hilduini comitis fratris eius, filorum eius Manassis et Hilduini, Burcardo de Mont
2 CONC emorenciaco, Evrardi filii Hilduini de Britoglio, Amalrici de Monteforti, Milonis de Caprosa…"[123].  He began the building of the castle of Montfort l'Amaury, which was finished by his son[124].  "Amalricus miles" founded the pri
2 CONC ory of Saint-Thomas d´Epernon, with the consent of "conjugis mee…Bertredis…et filiorum meorum…Simonis…atque Mainerii", by charter dated [11 Apr 1052/Jul 1053][125]. 
2 CONT
2 CONT m '''BERTRADE''', daughter of --- (-after Apr 1052).  "Amalricus miles" founded the priory of Saint-Thomas d´Epernon, with the consent of "conjugis mee…Bertredis…et filiorum meorum…Simonis…atque Mainerii", by charter dated [11 Apr
2 CONC  1052/Jul 1053][126]. 
2 CONT
2 CONT Amaury & his wife had [three] children: 
2 CONT
2 CONT 1.         '''SIMON de Montfort''' (-25 Sep [1087], bur Epernon).  "Amalricus miles" founded the priory of Saint-Thomas d´Epernon, with the consent of "conjugis mee…Bertredis…et filiorum meorum…Simonis…atque Mainerii", by charter 
2 CONC dated [11 Apr 1052/Jul 1053][127].  Sire de Montfort-l'Amaury. 
2 CONT
2 CONT 2.        ''' MAINIER de Montfort''' (-before 1091).  "Amalricus miles" founded the priory of Saint-Thomas d´Epernon, with the consent of "conjugis mee…Bertredis…et filiorum meorum…Simonis…atque Mainerii", by charter dated [11 Apr
2 CONC  1052/Jul 1053][128].  "Mainerium, fratrem Symonis de Monte Forti" donated property, with the consent of "Simone fratre eius comiteque Belli Montis Ivonis", by charter dated to before 1091, which also names "domnus Simon, filio su
2 CONC o Amalrico"[129].  He granted a free passage at Saint-Piat to the monks of Saint-Père, II, in which his wife and two sons are named[130].  Seigneur d'Epernon.  m ELISABETH, daughter of ---.  She is named in her husband's charter t
2 CONC o the monks of Saint-Père[131].  Mainier & his wife had two children: 
2 CONT
2 CONT a)        ''' AMAURY de Montfort''' .  He is named in his father's charter to the monks of Saint-Père[132].  1133.  Seigneur d'Epernon.  m ---.  The name of Amaury's wife is not known.  Amaury & his wife had two children: 
2 CONT
2 CONT i)          SIMON .  The primary source which confirms his parentage has not yet been identified. 
2 CONT
2 CONT ii)         MAINIER .  The primary source which confirms his parentage has not yet been identified. 
2 CONT
2 CONT b)         GUILLAUME de Montfort .  He is named in his father's charter to the monks of Saint-Père[133]. 
2 CONT
2 CONT 3.         ['''EVA''' (-23 Jan 1099, bur Bec abbey).  Her possible affiliation is explained in the Complete Peerage[134].  m GUILLAUME Crispin, son of GILBERT [I] Crispin & his wife Gunnora --- (-Bec 8 Jan 1074).]  
2 CONT
