2 CONT
2 CONT Information about Montfort-l'Amaury Castle in France:
2 CONT
2 CONT http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Montfort-l%27Amaury
2 CONT
2 CONT --------------------
2 CONT
2 CONT Amauri was also called Amalric.
2 CONT
2 CONT Amauri I, 1st seigneur de Montfort, attested a charter of Robert I of France as "Sie. Almaricus miles de Montforti" in 1022.
2 CONT
2 CONT He married Bertrade (?) before 1025.
2 CONT
2 CONT He attested a charter of Robert I of France as "S. Almarici de Monteforti" in 1028. He attested a charter for Notre-Dame de Chartres of Robert I of France as "Signum Amalrici de Monteforti" on 4 February 1031.
2 CONT
2 CONT Amauri began the building of Montfort, the castle which took its name for him, Montfort-l'Amaury, described as a "castrum" at Yvelines, Île-de-France.
2 CONT
2 CONT Amauri died circa 1053. The precise date of his death is unknown. Since his wife and children appear in a charter in this year, consenting to gifts he had made, it may well be he was already dead.
2 CONT
