2 CONT  Kone / partner:       Bertrade (d 'Epernon) de GOMETZ 
2 CONT   Børn:       Eva De Montfort   ,   Simon I (Sn., de) MONTFORT
2 CONT
2 CONT ----
2 CONT
2 CONT Hans (evt.) Børnebørn:       Gilbert III de Crispin   ,   Isabel (Elizabeth) De Montfort   ,   Bertrade De Montfort (l 'Amauri)   ,   Amauri III (Amaury, IV) De Montfort   ,   Eve De Montfort 
2 CONT
2 CONT --
2 CONT
2 CONT Fra http://fabpedigree.com/s056/f017515.htm
2 CONT
2 CONT --------------------
2 CONT http://fmg.ac/Projects/MedLands/PARIS%20REGION%20NOBILITY.htm#_Toc257353309
2 CONT
2 CONT The Seigneurs de Montfort-l'Amaury were vassals of the Comtes de Beaumont[sur-Oise], as shown by the charter dated to before 1091 under which "Mainerium, fratrem Symonis de Monte Forti" donated property, with the consent of "…comi
2 CONC teque Belli Montis Ivonis"[120]. The primary sources which confirm the parentage and marriages of the members of the following family have not yet been identified, unless otherwise stated below.
2 CONT
2 CONT AMAURY de Montfort, son of --- (-after Apr 1052). “Comes Ivo de Bello monte, Ebo miles, Guarinus miles Parisius, Almaricus miles de Monteforte” witnessed the charter dated 1022 under which Robert II King of France confirmed the po
2 CONC ssessions of the abbey of Saint-Mesmin de Micy[121]. “…Almarici de Monteforti…” witnessed the charter dated 1028 under which Robert II King of France confirmed the possessions of the abbey of Saint-Mesmin de Micy[122]. Robert II K
2 CONC ing of France confirmed the donation of "Manasses comes" to Chartres Notre-Dame by charter dated 4 Feb 1031, signed by "…Manasses comitis, Hilduini comitis fratris eius, filorum eius Manassis et Hilduini, Burcardo de Montemorencia
2 CONC co, Evrardi filii Hilduini de Britoglio, Amalrici de Monteforti, Milonis de Caprosa…"[123]. He began the building of the castle of Montfort l'Amaury, which was finished by his son[124]. "Amalricus miles" founded the priory of Sain
2 CONC t-Thomas d´Epernon, with the consent of "conjugis mee…Bertredis…et filiorum meorum…Simonis…atque Mainerii", by charter dated [11 Apr 1052/Jul 1053][125].
2 CONT
2 CONT m BERTRADE, daughter of --- (-after Apr 1052). "Amalricus miles" founded the priory of Saint-Thomas d´Epernon, with the consent of "conjugis mee…Bertredis…et filiorum meorum…Simonis…atque Mainerii", by charter dated [11 Apr 1052/J
2 CONC ul 1053][126].
2 CONT
2 CONT Amaury & his wife had [three] children:
2 CONT
2 CONT 1. SIMON de Montfort (-25 Sep [1087], bur Epernon). "Amalricus miles" founded the priory of Saint-Thomas d´Epernon, with the consent of "conjugis mee…Bertredis…et filiorum meorum…Simonis…atque Mainerii", by charter dated [11 Apr 1
2 CONC 052/Jul 1053][127]. Sire de Montfort-l'Amaury.
2 CONT
2 CONT 2. MAINIER de Montfort (-before 1091). "Amalricus miles" founded the priory of Saint-Thomas d´Epernon, with the consent of "conjugis mee…Bertredis…et filiorum meorum…Simonis…atque Mainerii", by charter dated [11 Apr 1052/Jul 1053]
2 CONC [128]. "Mainerium, fratrem Symonis de Monte Forti" donated property, with the consent of "Simone fratre eius comiteque Belli Montis Ivonis", by charter dated to before 1091, which also names "domnus Simon, filio suo Amalrico"[129]
2 CONC . He granted a free passage at Saint-Piat to the monks of Saint-Père, II, in which his wife and two sons are named[130]. Seigneur d'Epernon. m ELISABETH, daughter of ---. She is named in her husband's charter to the monks of Saint
2 CONC -Père[131]. Mainier & his wife had two children:
2 CONT
2 CONT a) AMAURY de Montfort . He is named in his father's charter to the monks of Saint-Père[132]. 1133. Seigneur d'Epernon. m ---. The name of Amaury's wife is not known. Amaury & his wife had two children:
2 CONT
2 CONT i) SIMON . The primary source which confirms his parentage has not yet been identified.
2 CONT
2 CONT ii) MAINIER . The primary source which confirms his parentage has not yet been identified.
2 CONT
2 CONT b) GUILLAUME de Montfort . He is named in his father's charter to the monks of Saint-Père[133].
2 CONT
2 CONT 3. [EVA (-23 Jan 1099, bur Bec abbey). Her possible affiliation is explained in the Complete Peerage[134]. m GUILLAUME Crispin, son of GILBERT [I] Crispin & his wife Gunnora --- (-Bec 8 Jan 1074).]
2 CONT
2 CONT ------------------------
2 CONT
2 CONT --------------------
2 CONT
2 CONT http://fmg.ac/Projects/MedLands/NORMAN%20NOBILITY.htm#_Toc172613568
2 CONT
2 CONT Information about Montfort-l'Amaury Castle in France:
2 CONT
2 CONT http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Montfort-l%27Amaury
2 CONT
2 CONT --------------------
2 CONT
2 CONT Amauri was also called Amalric.
2 CONT
2 CONT Amauri I, 1st seigneur de Montfort, attested a charter of Robert I of France as "Sie. Almaricus miles de Montforti" in 1022.
2 CONT
2 CONT He married Bertrade (?) before 1025.
2 CONT
2 CONT He attested a charter of Robert I of France as "S. Almarici de Monteforti" in 1028. He attested a charter for Notre-Dame de Chartres of Robert I of France as "Signum Amalrici de Monteforti" on 4 February 1031.
2 CONT
2 CONT Amauri began the building of Montfort, the castle which took its name for him, Montfort-l'Amaury, described as a "castrum" at Yvelines, Île-de-France.
2 CONT
2 CONT Amauri died circa 1053. The precise date of his death is unknown. Since his wife and children appear in a charter in this year, consenting to gifts he had made, it may well be he was already dead.
2 CONT
2 CONT See "My Lines"
2 CONT
2 CONT ( http://homepages.rootsweb.ancestry.com/~cousin/html/p343.htm#i5260 )
