2 CONT "Gundred,'s tombstone  at St. John's Church, Southover, Lewes reads: "Within this Pew stands the tombstone of Gundrad, daughter of William the Conqueror, and wife of  William, the First Earl of Warren, which having been deposited 
2 CONC over her remains in the Chapter-House of Lewes Priory and lately discovered in Iffield Church, was removed to this place at the expense of William Burrell Esq. in 1775 A.D.   Gundred died in childbirth at Castle Acre May 27, 1085,
2 CONC  and was buried in the Priory of Lewes in County Sussex."
