2 CONT     Note: From: Hyacinth@frost.snowhill.com (Jae Fleming)
2 CONT     Newsgroups: soc.genealogy.medieval
2 CONT     Subject: Companions of William the C reposted
2 CONT     Date: 20 Feb 1999 02:20:41 -0800
2 CONT
2 CONT     At 08:53 AM 2/19/99 -0500, Bill Martin wrote:
2 CONT     >Dear Todd A. Farmerie,
2 CONT     >
2 CONT     >I have a couple of questions for you, prompted by your recentposts...
2 CONT     >Who are the two dozen people known by name who fought with William the
2 CONT     >Conqueror at Hastings? Please list source(s) too.
2 CONT
2 CONT     Bill,
2 CONT     I saved this portion of an earlier post to the list, which Ibelieve from
2 CONT     from Mr. Farmerie:
2 CONT
2 CONT     The list was published in CP. It has also been posted here(several
2 CONT     times, I suspect), including the following from Mr. Reitwiesner:
2 CONT
2 CONT     >> The Falaise Roll is not an accurate list. The list ofpersons actually
2 CONT     >> known to have been at the Battle of Hastings on the side ofWilliam the
2 CONT     >> Conqueror is printed in the second edition of Cokayne's*Complete Peerage*,
2 CONT     >> vol XII, Part I, Appendix pp. 47-48, as part of Appendix L.Numbers 1-12
2 CONT     >> are recorded by William of Poitiers, number 13 is portrayedin a battle
2 CONT     >> scene in the Bayeux Tapestry, and 14 and 15 are named byOrderic. 16-19
2 CONT     >> were in William's army and almost certainly at the battle (16named by
2 CONT     >> William of Poitiers, 17-19 portrayed in the Bayeux Tapestry),but there is
2 CONT     >> no direct statement that they actually were at the Battle ofHastings.
2 CONT     >> Number 20 is stated by Orderic to have taken part in fightsin the English
2 CONT     >> war before William became King.
2 CONT     >>
2 CONT     >> 1. Robert de Beaumont, afterwards Count of Meulan and Earlof Leicester
2 CONT     >> 2. Eustace, Count of Boulogne
2 CONT     >> 3. William, afterwards 3rd Count of Evreux
2 CONT     >> 4. Geoffrey of Mortagne, afterwards Count of Perche
2 CONT     >> 5. William FitzOsbern, afterwards Earl of Hereford
2 CONT     >> 6. Aimery, vicomte of Thouars
2 CONT     >> 7. Hugh de Montfort, seigneur of Montfort-sur-Risle
2 CONT     >> 8. Walter Giffard, seigneur of Longueville
2 CONT     >> 9. Ralph de Toeni, seigneur of Conches
2 CONT     >> 10. Hugh de Grandmesnil, seigneur of Grandmesnil
2 CONT     >> 11. William de Warenne, afterwards Earl of Surrey
2 CONT     >> 12. William Malet, seigneur of Graville
2 CONT     >> 13. Eudes, Bishop of Bayeux, afterwards Earl of Kent
2 CONT     >> 14. Turstin FitzRou
2 CONT     >> 15. Engenulf de Laigle, seigneur of Laigle
2 CONT     >> 16. Geoffrey de Mowbray, Bishop of Coutances
2 CONT     >> 17. Robert, Count of Mortain, afterwards Earl of Cornwall
2 CONT     >> 18. Wadard
2 CONT     >> 19. Vital
2 CONT     >> 20. Goubert d'Auffay, seigneur of Auffay
2 CONT     >>
2 CONT     >> For further information, see the source I cited above, andthe sources
2 CONT     >> cited there.
2 CONT
