2 CONT =<nowiki>--------------------</nowiki>=
2 CONT (1) It is likely that almost everyone who has any recent British blood in them is descended from one or more of the people mentioned below so this family features in many genie databases. However, it appears that the only proven k
2 CONC nowledge that there is on the family is based on references to Gunnor, wife/mistress of Richard, Duke of Normandy. It is known that she had a brother called Herfastus but, although many sources also name her father as Herfastus (o
2 CONC r similar), her parentage is not known for sure. It is understood that the family was originally of Danish origin although whether it was Gunnor's father who moved from Denmark into Normandy or an earlier generation is not known. 
2 CONC Suggestions that Gunnor's father was a son of Harald 'Bluetooth', King of Denmark & Norway, appear to be wholly speculative. (2) The following was originally based on reports in various web sites which are inconsistent with each o
2 CONC ther, not least in respect of their dates. The position is further complicated by the fact that the different daughters are often confused with each other, different sources allocating their husbands differently between them. The 
2 CONC following now broadly but not fully follows the view taken by Todd Farmerie (reported on www.rootsweb.com/~medieval/, kindly brought to our attention by a site visitor (PK, 09.02.07)) which makes no mention at all of "Crepon" (but
2 CONC  does of Cotelin, Normandy) and which names only Senfria, Duvelina and Wevia as definitely Gunnor's sisters. This section remains subject to further review.
2 CONT =<nowiki>--------------------</nowiki>=
2 CONT Generation One 
2 CONT
2 CONT 1. TORF1 was born circa 920, and died between 950 and 1030. He married circa 950, ERTEMBERGE DE BRIQUEBEC. [67, 28, 103] 
2 CONT
2 CONT Seigneur de Torville 
2 CONT
2 CONT possibly a son of Bernard the Dane, the most powerful of the feudal nobles of 
2 CONT
2 CONT Normandy but this relationship has not been proved. 
2 CONT
2 CONT Children: + 2 i. TOURADE2 DE PONTAUDEMER, b. circa 950; m. EVA DE CREPON circa 980. 
2 CONT
2 CONT 3 ii. TURCHETIL. 
2 CONT
2 CONT Seigneur de Turqueville, ancestor of the famous harcourt family of Normandy and 
2 CONT
2 CONT England. 
2 CONT
2 CONT 4 iii. WILLIAM DE TORVILLE. 
2 CONT
2 CONT --------------------------------------------------------------------------------
2 CONT
2 CONT Generation Two 
2 CONT
2 CONT 2. TOURADE2 DE PONTAUDEMER (Torf1), son of (1) Torf1 and Ertemberge (de BRIQUEBEC) _____, was born circa 950 and died between 980 and 1060. He married circa 980, EVA DE CREPON. [67, 32, 103] 
2 CONT
2 CONT younger sister of the Dutchess Gunnora, wife of Richard I, Duke of normandy 
2 CONT
2 CONT (Cf), 
2 CONT
2 CONT Children: + 5 i. HUMPHREY3 DE VEULLES, b. circa 980; m. AUBEREE DE LA HAYE circa 1005. 
2 CONT
2 CONT 6 ii. HERBRARD DU PONTEAUDEMER. 
2 CONT
2 CONT 7 iii. GILBERD DU PONTEAUDEMER. 
2 CONT
2 CONT 8 iv. RICHARD DU PONTEAUDEMER. 
2 CONT
2 CONT 9 v. ILBERT DU PONTEAUDEMER. 
2 CONT
2 CONT 10 vi. JOSSELINE. 
2 CONT
2 CONT + 11 vii. JOSCELINE; m. (AAL-3) HUGUES DE MONTGOMERY in 994. 
2 CONT
