2 CONT --------------------
2 CONT Touroude was born about 950 in Normandy, France. By inheritance from his father was Seigneur du Ponteautorf, de Torville, Torcy, Torny, and Torly he became Sire du Ponteaudemer, which became his principal residence and by which na
2 CONC me he was commonly known. By his marriage he enhanced his position among the Norman nobility, and he was a prominent figure during the reigns of Dukes Richard II., Richard III., and Robert "the Devil" (996-1035). He married about 
2 CONC 980, WEVIA (Duceline) DE CRÃŠPON, born 942 of Pont-Audemer, Eure, France, who was a younger sister of the Duchess Gunnora, wife of Richard I., Duke of Normandy. 
2 CONT
2 CONT Children: Herbrard, Gilberd, Richard, Ilbert, Josseline, Humphrey de Vuelles
