2 CONT
2 CONT •41. Torf "The Rich" Baron DE TOURVILLE Prince of Denmark       Torf, which is a Danish name is probably a variant of Thorolf which means
2 CONT        Thor's Wolf, Thor being the God of Thunder.
2 CONT
2 CONT        Places in Normandy named for him. Torfville,Tourville,Tourneville,Turville
2 CONT        Turvile and Turquoville.
2 CONT
2 CONT        There were apparently two Torfs of the same name confused in genealogy
2 CONT        namely father and son.
2 CONT     b. ABT 930, Normandy, France
2 CONT     b. 937, Normandy, France
2 CONT     d. AFT 955
2 CONT     d. 1013, Normandy, France
2 CONT     m. Ertemberge de Bricanbert BARTRAM ABT 955, Normandy, France
2 CONT        b. 930, Normandy, France
2 CONT        d. 1001, Normandy, France
2 CONT        daughter of Anslac (or Aslac) de BASTEMBOURG
2 CONT     ch:   *Turchetil de HARCOURT [Next Generation],
2 CONT           *Touroude de PONT-AUDEMER (-1040) m(1) Awelina of Sweden (974-) [See 587-40 below],
2 CONT           Guillaume (WILLIAM) II
2 CONT
2 CONT http://homepages.rootsweb.ancestry.com/~pmcbride/rfc/l315.htm
