2 CONT Comte Gauthier [II] & his wife had four children: 
2 CONT
2 CONT 1. RAOUL de Mantes (-1060).  Comte de Valois et d'Amiens. 
2 CONT
2 CONT 2. DREUX [Drogo] de Mantes (-[13 Aug] [1035]). He accompanied Robert II Duke of Normandy to Jerusalem and died on the journey[24].
2 CONT
2 CONT m ([1025 or before]) as her first husband, GODGIFU [Goda] of England, daughter of ÆTHELRED II "the Unready" King of England & his second wife Emma de Normandie (-before 1049). 
2 CONT
2 CONT Godgifu married secondly ([1036]) as his first wife, Eustache [II] Comte de Boulogne [31].  
2 CONT
2 CONT Comte Drogo & his wife had three children.
2 CONT
2 CONT 3. FOULQUES de Mantes.
2 CONT
2 CONT 4. daughter .  
2 CONT
2 CONT The Chronicle of Alberic de Trois-Fontaines refers to the mother of "Waleranni comitis [Mellentini]" as daughter of "Gauterus Albus de Albamarla"[46].  Yves de Chartres names "Gualterius Albus" as father of "matrem Gualeranni comi
2 CONC tis"[47].  
2 CONT
2 CONT m HUGUES Comte de Meulan, son of GALERAN [II] Comte de Meulan & his wife --- (-after 25 Aug 1005). 
2 CONT
2 CONT ----------------------
2 CONT
2 CONT Ben M. Angel notes:
2 CONT
2 CONT On the question of Oda vs. Alix, French Wikipedia supports Oda de Vexin. Alix de Vexin appears to be supported only by numerous GEDCOM files that do not appear to have a reliable source (I welcome a correction on this, if a reliab
2 CONC le source, other than "someone else's GEDCOM or online family tree" does exist - "The Plantagenet Ancestry" by W.H. Turton provides no primary sources, see below). My best guess as to why Alix has appeared and proliferated on unso
2 CONC urced GEDCOM files is confusion with Alix/Alys de Vexin, who was born to King Robert VII of France a century and a half later:
2 CONT
2 CONT http://familypedia.wikia.com/wiki/Alix_de_Vexin_(c1170-c1220)
2 CONT
2 CONT http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Alys,_Countess_of_the_Vexin
2 CONT
2 CONT The Medlands project, meanwhile, supports neither name, regarding her to be (Unknown) de Valois. Until more definitive sources can be provided for an alternative name, that's how I'd recommend that Hugues' wife be named.
2 CONT
2 CONT ------------
2 CONT
2 CONT The Plantagenet Ancestry is cited as listing Alix de Vexin as husband of Hugues I (the online sample does not carry the page showing this, unfortunately). Although a fascinating collection of charts of 7,000 names showing what app
2 CONC ears to be researched relationships of the ancestry of the Plantagenets, the source material backing Alix de Vexin is not included within the online sample:
2 CONT
2 CONT http://books.google.cl/books?id=jcxwxO1723cC&pg=PT168&lpg=PT168&dq=%22The+Plantagenet+Ancestry%22+Turton&source=bl&ots=-HfaAYkDlb&sig=J9vmD2TXBOkEIyjEwLKQqmKb7jk#v=onepage&q&f=false
2 CONT --------------------
2 CONT From the Foundation for Medieval Genealogy page on Northern France Nobility:
2 CONT
2 CONT http://fmg.ac/Projects/MedLands/NORTHERN%20FRANCE.htm#GautierIIValoisB
2 CONT
2 CONT GAUTHIER [II] "le Blanc", son of GAUTHIER [I] Comte d'Amiens & his [first/second] wife [Eva---/Adela ---] (-after 1017).
2 CONT
2 CONT "Wauterii comitis, Walterii et Radulfi filiorum eius" subscribed a charter dated 975 under which "Hugo Francorum dux" restored the abbey of Saint-Jean to the abbey of Sainte-Croix d'Orléans[17]. A charter of "Hugo…Francorum rex" c
2 CONC onfirming the privileges of the monastery of Corvey dated 987 is subscribed by "Walteri comitis Ambianensis ac filiorum eius Walteri, Gotfredi, Rodulfi"[18]. Comte de Mantes. "Walterius comes" donated property "prope nostrum caste
2 CONC llum…Medanta" to "Carnotensi monasterio Sancti Petri", for the soul of "coniugis mee Adelidis filiorumque meorum", by charter to [1006], signed by "Walterii comitis, Rodulfi filii eius, Drogonis filii eius…"[19].
2 CONT
2 CONT Comte d'Amiens et du Vexin.
2 CONT
2 CONT m ADELA, daughter of ---.
2 CONT
2 CONT "Walterius comes" donated property "prope nostrum castellum…Medanta" to "Carnotensi monasterio Sancti Petri", for the soul of "coniugis mee Adelidis filiorumque meorum", by charter to [1006], signed by "Walterii comitis, Rodulfi f
2 CONC ilii eius, Drogonis filii eius…"[20].
2 CONT
2 CONT Comte Gauthier [II] & his wife had four children:
2 CONT
2 CONT 1. RAOUL de Mantes (-1060). Comte de Valois et d'Amiens.
2 CONT
2 CONT 2. DREUX [Drogo] de Mantes (-[13 Aug] [1035]). He accompanied Robert II Duke of Normandy to Jerusalem and died on the journey[24].
2 CONT
2 CONT m ([1025 or before]) as her first husband, GODGIFU [Goda] of England, daughter of ÆTHELRED II "the Unready" King of England & his second wife Emma de Normandie (-before 1049).
2 CONT
2 CONT Godgifu married secondly ([1036]) as his first wife, Eustache [II] Comte de Boulogne [31].
2 CONT
2 CONT Comte Drogo & his wife had three children.
2 CONT
2 CONT 3. FOULQUES de Mantes.
2 CONT
2 CONT 4. daughter .
2 CONT
2 CONT The Chronicle of Alberic de Trois-Fontaines refers to the mother of "Waleranni comitis [Mellentini]" as daughter of "Gauterus Albus de Albamarla"[46]. Yves de Chartres names "Gualterius Albus" as father of "matrem Gualeranni comit
2 CONC is"[47].
2 CONT
2 CONT m HUGUES Comte de Meulan, son of GALERAN [II] Comte de Meulan & his wife --- (-after 25 Aug 1005).
2 CONT
2 CONT ----------------------
