1 NOTE {geni:about_me} From the Foundation for Medieval Genealogy page on Normandy Nobility:
2 CONT
2 CONT http://fmg.ac/Projects/MedLands/NORMAN%20NOBILITY.htm#HuguesMeulanMdauGauthierValois
2 CONT
2 CONT GALERAN [II] de Meulan (-10 Apr <nowiki>----</nowiki>).  Comte de Meulan.  
2 CONT
2 CONT m ---.  The name of Galéran's wife is not known.  
2 CONT
2 CONT Galéran [II] & his wife had three children: 
2 CONT
2 CONT i)  HUGUES [I] de Meulan (-after 25 Aug 1005).  "…Hugo filius Waleranni comitis" are named as present in the charter dated 1035 under which "Willelmus adhuc puerulus…Roberti comitis filius" donated "Turstini villa" to the abbey of
2 CONC  Préaux[1891].  Comte de Meulan 998.  
2 CONT
2 CONT m --- de Valois, daughter of GAUTHIER [II] "le Blanc" Comte d'Amiens, de Mantes, de Valois et du Vexin & his wife Adela ---.  
2 CONT
2 CONT The Chronicle of Alberic de Trois-Fontaines refers to the mother of "Waleranni comitis [Mellentini]" as daughter of "Gauterus Albus de Albamarla"[1892].  Yves de Chartres names "Gualterius Albus" as father of "matrem Gualeranni co
2 CONC mitis"[1893].  
2 CONT
2 CONT Hugues & his wife had three children: 
2 CONT
2 CONT (a)  GALERAN [III] de Meulan (-8 Dec 1069).  The Chronicle of Alberic de Trois-Fontaines names "Waleranni comitis [Mellentini]" as son of "filia Gauterus Albus de Albamarla"[1894].  Comte de Meulan. 
2 CONT
2 CONT References:
2 CONT
2 CONT [1891] Delisle (1867), Pièces justificatives, 12, p. 12, citing Gallia Christiana XI, instr. col. 200. 
2 CONT
2 CONT [1892] Chronica Albrici Monachi Trium Fontium 1062, MGH SS XXIII, p. 793. 
2 CONT
2 CONT [1893] Yves de Chartres, Epistola 45, Patrologia Latina, Tome 162, col. 57. 
2 CONT
2 CONT [1894] Chronica Albrici Monachi Trium Fontium 1062, MGH SS XXIII, p. 793. 
2 CONT
2 CONT --------------------
2 CONT
2 CONT From the French Wikipedia page on Hugues I de Meulan:
2 CONT
2 CONT http://fr.wikipedia.org/wiki/Hugues_Ier_de_Meulan
2 CONT
2 CONT Hugues Ier fut vicomte de Meulan à la fin du XIe siècle. Né aux alentours de 965, il succéda à son père Galéran II. Il est cité comme vicomte de Meulan en 998 et pourrait l'avoir été dès 991, selon les Europaïsche Stammtafelm.
2 CONT
2 CONT Il épousa Oda de Vexin, fille de Gautier II, comte de Vexin, d'Amiens et de Valois et d'Adèle, et eut :
2 CONT
2 CONT 1`. Galéran III († 1068), vicomte puis comte de Meulan
2 CONT
2 CONT 2. Hugues II, vicomte de Vexin
2 CONT
2 CONT 3. Hellouin, vicomte du Mantois, père d'un Richard de Meulan, cité en 1066.
2 CONT
2 CONT Il mourut peu après le 25 août 1005.
2 CONT
2 CONT Sources 
2 CONT
2 CONT (de) Detlev Schwennicke, Europäische Stammtafeln, vol. III.4, 1983, p. 700 
2 CONT
2 CONT (fr) Comtes de Meulan
2 CONT
2 CONT In English:
2 CONT
2 CONT Hugh I was the Viscount of Meulan at the end of the 10th century. Born around 965, he succeeded his father Galeran II. He is cited as the Viscount of Meulan in 998 and may have been so from 991, according to the Europaische Stammt
2 CONC afalm.
2 CONT
2 CONT He married Oda de Vexin, daughter of Gautier II, Comte de Vexin, Amiens, and Valois, and his wife Adele. they had:
2 CONT
2 CONT 1. Galeran II (d. 1068), Viscount and Count of Meulan
2 CONT
2 CONT 2. Hugh II, Viscount of Vexin
2 CONT
2 CONT 3. Hellouin, Viscount Mantois, father of Richard Meulan, cited 1066.
2 CONT
2 CONT Hugh died shortly after August 25, 1005.
2 CONT
2 CONT ----------------------
2 CONT
2 CONT Ben M. Angel notes:
2 CONT
2 CONT On the question of Oda vs. Alix, French Wikipedia supports Oda de Vexin. Alix de Vexin appears to be supported only by numerous GEDCOM files that do not appear to have a reliable source (I welcome a correction on this, if a reliab
2 CONC le source, other than "someone else's GEDCOM or online family tree" does exist - "The Plantagenet Ancestry" by W.H. Turton provides no primary sources, see below). My best guess as to why Alix has appeared and proliferated on unso
2 CONC urced GEDCOM files is confusion with Alix/Alys de Vexin, who was born to King Robert VII of France a century and a half later:
2 CONT
2 CONT http://familypedia.wikia.com/wiki/Alix_de_Vexin_(c1170-c1220)
2 CONT
2 CONT http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Alys,_Countess_of_the_Vexin
2 CONT
2 CONT The Medlands project, meanwhile, supports neither name, regarding her to be (Unknown) de Valois. Until more definitive sources can be provided for an alternative name, that's how I'd recommend that Hugues' wife be named.
2 CONT
