2 CONT (wikipedia)
2 CONT
2 CONT Robert II (27 March 972 – 20 July 1031), called the Pious or the Wise, was King of France from 996 until his death. The second reigning member of the House of Capet.
2 CONT
2 CONT Parents:Hugh Capet and Adelaide of Aquitaine.
2 CONT
2 CONT Birth place: Orléans, France. 
2 CONT
2 CONT Death:20 July 1031 (aged 59), Melun, France
2 CONT
2 CONT Buriel: Saint Denis Basilica, Paris, France
2 CONT
2 CONT Co-reign
2 CONT
2 CONT Solo-reign 	30[citation needed]. December 987 – 24 October 996;
2 CONT
2 CONT 24 October 996 – 20 July 1031
2 CONT
2 CONT Coronation 	30[citation needed] December 987
2 CONT
2 CONT Predecessor 	Hugh
2 CONT
2 CONT Successor 	Henry I
2 CONT
2 CONT Spouse 	Rozala of Italy
2 CONT
2 CONT Bertha of Burgundy
2 CONT
2 CONT Constance of Arles
2 CONT
2 CONT Issue
2 CONT
2 CONT Hugh Magnus, Rex Filius
2 CONT
2 CONT Henry I
2 CONT
2 CONT Adela, Countess of Flanders
2 CONT
2 CONT Robert I, Duke of Burgundy
2 CONT
2 CONT Father 	Hugh Capet
2 CONT
2 CONT Mother 	Adelaide of Aquitaine
2 CONT
2 CONT Robert had no children from his short-lived marriage to Susanna. His illegal marriage to Bertha gave him one stillborn son in 999, but only Constance gave him surviving children:[7]
2 CONT
2 CONT     * Constance, married Manasses de Dammartin
2 CONT
2 CONT     * Hedwig (or Advisa) of France, married Renauld I, Count of Nevers on 25 January 1016 and had issue.
2 CONT
2 CONT     * Hugh Magnus, co-king (1017–1025)
2 CONT
2 CONT     * Henry I, successor
2 CONT
2 CONT     * Robert, became Duke of Burgundy
2 CONT
2 CONT     * Odo (1013–c.1056), who may have been mentally retarded and died after his brother's failed invasion of Normandy
2 CONT
2 CONT     * Adela (d. 1079), married firstly Richard III of Normandy and secondly Baldwin V of Flanders.
2 CONT
2 CONT Robert also left an illegitimate son: Rudolph, Bishop of Bourges.
2 CONT
2 CONT --------------------
2 CONT
2 CONT Robert II (27 March 972 – 20 July 1031), called the Pious or the Wise, was King of France from 996 until his death. The second reigning member of the House of Capet, he was born in Orléans to Hugh Capet and Adelaide of Aquitaine.
2 CONT
2 CONT Robert had no children from his short-lived marriage to Susanna. His illegal marriage to Bertha gave him one stillborn son in 999, but only Constance gave him surviving children:[7]
2 CONT
2 CONT     * Constance, married Manasses de Dammartin
2 CONT
2 CONT     * Hedwig (or Advisa) of France, married Renauld I, Count of Nevers on 25 January 1016 and had issue.
2 CONT
2 CONT     * Hugh Magnus, co-king (1017–1025)
2 CONT
2 CONT     * Henry I, successor
2 CONT
