2 CONT Guy I was the second lord of Bray and the second lord of Montlhéry. He was probably the son of Thibaud of Montmorency, but some sources say that his father was named Milo. Thibaud may instead have been his grandfather.
2 CONT He married Hodierna of Gometz, daughter of William, lord of Gometz.
2 CONT Together with his wife and with the support of the Bishop of Paris Guido 1061 founded the Benedictine Priory of Notre-Dame of Longpont-sur-Orge, which they handed over to twenty-two monks from the Abbey of Cluny. Longpont thus bec
2 CONC ame the first branch of the Association of clunizianischen monastery in the region around Paris. According to legend his wife with own hands participated in the construction.
2 CONT Gui and Hodierna had seven children:
2 CONT Milo I the Great, (also called Milon I) lord of Monthléry, married Lithuaise, sister of Stephen of Blois.
2 CONT Melisende of Montlhéry, married Hugh I, count of Rethel, mother of Baldwin II of Jerusalem (died 1118)
2 CONT Elizabeth of Montlhéry, married Joscelin, lord of Courtenay, mother of Joscelin I, Count of Edessa
2 CONT Guy II the Red (died 1108), lord of Rochefort
2 CONT Beatrice of Rochefort, married Anseau of Garlande (1069–1117)
2 CONT Hodierna of Montlhéry, married Walter of Saint-Valéry
2 CONT Alice of Montlhéry (also called Adele & Alix) (1040–1097), married Hugh I, lord of Le Puiset (1035–1094)
2 CONT Guy died in 1095, the same year Pope Urban II launched the First Crusade. Many of his descendants had illustrious careers in the Holy Land, through the Montlhéry, Courtenay, and Le Puiset branches of his family.
2 CONT
