2 CONT
2 CONT Hodierne DE GOMETZ-LA-FERTE
2 CONT 	Born: Abt 1014, Normandie, France 
2 CONT 	Married: 
2 CONT
2 CONT Ancestral File Number: 9FPM-5T. 
2 CONT
2 CONT Marriage Information:
2 CONT Hodierne married Sn Guy I DE MONTLHÉRY chatelain de Rochefort-en-Yvelines, son of Milon DE MONTELEHERICO seigneur de la Ferte and Miss DE MONTLHÉRY. (Sn Guy I DE MONTLHÉRY chatelain de Rochefort-en-Yvelines was born about 1009 in 
2 CONC Montlhéry, S-Oise, France and died in 1095 in Longpont, France.)
2 CONT
2 CONT www.findagrave.com
2 CONT
2 CONT Hodierna de Gometz
2 CONT BIRTH unknown
2 CONT Île-de-France, France
2 CONT DEATH 7 Dec 1074
2 CONT Montlhery, Departement de l'Essonne, Île-de-France, France
2 CONT BURIAL
2 CONT Basilique Notre-Dame-de-Bonne-Garde de Longpont-sur-Orge
2 CONT Longpont-sur-Orge, Departement de l'Essonne, Île-de-France, France 
2 CONT PLOT
2 CONT Before the High Altar
2 CONT MEMORIAL ID 104556523
2 CONT
2 CONT Hodierna of Gometz was the daughter of Guillame de Gometz Lord of Gometz; wife of Gui I of Montlhéry.
2 CONT Together with her husband and with the support of the Bishop of Paris Guido in 1061 they founded the Benedictine Priory of Notre-Dame of Longpont-sur-Orge, which they handed over to twenty-two monks from the Abbey of Cluny. Longpo
2 CONC nt thus became the first branch of the Association of
2 CONT clunizianischen monastery in the region around Paris. Hodierna gave the Abbey a chalice of Gold 30 Oz and a valuable chasuble.
2 CONT According to legend Hodierna with her own hands participated in the construction and that she was going to fetch water at a distant fountain, which still had the reputation to cure the fever. One day Hodierne came asking the black
2 CONC smith to provide her with an iron bar that would help her to better carry buckets. The blacksmith, influenced by his nasty wife, gives her derisively, a red fire bar. Hodierne is spared any burning. The 'red iron cross' is today p
2 CONC reserved at the bottom of the Basilica.
2 CONT The legend also claims that she cursed the blacksmith and he died soon after.
2 CONT The Basilique is beautiful, very large, and contained a large number of tombs. Hodierne was buried before the high altar, under a grave which read: Hodierae inclytcae omitisshae erici montis sacrarum harum Aedium fundatricis ossa 
2 CONC Sub dio jacentia ab anno millesimo, pro nichaelis Lewis Domni of rocks, hujusce domus priori studio hic translata fuere anno 1651 die ultima mensis augusti.
2 CONT
2 CONT Family Members
2 CONT Spouse
2 CONT Gui de Montlhéry
2 CONT unknown–1095
2 CONT
2 CONT Children
2 CONT Elizabeth of Montlhéry de Courtenay
