2 CONT Robert 'le Danois' d'Evreux, Archbishop of Rouen.
2 CONT
2 CONT Parents: Richard I Sans-Peur of Normandy & Gunnora
2 CONT
2 CONT Spouse: Herlève de Rouen
2 CONT
2 CONT Children:
2 CONT
2 CONT 1. Richard, Count of Évreux (d. 1067). m. Godechildis, widow of Roger de Conches de Tosny
2 CONT
2 CONT 2. Raoul d'Évreux married Basilie, daughter of Gerard de Fleitel
2 CONT
2 CONT 3. Guilllaume d'Évreux m. Hawise d'Echaffour
2 CONT
2 CONT 4. Gautier (Walter) de Rosmar, possible father of Edward of Salisbury: [According to the Book of Lacock, “Edwardum, natione Anglicum natum, postea vicecomitem Wiltes” was the son of “Walterus le Ewrus, comes de Rosmar”[1430]. The 
2 CONC Complete Peerage describes this supposed father as “a fictitious person” and states that Edward´s parentage is unknown] (from http://fmg.ac/Projects/MedLands/ENGLISH%20NOBILITY%20MEDIEVAL1.htm, Earls of Salisbury)
2 CONT
2 CONT Robert had one illegitimate child by an unknown mistress:
2 CONT
2 CONT 5. RAOUL de Vacé (aka Ralph de Gace).
2 CONT
2 CONT NOTE:
2 CONT
2 CONT French sources show that Robert the Archbishop is identical to Robert "the Dane" - le Danois.
