2 CONT [https://fasg.org/projects/henryproject/data/amaur000.htm '''The Henry Project: The Ancestors of King Henry II of England'''] 
2 CONT Amaury I de Montfort l'Amaury, Lord of Montfort l'Amaury, fl. 1022-1060.
2 CONT
2 CONT Possible father: Guillaume de Hainaut.
2 CONT Possible mother: NN de Nogent.
2 CONT See the Commentary section for a discussion of the evidence.
2 CONT
2 CONT Possible father: '''Guillaume de Hainaut'''.
2 CONT Stated by Orderic Vitalis to have been the father of Amaury I de Montfort, he is otherwise unknown ["''Rex Henricus, ..., consultu Amalrici senioris de Monte-Forti, filii Guillelmi Hanoensis'', ..." OV vii, 14 (3: 223)]. As noted 
2 CONC below, he has often been conjectured as a son of the tenth century count Amaury.
2 CONT
2 CONT ----
2 CONT
2 CONT http://racineshistoire.free.fr/LGN/PDF/Broyes.pdf
2 CONT
2 CONT Hugues de Blois ''dit «de Beauvais»''
2 CONT before 970 +X 1008 (assassinated on the orders of Count Fulk "Nerra" of Anjou), Count Palatine, Count of Nogent (-l'Erambert, now -Le Roi) then of Dreux (~1006/08), loyal to King Robert II "the Pious," Forester of the Yveline Fore
2 CONC st, Advocate of the church of Orléans, served his relative Odo II of Blois in the county of Dreux (ceded Dreux to the King and recovered his rights over Beauvais) married ? (perhaps from the Epernon lineage, said to be '''Lady of 
2 CONC Nogent''' (-Le-Roi); married 2) '''William of Hainaut,''' Forester of Yveline, castellan of Montfort, Beynes and Epernon, invested by King Robert II)
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT -----
2 CONT
2 CONT BE1883** (Montfort) reports that the first Almaric/Amaury/Aymer of Montfort was an illegitimate son of Robert, King of France. The only Kings Robert of France at or before this period were the Robert I (grandfather of Hugh Capet) 
2 CONC who died in 923 and Robert II 'the Pious' (son of Hugh Capet) who lived 972-1031. The article in BE1883 says that this Almaric, son of King Robert, was great-grandfather of the Simon who married Amicia de Beaumont but gives no dat
2 CONC es for any of the family until that Simon. As BE1883 appears to miss out some generations, we follow 'The Complete Peerage' (TCP). As the dates given in TCP are broadly consistent with other sources, and as the dates found in vari
2 CONC ous web sites (eg 'Mathematical') report that the first Amaury de Montfort was born about 935, we believe that the first Amaury here reported could not have been a son of a King Robert of France. It is possible that he was a grand
2 CONC son of King Robert I but that has not been proved.
2 CONT
2 CONT **BE1883 = Burke's Extinct Peerage "Genealogical History of the Dormant, Abeyant, Forfeited and Extinct Peerages of the British Empire by Burke" (1883 edition).
2 CONT
2 CONT '''Amaury de Montfort''' (b c935, d after 04.02.1031)
2 CONT
2 CONT m. ?? de Cambray (b c940)
2 CONT
2 CONT 1. '''Guillaume de Montfort''' (b c960, dvp 1003)
2 CONT
2 CONT William was also called '''Guillaume de Hainaut.'''
2 CONT
2 CONT He was invested with the lordship of Montfort by Hugh Capet before 996. He was Seigneur de Monfort at France in 996. 
2 CONT
2 CONT =<nowiki>--------------------</nowiki>=
2 CONT
2 CONT On ne sait que peu de choses sur Guillaume de Hainaut, le premier seigneur de Montfort-l'Amaury. Les seules certitudes familiales sont qu'il était petit-fils du comte Régnier II et cousin de Régnier IV. Après les continuelles rébe
2 CONC llions de Régnier III et son châtiment et son exil par Brunon de Cologne, les membres de la famille de Hainaut se réfugièrent à la cour de France.
2 CONT
2 CONT Robert II le pieux, roi de France le chargea de bâtir deux forteresses en forêt d'Yvelines, afin de défendre le domaine royal contre le comte de Blois. L'une sera bâtie à Épernon, l'autre plus au nord, sur une butte naturelle dont
2 CONC  il fera défricher les alentours, afin de permettre l'installation de paysans. Cette seconde forteresse prendra le nom de Montfort. Plusieurs de ses successeurs ayant le prénom d'Amaury, la nouvelle cité prendra par la suite le no
2 CONC m de Montfort-l'Amaury.
2 CONT
2 CONT Il devint le châtelain de Montfort et, ayant épousé une fille d'Hugues de Beauvais, administrateur du pays d'Yvelines, lui succèdera lorsque ce dernier sera assassiné. Il réussit à rendre héréditaire la nouvelle seigneurie, et la 
2 CONC transmettra à son fils Amaury Ier
2 CONT
2 CONT http://fr.wikipedia.org/wiki/Guillaume_de_Montfort
