2 CONT '''[GUILLAUME [de Hainaut],''' son of --- . Orderic Vitalis names "Guillelmi Hanoensis" as father of "Amalrici senioris de Monte-Forti", when recording a visit by Henri I King of France to Fécamp on the advice of Amaury, dated to 
2 CONC [1032][669].  The accuracy of the information is uncertain, although presumably it cannot be dismissed entirely.  Dion suggests that he was a cousin of Reginar [IV] Comte de Hainaut[670].  No other trace of such a person has yet b
2 CONC een found.]  
2 CONT
2 CONT m --- dame de Nogent, daughter of ---.  Her marriage is confirmed by an apparently incomplete fragmentary passage of the mid-12th century continuation of the Historia of Monk Aimon which records that, during the reign of Robert II
2 CONC  King of France, [name omitted] fortified "Sparnonem et Montifortem" and married "de Novigento dominam"[671].  One child: 
2 CONT
