2 CONT
2 CONT From the Foundation for Medieval Genealogy Medlands Project page on Champagne Nobility (covering her married family):
2 CONT
2 CONT http://fmg.ac/Projects/MedLands/CHAMPAGNE%20NOBILITY.htm#HilduinIVMontdidierdied1063
2 CONT
2 CONT HILDUIN [IV] de Ramerupt, son of HILDUIN [III] Seigneur de Ramerupt & his wife --- (-[1063]).  
2 CONT *Robert II King of France confirmed the donation of "Manasses comes" to Chartres Notre-Dame by charter dated 4 Feb 1031, signed by "…Manasses comitis, Hilduini comitis fratris eius, filiorum eius Manassis et Hilduini, Burcardo de 
2 CONC Montemorenciaco, Evrardi filii Hilduini de Britoglio, Amalrici de Monteforti, Milonis de Caprosa…"[1236].  "…Hilduinus comes et Hilduinus filius eius…" subscribed the charter dated 1032 under which "Odo comes palatinus Francorum r
2 CONC egis" founded Epernay abbey[1237].  
2 CONT *Comte [de Montdidier].  
2 CONT *Seigneur de Ramerupt.  
2 CONT *"Vir nobilis Hugo Bardul" donated property to Montiérender by charter dated [1061/62 or before], subscribed by "Teobaldi comitis, Hilduini comitis, Burdini de Belfort, Manasse filii eius"[1238].  Hermann´s Miracles of Laon Sainte
2 CONC -Marie records that Philippe I King of France sent "comitem Hilduinum cum domno Helinando Laudunensi Episcopo" as ambassadors to Rome, undated[1239]. 
2 CONT
2 CONT m ADELAIDE de Roucy, daughter of EBLES Comte de Roucy & his wife Beatrix de Hainaut ([1015/20]-1062).  
2 CONT *The Chronicle of Alberic de Trois-Fontaines names "Aelidam et Hadewidem" as the two daughters of "Ebalus de Roceio " & his wife, specifying that "omnes comites de Roceio et de Arceis sive de Ramerupt vel de Brena super Albam" des
2 CONC cended from Adelaide[1240].  The Genealogiæ Scriptoris Fusniacensis names "Adelidem et Hadevidem" as the two daughters of "Ebalus de Roceio " and his wife Beatrix, specifying that "secunda filia…soror…Hadevidis nupsit Helduino com
2 CONC iti de Ramerut[1241].  
2 CONT *Her birth date is estimated from her mother's estimated birth date and the fact that Adelaide herself gave birth to her youngest child in [1060]. 
2 CONT
2 CONT Hilduin [III] & his wife had nine children: 
2 CONT
2 CONT 1.         EBLES  [II] de Ramerupt (-May 1103).  
2 CONT *The Chronicle of Alberic de Trois-Fontaines names "Ebalus…de Roceio et Andreas de Ramerut et Arceis comites" as the two sons of "Hilduinus de Ramerut" & his wife Adelaide[1242].  
2 CONT *Comte de Roucy. 
2 CONT
2 CONT 2.         ANDRE de Ramerupt (-after 1118).  
2 CONT *The Chronicle of Alberic de Trois-Fontaines names "Ebalus…de Roceio et Andreas de Ramerut et Arceis comites" as the two sons of "Hilduinus de Ramerut" & his wife Adelaide[1243].  The Genealogiæ Scriptoris Fusniacensis names "Ebal
2 CONC um comitem…et Andream comitem de Ramerut et filias" as children of "comes Helduinus [et] Adelaide"[1244].  
2 CONT *Seigneur de Ramerupt et d'Arcis-sur-Aube.  
2 CONT *"Duo fratres Ebolus et Andreas et uxores nostre Sibilla et Adelisa et cognatus noster Hugo comes de Domno Martino uxorque eius Rothaidis" donated property to the church of Ramerupt Sainte-Marie by charter dated 1082, which also r
2 CONC ecords that "post hæc comes Andreas" donated "molendinorum suorum de Grandi Prato" with the consent of "uxore sua Guindesmode et filiis duobus Hugone…et Oliverio"[1245].  
2 CONT *m firstly ADELISA, daughter of --- (-after 1082).  "Duo fratres Ebolus et Andreas et uxores nostre Sibilla et Adelisa et cognatus noster Hugo comes de Domno Martino uxorque eius Rothaidis" donated property to the church of Rameru
2 CONC pt Sainte-Marie by charter dated 1082[1246].  
2 CONT *m secondly as her second husband, GUISEMODE, widow of HUGUES Seigneur de Pleurs, sister of BAUDOUIN Monk at Molesme, daughter of ---.  "Duo fratres Ebolus et Andreas et uxores nostre Sibilla et Adelisa et cognatus noster Hugo com
2 CONC es de Domno Martino uxorque eius Rothaidis" donated property to the church of Ramerupt Sainte-Marie by charter dated 1082, which also records that "post hæc comes Andreas" donated "molendinorum suorum de Grandi Prato" with the con
2 CONC sent of "uxore sua Guindesmode et filiis duobus Hugone…et Oliverio"[1247].  The primary source which confirms her origin and first marriage has not yet been identified.  André & his first wife had five children: Ebles de Ramerupt 
2 CONC (d. 21 June 1126); Hugues "Brito" de Ramerupt (d. 1108 or later); Olivier de Ramerupt; Alix de Ramerupt (d. 1143 or later, m. Erard I,Comte de Brienne); and a second daughter (m. Jean, Vicomte de Mareuil).
2 CONT
2 CONT 3.         BEATRIX de Ramerupt (-2 Sep after 1129).  
2 CONT *The Chronicle of Alberic de Trois-Fontaines names "Beatrix" as second daughter of Ebles Comte de Roucy and incorrectly names her husband "Rotroldo comiti de Pertico"[1259].  The Genealogiæ Scriptoris Fusniacensis names "comitis H
2 CONC ilduini de Rameruth maior natu filia dicta Beatrix" as wife, also incorrectly, of "Rotaldo comiti de Pertica"[1260].  She is named as wife of Geoffroy Comte du Perche by Orderic Vitalis, incorrectly saying that she was daughter of
2 CONC  "the count of Rochefort"[1261] and specifying in another passage that her son Rotrou was consanguineus of Alfonso I King of Aragon[1262].  
2 CONT *m GEOFFROY de Châteaudun, son of ROTROU Vicomte de Châteaudun, Comte de Mortagne & his wife Adelise de Bellême (-mid-Oct 1100, bur Nogent-le-Rotrou[1263]).  He succeeded his father in [1080] as Comte de Mortagne.  He adopted the 
2 CONC title Comte du Perche after 1090. 
2 CONT
2 CONT 4.         MARGUERITE de Ramerupt .  
2 CONT *The Chronicle of Alberic de Trois-Fontaines names "Margareta" as third daughter of Ebles Comte de Roucy and names her husband "comiti Hugonis de Claromonte Baluacensi"[1264].  The Genealogiæ Scriptoris Fusniacensis names "secunda
2 CONC m filiam comitis Helduini de Rameruth dictam Margaretam" as wife of "Hugo comes de Claro-monte"[1265].  
2 CONT *m HUGUES de Clermont [en-Beauvaisis] dit de Mouchy, son of ---.  1067. 
2 CONT
2 CONT 5.         ERMENTRUDE de Ramerupt (-1102 or after).  
2 CONT *The Chronicle of Alberic de Trois-Fontaines names "Ermentrudis" as fourth daughter of Ebles Comte de Roucy and names her husband "Theobaldo comiti de Rimnello"[1266].  The Genealogiæ Scriptoris Fusniacensis names "tertiam…Hilduin
2 CONC i comitis filiam Ermentrudem" as wife of "Theobaldus comes de Rinnel"[1267].  
2 CONT *m THIBAUT [I] Comte de Reynel, son of OLRI Comte de Reynel & his wife --- (-before 11 Apr 1101). 
2 CONT
2 CONT 6.         ADA de Ramerupt (-after 1021, bur Abbaye de Liessies).  
2 CONT *The Chronicle of Alberic de Trois-Fontaines names "Ada…de Guisia" as sixth daughter of Ebles Comte de Roucy[1268].  The Genealogiæ Scriptoris Fusniacensis names "quartam…Hilduini comitis filiam Adam" as wife firstly of "Godefridu
2 CONC s de Guisia" and secondly of "Galterum de Aat" and thirdly of "Theoderico de Avesnis"[1269].  "Wido Lescheriensis…et Guisiensis" granted rights to the abbey of Saint-André du Câteau, for the souls of "meæ et coniugis meæ Adeluyæ",
2 CONC  by undated charter, signed by "filiorum meorum Adam et Burgardi…" and later confirmed by the bishop of Laon by charter dated 1121 at the request of "Guido de Gusia rogatu uxoris suæ Adeluyæ et matris suæ Adæ" and with the consent
2 CONC  of "filiis suis Adam et Burchardo"[1270].  
2 CONT *She built the convent of Lessies with her third husband, where she retired after his death and was buried[1271].  
2 CONT *m firstly GEOFFROY Seigneur de Guise, son of ---.  
2 CONT *m secondly GAUTHIER Seigneur de Ath, son of ---.  
2 CONT *m thirdly THIERRY Seigneur d'Avesnes, son of WEDRICUS "Ad-barbam" d'Avesnes & his wife --- (-[1106]). 
2 CONT
2 CONT 7.         ADELA de Ramerupt (-[1068/69], bur Saint-Hubert, Ardennes).  
2 CONT *The Chronicle of Alberic de Trois-Fontaines names "Adele" as seventh daughter of Ebles Comte de Roucy and names her husband "Arnulfo comiti de Chisneio"[1272], although the chronology favours Adela being the sister rather than da
2 CONC ughter of Ebles.  The Genealogiæ Scriptoris Fusniacensis clarifies the question when it refers to, but does not name, "quintam…Hilduini comitis filiam" as wife of "Arnulfus comes de Cinni"[1273].  “Arnulphus comes cum coniuge mea 
2 CONC Adelais, filius Ludovici comitis” founded a monastery “in villa Pyrorum…in honore S. Sulpitii”, subject to “ecclesiæ S. Petri et S. Hugberti in Ardenna”, by undated charter signed by “Arnulphi comitis et Manasse fratris eius”[1274
2 CONC ].  "Arnulfus comes cum coniuge mea Adelais filius Ludoguici comitis" donated revenue from the church of Prix to Ardenne Saint-Hubert by charter dated to 1066, signed by "Arnulfi comitis et Manasse fratris eius…"[1275].  
2 CONT *"Arnulfus comes cum coniuge mea Adelail, filius Ludoguici comitis" founded the priory of Priez by charter dated 1068, signed by "Arnulphi comitis et Manasse fratris eius…"[1276].  
2 CONT *The Chronicle of Saint-Hubert records the burial of "Adeladis uxor Arnulphi, soror…Ebali Roceiensis" at Saint-Hubert, dated to [1068/69] from the context[1277]. 
2 CONT *m as his first wife, ARNOUL [II] Comte de Chiny, son of LOUIS [II] Comte de Chiny & his wife Sophie --- (-16 Apr 1106). 
2 CONT
2 CONT 8.         AELIS de Ramerupt .  
2 CONT *The Chronicle of Alberic de Trois-Fontaines names "Aeliz de Sarrata in Burgundia" as fifth daughter of Ebles Comte de Roucy[1278].  The Genealogiæ Scriptoris Fusniacensis names "sexta filia Hilduini comitis Adelidis" as mother of
2 CONC  "filium columbine simplicitatis nomine Bartholomeum…[et] Ebalum"[1279].  
2 CONT *m CONON "Falcon" de La Sarraz [Grandson], son of ADALBERT & his wife --- (-before 1114). 
2 CONT
2 CONT 9.         FELICIE de Ramerupt ([1060]-3 May 1123[1280], bur Monastery of San Juan de la Peña).  
2 CONT *The Chronicle of Alberic de Trois-Fontaines refers to the first of the seven daughters of Count Ebles as, inaccurately, wife of "regi Galicie Sanctio" but does not name her[1281].  The Genealogiæ Scriptoris Fusniacensis is somewh
2 CONC at more accurate in referring to, but still not naming, "septima filia…Hilduini" as wife of "Sanctio regi Hispanie" by whom she had "Hildefonsum regem et fratrem eius, qui ei successit in regnum.  Cuius filiam cum regni gubernacul
2 CONC is comes inclitus Barcinonensis, qui paganos impugnare non desinit, duxit uxorem"[1282].  
2 CONT *The Crónica de San Juan de la Peña records that King Sancho married "muller Doña Felicia"[1283].  The Monumenta Historiæ Tornacensis names "Feliciæ materteræ vestræ filium" as wife of "in Hispaniam regem Hildefonsum"[1284].  "San
2 CONC cius rex Aragonensium…cum filio meo Petro et uxore mea regina…Felicia" granted the monastery of Sauve-Majeure, Gironde to the church of Pamplona by charter dated to [1086/94][1285].  
2 CONT *m (1076[1286] or before) as his second wife, SANCHO I King of Aragon [SANCHO V King of Navarre], son of don RAMIRO I King of Aragon & his first wife Gerberge [Ermesenda] de Foix ([1042/43]-Huesca 4 Jun 1094, bur Monastery of San 
2 CONC Juan de la Peña). 
2 CONT
