1 NOTE {geni:about_me} ===Ranulph II de Warenne1
2 CONT b. after 1036, d. after 1074
2 CONT
2 CONT Father	Ranulph I de Varennes b. circa 998, d. after 1074
2 CONT Mother	Beatrice of Rouen b. circa 980
2 CONT
2 CONT Ranulph II de Warenne was born after 1036. He was the son of Ranulph I de Varennes and Beatrice of Rouen. Ranulph II de Warenne died after 1074.
2 CONT
2 CONT Family
2 CONT Child	
2 CONT * Ranulph III de Warenne b. c 1064
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT ----
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT Rudolf II de Warenne, son of Rudolf I of Warenne, was a Norman aristocrat and progenitor of the Earl of Surrey family line.
2 CONT
2 CONT He is known only from his subscriptions to two charters of his father for the Holy Trinity of Rouen. As his fathers lands near Rouen and in the Pays de Caux did not pass to his son William or William's descendants, it is likely th
2 CONC at Rodulf succeeded to them on his father's death.
2 CONT
2 CONT The Family of Warenne originated from near Normandy, France. The de Warenne surname derives from the castle of that name on the Varenne River, which flows through the territory William acquired in Upper Normandy.
2 CONT
2 CONT [edit] Family
2 CONT
2 CONT He married Emma in or before 1059 - both were still living in 1074, and had several children.
2 CONT
2 CONT *Rudolf III de Warenne - who inherited most of the family lands in Normandy.
2 CONT *William de Warenne, 1st Earl of Surrey - who fought with William the Conqueror at the Battle of Hastings and was reward with vast land holdings as the Earl of Surrey.
2 CONT *Frederick de Warenne - who was killed by Hereward the Wake. He is listed in the Domesday book holding lands in Cambridgeshire and Norfolk. (Domesday, ff.196, ii.465b, 170b, 172b). Another source lists Frederick as the brother of 
2 CONC William's wife, Gundred [1].
2 CONT
2 CONT References
2 CONT
2 CONT  * Orderic Vitalis Vol II, P 219
2 CONT *     * K.S.B. Keats-Rohan, Nottingham Med. Studies, vol. 37, 1993, pp. 21-4.
2 CONT *     * Cartography of Ste Trinité Abbey - cf. vol. 12, part 1, p. 492, notes h and i, citing Cart. Ste Trinité, nos xxix and xxxv.
2 CONT *     * Corrections to Early British Genealogy
2 CONT *     * Warren Family History Project
2 CONT
2 CONT --------------------
