1 OCCU Seigneur de Clermont-en-Beauvaisis, Sieur de Creil, de Mouchy, de Roucy, de Montdidier, de Gournay, de Luzarches
1 NOTE {geni:about_me} '''Hugues, Count de Clermont Lord of Creil & Mouchy''' was born circa 1030 in Clermont, Oise, France, and died in 1101. 
2 CONT
2 CONT b. 1030, of Clermont, Beauvais, France d. 1101, of Northamptonshire, Eng.
2 CONT
2 CONT Son of Renaud I de Breteuil, Count Clermont (-1087) and Ermengardis de Clermont
2 CONT
2 CONT He married '''Margaret (Marguerite) de Montdidier''', daughter of Hildouin IV de Montdidier Seigneur De Rameru and Alice (Adela) de Roucy, circa 1065 in Picardy, France. 
2 CONT
2 CONT ===Children===
2 CONT
2 CONT * Renaud II Comte de Clermont (-1162) m(2) Clemence of Bar-le-duc (-1183) 
2 CONT * Adelaide/Adeliza de_Clermont (1074-) m. Gilbert FitzRichard de CLARE 2nd Earl of Clare (1066-1114) 
2 CONT * Richilde de CLERMONT m. Dreux II de Mello Seigneur de Mouchy 
2 CONT * Ermentrude de CLERMONT (1051-) m(1) Hugh d' (Lupus) AVRANCHES Earl of Chester (-1101) 
2 CONT
2 CONT NOTE: From Wikipedia, the free encyclopedia The Counts of Clermont-en-Beauvaisis first appear in the early 11th century. Its principal town was Clermont, now in the Oise department but then within the ancient county of Beauvaisis 
2 CONC in the province of Île-de-France. The county was sold by their descendant, Theobald VI of Blois, to the French crown in 1218. It was first granted as an appanage in 1218 to Philip Hurepel; with the extinction of his line, it was g
2 CONC ranted in 1268 to the House of Bourbon, and was confiscated with the Duchy of Bourbon in 1527.[1]
2 CONT
2 CONT See "My Lines"
2 CONT
2 CONT ( http://homepages.rootsweb.ancestry.com/~cousin/html/p355.htm#i7069 )
2 CONT
2 CONT from Compiler: R. B. Stewart, Evans, GA
2 CONT
2 CONT __________________________________
2 CONT
2 CONT Hugh was the Count of Clermont-en-Beauvaisis in France.
2 CONT
2 CONT Find A Grave Memorial
2 CONT
2 CONT Hugh De Breteuil, I
2 CONT
2 CONT BIRTH	5 Sep 1030
2 CONT
2 CONT Clermont, Departement de l'Oise, Picardie, France
2 CONT
2 CONT DEATH	9 Jun 1101 (aged 70)
2 CONT
2 CONT Clermont, Departement de l'Oise, Picardie, France
2 CONT
2 CONT BURIAL	
2 CONT
2 CONT Clermont de l'Oise Clermont, Departement de l'Oise, Picardie, France
2 CONT
2 CONT MEMORIAL ID	160236090 · View Source
2 CONT
2 CONT Hugh de Breteuil, 4th Count of Clermont-en-Beauvaisis, Lord of Luzarches, was the son of Ronald de Breteuil, 3rd Count of Clermont-en-Beauvaisis (1010-1088) and Ermengardis de Clermont, Dame de Clermont-en-Beauvaisis (1008-1050). 
2 CONC He married Marguerite de Ramerupt, Dame de Roucy (1045-1110), daughter of Hildouin de Ramerupt IV, Count of Montdidier et de Roucy (1010-1063) and had six children by that marriage:
2 CONT
2 CONT * Adeliza de Breteuil; 
2 CONT * Ermentrude de Breteuil;
2 CONT * Béatrix de Breteuil, Dame de Luzarches; 
2 CONT * Richilde de Breteuil; 
2 CONT * Renaud de Breteuil II, 5th Count of Clermont-en-Beauvaisis;
2 CONT * Guiselle ou Gisèle de Breteuil 
2 CONT
2 CONT The nobility from the House of Creil were also know as those "of Clermont." Thus, Hugh de Breteuil is also know as "Hugh of Clermont" to history. This is true for his descendants as well.
2 CONT
2 CONT Family Members
2 CONT
