2 CONT '''Ertembourge de Briquebec''' (Briquiobec)	
2 CONT
2 CONT * Daughter of Anslec (Lancelot) de Bastembourg, seigneur de Briquebec and Gilette 'the Dane' de Beaumont
2 CONT * Wife of Torfe "the Rich" de Harcourt [only son and heir of Bernard "the Dane" (second-in-command to Rollo in the invason and conquest of Normandy, and Lord of Harcourt, Caileville and Beaufical) and his wife Sprota of Burgundy] 
2 CONC Ford also of Torville, Torcy, Torny and Potatou
2 CONT * Mother of  (1) Thorold, seigneur de Pont-Audemer; also Torville, Torny, Potatou and Borrye Tourode. Joint governor and Guardian of Duke William, with his brother Turchetil. (2) Turchetil d'Harcourt, seigneur de Tourville, de Tur
2 CONC queville, de Turqueraye & d'Harcourt.  Joint governor and Guardian of Duke William, with his brother Thorold.. (3) Guillaume d'Harcourt
2 CONT * Sister of Richard Thurstan (Toustain) de Bastembourg
2 CONT
2 CONT =<nowiki>--------------------------------------</nowiki>=
2 CONT
2 CONT Ertemberge de Brioquibec [Parents] 1, 2 was born 3 about 931 in Normandie, France. She married 4 Torf d'Harcourt about 944 in France. Ertemberge was born 5 about 930 in Normandie, France.
2 CONT
2 CONT They had the following children:
2 CONT
2 CONT       		M 	i 	Thorold de Ponteaudemer d'Harcourt
2 CONT
2 CONT       		M 	ii 	Turchetel d'Harcourt Seigneur de Torqueville
2 CONT
2 CONT --------------------
2 CONT
2 CONT Torf the Rich married in 955 Ensorberge. They had two sons as follows:
2 CONT
2 CONT 1. Thurbold de Pontaudemer, the eldest son.
2 CONT
2 CONT 2. Turquetil, Turqueville or Tanqueraye, de Neufmarche, second son. died about 1036. He married Anceline, sister of Turstain of Montfort-sur-Risle.
2 CONT
2 CONT --------------------
2 CONT
2 CONT http://stanhopefamilyhistory.webs.com/
2 CONT
2 CONT Ertemburge de Briquebec, married her second-cousin [1.1.1.2.3.1.] Torf the Rich - conveyed Crispin lands to him as maritagium.
2 CONT
2 CONT More context from above link (stanhopefamily), giving the parentage of Ertemberge de Briquebec:
2 CONT
2 CONT > 1.1.1.2.2.1.  Anslech de Briquebec - alias Oslac de Briquebec, a powerful baron, associated with [1.1.1.2.3] Bernard the Dane in the administration of Normandy - tutor to 'Duke' Richard of Normandy. He married Gillette de Beaumo
2 CONC nt -unknown pedigree. In the rebellion of Richard de St. Saveur, son of [1.1.3.1.] Helgi against    [1.1.1.3.1.1.] 'Duke' William Longsword, in 933, Anslech is mentioned by Wace as one of the three Barons who alone remained faithf
2 CONC ul to the Duke, his second-cousin, by rendering him military service at the seige of Rouen. Their son was Turstain de Bastembourg, 'père de Guillaume, tige des Bertran' [Gustave Saige, Cartulaire de la seigneurie de Fontenay le Ma
2 CONC rmion, p. 29, 1895]. 'It is deserving of observation that the senior branch of the family held the extensive barony of Bricquebac in Normandy for eight successive generations. The last died as late as the 14th Century, leaving his
2 CONC  large possessions, and the castle of Bricquebec, which one of his early ancestors had built, to his eldest daughter, who carried them by marriage to William Paisnel [Paganel], Baron of Hambie' [Memoirs Chiefly Illustrative of the
2 CONC  History and Antiquities of Northumberland, Royal Archeological Institute of Great Britain and Ireland, vol. ii., pp. 48-50, 1859].
2 CONT
2 CONT >> 1.1.1.2.2.1.1. Ertemburge de Briquebec, married her second-cousin [1.1.1.2.3.1.] Torf the Rich - conveyed Crispin lands to him as maritagium.
