2 CONT From http://www.rpi.edu/~holmes/Hobbies/Genealogy/ps04/ps04_179.htm
2 CONT
2 CONT Turof, son of Torf, inherited from his mother the Pont Audemar estate on the banks of the Risele ten miles from the Seine. There is some doubt as to the identity of his wife {-see ref. under ID2888}. 
2 CONT
2 CONT Alternate spelling: Touroude de PONT-AUDEMER
2 CONT --------------------
2 CONT ''Vital Statistics'''
2 CONT
2 CONT * Michael Stanhope cites Robert de Torigny (see below) as the source for the parents of Turold (Turulf) and Turchetil being Torf and Ertemberga.  FMG only gives Torf, saying Torf's wife is unknown.
2 CONT * Similarly, de Torigny says that Turchetil was Torf and Ertemberga's son, whereas FMG says that a daughter of Torf married Turchetil but then seems to contradict himself.
2 CONT
2 CONT '''Sources and Notes'''
2 CONT
2 CONT http://stanhopefamilyhistory.webs.com/
2 CONT
2 CONT * Turold of Pont-Audemer - according to Robert of Torigny [GND, viii. c. 37], Torf and Ertemberga were the parents of Turold alias Turulf, and Turchetil [see also OV ii. 12]; the latter being Seigneur de Turqueville et de Tanquera
2 CONC ye, who married Anceline de Bertrande, daughter of Ansfrid the Dane and Helloe de Beulac. Ansfrid was another son of [1.1.1.2.2.] Heriolfr Turstain. It is wrongly assumed that this Turchetil was a forefather of the Harcourts; he d
2 CONC ied childless, passing his estate to his great-nephew [cart. Preaux, fol. 97v; CP xi. Instr., col. 201 a. d., Du Monstier, Neustria Pia, p. 522, 1663]. Turold married Duvelina de Crepon, sister of Gunnor, the wife of [1.1.1.3.1.1.
2 CONC 1.] 'Duke' Richard; they were ancestors of the Beaumont family of Pont-Audemer, and, according to Auguste le Prevost, of the Harcourts, with Turold and Duvelina being the parents of both [1.1.1.2.3.1.1.2.] Onfroi de Vieilles [GND 
2 CONC vii. 1. 3.], and[1.1.1.2.3.1.2.] Turchetil de Neufmarche [Ordericus, ed. Prevost, vol. i., p. 180; ii. pp. 14, 369, 370; iii. pp. 42, 229]. 
2 CONT --------------------
