2 CONC andson of one of the viking chiefs of Scandinavia whoaccompanied Rollo about 900 A.D. in the Norse invasion of northern Francewhere they permanently settled and gave to the country its name"Normandie". Torf possessed numerous lord
2 CONC ships in Normandie, beingSeigneur de Torville, Torcy, Torny, Torly, du Ponteautord, etc. (P) Hemarried about 950, ERTEMBERGE DE BRIQUEBEC. Children: i. TOUROUDE, SIRE DU
2 CONT PONTEAUde MER, b. about 950. ii. TURCHETIL, SEIGNEUR DE TURQUEVILLE,ancestor of the celebrated Harcourt family of Normandie and England. iii.WILLIAM DE TORVILLE."
