2 CONT http://fmg.ac/Projects/MedLands/NORTHERN%20FRANCE.htm:
2 CONT
2 CONT GAUTHIER [II] "le Blanc", son of GAUTHIER [I] Comte d'Amiens & his [first/second] wife [Eva---/Adela ---] (-after 1017).
2 CONT
2 CONT "Wauterii comitis, Walterii et Radulfi filiorum eius" subscribed a charter dated 975 under which "Hugo Francorum dux" restored the abbey of Saint-Jean to the abbey of Sainte-Croix d'Orléans[17]. A charter of "Hugo…Francorum rex" c
2 CONC onfirming the privileges of the monastery of Corvey dated 987 is subscribed by "Walteri comitis Ambianensis ac filiorum eius Walteri, Gotfredi, Rodulfi"[18]. Comte de Mantes. "Walterius comes" donated property "prope nostrum caste
2 CONC llum…Medanta" to "Carnotensi monasterio Sancti Petri", for the soul of "coniugis mee Adelidis filiorumque meorum", by charter to [1006], signed by "Walterii comitis, Rodulfi filii eius, Drogonis filii eius…"[19]. Comte d'Amiens et
2 CONC  du Vexin.
2 CONT m ADELA, daughter of ---. "Walterius comes" donated property "prope nostrum castellum…Medanta" to "Carnotensi monasterio Sancti Petri", for the soul of "coniugis mee Adelidis filiorumque meorum", by charter to [1006], signed by "W
2 CONC alterii comitis, Rodulfi filii eius, Drogonis filii eius…"[20].
2 CONT
2 CONT Comte Gauthier [II] & his wife had four children:
2 CONT
2 CONT 1. RAOUL de Mantes (-1060). "Walterius comes" donated property "prope nostrum castellum…Medanta" to "Carnotensi monasterio Sancti Petri", for the soul of "coniugis mee Adelidis filiorumque meorum", by charter to [1006], signed by 
2 CONC "Walterii comitis, Rodulfi filii eius, Drogonis filii eius…"[21]. Comte de Valois et d'Amiens. - COMTES de VALOIS.
2 CONT
2 CONT 2. DREUX [Drogo] de Mantes (-[13 Aug] [1035]). "Walterius comes" donated property "prope nostrum castellum…Medanta" to "Carnotensi monasterio Sancti Petri", for the soul of "coniugis mee Adelidis filiorumque meorum", by charter to
2 CONC  [1006], signed by "Walterii comitis, Rodulfi filii eius, Drogonis filii eius…"[22]. He succeeded his father as Comte de Mantes. Comte d'Amboise. "Droco comes Ambianensium" donated property to "Sancti Petri Gismoensis" by undated 
2 CONC charter, signed by "Droconis comitis, Eotde comitissæ, Falconis fratris comitis, Rodulfi filiii comitis, Gualterii alterius filii…"[23]. He accompanied Robert II Duke of Normandy to Jerusalem and died on the journey[24]. According
2 CONC  to Orderic Vitalis, Henri I King of France took back the Vexin after the death of Comte Drogo[25]. The necrology of Reims Saint-Rémi records the death "X Kal Aug" of "Drogo comes"[26]. m ([1025 or before]) as her first husband, G
2 CONC ODGIFU [Goda] of England, daughter of ÆTHELRED II "the Unready" King of England & his second wife Emma de Normandie (-before 1049). Her parentage is stated by Orderic Vitalis, who says that Godgifu went into exile in Normandy with
2 CONC  her brother[27] in 1013. According to Orderic Vitalis, her first marriage was arranged by Robert II Duke of Normandy[28], indicating that she probably did not return to England. This information is suspect, assuming that the char
2 CONC ter of "Robertus Rex", which names "Comes Drogo…cum duobus fratribus Fulcone…et Rodulpho necnon uxore cum filiis supra memorati Drogonis", is correctly dated to 1025 as Duke Robert did not succeed as duke until 1027[29]. Another p
2 CONC ossibility is that Drogo's children at that date were born from an earlier otherwise unrecorded marriage. There is no indication of the birth dates of his known children shown below, but the fact that none of them was given a typi
2 CONC cally Anglo-Saxon name also suggests that Godgifu may not have been the mother of all of them (although she is attested as mother of the son Raoul, see below). "Droco comes Ambianensium" donated property to "Sancti Petri Gismoensi
2 CONC s" by undated charter, signed by "Droconis comitis, Eotde comitissæ, Falconis fratris comitis, Rodulfi filiii comitis, Gualterii alterius filii…"[30]. Godgifu married secondly ([1036]) as his first wife, Eustache [II] Comte de Bou
2 CONC logne . Her second marriage is referred to by Florence of Worcester[31]. ...
2 CONT
2 CONT 3. FOULQUES de Mantes . "Comes Drogo…cum duobus fratribus Fulcone…et Rodulpho necnon uxore cum filiis supra memorati Drogonis" are named in a charter of "Robertus Rex" dated 1030[44]. "Droco comes Ambianensium" donated property to
2 CONC  "Sancti Petri Gismoensis" by undated charter, signed by "Droconis comitis, Eotde comitissæ, Falconis fratris comitis, Rodulfi filiii comitis, Gualterii alterius filii…"[45].
2 CONT
2 CONT 4. daughter . The Chronicle of Alberic de Trois-Fontaines refers to the mother of "Waleranni comitis [Mellentini]" as daughter of "Gauterus Albus de Albamarla"[46]. Yves de Chartres names "Gualterius Albus" as father of "matrem Gu
2 CONC aleranni comitis"[47]. m HUGUES Comte de Meulan, son of GALERAN [II] Comte de Meulan & his wife --- (-after 25 Aug 1005).
2 CONT
2 CONT ---------------------
2 CONT
2 CONT Unattributed basic information on Gautier II "the White" (at least it has sources):
2 CONT
2 CONT Gautier II "the White", comte de Vexin, Valois, et Amiens[1],[2],[3],[4]
2 CONT
2 CONT b. circa 944,
2 CONT
2 CONT d. 1027
2 CONT
2 CONT Father	Gautier I, comte de Vexin, Valois, et Amiens[5]
2 CONT
2 CONT b. circa 925,
2 CONT
2 CONT d. between 992 and 998
2 CONT
2 CONT Mother	Adèle d'Anjou[5]
2 CONT
2 CONT b. circa 924
2 CONT
2 CONT Gautier II "the White", comte de Vexin, Valois, et Amiens was born circa 944 at Vexin, Normandy, France. He was the son of Gautier I, comte de Vexin, Valois, et Amiens and Adèle d'Anjou.[5]
2 CONT
2 CONT Gautier II "the White", comte de Vexin, Valois, et Amiens married Adèle de Senlis before 974.
2 CONT
2 CONT Gautier II "the White", comte de Vexin, Valois, et Amiens died in 1027.
2 CONT
2 CONT Family
2 CONT
2 CONT Adèle de Senlis
2 CONT
2 CONT b. circa 944
2 CONT
2 CONT Children
2 CONT
2 CONT 1. Dreux, comte d'Amiens+ b. c 974, d. 1035
2 CONT
2 CONT 2. Raoul II de Vexin+ b. a 974, d. 1040
2 CONT
2 CONT 3. N. N. de Vexin+ b. a 974
2 CONT
2 CONT Citations
2 CONT
2 CONT 1. [S204] Roderick W. Stuart, RfC, 37-35, 268-35.
2 CONT
2 CONT 2. [S206] With additions and corrections by Walter Lee Sheppard, Jr. and assisted by David Faris Frederick Lewis Weis, Weis: AR 7th ed., 250-19.
2 CONT
2 CONT 3. [S204] Roderick W. Stuart, RfC, 268-35.
2 CONT
2 CONT 4. [S204] Roderick W. Stuart, RfC, 185-35.
2 CONT
