1 NOTE {geni:about_me} The FMG Medieval Lands database positions her as the daughter of Hilduin, Vicomte of Chartres, Comte de Breteuil, and his wife Emmeline.
2 CONT
2 CONT http://fmg.ac/Projects/MedLands/CENTRAL FRANCE.htm
2 CONT
2 CONT ADELA [Alix] de Breteuil (-11 Sep 1051).  The primary source which confirms her parentage and marriage has not yet been identified.  m RAOUL [II] Comte de Valois, d'Amiens et de Crépy, son of GAUTHIER [II] "le Blanc" Comte de Mant
2 CONC es, de Valois, d'Amiens et de Crépy & his wife Adela --- (-1060).  
2 CONT
2 CONT She is easily confused with her nieces, daughters of Erard de Breteuil, who are sisters with similar names:
2 CONT
2 CONT ADELAIDE de Breteuil (-1073 or after). "…Gerduini vicecomitis, Ebrardi filii eius, Ebrardi filii Ebrardi, Hugonis fratris eius, Adeladis sororis eorum…" signed the charter dated to [1046/64] under which "Gelduinus…vicecomes" donat
2 CONC ed a serf to Marmoutier[466]. Nun at Marmoutiers [1039/42]/1073.
2 CONT
2 CONT ADELAIS de Breteuil . Orderic Vitalis names Adelais, daughter of Everard du Puiset, as second wife of Roger de Montgommery and says that she was "remarkable for her gentleness and piety"[470]. m (after 1082) as his second wife, RO
2 CONC GER II de Montgommery Earl of Shrewsbury Baron de Bellême, son of ROGER I Seigneur de Montgommery and Vicomte de l'Hiémois & his wife Josceline --- (-Shrewsbury 27 Jul 1094, bur Shrewsbury Abbey). 
2 CONT
2 CONT --------------------
2 CONT
2 CONT Adelaide de Breteuil
2 CONT
2 CONT b. 980
2 CONT
2 CONT Father	Hildouin de Breteuil b. circa 960, d. 18 May 1060
2 CONT
2 CONT      Adelaide de Breteuil was born in 980.1 She was the daughter of Hildouin de Breteuil. Adelaide de Breteuil married Raoul II de Vexin, son of Gautier II "the White", comte de Vexin, Valois, et Amiens and Adèle de Senlis, before
2 CONC  1025.
2 CONT
2 CONT Family
2 CONT
2 CONT Raoul II de Vexin b. after 974, d. 1040
