1 NOTE {geni:about_me} Curator (dvb) note: Nocher’s son and namesake became Count of Bar-sur-Aube upon his death, and the countship of Soissons reverted to his wife. His son Renaud would eventually become the Count of Soissons.
2 CONT
2 CONT —————————
2 CONT
2 CONT According to the [http://fmg.ac/Projects/MedLands/CHAMPAGNE%20NOBILITY.htm#_Toc219265859 FMG Medieval Lands database], '''Nocher III, Comte de Bar-sur-Aube''', was the son of '''Nocher II Comte de Bar-sur-Aube, Comte de Soissons''
2 CONC ', and '''Adelisa Comtesse de Soissons''':
2 CONT
2 CONT '''NOCHER [III]''' (-[1040]).  The primary source which confirms his parentage has not yet been identified.  '''Comte de Bar-sur-Seine'''.  
2 CONT
2 CONT m ---.  The name of Nocher's wife is not known.  
2 CONT
2 CONT Nocher [III] & his wife had two children: 
2 CONT
2 CONT (1)       '''AELIS''' (-11 Sep 1053).  The primary source which confirms her parentage and her marriages has not so far been identified.  Ctss de Bar-sur-Aube.  Her origin is indicated by the undated charter under which her son "S
2 CONC ymon comes Barrensium" donated property to the abbey of Molesme for the souls of "parentum suorum Radulfi…comitis et Walterii fratris suis et matris sue Adele"[101].  The Chronicle of Alberic de Trois-Fontaines names "Adala" wife 
2 CONC of "comitis Veromandie [error for Valois] Rodolfi" and mother of "Symonem et filiam…Adala", but does not give her origin[102].  "Symon comes Barrensium" donated property to the abbey of Molesme for the souls of "parentum suorum Ra
2 CONC dulfi…comitis et Walterii fratris suis et matris sue Adele" by undated charter, the entry stating that "Adelina comitissa" died "III Id Sep"[103].  
2 CONT
2 CONT # m firstly (1040) RENAUD de Semur-en-Brionnais, son of GEOFFROY I Seigneur de Semur & his first wife --- de Brioude.  
2 CONT # m secondly RENARD Comte de Joigny, son of GEOFFROY de Joigny & his wife Alix de Sens.  
2 CONT # m thirdly as his second wife, ROGER [I] avoué de Vignory, son of GUY [I] de Vignory & his wife --- (-after [1050/52]).  
2 CONT # m fourthly (after [1050/52]) as his first wife, RAOUL III Comte de Valois, de Vexin, d'Amiens et de Vitry, son of RAOUL II Comte de Valois & his wife Adela de Breteuil (-Péronne 23 Feb or 8 Sep 1074, bur Montdidier, later transf
2 CONC erred to Crépy-en-Valois, église collégiale Saint-Arnoul).  
2 CONT
2 CONT The county of Bar-sur-Aube was transmitted to the issue of this fourth marriage. 
2 CONT
2 CONT (2)      ''' ISABELLE''' .  The primary source which confirms her parentage and marriage has not yet been identified.  m GAUTHIER de Clamecy.  
