2 CONT Conrad the Peaceful (c. 925 – 19 October 993) was the king of Burgundy from 937 until his death. He was the son of King Rudolph II, the first king of a united Burgundy and Bertha of Swabia. Conrad is sometimes numbered Conrad I as
2 CONC  king of Burgundy and as Conrad III of Provence, since he inherited Provence in 948.[1]
2 CONT
2 CONT His reign was peaceful (hence his byname) and he was popular with his subjects. The only war in which he got involved was a simultaneous invasion of Saracens and Magyars in which he played them off against each other. He then rout
2 CONC ed them in combat.
2 CONT
2 CONT Conrad's wife, Matilda He married Matilda, daughter of Louis IV of France and Gerberga of Saxony. They had at least five children:
2 CONT     * Bertha (967 – 16 January 1016), married Odo I, Count of Blois, and then Robert II of France
2 CONT     * Matilda (born 969), possibly married Robert, Count of Geneva
2 CONT     * Rudolph (971 – 6 September 1032)
2 CONT     * Gerberga (born 965), married Herman II, Duke of Swabia
2 CONT
2 CONT He was secondly married to Adelaide of Bellay. They were parents to at least one daughter:
2 CONT     * Gisela (975 – 21 July 1006), married Henry II, Duke of Bavaria
2 CONT
