1 NOTE 27724418. Grev Wilhelm I BOSOSONBOSOSON av Provence(5726) died about 992.(5727) Han døde som munk, begravet i Sarrian eller Cluny. He was a Greve in Provence. (5728) Han synes å ha hatt en betydligere sosial posisjon enn faren Bo
2 CONC so. Han og broren Rothbald II (g.m Ermengard) rådet over utstrakte arvegodser i grevskapene Frejus, Sisteron, Avignon, Riez, Marieille, Aix, Orange, Arles, Gap og mange andre. Han forestår retten ikke alene 967 eller 968 i Arles
2 CONC  selv, men også 978 eller 984 i Manosque i grevskapet Sisteron. Han var sammen med broren rådgiver for biskoppene i Marseille, Vavaillon o.s.v. P.g.a sin store inflytelse føte disse ikke alene titelen markgreve men også fyrste 
2 CONC av Provence, og ble i dokumenter benevnet slik. De innla seg stor fortjeneste, da de som anførere for hæren 973, visstnok hjulpet av markgreve Aduin av Turin, knekket og ødela fullstadig de herjende Saracenere. som overalt la land
2 CONC et øde. Wilhelm var i det hele tatt en sjelden mann og ble også kalt "Fedrelandets far". Det er derfor lett å forstå disse børdrenes store makt og anseelse He was married to Grevinne Adelheid (Adelais) N.NSDTR av Anjou about 98
2 CONC 5.(5729) hennes 3 g.m
1 NOTE 27724536. Grev Wilhelm III Taillefer av Toulouse +(5827) was born about 947.(5828) He was a Greve about 961 in Toulouse.(5829) under sin mors, Garsindes, formynderskap. Han delte med sin tremening, Raimund II. grevskapene Rouergue
2 CONC , Quercy og Albigeois. Var ogs·greva av Auvergne, men overdro dette til Gui, vicomte av Clermont. Wilhelm fikk med sin hustru, Emma, halvdelen av Provence He died in 1037. (5830) Begravet i St. Sernin i Toulouse, hvor hans grav en
2 CONC nå finnes. Han ble stamfar til grevene St. Gille (ca 975). I 981 bemektiger han seg klostret Beaulieu i Nedre Lomousin. I 988 nekter han å anerkjenne Hugo Capet som kong. Det synes som han først var gift med en dame, hvis navn e
2 CONC r ukjent og som han forstøtte. Han regnes for å ha vært gift to ganger. He was married to Grevinne Emma av Provence about 991
1 NOTE 55449074. Grev Rotbold Provence(7460) died after 1008. (7461) He was a Greve eller marquis in Provence. (7462) sammen med sin bror Wilhelm I, idet begge etterfulgte sinfar Boso II. Sammen med sin bror Vilhelm undertegner han et do
2 CONC kument i mai 961. I 992 undertegner han et dokument, som ikke er underskkrevet av Ermengarde. I 1004 var han til stede på et møte i klostret Psalmodi, hvor han undertegner. Og et dokument av 1005 ang. en gave til klostret S. Vict
2 CONC or er undertegnet av ham , hans sønner og av Ermengarde, som dog står etter sønnene, hvilket tyder på at hun ikke var deres mor. Etter 1008 hørte man ikke mere fra ham. He was married to Ermengarde
1 NOTE BIOGRAPHY
2 CONT Guillaume was born about 950, the son of Boso II, comte d'Avignon et Arles, and Constance de Provence. Called 'le Liberateur' (the Liberator), Guillaume was count of Provence from 968 to his abdication. In 975 or 979 he took the t
2 CONC itle of _marchio_ or margrave. He is often considered the founder of the county of Provence. He and his elder brother Roubaud II both carried the title of _comes_ or count concurrently, but it is unknown if they were joint-counts 
2 CONC of the whole of Provence or if the region was divided. His brother never bore any other title than count so long as Guillaume lived, so Guillaume seems to have attained a certain supremacy.
2 CONT
2 CONT Guillaume's first marriage was with Arsenda de Comminges. They had at least two children, Arsinde and Guillaume III, both of whom would have progeny. Between 984 and 986, against papal advice he married Adelaide dite Blanche d'Anj
2 CONC ou, daughter of Foulques II 'the Good', comte d'Anjou, and Gerberge de Tours. Adelaide was a widow thrice over (her last husband had been Louis V, king of France), but none of her marriages had resulted in progeny. With Guillaume 
2 CONC she had at least two daughters, both of whom would have progeny.
2 CONT
2 CONT In 980, Guillaume was installed as Count of Arles. His sobriquet comes from his victories against the Saracens by which he liberated Provence from their threat, which had been constant since the establishment of a base at Fraxinet
2 CONC . At the Battle of Tourtour in 973, with the assistance of the counts of the High Alps and the viscounts of Marseille and Fos, he definitively routed the Saracens, chasing them forever from Provence. He reorganised the region east
2 CONC  of the Rhône, which he conquered from the Saracens and which had been given him as a gift from King Conrad of Burgundy. Also by royal consent, he and his descendants controlled the _fisc_ (the royal demesne which paid taxes, enti
2 CONC rely in kind, from which the royal household was meant to be supported) in Provence. With Isarn, bishop of Grenoble, he repopulated the Dauphiny and settled an Italian count named Ugo Blavia near Fréjus in 970 in order to bring th
2 CONC at land back to cultivation. For all this, he figures prominently in Ralph Glaber's chronicle with the title of _dux_ and he appears in a charter of 992 as _pater patriae._
2 CONT
2 CONT Guillaume donated land to Cluny and retired to become a monk, dying about 994 at Avignon, where he was buried in the church of Saint-Croix at Sarrians. He was succeeded as margrave by his brother Roubaud II. His great principality
2 CONC  began to diminish soon after his death as the castles of his vassals, which he had kept carefully under ducal control, soon became allods of their possessors.
