2 CONT      Fulk II d'Anjou, Comte d'Anjou was the son of Fulk I d'Anjou, Comte d'Anjou and Roselle de Loch. He married Gerberga de Gatinois.1 He died in 958 at Tours, France.1
2 CONT      Fulk II d'Anjou, Comte d'Anjou also went by the nick-name of Fulk 'the Good'. He gained the title of Comte d'Anjou. Children of Fulk II d'Anjou, Comte d'Anjou and Gerberge de Tours
2 CONT
