2 TITL Hugh Capet, King of France
2 NOTE Hugh Capet, King of France, founder of the Capetian dynasty, b. about the middle of the tenth century; d. about 996, probably 24 October. He was the second son of Hugh the Great, Count of Paris, and Hedwig, sister of Otto I, Germa
3 CONC n Emperor, and was about ten years old when he inherited from his father the Countship of Paris and the Duchy of France.
3 CONT
3 CONT Read more about Hugh Capet jn his profile.
