2 CONT ----------
2 CONT
2 CONT Thibaut, also called Theobald, surnamed Filans-stupas, Forester [of King Robert], father of "Guidone [Guy] ...[of] Monte-Lethericum"[974].  Parents unknown.
2 CONT
2 CONT ''H.      SEIGNEURS de MONTLHERY
2 CONT Montlhéry is located due south of Paris, west of Corbeil and east of Rambouillet.  The chronology of the documents quoted below suggests that the castle of Montlhéry was first constructed in the early 11th century during the reign
2 CONC  of Robert II King of France. ''
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT https://fmg.ac/Projects/MedLands/parcorroc.htm#GuyIMontlherydied1095 
2 CONT
2 CONT 1.     '''    THIBAUT''' “Filans-stupas/File-Etoupes” .  The Historia of Monk Aimon names "Theobaldus cognomina Filans-stupas, Forestarius [Roberti Regis]" as father of "Guidonem...[de] Montem-Lethericum"[974].  Brémeron’s history
2 CONC  of Longpont, written in 1713 calls him "Thibaud de Montmorency surnommé File-Etoupes seigneur de Bray" (without citing the corresponding primary source)[975].  No primary source has been found that indicates that Thibaut was rela
2 CONC ted to the seigneurs de Montmorency. 
2 CONT
2 CONT '''m''' ---.  The name of Thibaut’s wife is not known. 
2 CONT
2 CONT  Thibaut & his wife had one child: 
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT > a)         GUY [I] (-[24 Jul] 1095, bur abbaye de Longpont).  Married HODIERNE de Gometz-la-Ferté, , daughter of - (-26 Apr --, bur -, transferred 1641 to Longpont church). 
2 CONT
2 CONT http://fmg.ac/Projects/MedLands/parcorroc.htm#_Toc495733088
2 CONT -----------
2 CONT
2 CONT https://books.google.com/books?id=DSwAAAAAQAAJ&printsec=frontcover&dq=de+marisco+genealogy&hl=en&sa=X&ved=0ahUKEwjv07WQ8oXcAhVE04MKHWBIALQQ6AEIKTAA#v=onepage&q=de%20marisco%20genealogy&f=false
2 CONT
2 CONT Thibaud "Fille-Etoupe", Seigneur de Bray & de Montlhéry and Bouchard I "le Barbu", Seigneur de Montmorency appear to have been a brothers.
2 CONT
2 CONT He was living in the time of Hugh Capet. He was built the castle which was to become the family seat in 1015 in Montlhéry, France. 
2 CONT
2 CONT He was Grand Forester of King Robert II of France [Anselme de Sainte-Marie (augustin déchaussé), Histoire généalogique et chronologique de la maison royale de France, des pairs, grands officiers de la couronne et de la maison du r
2 CONC oy et des anciens barons du royaume. (Reprod. de l'éd. de Paris : chez Estienne Loyson, 1674: Num. BNF de l'éd. de Paris : Bibliothèque nationale de France, 1987. 1 microfilmReprod. de l'éd. de Paris : Compagnie des libraires asso
2 CONC ciez, 1730, 1730), III:664].
2 CONT
2 CONT He died in 1031 [Roderick W. Stuart, Royalty for Commoners: The Complete Lineage of John of Gaunt, Son of Edward III, Kings of England, and Queen Philippa (.: ., 3rd Ed., 1998), 241-34].
2 CONT --------------------
2 CONT Thibaud "Fille-Etoupe", seigneur de Bray & de Montlhéry, and Bouchard I "le Barbu", seigneur de Montmorency, appear to have been a brothers.
2 CONT
2 CONT Thibaud was recorded as living in the time of Hugh Capet.
2 CONT
2 CONT He built the castle which was to become the family seat in 1015 at Montlhéry, France. 
2 CONT
2 CONT He was Grand Forester of King Robert II of France.
2 CONT
