1 NOTE Ancestral File Number:<AFN> FLH9-LK
1 NOTE Gunnora or Gunnor (c. 936–1031) was the wife and consort of Richard I of Normandy. Her parentage is unknown, earliest sources reporting solely that she was of Danish ancestry and naming siblings including brother Herefast de Crepo
2 CONC n who is sometimes erroneously given as her father.
2 CONT She was living with her sister Seinfreda, the wife of a local forester, when Richard passed by hunting. He is said to have approached Seinfreda with amorous intentions, but the lady rejected his advance, suggesting that her unmarr
2 CONC ied sister Gunnor might prove more receptive. They became lovers, Gunnor first acting as his mistress and eventually marrying him.
1 NOTE 110904717. Gunnor N.NSDTR(10079) was born about 950.(10080) She died in 1030/31.(10081) Hun skal først ha vært Richard I's elskerinne, hvilket dog synes tvilsomt, og ble etter Emmas død gift med Richard, antagelig kort etter 968. 
2 CONC Hun var en høyt begavet kvinne med mange fortrinnlige egenskaper og av ansett slekt. man kjenner en bror Herfast og tre søstre: Sainfrida, Weiwa og Awelina. Hun viste stor klokskap i verdslige anliggender, var veltalende, hadde en
2 CONC  god hukommelse og stor interesse for slektens historie.
1 NOTE
2 CONT Please contact luseaann@excite.com with any corrections/additions.
