1 NOTE Sources: RC 24, 89, 166, 168, 222; Kraentzler 1153, 1156, 1174, 1180, 
2 CONT 1194,
2 CONT 1211, 1432, 1443; A. Roots 121E; Coe; Norr; Onslow; Pfafman; Davis.
2 CONT Roots: (Danish wife) Gunnor, died 1027 or 1031, daughter of forester
2 CONT of Arques.
2 CONT K. calls her Gonnor de Crepon. Norr: Gunnor (Gunora), (952)-1031.
2 CONT Onslow in "The Dukes of Normandy and Their Orgin" says:
2 CONT Richard I heard about a charming woman married to the superintendent of
2 CONT forests at Secheville near Arques. Richard visited Secheville, met the
2 CONT forester's beautiful wife, Sainfrida, and "had the impudence to suggest
2 CONT to her husband that he should be allowed to make her better acquaintance.
2 CONT "The poor man was much perturbed and went in trouble to his wife. The lady
2 CONT had no mind to become the mistress of the Duke, but her morals werenot so
2 CONT rigid as to prevent her from making capital our of the situation for her
2 CONT family. Sainfrida had three sisters, Gunnor, Adelina and Veva (Wevia), 
2 CONT and a
2 CONT brother named Herfast. Gunnor was a very pretty girl and by no means
2 CONT particular. Sainfrida told her husband to pretend to fall in with the 
2 CONT Duke's
2 CONT proposals and give Richard facilities to pay her a visit. But when Richard
2 CONT arrived, Gunnor took Sainfrida's place. The Duke did not discover the 
2 CONT trick
2 CONT until the following day; but so delighted was he with Gunnor that not 
2 CONT only did
2 CONT he forgive Sainfrida, but thanked her for having saved him from mortal 
2 CONT sin! The
2 CONT result was that Gunnor became his wife by Danish custom and eventually the
2 CONT mother of a numerous family, the eldest of which was Richard II of 
2 CONT Normandy."
2 CONT Gunnor apparently had children by Richard before they were married and 
2 CONT before
2 CONT his marriage to Emma. Evidently the Richard-Gunnor union was legitimized 
2 CONT later.
2 CONT RC 166 says Gunnor's father was Herbastus de Crepon, Forester of Arques 
2 CONT (in
2 CONT Denmark). Were there two foresters, the father of Gunnor and Sainfrida 
2 CONT and also
2 CONT the husband of Sainfrida? Or did the story become tangled over the years?
2 CONT Coe spells name Gunore.
2 CONT Davis: Gonnor, daughter of a forester of Sauqueville in Britanny. Second
2 CONT wife of Richard I. She married (2) Eperleng, "farmer"of the mills of 
2 CONT Pitres.
