2 CONT The Henry Project: Richard I of Normandy
2 CONT
2 CONT --------------------
2 CONT
2 CONT Richard I "the Fearless" of Normandy (3° D. Normandy)
2 CONT
2 CONT Born: 28 Aug 933, Fecamp, Normandy, France
2 CONT
2 CONT Acceded: 942
2 CONT
2 CONT Died: 20 Nov 996, Fecamp, Normandy
2 CONT
2 CONT Buried: Fecamp, Seine-Inferieure, France
2 CONT
2 CONT Notes: The line to the dukes of Normandy comes through Isabel St. Liz, and the line to Charlemagne comes through her husband, William Mauduit. The lines merge again with the marriage of Richard I, Duke of Normandy, and Emma, daugh
2 CONC ter of Hugh, who was -in all but name- King of France. His son, Hugh Capet, later assumed the title, and primogeniture began in the French line of kings.
2 CONT
2 CONT The two lines met again later with the marriage of Adele, daughter of King Robert II, and Richard III, Duke of Normandy. Richard I, "the Fearless"; named father's heir 29 May 942. 
2 CONT
2 CONT Married first (Danish wife) Gunnora but betrothed ca. 945 and eventually married 960 to Emma. 
2 CONT
2 CONT Richard was betrothed to Emma for some time but did not marry her until about 960, after the death of her father, Hugh the Great, in 956. Richard was the guardian of Hugh's son, the Duke of Paris, and eventually married Emma to st
2 CONC rengthen his position. He did not treat her unkindly, he merely loved Gunnora. Poor Emma passed her life at Rouen alone and solitary, and eventually she pined away and died about the year 962. After Emma's death he married (Christ
2 CONC ian marriage) Gunnora to legitimize their children.
2 CONT
2 CONT Father: William I "Longsword" of Normandy (2º Duke of Normandy)
2 CONT
2 CONT Mother: Adele (Sprota) of Bretagne
2 CONT
2 CONT Married 1: Emma (Agnes) CAPET of France 960/962, France
2 CONT
2 CONT Associated with: Gunnora De CREPON (D. of Normandy)
2 CONT
2 CONT Children:
2 CONT
2 CONT 1. Richard II "the Good" of Normandy (4º D. Normandy)
2 CONT
2 CONT 2. Robert of Normandy (Archbishop 1º Count d' Evreux)
2 CONT
2 CONT 3. Maud of Normandy (Countess of Blois)
2 CONT
2 CONT 4. Beatrice of Normandy Viscountess
2 CONT
2 CONT 5. Emma of Normandy (Queen of England)
2 CONT
2 CONT 6. Geoffrey De BRIONNE (1º Count of Brionne)
2 CONT
2 CONT 7. Mauger De Mortain (Comte De Corbeil)
2 CONT
2 CONT 8. William HIESMES (1º Count of Eu)
2 CONT
2 CONT 9. Hawise of Normandy (Duchess of Brittany)
2 CONT
2 CONT Associated with:?
2 CONT
2 CONT Children:
2 CONT
2 CONT 10. Hawise of Normandy
2 CONT
2 CONT Associated with: Papia d'Envermeu
2 CONT
2 CONT Children:
2 CONT
2 CONT 11. Papia of Normandy
2 CONT
2 CONT Associated with: ?
2 CONT
2 CONT Children:
2 CONT
2 CONT 12. William of Normandy (b. 980 - d. 1015)
2 CONT
2 CONT 13. Sprota of Normandy
2 CONT
2 CONT Associated with:
2 CONT
2 CONT Children:
2 CONT
2 CONT 14. Muriella of Normandy
2 CONT
2 CONT 15. Fredesende of Normandy (b. 995 - d. 1057)
2 CONT
2 CONT --------------------
2 CONT
2 CONT Richard I or the fearless as he became known, married a French princess but maintained a mistress on the side. She was known as Gunnor. Gunnor bore all of Richard's children. Gunnor was from an important Danish family and eventual
2 CONC ly married him on the princess's death. This meeting with Gunnor is steeped in French folklore. When Richard was out hunting, he stayed on the property of one of his subjects. It was normal in that period for the husband to offer 
2 CONC his wife for the lords comfort. His quick thinking wife introduced her sister Gunnor to Richard. They immediately fell in love and were soon meeting on a regular basis. From this liaison came all Richard's children. How many child
2 CONC ren there were is uncertain but at least four are known.
2 CONT
2 CONT 3rd Duke of Normandy, b. 933 Fecamp, France, (age 10 when father died), d. 20 November 966. 
2 CONT
2 CONT --------------------
2 CONT
2 CONT Titles: comes Rothomagensium, and from 966 Marquis des Normands/marchio Normannorum
2 CONT
2 CONT --------------------
2 CONT
2 CONT Notes: The line to the dukes of Normandy comes through Isabel St. Liz, and the line to Charlemagne comes through her husband, William Mauduit. The lines merge again with the marriage of Richard I, Duke of Normandy, and Emma, daugh
2 CONC ter of Hugh, who was -in all but name- King of France. His son, Hugh Capet, later assumed the title, and primogeniture began in the French line of kings. 
2 CONT
2 CONT The two lines met again later with the marriage of Adele, daughter of King Robert II, and Richard III, Duke of Normandy. Richard I, "the Fearless"; named father's heir 29 May 942. Married first (Danish wife) Gunnora but betrothed 
2 CONC ca. 945 and eventually married 960 to Emma. Richard was betrothed to Emma for some time but did not marry her until about 960, after the death of her father, Hugh the Great, in 956. Richard was the guardian of Hugh's son, the Duke
2 CONC  of Paris, and eventually married Emma to strengthen his position. He did not treat her unkindly, he merely loved Gunnora. Poor Emma passed her life at Rouen alone and solitary, and eventually she pined away and died about the yea
2 CONC r 962. After Emma's death he married (Christian marriage) Gunnora to legitimize their children.
2 CONT
