1 NOTE Possiveis Discrepancias:
2 CONT Na Wikipédia a menção a um Ricardo I da Normandia que teria sido duque, e não conde. Ele teria se casado com um plebéia (e não princesa)  de nome Gunora (possível curruptela de Gunnor) e tido Ricardo II, Roberto II, Mauger, Robert
2 CONC  Danus, Ema e Maud. A data de nascimento, 933, é compativel com o período em que pode ter se dado o nascimento desse Ricardo da Normandia.
2 CONT
2 CONT Os nomes dos filhos não batem, e foi encontrada uma 2a referëncia a existëncia de um Ricardo I que foi conde e se casou com a princesa Gunnor, mas os nomes dos pais de ambos os Ricardos é IDENTICO (Guilherme, conde para os sites d
2 CONC e genealogia, Duque para a Wikipédia, e Sprota), optei pela versão da wikipédia tanto para o título como para a origem da esposa.
1 NOTE --Other Fields
2 CONT
2 CONT Ref Number: 230
1 NOTE _P_CCINFO 1-20792
2 CONT According to Stuart--Royalty for Commoners 1-3 & Weis Ancestral Roots 4-10
2 CONT
2 CONT Richard I "the Fearless" Duke of Normandy
2 CONT
2 CONT Sources: RC 24, 89, 166, 168, 222; Coe; AF; Kings and Queens ofBritain; Norr (pages 46, 60); The Dukes of Normandy by Onslow; Butler; Pfafman; A. Roots 1-19, 39, 121E; Kraentzler 1153, 1156, 1174, 1176, 1180, 1194,1211, 1218, 1265
2 CONC , 1432, 1443; Davis; Magna Charta Sureties 157-1.
2 CONT Roots: Richard I, "the Fearless," b. Fecamp, ca. 933; named father'sheir 29 May 942. Married first (Danish wife) Gunnor but betrothed ca. 945 and eventually married 960 to Emma. After Emma's death he married (Christian marriage) G
2 CONC unnor to legitimize their children.
2 CONT Sureties: Richard I, the Fearless, Duke of Normandy.
2 CONT Richard "sans Peur," Third Duke of Normandy, 942-996.
2 CONT The line to the dukes of Normandy comes through Isabel St. Liz, andthe line to Charlemagne comes through her husband, William Mauduit. The linesmerge again with the marriage of Richard I, Duke of Normandy, and Emma,daughter of Hug
2 CONC h "The Grand," who was--in all but name--King of France. His son, Hugh Capet, later assumed the title, and primogeniture began in the Frenchline of kings.
2 CONT The two lines met again later with the marriage of Adele, daughter ofKing Robert II, and Richard III, Duke of Normandy.
2 CONT Richard was betrothed to Emma for some time but did not marry heruntil about 960, after the death of her father, Hugh the Great, in 956. Richardwas the guardian of Hugh's son, the Duke of Paris, and eventually marriedEmma to stren
2 CONC gthen his position. He did not treat her unkindly, he merely lovedGunnor.
2 CONT "Poor Emma passed her life at Rouen alone and solitary, and eventuallyshe pined away and died about the year 962," Onslow says.
2 CONT
2 CONT Davis: Richard I, the Fearless, Duke of Normandy from 942-996.
2 CONT Norr: Richard I, the Fearless (san Peur), born about 933, 3rd duke.Married (1) Agnes, daughter of Hugh le Grand and had issue. Married (2) Gunora,born about 952, sister of a forester's wife whom Richard desired but whotricked him 
2 CONC with her younger sister.
2 CONT ***** Richard I, "the Fearless" (sans Peur), 3rd Duke of Normandy (942/3-996),son of William Longsword and Sprote de Bretagne.
2 CONT
2 CONT SOURCES:
2 CONT 1.  Stuart, Roderick W.  _Royalty for Commoners_.  2nd Edition.Baltimore,
2 CONT MD: Genealogical Publishing Company, Inc., 1992; line 166-33.  Onlysays
2 CONT that he was born about 933.  Died 20 Nov 996 at Fecamp.  Marriedafter
2 CONT 962, (1) Emma (Agnes), daughter of Hugh le Grand, Count of Paris.
2 CONT 2.  Taute, Anne.  "Kings and Queens of Great Britain" chart.  __Edition.
2 CONT Gives her date of death as 996.
2 CONT 3.  Norr, Vernon M.  _Some Early English Pedigrees_, page 60,generation 38.
2 CONT Gives his death date as 996.  This source states that he married(1)
2 CONT Agnes, daughter of Hugh le Grand; had issue by and later married(2),
2 CONT after Agnes' death, Gunora, born 952.
2 CONT 4.  Ancestral File (AFN:9HMD-VF).  Gives his birth date as 28 Aug 933.Death
2 CONT date agrees with that given in Stuart.
