1 NOTE [FAVthomas.FTW]
2 CONT
2 CONT    Byname Richard The Fearless, French Richard Sans Peur duke ofNormandie (942/996), son of William I Longsword.
2 CONT    Louis IV of France took the boy-duke into his protective custody,apparently intent upon
2 CONT reuniting Normandie to the crown's domains; but in 945 Louis was capturedby the Normans, and Richard was returned to his people. Richard withstoodfurther Carolingian attempts to subdue his duchy and, in 987, wasinstrumental in sec
2 CONC uring the French crown for his brother-in-law, theRobertian Hugh Capet.
2 CONT
2 CONT To cite this page: "Richard I" Encyclopædia Britannica
2 CONT <http://www.britannica.com/eb/article?eu=65173&tocid=0&query=richard%20i%2C%20the%20fearless>
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT Richard I, byname RICHARD THE FEARLESS, French RICHARD SANS PEUR (b. c.932--d. 996), Duc de Normandie (942-996), son of William I Longsword.
2 CONT
2 CONT Louis IV of France took the boy-duke into his protective custody,apparently intent upon reuniting Normandie to the crown's domains; but in945 Louis was captured by the Normans, and Richard was returned to hispeople. Richard withst
2 CONC ood further Carolingian attempts to subdue hisduchy and, in 987, was instrumental in securing the French crown for hisbrother-in-law, the Robertian Hugh Capet. [Encyclopaedia Britannica CD'97]
