1 NOTE {geni:about_me} '''Amaury I''' (?-after 973), Comte de la marche de Valenciennes.
2 CONT
2 CONT ''His parents are unknown or uncertain. He was not the same person as Amauri I de Montfort.''
2 CONT
2 CONT ----
2 CONT
2 CONT http://www.histoireeurope.fr/RechercheLocution.php?Locutions=de+Landas%0D%0A&Date1=&Date2=&maf=1
2 CONT
2 CONT Mariage d'Amaury Ier de Hainaut avec Judith de Cambrai
2 CONT Amaury Ier de Hainaut épouse vers 952 Judith de Cambrai.
2 CONT
2 CONT Leurs enfants sont :
2 CONT
2 CONT # Amaury de Landas (vers 940-après 985) qui épousera Judith de Cysoing,
2 CONT # Guillaume Ier de Montfort (mort en 1003),
2 CONT # Raoul de Valenciennes (avant 973-1055).
2 CONT
2 CONT == MedLands ==
2 CONT
2 CONT * http://fmg.ac/Projects/MedLands/HAINAUT.htm#Amaurydiedafter973
2 CONT
2 CONT AMAURY [I] (-after 12 Feb 973).  Comte [de Hainaut].  [Comte de la marche de Valenciennes].  The Gesta Episcoporum Cameracensium records that Foubert Bishop of Cambrai purported to dissolve the marriage between "filiam Isaac" and 
2 CONC "Amulricum comitem…ex pago Heinou" on grounds of consanguinity[162], dated to [953/56] because the preceding passage in the same source discusses the Hungarian invasion in 953 and because Bishop Foubert died in 956.  Emperor Otto 
2 CONC I donated property to the monastery at Crespin, at the request of "Richizonis atque Amelrici comitum", by charter dated 12 Feb 973[163].  If these two sources are correctly dated, Amaury was count in Hainaut for approximately 20 y
2 CONC ears from 953 to 973.  This period overlaps with the countships of the other known counts of Hainaut who are shown in Chapter 1 of this document.  This anomaly is discussed in the Introduction to this chapter.  It should be noted 
2 CONC that the extract from the Gesta Episcoporum Cameracensium which refers to Amaury's wife describes him as "comitem…ex pago Heinou" rather than "comitem Hainonensis". 
2 CONT
2 CONT m ([separated] [953/56]) '''--- de Cambrai''', daughter of ISAAC Comte de Cambrai & his wife ---.  The Gesta Episcoporum Cameracensium records that Foubert Bishop of Cambrai purported to dissolve the marriage between "filiam Isaac
2 CONC " and "Amulricum comitem…ex pago Heinou" on grounds of consanguinity[164], dated to [953/56] because the preceding passage in the same source discusses the Hungarian invasion in 953 and because Bishop Foubert died in 956.  No cont
2 CONC emporary Isaac has been identified other than the Comte de Cambrai, so it is assumed that he was the father of Amaury's wife.
2 CONT
2 CONT ----
2 CONT {{https://www.geni.com/media/proxy?media_id=6000000185703923865&size=large}}
2 CONT
2 CONT ----
2 CONT
