2 CONT
2 CONT ----
2 CONT
2 CONT ===Origins 
2 CONT
2 CONT https://fr.wikipedia.org/wiki/Liste_des_seigneurs_de_Broyes
2 CONT
2 CONT Renart de Nogent[2], (or Renard, Rainard, Renaud de Broyes), (before 960 - Rome around 999), lord around 980 of Broyes and other Champagne properties. His second wife is Héloïse de Pithiviers.
2 CONT
2 CONT Renart died in Rome during a pilgrimage around 997/998. His death is interpreted as a probable penance following the role he played in the conflict of 992-996[8] between King Hugues Capet and Eudes I of Blois. In his memory, his w
2 CONC idow will found, instead of the castle church, the Collegiate Saint-Georges in Pithiviers[1].
2 CONT
2 CONT Marriages and succession:
2 CONT
2 CONT *His first wife is unknown. He has from this first marriage:
2 CONT **Isembart[9] which follows,
2 CONT *He married in the second marriage in the mid-980s, Héloïse (or Alluise/Ayluise/Heloyse/Helvise/Helvide) of Pithiviers. He has[10] of this second marriage:
2 CONT **[https://www.geni.com/people/Oury-Bishop-of-Orleans/6000000002188271013 Oury] [11] (or Odry/Orri/Oldoric/Odalric), bishop of Orleans from 1022 to 1033, lord of Pithiviers,
2 CONT **'''Héloïse''', wife of Geoffroi II of Châteaudun and Ierdu Perche, † 1040.
2 CONT
2 CONT ----
2 CONT ===Family 
2 CONT
2 CONT https://www.francebalade.com/chartres/ctdunois.htm
2 CONT
2 CONT Geoffrey III (1023-1040) 
2 CONT
2 CONT Son of Geoffroy II, he became Vicomte de Chateaudun following his father, He was also Lord of Nogent in the Perche.
2 CONT
2 CONT He marries Helvise (Héloise) daughter of Foulques Comte de Mortagne (also called Corbon), they have children:
2 CONT
2 CONT # - Hugues Vicomte de Chateaudun in 1040,
2 CONT # - Rotrou first Lord of Nogent and Count of Mortagne then also Vicomte de Chateaudun following Hugues.
2 CONT
2 CONT Geoffroy had serious ties with the Evique Fulbert of Chartres and even went to war with him. He built two castles in Illiers and Gallardon which allowed him to control Chartres and Fulbert, after having vainly appealed to the Coun
2 CONC t of Blois and then to the King of France Robert II the Pious, was forced to pronounce a sentence of excommunication against Viscount Geoffrey. The latter eventually submitted and for his forgiveness founded the Church of the Holy
2 CONC  Sepulchre in Chateaudun in 1029. In 1031 he founded a Monastery dedicated to Saint Denis in the Bourg de Nogent and attached the Church of Saint Sepulchre to it.
2 CONT
2 CONT Geoffroy died in 1040 in Chartres following a riot by the inhabitants against him.
2 CONT
2 CONT ----
2 CONT
2 CONT {{https://www.geni.com/media/proxy?media_id=6000000223172672838&size=large}}
2 CONT
2 CONT >Source: https://www.academia.edu/39227545/Hugues_de_Beauvais_le_comte_palatin_de_lan_Mil. Page 6.
