2 CONT HUGUES [II] de Gournay (-[killed in battle Cardiff 1074]).  The Chronique Manuscrite de Normandie records that, after the death of Canute King of England in 1035, "le Conte Neel de Coustantin…le sire de Guerarville, le sire de Gou
2 CONC rnay" sailed from Harfleur to England with Edward Prince of England to claim the English throne[916].  Guillaume de Poitou records that "Hugonis Gornacensis" joined forces with "Roberti Aucensis comitis", dated to after 1053[917].
2 CONC   "…Hugo de Gornai…" witnessed the charter dated to [1060] under which Guillaume II Duke of Normandy granted "Brenerias" to the abbey of Bayeux[918].  The Chronique de Normandie, based on le Roman de Rou, names "Hue de Gournay sir
2 CONC e de Bray" and "le Conte Hue de Gournay" among those who took part in the conquest of England in 1066, the two similar names suggesting that they were father and son[919].  [The Histoire et Chronique de Normandie, printed in 1610 
2 CONC at Rouen, records that "Hue de Gournay et le comte d´Evreux" died in Normandy from wounds received in battle at Cardiff in 1074, fighting an invasion led by "Canut [roi] de Norvège"[920].  The account must be garbled as there was 
2 CONC no king named Canute in either Norway or Denmark at the time, nor has any record been found of a comte d´Evreux dying around that period.  The historical basis of the account is uncertain.]  
2 CONT
2 CONT References:
2 CONT
2 CONT [916] Chronique Manuscrite de Normandie, RHGF XI, p. 339. 
2 CONT
2 CONT [917] Gesta Willelmi ducis Normannorum et regis Anglorum a Willelmo Pictaviensi…archidiacono, p. 98. 
2 CONT
2 CONT [918] Delisle (1867), Pièces justificatives, 30, p. 33. 
2 CONT
2 CONT [919] Extrait de la Chronique de Normandie, RHGF XIII, p. 237. 
2 CONT
2 CONT [920] Gurney (1845), p. 41, quoting L´histoire et chronique de Normandie, p. 117b. 
2 CONT
2 CONT Hugh II de Gournay was said to be one of the Norman Barons who commanded at the Battle of Mortimer against the French in 1054.https://familytrees.genopro.com/azrael/3044567/DeGournay-HughII-I30949.htm
2 CONT
2 CONT Hugh II De Gournay
2 CONT Hugh II was born about 0995 in Gournay-en-Bray, Seine-Inferieure, Normandy, France.1   Hugh II's father was Renaud De Gournay and his mother was Alberada Wife Of Renaud De Gournay.  His paternal grandfather was Hugh I De Gournay. 
2 CONC  He was an only child.  He died about 1074.1 
