1 NOTE {geni:about_me} Unattributed basic information (at least it has sources):
2 CONT
2 CONT Adèle d'Anjou[1]
2 CONT
2 CONT b. circa 924
2 CONT
2 CONT Father, Foulques I "le Roux", comte d'Anjou 
2 CONT
2 CONT b. 870, 
2 CONT
2 CONT d. 942
2 CONT
2 CONT Mother, Roscille, dame de Loches 
2 CONT
2 CONT b. 874
2 CONT
2 CONT Adèle d'Anjou was born circa 924. She was the daughter of Foulques I "le Roux", comte d'Anjou and Roscille, dame de Loches. 
2 CONT
2 CONT Adèle d'Anjou married Gautier I, comte de Vexin, Valois, et Amiens, son of Raoul de Gouy and Eldegarde d' Amiens, before 944.
2 CONT
2 CONT Family
2 CONT
2 CONT Gautier I, comte de Vexin, Valois, et Amiens 
2 CONT
2 CONT b. circa 925, 
2 CONT
2 CONT d. between 992 and 998
2 CONT
2 CONT Children	
2 CONT
2 CONT 1. Gautier II "the White", comte de Vexin, Valois, et Amiens+ 
2 CONT
2 CONT b. c 944, 
2 CONT
2 CONT d. 1027[2]
2 CONT
2 CONT 2. Bishop of Soissons Guy de Vexin 
2 CONT
2 CONT b. 946?[2]
2 CONT
2 CONT 3. Geoffrey de Vexin+ 
2 CONT
2 CONT b. 950?[2]
2 CONT
2 CONT 4. Fulk de Vexin 
2 CONT
2 CONT b. 952?
2 CONT
2 CONT Citations
2 CONT
2 CONT 1. [S204] Roderick W. Stuart, RfC, 37-36, 109-36.
2 CONT
2 CONT 2. [S1073] Bernard S. Bachrach, Bachrach, pg. 264.
2 CONT
2 CONT --------------------
2 CONT
2 CONT From the Foundation for Medieval Genealogy page on Anjou:
2 CONT
2 CONT http://fmg.ac/Projects/MedLands/ANJOU,%20MAINE.htm#Ingelgerdied888A
2 CONT
2 CONT 1. FOULQUES ([888]-[Aug 941/942], bur Châteauneuf, église Saint-Martin). Comte de Nantes 908-919. Vicomte de Tours et d'Anjou.  
2 CONT
2 CONT He was installed as FOULQUES I "le Roux" Comte d'Anjou in 929 by Raoul King of France.  
2 CONT
2 CONT His lay abbacies are noted in the charter dated to [929/30] under which "Fulco Andecavorum comes abbas quoque Sancti Albini Sanctique Lizinii necnon et uxor mea Roscilla et filii mei Widdo ac Fulco" donated property to Saint-Aubin
2 CONC  d'Angers for the souls of "Ingelgerio genitore meo atque Ingelgerio filio meo necnon…Warnerio socro meo et uxore sua Tescenda"[46]. 
2 CONT
2 CONT m (before 5 Jul 905) ROSCILLE [de Loches], daughter of GARNIER Seigneur de Loches, Villentrasti et Haia & his wife Tescenda --- ([870]-). 
2 CONT
2 CONT Comte Foulques I & his wife had five children:
2 CONT
2 CONT a) INGELGER d'Anjou (-killed in battle [927]), killed fighting the Normans[52].
2 CONT
2 CONT b) GUY d'Anjou (-[970]). His father offered him as a hostage to the Normans in return for the release of Charles III "le Simple" King of the Franks in 922. 
2 CONT
2 CONT c)  FOULQUES d'Anjou ([920]-11 Nov 958), succeeded his father in 942 as FOULQUES II "le Bon" Comte d'Anjou. 
2 CONT
2 CONT d) ROSCILLE d'Anjou (-[943/51]) m (943) as his first wife, ALAIN II "le Barbetorte" Duke of Brittany, son of MATHEDOI [I] Comte de Poher & his wife --- de Bretagne (in Brittany [before 919]-952). 
2 CONT
2 CONT e) [ADELA d'Anjou .
2 CONT
2 CONT A list of members of the Cathedral of Paris lists (in order) "…Walterius comes, Adela comitissa…"[59].  
2 CONT
2 CONT According to Europäische Stammtafeln[60], Adela was the possible daughter of Foulques I Comte d'Anjou.  The primary source which confirms her origin has not yet been identified.  
2 CONT
2 CONT It is possible that it is speculative, based on one of her sons being named Foulques.  
2 CONT
2 CONT m as his second wife, GAUTHIER [I] Comte de Valois, d'Amiens et du Vexin, son of --- ([925]-987).]  
2 CONT
2 CONT References:
2 CONT
2 CONT [59] Obituaires de Sens Tome I.2, Eglise cathedrale de Paris, p. 1015. 
2 CONT
2 CONT [60] ES III 657. 
2 CONT
2 CONT ---
2 CONT
2 CONT From the Foundation for Medieval Genealogy page on Northern France:
2 CONT
2 CONT http://fmg.ac/Projects/MedLands/NORTHERN%20FRANCE.htm#GautierIValoisdied987
2 CONT
2 CONT GAUTHIER [I] ([before 925]-987), Comte d'Amiens, m secondly ADELA, daughter of ---.  
2 CONT
2 CONT A list of members of the Cathedral of Paris lists (in order) "…Walterius comes, Adela comitissa…"[11].  
2 CONT
2 CONT According to Europäische Stammtafeln[12], she was Adela d'Anjou, daughter of Foulques [I] "le Roux" Comte d'Anjou & his wife Roscilla [de Loches] (after 909-).  The primary source on which this is based has not yet been identified
2 CONC ; it is possible that it is speculative, based on one of her sons being named Foulques.  
2 CONT
2 CONT Comte Gauthier [I] & his [first/second] wife had five children: 
2 CONT
2 CONT a) GAUTHIER [II] "le Blanc" (-after 1017).  A charter of "Hugo…Francorum rex" confirming the privileges of the monastery of Corvey dated 987 is subscribed by "Walteri comitis Ambianensis ac filiorum eius Walteri, Gotfredi, Rodulfi
2 CONC "[13].  Comte d'Amiens et du Vexin. 
2 CONT
2 CONT b) RAOUL .  "Wauterii comitis, Walterii et Radulfi filiorum eius" subscribed a charter dated 975 under which "Hugo Francorum dux" restored the abbey of Saint-Jean to the abbey of Sainte-Croix d'Orléans[14].  A charter of "Hugo…Fra
2 CONC ncorum rex" confirming the privileges of the monastery of Corvey dated 987 is subscribed by "Walteri comitis Ambianensis ac filiorum eius Walteri, Gotfredi, Rodulfi"[15]. 
2 CONT
2 CONT c) GUY .  The primary source which confirms his parentage has not yet been identified. 
2 CONT
2 CONT d) GODEFROY .  A charter of "Hugo…Francorum rex" confirming the privileges of the monastery of Corvey dated 987 is subscribed by "Walteri comitis Ambianensis ac filiorum eius Walteri, Gotfredi, Rodulfi"[16]. 
2 CONT
2 CONT e) FOULQUES .  The primary source which confirms his parentage has not yet been identified. 
2 CONT
2 CONT References:
2 CONT
2 CONT [11] Obituaires de Sens Tome I.2, Eglise cathedrale de Paris, p. 1015. 
2 CONT
2 CONT [12] ES III 657. 
2 CONT
2 CONT [13] RHGF X, IV, p. 552. 
2 CONT
2 CONT [14] Sainte-Croix d'Orléans LXIII, p. 123. 
2 CONT
2 CONT [15] RHGF X, IV, p. 552. 
2 CONT
2 CONT [16] RHGF X, IV, p. 552. 
2 CONT --------------------
2 CONT Adèle married Cte Gautier I DE VEXIN Count of Valois & Amiens, son of Raoul II DE CAMBRAI and Hildegard DE FLANDRES Countess of Flanders. (Cte Gautier I DE VEXIN Count of Valois & Amiens was born in 919 in Vexin, Normandy, France 
2 CONC and died in 996.)
2 CONT
2 CONT Born: 925, Anjou/Pays-de-la-Loire, France
