1 NOTE {geni:about_me} Curator's Note (PW): There are two Gauthiers who may or may not be the same person:''' Gauthier Count of Amiens, Vexin & Valois''', and '''Gauthier Count of Dreux'''. 
2 CONT
2 CONT Gauthier Count of Amiens is generally believed to have been the son of [http://www.geni.com/people/Raoul-de-Gouy-comte-d-Ostrevent/6000000002187903890 '''Raoul de Cambrai -- Count of Valois and Vexin, Ostervant and Amiens'''] -- a
2 CONC nd '''Liegarde (de Meulan)'''
2 CONT
2 CONT Gauthier Count of Dreux's parentage is vague, with one source naming his parents as '''Waleran and Eldegardis'''. This may be [http://www.geni.com/people/Val%C3%A9ran-de-Tirel/6000000003827685590  Valéran de Tirel].
2 CONT
2 CONT Note that Liegarde, wife of Raoul de Cambrai, also married Waleran de Meulan as her second husband. One wonders if the document referring to Eldegardis and Waleran might be referring to Liegardis and Waleran, interchanging Eldegar
2 CONC dis/Liegardis.
2 CONT
2 CONT This profile is combining the two identities into one personnage.
2 CONT
2 CONT Notes from Charles Cawley's Medieval Lands Database discuss this dilemma http://fmg.ac/Projects/MedLands/NORTHERN%20FRANCE.htm
2 CONT
2 CONT '''GAUTHIER [I] d'Amiens''' ([before 925]-987).  
2 CONT
2 CONT Edouard de Saint-Phalle suggests that he was Gauthier, son of Raoul [I] Comte [d'Ostrevant][4].  This possible parentage is also shown in Europäische Stammtafeln[5].  The primary source which suggests that this might be the case h
2 CONC as not yet been identified.  
2 CONT
2 CONT Another possibility is that he was the same person as Gauthier Comte de Dreux.  The editor of the compilation of Chartres charters suggests that "Walterius…comitis Waleranni filius" (PW: Walter count [of Dreux], son of Waleran) in
2 CONC herited "comes Velcassinus" (Vexin) from his father, and "Ambianensis" (Amiens) from "matre autem Eldegarde" (acquiring Dreux from his wife's family)[6].  The primary sources on which this information is based have not yet been id
2 CONC entified.  
2 CONT
2 CONT However, two facts suggest that this hypothesis may be correct.  
2 CONT
2 CONT Firstly, Gauthier Comte de Dreux is also recorded with a wife named Eva (although the necrology entries quoted here and in PARIS REGION NOBILITY (Comtes de Dreux) suggest that there were two countesses of this name at the time).  
2 CONT
2 CONT Secondly, the castle of Mantes, occupied by the descendants of Gauthier Comte d'Amiens, was near Dreux.  
2 CONT
2 CONT "Wauterii comitis, Walterii et Radulfi filiorum eius" subscribed a charter dated 975 under which "Hugo Francorum dux" restored the abbey of Saint-Jean to the abbey of Sainte-Croix d'Orléans[7].  
2 CONT
2 CONT Comte d'Amiens.  
2 CONT
2 CONT A charter of "Hugo…Francorum rex" confirming the privileges of the monastery of Corvey dated 987 is subscribed by "Walteri comitis Ambianensis ac filiorum eius Walteri, Gotfredi, Rodulfi"[8].  
2 CONT
2 CONT The necrology of the abbey of Saint-Germain-des-Prés records the death "XIX Kal Feb" of "Gualterii comitis"[9].  
2 CONT
2 CONT m firstly EVA, daughter of --- (-[19 Jan or 23 Nov] <nowiki>----</nowiki>).  The necrology of the abbey of Sainte-Colombe records the death "XIV Kal Feb" of "Eve comitisse"[10].  
2 CONT
2 CONT m secondly ADELA, daughter of ---.  A list of members of the Cathedral of Paris lists (in order) "…Walterius comes, Adela comitissa…"[11].  According to Europäische Stammtafeln[12], she was Adela d'Anjou, daughter of Foulques [I] 
2 CONC "le Roux" Comte d'Anjou & his wife Roscilla [de Loches] (after 909-).  The primary source on which this is based has not yet been identified; it is possible that it is speculative, based on one of her sons being named Foulques.  
2 CONT
2 CONT Comte Gauthier [I] & his [first/second] wife had five children: 
2 CONT
2 CONT a)         GAUTHIER [II] "le Blanc" (-after 1017).  A charter of "Hugo…Francorum rex" confirming the privileges of the monastery of Corvey dated 987 is subscribed by "Walteri comitis Ambianensis ac filiorum eius Walteri, Gotfredi,
2 CONC  Rodulfi"[13].  Comte d'Amiens et du Vexin. 
2 CONT
2 CONT -        see below. 
2 CONT
2 CONT b)         RAOUL .  "Wauterii comitis, Walterii et Radulfi filiorum eius" subscribed a charter dated 975 under which "Hugo Francorum dux" restored the abbey of Saint-Jean to the abbey of Sainte-Croix d'Orléans[14].  A charter of "
2 CONC Hugo…Francorum rex" confirming the privileges of the monastery of Corvey dated 987 is subscribed by "Walteri comitis Ambianensis ac filiorum eius Walteri, Gotfredi, Rodulfi"[15]. 
2 CONT
2 CONT c)         GUY .  The primary source which confirms his parentage has not yet been identified. 
2 CONT
2 CONT d)         GODEFROY .  A charter of "Hugo…Francorum rex" confirming the privileges of the monastery of Corvey dated 987 is subscribed by "Walteri comitis Ambianensis ac filiorum eius Walteri, Gotfredi, Rodulfi"[16]. 
2 CONT
2 CONT e)         FOULQUES .  The primary source which confirms his parentage has not yet been identified. 
2 CONT
2 CONT Sources
2 CONT
