2 CONT
2 CONT Also, there is a strong likelihood that he was the same as Gauthier Comte de Dreux; see http://fmg.ac/Projects/MedLands/PARIS%20REGION%20NOBILITY.htm#_Toc257353336:
2 CONT
2 CONT WALERAN .  m ELDEGARDIS, daughter of ---.  "Eldegardis" donated property "de prædiorum meorum possessionibus hereditariam…Guntherii villa" (Gondreville) to "Sancti Petri Carnotensis", for the soul of "senioris mei Valeranni", and 
2 CONC with the agreement of "Walterio comite filio meo", by charter dated to before 967, subscribed by "Hugonis ducis, Walterii comitis"[1101].  Waleran & his wife had one child: 
2 CONT
2 CONT a)         '''GAUTHIER''' (-14 Jan, after 965).  
2 CONT
2 CONT "Eldegardis" donated property "de prædiorum meorum possessionibus hereditariam…Guntherii villa" (Gondreville) to "Sancti Petri Carnotensis", for the soul of "senioris mei Valeranni", and with the agreement of "Walterio comite fili
2 CONC o meo", by charter dated to before 967, subscribed by "Hugonis ducis, Walterii comitis"[1102].  
2 CONT
2 CONT Comte de Dreux.  
2 CONT
2 CONT "Walterius, comes Dorcassini comitatus" donated property "ecclesiam…sancti Georgii" to "monasterio Sancti Petri Carnotensis", for the soul of "prædecessoris mei Landrici comitis", by charter dated 965, subscribed by "…Richardi duc
2 CONC is…"[1103].  The editor of the compilation of these charters suggests that "Walterius…comitis Waleranni filius" inherited "comes Velcassinus" from his father, and "Ambianensis" from "matre autem Eldegarde"[1104].  
2 CONT
2 CONT The primary sources on which this information is based have not yet been identified.  It is therefore possible that Gauthier was the same person as Gauthier Comte d'Amiens.  Two facts suggest that this hypothesis may be correct.  
2 CONT
2 CONT Firstly, Gauthier Comte d'Amiens is also recorded with a wife named Eva (although the necrology entries quoted here and in the document NORTHERN FRANCE (Comtes de Valois et d'Amiens) suggest that there were two countesses of that 
2 CONC name at the time).  
2 CONT
2 CONT Secondly, the descendants of Gauthier Comte d'Amiens are recorded as counts at Mantes, which is near Dreux.  
2 CONT
2 CONT "Comes Walterius" donated property to "Sancti Petri Carnotensis" with the consent of "uxoris meæ Evæ", by undated charter at Dreux[1105].  
2 CONT
2 CONT The necrology of Chartres Cathedral records the death "XIX Kal Feb" of "Walterius comes" and his donation of "alodos suos…in pago Dorcasino et Carnoto"[1106].  
2 CONT
2 CONT The necrology of the abbey of Saint-Père-en-Vallée records the death "XIX Kal Feb" of "Gualterius comes Dorcassini castri qui dedit Sancto Petro ecclesiam Roheris"[1107] (it is assumed that "ecclesiam Roheris" is the same as "eccl
2 CONC esiam…sancti Georgii" which Gauthier donated under the first charter quoted above).  
2 CONT
2 CONT m EVA, daughter of --- (-23 Nov <nowiki>----</nowiki>).  "Comes Walterius" donated property to "Sancti Petri Carnotensis" with the consent of "uxoris meæ Evæ", by undated charter at Dreux[1108].  As noted above, the editor of the 
2 CONC compilation of Chartres charters suggests that "Landricus…comes Dorcassinus" was father of "Evæ, Walterii I uxoris" and that Gauthier inherited the county of Dreux from his father-in-law[1109].  The primary source on which this is
2 CONC  based has not yet been identified.  The necrology of the abbey of Saint-Père-en-Vallée records the death "IX Kal Dec" of "Eva comitissa"[1110].  The necrology of the abbey of Saint-Germain-des-Prés records the death "IX Kal Dec" 
2 CONC of "Æva comitissa"[1111]. 
2 CONT -----------------------
2 CONT
2 CONT From http://www.rpi.edu/~holmes/Hobbies/Genealogy/ps04/ps04_230.htm
2 CONT
2 CONT "Ancestral Roots..." (Balt., 1992) 250-18 gives him as "Walter I, Count of Aiens, Valois and the Vexin, d. 992/998; m. Adele, dau., perh. of Fulk I, Count of Anjou....Walter I was son of Ralph, Count of Valois", either the one sho
2 CONC wn here as his father or a son of this Ralph. 
2 CONT
2 CONT References: [AR7],[RFC],[RoyalAAF]
