2 CONT     * Born: 919, Vexin, Normandy, France
2 CONT     * Died: 996 http://www.celtic-casimir.com/webtree/3/6102.htm
2 CONT --------------------
2 CONT There are two Gauthiers who may or may not be the same person: Gauthier Count of Amiens, Vexin & Valois, and Gauthier Count of Dreux.
2 CONT
2 CONT Gauthier Count of Amiens is believed to have been the son of Raoul de Cambrai -- Count of Valois and Vexin, Ostervant and Amiens -- and Liegarde (de Meulan)
2 CONT
2 CONT Liegarde, wife of Raoul de Cambrai, also married Waleran de Meulan as her second husband.
2 CONT
2 CONT Gauthier Count of Dreux's parentage is vague, with one source naming his parents as Waleran and Eldegardis. It is believed that Eldegardis and Waleran might be referring to Liegardis and Waleran, interchanging Eldegardis/Liegardis
2 CONC . 
2 CONT
2 CONT The reason of naming them as his parents would likely be because Raoul de Cambrai died in 926 AD at the age of 53 in Valois,Oise,Picardy,France. Gauthier at the time of his fathers death would have been seven. 
2 CONT
2 CONT This profile is combining the two identities into one personnage.
2 CONT --------------------
2 CONT Curator's Note (PW): There are two Gauthiers who may or may not be the same person: Gauthier Count of Amiens, Vexin & Valois, and Gauthier Count of Dreux.
2 CONT
2 CONT Gauthier Count of Amiens is generally believed to have been the son of Raoul de Cambrai -- Count of Valois and Vexin, Ostervant and Amiens -- and Liegarde (de Meulan)
2 CONT
2 CONT Gauthier Count of Dreux's parentage is vague, with one source naming his parents as Waleran and Eldegardis.
2 CONT
2 CONT Note that Liegarde, wife of Raoul de Cambrai, also married Waleran de Meulan as her second husband. One wonders if the document referring to Eldegardis and Waleran might be referring to Liegardis and Waleran, interchanging Eldegar
2 CONC dis/Liegardis.
2 CONT
2 CONT This profile is combining the two identities into one personnage.
2 CONT
2 CONT Notes from Charles Cawley's Medieval Lands Database discuss this dilemma http://fmg.ac/Projects/MedLands/NORTHERN%20FRANCE.htm
2 CONT
2 CONT GAUTHIER [I] d'Amiens ([before 925]-987).
2 CONT
2 CONT Edouard de Saint-Phalle suggests that he was Gauthier, son of Raoul [I] Comte [d'Ostrevant][4]. This possible parentage is also shown in Europäische Stammtafeln[5]. The primary source which suggests that this might be the case has
2 CONC  not yet been identified.
2 CONT
2 CONT Another possibility is that he was the same person as Gauthier Comte de Dreux. The editor of the compilation of Chartres charters suggests that "Walterius…comitis Waleranni filius" (PW: Walter count [of Dreux], son of Waleran) inh
2 CONC erited "comes Velcassinus" (Vexin) from his father, and "Ambianensis" (Amiens) from "matre autem Eldegarde" (acquiring Dreux from his wife's family)[6]. The primary sources on which this information is based have not yet been iden
2 CONC tified.
2 CONT
2 CONT However, two facts suggest that this hypothesis may be correct.
2 CONT
2 CONT Firstly, Gauthier Comte de Dreux is also recorded with a wife named Eva (although the necrology entries quoted here and in PARIS REGION NOBILITY (Comtes de Dreux) suggest that there were two countesses of this name at the time).
2 CONT
2 CONT Secondly, the castle of Mantes, occupied by the descendants of Gauthier Comte d'Amiens, was near Dreux.
2 CONT
2 CONT "Wauterii comitis, Walterii et Radulfi filiorum eius" subscribed a charter dated 975 under which "Hugo Francorum dux" restored the abbey of Saint-Jean to the abbey of Sainte-Croix d'Orléans[7].
2 CONT
2 CONT Comte d'Amiens.
2 CONT
2 CONT A charter of "Hugo…Francorum rex" confirming the privileges of the monastery of Corvey dated 987 is subscribed by "Walteri comitis Ambianensis ac filiorum eius Walteri, Gotfredi, Rodulfi"[8].
2 CONT
2 CONT The necrology of the abbey of Saint-Germain-des-Prés records the death "XIX Kal Feb" of "Gualterii comitis"[9].
2 CONT
