1 NOTE {geni:about_me} https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Gerberge_of_Lorraine
2 CONT
2 CONT Not to be confused with https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Gerberga_of_Lorraine
2 CONT
2 CONT '''Gerberge of Lorraine''' (c. 935-978) was the daughter of Giselbert, Duke of Lorraine,[1] and Gerberga of Saxony,[2] daughter of Henry I the Fowler, King of Germany. She was a descendant of Charlemagne through both her parents.[
2 CONC 1][2] Gerberge died sometime after 7 September 978.[1]
2 CONT
2 CONT In or before 954, she married Adalbert I of Vermandois.[1] 
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT ===Family
2 CONT https://www.wikitree.com/wiki/Vermandois-196
2 CONT
2 CONT Issue
2 CONT
2 CONT Adalbert and Gerberge had these children. Heribert was presumably the eldest son. Not much is known about any other offspring. Bishop Liudolf seems to be accepted, on little evidence. [https://www.geni.com/people/Gisele-de-Vermand
2 CONC ois/6000000002666077567?through=6000000002466110291 '''Gisele] is presumably spurious, like her aunts.'''
2 CONT
2 CONT Guy de Soissons is provisionally placed by MedLands in the previous generation, as Adalbert's brother, citing several explicit records, but there seem to be possible difficulties with dates. French Wikipedia shows neither placing.
2 CONT
2 CONT # Heribert IV (954 - 29 Aug 993) [8]
2 CONT # Otto (950/5 - after 02 Nov 958/9). [8][11] He was thought to be Comte de Chiny (unproven). [12][11]
2 CONT # Liudolf, Bishop of Noyon (957 - ante 09 Nov 986) [8]
2 CONT # Eleonore [8]
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT ----
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT MEDIEVAL LANDS
2 CONT
2 CONT ADALBERT [Albert] [I], son of HERIBERT [II] Comte de Vermandois & his wife Adela [Capet] (-8 Sep 987).  Flodoard names "Adalbertus filius Heriberti"[1327].  Under the division of territories organised after his father's death in 9
2 CONC 43, he became Comte de Vermandois.  Comte Albert re-established the abbey of Homblières and built Mont-Saint-Quentin[1328].  When his brother Hugues was deposed as archbishop of Reims in 948, Comte Albert gave up the family's stru
2 CONC ggle with Louis IV "d'Outremer" King of France and swore allegiance to the king.  He opposed the election of Hugues Capet as king of France, but eventually submitted[1329]. 
2 CONT
2 CONT [m firstly HERESINDE, daughter of ---.  According to the Histoire de Guise, Comte Albert constructed the abbey of Saint-Michel at Rochefort in 945 "d'accord avec la comtesse Hérésinde sa femme", while in 947 Hérésinde founded the 
2 CONC nearby Benedictine convent of Bucilly[1330].  The source assumes that this refers to Albert Comte de Vermandois, but his supposed first marriage is not mentioned by Settipani[1331].  According to the introduction to the Cartulaire
2 CONC  de l'abbaye de Bucilly, Bucilly was founded by "Gerberge, femme d'Albert I Comte de Vermandois" although it notes that "certains auteurs ont voulu faire remonter [sa foundation] à la libéralité de Hersinde femme d'Herbert Comte d
2 CONC e Vermandois morte en 901"[1332].  The Cartulaire reproduces a French translation of a declaration by Barthélemy Bishop of Laon dated 1120 entitled "Privilegium de domino Elberto, Viromandensi comite" according to which the bishop
2 CONC  declares that he has read the original charter under which "Elbert comte de Vermandois…et sa femme Gertrude [error for Gerberge]" founded Bucilly[1333].  Further research in the original charter documentation is needed to clarify
2 CONC  this confusion, not the least of which is that, even if Hérésinde was not the wife of Comte Albert, no other reference has been found to her being the wife of Comte Héribert [I] (see above).] 
2 CONT
2 CONT m [secondly] ([949/54]) GERBERGA, daughter of GISELBERT Duke of Lotharingia & his wife Gerberga of Germany ([935]-after 7 Sep 978).  Settipani names her as the wife of Comte Albert, and gives her parentage, but does not cite the p
2 CONC rimary source on which this is based.  A list of members of the Cathedral of Paris lists (in order) "Albertus comes, Girberga comitissa, Harbertus, Otto, Lewultus, Girbertus, Gondrada, Ricardus, Harbertus comes…", the first four i
2 CONC ndividuals named apparently being Comte Albert, his wife and three sons, and the last named maybe his brother or nephew[1334].  The primary source which confirms her parentage and marriage more precisely has not yet been identifie
2 CONC d. 
2 CONT
2 CONT Comte Albert & his [second] wife had [four] children: 
2 CONT
2 CONT 1.         HERIBERT [IV] ([954]-29 Aug [993]).  A list of members of the Cathedral of Paris lists (in order) "Albertus comes, Girberga comitissa, Harbertus, Otto, Lewultus, Girbertus, Gondrada, Ricardus, Harbertus comes…", the fir
2 CONC st four individuals named apparently being Comte Albert, his wife and three sons, and the last named maybe his brother or nephew[1335].  Héribert [IV] succeeded his father in 987 as Comte de Vermandois.  
2 CONT
2 CONT m (before [982/86]) [as her first husband,] ERMENGARDIS, daughter of ---.  "Comes Heribertus" names "materque mea Pavia…pater meus Otto, eius genitrix, avia mea Ermengardis" donated property to Notre-Dame de Homblières by charter 
2 CONC dated [13 Jan/13 Oct] 1045[1336].  According to Ernest Petit[1337], Ermengardis was the widow of Milo [IV] Comte de Tonnerre.  The author highlights a charter of Ermengardis Ctss de Vermandois witnessed by Renaud Comte de Tonnerre
2 CONC .  He suggests that Comte Renaud would only have done this if he were the son of Ermengardis, although other explanations must be possible.  Settipani points out[1338] that Ermengardis is named as the wife of Héribert [IV] in a do
2 CONC cument of her father-in-law Albert [I] Comte de Vermandois, relating to the abbey of Homblières, dated some time between 982 and the death of Comte Albert (in 987).  If the two marriages apply to the same Ermengardis, Comte Héribe
2 CONC rt must have been her first husband and Comte Milon her second.  However, it is not clear that this suggested co-identity is correct, a simpler explanation being that there were two different individuals named Ermengardis.  Ernest
2 CONC  Petit also suggests[1339] that Ermengardis (wife of Comte Milon) was heiress of Bar-sur-Seine, in order to explain how her granddaughter by Comte Milon, Eustachie, transmitted this county to her husband Gauthier de Brienne.  He i
2 CONC dentified the father of Ermengardis as "Renaud Comte de Bar-sur-Seine" based on two charters, which he dated to 992 and 997, which name "Rainardus comes" whom he identifies with Rainard, son of miles Raoul de Bar, who is mentioned
2 CONC  in the Chronicle of St Bénigne[1340].  There appears to be no other evidence of the existence of this person, and Bouchard[1341] points out that the dating of the two charters in question is uncertain.  She suggests that it is mo
2 CONC re likely that "Rainardus" is identified with Renaud Comte de Sens or with "Rainaldus" son of Ermengardis.  This of course leaves open the question how Bar-sur-Seine was transmitted to the Tonnerre family.  Comte Heribert [IV] & h
2 CONC is wife had two children:
2 CONT
2 CONT a)         ALBERT [II] ([985/90]-[1 Feb 1015/1017]).  The Gesta Episcoporum Cameracensium names "Alberto Vermandensi comiti, fratri Ottonis"[1342].  He succeeded his father in [1000] as Comte de Vermandois.  He abdicated before 15
2 CONC  Jul 1010[1343]. 
2 CONT
2 CONT b)         EUDES [Otto] ([985/90]-25 May 1045).  He succeeded in [1021] as Comte de Vermandois.   
2 CONT
2 CONT -        see below. 
2 CONT
2 CONT 2.         OTTO ([950/55]-after 2 Nov [958/59]).  "Ottonem, Alberti Vermandensium comitis filium" is named in the Gesta Episcoporum Cameracensium[1344].  A list of members of the Cathedral of Paris lists (in order) "Albertus comes
2 CONC , Girberga comitissa, Harbertus, Otto, Lewultus, Girbertus, Gondrada, Ricardus, Harbertus comes…", the first four individuals named apparently being Comte Albert, his wife and three sons, and the last named maybe his brother or ne
2 CONC phew[1345].  Otto is named with his parents in a charter of Comte Adalbert dated 2 Nov [958/59][1346].  same person as…?  OTTO (-[986/87] or after).  There appears to be no direct proof that Otto, ancestor of the Comtes de Chiny, 
2 CONC was the same person as Otto, son of Adalbert Comte de Vermandois.  The Historia Monasterii Mosomense records that "Ottonem comitem" built "castellum…Warcus" (Warcq, Ardennes) in 971, and suggests his affiliation when, in a later p
2 CONC assage, it clarifies that "superius dictus Ottho erat comes, Otthonum…Romanorum imperatorum…germanissima progenies"[1347].  The editor of the MGH SS edition of the Historia identifies Otto with the son of Adalbert Comte de Vermand
2 CONC ois and Gerberge, daughter of Emperor Otto I's sister[1348].  A subsequent passage of the Historia dates the foundation of the monastery to 24 Jul 971[1349], implying that the events recorded earlier in the text predated this foun
2 CONC dation.  If this is correct, 971 seems early for Otto de Vermandois to have constructed Warcq in light of his estimated birth date (which appears reasonably robust).  Gerbert, in a letter dated to Oct 986, records that "dux Cono p
2 CONC ro suo Ottone insidias molitur"[1350].  In the same letter, he also records that "Laudunensis episcopus" left "Dordingum" (Dourdon?) on the advice of "Ottonis et Heriberti" in support of "ducem" (which appears to refer to Hugues C
2 CONC apet).  Settipani suggests that "Otto" in this text refers to the holder of Warcq[1351].  However, all other passages in Gerbert's letters which name "Ottonis et Heriberti" (in that order) appear to refer to Eudes I Comte de Blois
2 CONC  and his first cousin Héribert [V] Comte de Troyes.  It is unclear from the full text of this letter whether "Ottone" and "Ottonis" relate to the same person.  "Dux Cono" has not been identified, although it may refer to Konrad I 
2 CONC Duke of Swabia.  If this is correct, it is possible that the first "Ottone" is a different person from the second "Ottonis" as there is no other passage which links the Blois count to the Swabian duke.  Settipani states that Otto 
2 CONC died "between 986 and 987", without specifying the basis for this speculation[1352]. 
2 CONT
2 CONT -        COMTES de CHINY. 
2 CONT
2 CONT 3.         LIUDOLF ([957]-before 9 Nov 986).  A list of members of the Cathedral of Paris lists (in order) "Albertus comes, Girberga comitissa, Harbertus, Otto, Lewultus, Girbertus, Gondrada, Ricardus, Harbertus comes…", the first
2 CONC  four individuals named apparently being Comte Albert, his wife and three sons, and the last named maybe his brother or nephew[1353].  Appointed Bishop of Noyon 978, consecrated 979. 
2 CONT
2 CONT 4.         [ELEONORE .  According to the Histoire de Guise, "Gauthier de Saint-Aubert avait épousé vers 986 une sœur du comte de Vermandois…Eleonore", the author speculating on the possibility of a relationship between Gauthier de
2 CONC  Saint-Aubert and the later Seigneurs de Guise[1354].  No other reference has been found to this couple.  
2 CONT
2 CONT m ([986]) GAUTHIER de Saint-Aubert, son of ---.]  
2 CONT
