2 CONT
2 CONT --------------------
2 CONT
2 CONT Eric the Victorious (VI), Old Norse: Eiríkr inn sigrsæli, Modern Swedish: Erik Segersäll, (945?- c 995), was the first Swedish king (970-995) about whom anything definite is known.
2 CONT
2 CONT His original territory lay in Uppland and neighbouring provinces. He was victorious over an invasion from the south in the Battle of the Fýrisvellir close to Uppsala. Reports that Eric's brother Olof was the father of Styrbjörn th
2 CONC e Strong belong to the realm of myth.
2 CONT
2 CONT The extent of his kingdom is unknown. In addition to the Swedish heartland round lake Mälaren it may have extended down the Baltic Sea coast as far south as Blekinge.
2 CONT
2 CONT According to the Flateyjarbok, his success was due to the fact that he allied with the peasants against the nobility, and it is obvious from archeological findings that the influence of the latter diminished during the last part o
2 CONC f the tenth century.[4] He was also, probably, the introducer of the famous medieval Scandinavian system of universal conscription known as the ledung in the provinces around Mälaren.
2 CONT
2 CONT According to Adam of Bremen, Eric allied himself with the Polish prince Boleslav to conquer Denmark and chase away its king Sweyn Forkbeard. He proclaimed himself the king of Sweden and Denmark which he ruled until his death which
2 CONC  would have taken place in 994 or 995.[citation needed] Adam says that Eric was baptised in Denmark, but later returned to the Norse gods. Adam of Bremen gives Emund Eriksson as Eric's predecessor.
2 CONT
2 CONT In all probability he founded the town of Sigtuna, which still exists and where the first Swedish coins were stamped for his son and successor Olof Skötkonung.
2 CONT
2 CONT --------------------
2 CONT
2 CONT Erik Segersäll är den förste kung som man kan vara helt säker på att han verkligen har existerat. De källor som berättar om vad han uträttade som kung är dock osäkra och delvis motstridiga. Han antas ha blivit kung omkring år 970.
2 CONC  Till en början regerade han tillsammans med sin bror Olof. Efter dennes död styrde han svearnas rike ensamt (det är okänt ifall Götaland ingick i sveaväldet vid den här tiden). Han kom dock i konflikt med sin brorson Styrbjörn St
2 CONC arke som krävde att få inta sin faders plats som medkung till Erik. Konflikten kulminerade med slaget vid Fyrisvallarna i närheten av Uppsala som Erik vann. Det är denna seger som gav honom tillnamnet Segersäll (den segerrike). St
2 CONC yrbjörn hade fått stöd av Danmark och som hämnd anföll han riket. Erik Segersäll kontrollerade sannolikt delar av Danmark i slutet av sin regeringstid. Han sägs också ha låtit döpa sig i Danmark men avföll till hedendomen när han 
2 CONC återvände till Sverige.
2 CONT
2 CONT --------------------
2 CONT
2 CONT Was baptized in Sweden, but eventually went back to worshiping the Norse gods.
2 CONT
2 CONT Sources:
2 CONT
2 CONT The book, 'Kings & Queens of Europe'
2 CONT
2 CONT The book, 'The Oxford History of the British Monarchy'
2 CONT
