2 CONT
2 CONT iii)       ''' ['''CONSTANTIA ([920/30]-after May [963]).  The affiliation of Constantia, wife of Boson, is unknown.  <br/>
2 CONT ''Chaume[66] proposed that she was the daughter of [https://www.geni.com/people/Charles-Constantine-Count-of-Vienne/6000000000347520217  Charles Constantin Comte de Vienne] for onomastic reasons only, stating that names with the r
2 CONC oot "Constant" were unknown in western royal genealogy before Charles Constantin himself.  This supposition is incorrect as numerous charters of the monastery of Cluny dated between 891 and 946 include the name "Constantia"[67], a
2 CONC nd many others during the same period name "Constantius" and "Constantinus".  Poly suggests that Constantia was in fact Charles Constantin's sister rather than his daughter[68], although this is more difficult to sustain chronolog
2 CONC ically bearing in mind the birth of her children in the early 950s.  ''
2 CONT
2 CONT '''m''' (before 942) BOSON Comte d'Avignon, son of ROTBALD I d'Agel & his wife --- (-[965/67]).  He succeeded as Comte d'Arles in 949.''']''' 
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT ----------
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT   From the Francogene website:
2 CONT
2 CONT http://www.francogene.com/quebec--genealogy/128/128948.php
2 CONT
2 CONT The family of Boso de PROVENCE and Constance de PROVENCE
2 CONT
2 CONT [128948] PROVENCE (de), Boso (Rotbold & Ermengarde d'AQUITAINE [129059])
2 CONT
2 CONT * married about 945, from France ? (France)
2 CONT
2 CONT PROVENCE (de), Constance (Charles-Constantin & .. [128947]), born about 925
2 CONT
2 CONT 1) Guillaume II, comte de Provence et d'Arles, born about 950, married about 980 Adèle dite Blanche d'ANJOU
2 CONT
2 CONT Bibliographie : Essai sur l'histoire des comtes souverains de Provence; Histoire de la maison royale de France (Père Anselme) 
2 CONT
2 CONT --------------- 
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT *http://fr.wikipedia.org/wiki/Constance_de_Provence
2 CONT
2 CONT Constance, née aux alentours de l'an 920, morte entre 963 et 966 fut comtesse de Provence par mariage.
2 CONT
2 CONT Une filation mal connue
2 CONT
2 CONT Sa filiation n'est pas connue et l'abbé Maurice Chaume a le premier mis en évidence que le prénom de cette dernière renvoyait au comte de Vienne Charles-Constantin. Il cite d'autres indices qui ne se révélèrent pas probants par la
2 CONC  suite, mais considérer Charles Constantin, comte de Vienne comme le père de Constance de Provence reste la meilleure hypothèse de la filiation de Constance.
2 CONT
2 CONT Certains chercheurs ont pensé qu'elle était sœur de Charles Constantin, mais Guillaume le Libérateur, son fils, étant né vers 950-955, elle même n'a pas pu naître avant 910-915. Or la mère de Charles Constantin, qui a transmis les
2 CONC  prénoms de Constance et Constantin, est morte en 903. Il est vrai que Constance pourrait être une nièce de Charles Constantin, mais il est très improbable que ce dernier aie eu une sœur ou un frère germain (brièveté du mariage de
2 CONC s parents et absence dans les sources).
2 CONT
2 CONT Mariage et enfants
2 CONT
2 CONT Elle épousa avant 942, ou plus probablement vers 945-948, Boson II (928 † 968), comte d'Arles et eut deux fils[1] :
2 CONT
2 CONT 1. Rotbald (Roubaud) († 1008) et
2 CONT
2 CONT 2. Guillaume dit le Libérateur (†993) , né vers 950 et mort après le 29 août 993, comte d'Arles et de Provence puis marquis de Provence en 975. Il est le père de Constance d'Arles épouse du roi de Robert II de France.
2 CONT
2 CONT Sources
2 CONT
2 CONT Christian Settipani, Nos ancêtres de l'Antiquité : étude des possibilités de liens généalogiques entre les familles de l'Antiquité et celles du haut Moyen-Âge européen, Christian, Paris, 1991, 263 p. (ISBN 2-86496-050-6) 
2 CONT
2 CONT Christian Settipani, La Préhistoire des Capétiens (Nouvelle histoire généalogique de l'auguste maison de France, vol. 1), éd. Patrick van Kerrebrouck, 1993 (ISBN 2-9501509-3-4) 
2 CONT
2 CONT Notes
2 CONT
2 CONT 1.↑ Constantia is named as the wife of Comte Boson, and mother of Guillaume and Rotbald, in the Cartulaire de Montmajour dated May 963 (Chartrier de Saint-Pierre de Montmajour, ed. Dom Chantelou (1890/1), pp. 1-384, quoted in Sett
2 CONC ipani (1991), p. 3 footnote 3.)
2 CONT
2 CONT In English:
2 CONT
2 CONT Constance was born around 920 and died between 963 and 966. She was Comtesse de Provence by marriage.
2 CONT
2 CONT A little known woman
2 CONT
2 CONT Her parentage is unknown, though Father Maurice Chaume suggested that her name came from the Comte de Vienne, Charles Constantine. He cites other evidence that proved to be inconclusive afterward, but considering Charles Constanti
2 CONC ne, Comte de Vienne, as the father of Constance de Provence is the best hypothesis so far of Constance's ancestry.
2 CONT
2 CONT Some researchers have thought she was the sister of Charles Constantine, but his son, William the Deliverer, was born around 950-955, and Charles himself was not born before 910-915. Now the mother of Charles Constantine, who carr
2 CONC ied forward the names of Constance and Constantine, died in 903. It is true that Constance could be a niece of Charles Constantine, but it is unlikely that the latter was a sister or brother (short of an omission of parentage or m
2 CONC arriage in the sources).
2 CONT
2 CONT Marriage and Children
2 CONT
2 CONT She married before 942, or more likely 945-948, to Boson II (928-968), Comte d'Arles. They had two sons [1]:
2 CONT
2 CONT 1. Rotbald (Robaud) (d. 1008)
2 CONT
2 CONT 2. William The Liberator (d. 993), born c. 950 and died after 29 August 993, Comte d'Arles and Provence, and Marquis de Provence in 975. He is the father of Constance of Arles, who became wife of King Robert II of France.
2 CONT
2 CONT Notes:
2 CONT
2 CONT 1. Constantia is named as the wife of Count Boson, and mother of Guillaume and Rotbald, in the Cartulary Montmajour dated May 963 (Charter of St-Pierre-Montmajour, ed. Chantelou Dom 1890/1, pp 1-384, quoted in Settipani 1991, p. 3
2 CONC , footnote 3.)
2 CONT
2 CONT --------------------
2 CONT
2 CONT Constance OF VIENNE7,207 was born about 935. ARSC 6TH ED LINE 141A,B PED OF A.H.AYERS Parents: \Count Of Vienne\ Charles CONSTANTINE and TEUTBERGE.
2 CONT
2 CONT Spouse: Count Of Provence & Arles BOSO. Count Of Provence & Arles BOSO and Constance OF VIENNE were married. Children were: Count Of Provenc\ Rotbaud II, Count Of Provenc\ William I.
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT --------------------
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT William I, Count of Provence, and Adelaide of Anjou. William '''was the son of Boso II, Count of Arles, and Constance of Viennois.''' Adelaide was the daughter of Fulk II the the Good of Anjou and Gerberga. 
2 CONT
2 CONT http://www.fulkerson.org/royalty.html
2 CONT
2 CONT ========================
2 CONT
2 CONT Charles Constantine of Vienne
2 CONT
2 CONT Charles-Constantine (died 962) was the Count of Vienne, son of Louis the Blind, King of Provence, and the Holy Roman Emperor.
2 CONT
2 CONT Name and maternity
2 CONT
2 CONT About his name; he was never called "Charles Constantine", rather Flodoard, copied later by Richar, calls him "Constantinus". We know that his proper name was "Carolus" (Charles), from a diploma of his father, and from his own cha
2 CONC rters. Modern scholars have typically called him Charles Constantine, but this was not a name used during his lifetime.
2 CONT
2 CONT Some modern genealogical scholars speculated that his mother was Anna of Constantinople, daughter of Leo VI the Wise and his second wife Zoe Zaoutzaina. However, his father's marriage to this princess is much disputed and rather u
2 CONC nlikely. Christian Settipani postulates that his name refers to the founders of the empires governed by his father and maternal grandfather, i.e., to Charlemagne and Constantine the Great.
2 CONT
2 CONT Regarding his birthyear, or age, we have few datapoints. He was Count of Vienne and acting as an adult by (but not in) December 927. This evidences that his father must have had a prior union. Some speculation would place him born
2 CONC  in 901/3 but this is just a force-fit to allow Anna to be his mother and his father's wife.
2 CONT
2 CONT Life
2 CONT
2 CONT When Charles' father Louis died in 929, Hugh of Arles, who was already king of Italy, took over Provence and gave it, in 933, to King Rudolf II of Burgundy. Charles-Constantine for whatever reason, could not inherit his father's r
2 CONC ight to the imperial throne or his right to rule Provence. This has led many to believe he was, in fact, a bastard. He did however rule the county of the Viennois, until his death in 962.
2 CONT
2 CONT He was married to Thiberge de Troyes.
2 CONT
2 CONT '''It has been speculated that Constance, wife to Boso II of Arles'''   and grandmother of Queen Constance of Arles, '''was their daughter''' .Through her, Charles Constantine would be an ancestor of the Capetian kings of France a
2 CONC nd the Norman and Plantagenet kings of England (through Queen Constance's daughter Adela Capet, and Adela's daughter Queen Matilda of Flanders, who married William the Conqueror).
2 CONT
2 CONT http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Charles_Constantine_of_Vienne
2 CONT
2 CONT ----
2 CONT
2 CONT Information de l'Université d'Orléans.
2 CONT
2 CONT -----------
