1 NOTE She married first Gilbert, Duke of Lorraine.
2 CONT
2 CONT They had four children:
2 CONT Gerberge of Lorraine b. about 925. Married Adalbert I of Vermandois. 
2 CONT Alberade of Lorraine b. about 929. Married Renaud (originally as Ragenold), a Viking chieftain who became the Count of Roucy [1]. 
2 CONT Henri, Duke of Lorraine b. about 932 
2 CONT Wiltrude, Duchess of Bavaria b. about 937. Married Berthold, Duke of Bavaria.
2 CONT --------------------------------------------------------------
2 CONT She married secondly Louis IV of France in 939.
2 CONT
2 CONT They were parents to eight children:
2 CONT Lothair of France (941-986) 
2 CONT Mathilde b. about 943; married Conrad of Burgundy 
2 CONT Hildegarde b. about 944 
2 CONT Carloman b. about 945 
2 CONT Louis b. about 948 
2 CONT Charles, Duke of Lower Lorraine (953-993) 
2 CONT Alberade b. before 953 
2 CONT Henri b. about 953
1 NOTE  Gerberga van Saksen, (zie dezelfde persoon hierboven in generatie 33) geb. 0913/14 in Nordhausen (Harz), ovl. 05.05.0984 in Reims, begraven in Reims, St-Remy, ref. nr. 01.08.2003 KdG0, ES I.2-236.6,3  Zij trouwde met (1) Giselber
2 CONC t (II) van Lotharingen, getrouwd 928/29, ovl. 02.10.0939 verdronken in de Rijn bij Andernach, ref. nr. 11.01.2007 GM17.04.2003, ES I.2-236, KdG51, GN1991p580.13,3,6,14. Zij trouwde met (2) Lodewijk IV van West-Francië, ook bekend 
2 CONC als van Overzee, getrouwd einde 939, geb. 0920/21, ovl. 10.09.0954 in Reims (val van zijn paard), begraven in Reims, St-Remy, ref. nr. 12.03.2004 KdG0, GrJ554.6,5
1 NOTE Gerberga of Saxony (c. 913-5 May 984) was a daughter of Henry the Fowler, king of Germany, and Matilda of Ringelheim.
2 CONT
2 CONT She married first Gilbert, Duke of Lorraine. They had four children:
2 CONT
2 CONT Alberade of Lorraine b. about 929. Married Renaud (originally as Ragenold), a Viking chieftain who became the Count of Roucy [1]. 
2 CONT Henri, Duke of Lorraine b. about 932 
2 CONT Gerberge of Lorraine b. about 935. Married Adalbert I of Vermandois. 
2 CONT Wiltrude, b. about 937. 
2 CONT She married secondly Louis IV of France in 939. They were parents to eight children:
2 CONT
2 CONT Lothair of France (941-986) 
2 CONT Mathilde b. about 943; married Conrad of Burgundy 
2 CONT Hildegarde b. about 944 
2 CONT Carloman b. about 945 
2 CONT Louis b. about 948 
2 CONT Charles, Duke of Lower Lorraine (953-993) 
2 CONT Alberade b. before 953 
2 CONT Henri b. about 953 
2 CONT Contemporary sources describe her as a highly educated, intelligent and forceful player in the political game of the time.
2 CONT
2 CONT Louis IV died on 10 September 954. As a widow, Gerberga became a nun and served as the abbess of Notre Dame in Laon. She died in Reims, Champagne.
2 CONT
2 CONT Sources
2 CONT Bouchard, Constance Brittain. (2001) Those of My Blood: Constructing Noble Families in Medieval Francia. University of Pennsylvania Press. 
2 CONT " Women in power 750-1000" from Guide2womenleaders.com, last accessed January 13, 2007 
