1 NOTE Fulk II of Anjou (died 960), son of Fulk the Red, was count of Anjou from 942 to 960.[1] He was often at war with the Bretons. He seems to have been a man of culture, a poet and an artist. In 960 he was succeeded by his son Geoffr
2 CONC ey Greymantle.
2 CONT
2 CONT Fulk II died at Tours. By his spouse, Gerberge of Maine, he had several children:
2 CONT
2 CONT Adelais of Anjou, married five times 
2 CONT Geoffrey I, Count of Anjou, married Adelaide of Vermandois 
2 CONT Bouchard IV, Count of Vendome, married Elizabeth of Vendome; their daughter, Elizabeth married her cousin, Geoffrey I's son, Fulk the Black, only to be burnt at the stake by her husband in her wedding dress. 
