2 CONT Was mild, religious and lite krigersk. La vekt of aa fremme jordbruket in
2 CONT    Anjou,
2 CONT       after at det was blitt *delagt in krig. I et dokument of 942 bekrefter
2 CONT han
2 CONT    en
2 CONT       gave til klostret in St. Julien in Tours. I julen 943 was han in Paris
2 CONT    sammen with
2 CONT       sin bror Guy, bishop in Soissons.
1 NOTE Line 4088 from GEDCOM File not recognizable or too long:
2 CONT   NAME Foulques II "le Bon" Count Of /ANJOU/
1 NOTE BIOGRAPHY
2 CONT Foulques was the son of Foulques I, count of Anjou, and Roselle de Loche. In 937 he married Gerberge de Tours. Four of their children would have progeny, including his heir Geoffrey I. He was often at war with the Bretons. He seem
2 CONC s to have been a man of culture, a poet and an artist. By reputation a saintly man, he dressed as a cleric. Of Louis IV, king of France, who had mocked his piety, Foulques commented, 'an illiterate king is a crowned ass'. Foulques
2 CONC  died on 11 November 958.
