1 OCCU Princess of Normandy, Countess of Poitou, Otherwise known as "Gerloc", Daughter of Hrolf Duke of Normandy, Duchess of Normandy, Countess of Pointiers, princesse / comtesse de Poitiers et duchesse d'Aquitaine
1 TITL Duchesse
1 NOTE {geni:about_me} Gerloc Adela Hrólfsdóttir de Normandie (c.897 - 962) was the daughter of Gange-Hrolfr 'Rollo' & Poppa De Valois.
2 CONT
2 CONT http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Gerloc
2 CONT
2 CONT http://fmg.ac/Projects/MedLands/NORMANDY.htm#_Toc148955357
2 CONT
2 CONT Her original name was Geirlaug or Gerloc, but she was baptised in Rouen as Adela (or Adèle) in 912. She was the sister of Duke William Longsword.
2 CONT
2 CONT In 935, she married William or Guillaume Towhead, the future count of Poitou and duke of Aquitaine. She gave him two children before dying on 14 October 962:
2 CONT
2 CONT *William IV of Aquitaine
2 CONT *Adelaide of Aquitaine, wife of Hugh Capet
2 CONT
2 CONT --------------------
2 CONT
2 CONT GERLOC (-after 969).  
2 CONT
2 CONT Guillaume de Jumièges names "Guillaume et…Gerloc" as children of Rollo and Poppa, in a later passage records her marriage to "Guillaume comte de Poitou"[66].  
2 CONT
2 CONT Robert of Torigny also names "Willermum Longum Spatam et Gerloch" as children of "Rollo dux Northmannorum" and Poppa[67].  
2 CONT
2 CONT The Chronico Richardi Pictavensis records that "Heblus…Pictavorum Comes et Dux Aquitaniæ duxit Adelam filiam Rolli Rothomagensis"[68], although this is presumably an error for Guillaume son of Ebles.  She adopted the name ADELA wh
2 CONC en baptised.  "Guillelmi comitis, Adeleidis comitisse" subscribed a charter recording a donation to Cluny dated [963][69].  Lothaire King of France granted her 14 Oct 962 the right to dispose of extensive property in Poitiers, la 
2 CONC Cour de Faye, this grant effectively putting an end to the long dispute between her husband and the family of Hugues "Capet".  She used the property to found the Monastery of Sainte-Trinité[70].  
2 CONT
2 CONT m (935) GUILLAUME I "Tête d'Etoupe" Comte de Poitou, son of EBLES "Mancer" Comte de Poitou, Duke of Aquitaine & his first wife Aremburga ([900]-3 Apr 963).  He succeeded in 959 as GUILLAUME III Duke of Aquitaine.    
2 CONT
2 CONT --------------------
2 CONT
2 CONT --------------------
2 CONT
2 CONT Last Edited=20 Feb 2002
2 CONT
2 CONT      Adele de Normandie was born circa 917. (1) She was the daughter of Rollo Ragnvaldsson, 1st Duc de Normandie and Poppa of Normandy de Valois. (1) She married Guillaume III, Duc d'Aquitaine, son of Ebalus, Duc d'Aquitaine, in 9
2 CONC 35. (1) 
2 CONT
2 CONT She died after 14 October 962 at France. (1)
2 CONT
2 CONT Children of Adele de Normandie and Guillaume III, Duc d'Aquitaine
2 CONT
2 CONT -1. Guillaume IV, Duc d'Aquitaine+ b. c 937, d. bt 995 - 996 (1)
2 CONT
2 CONT -2. Adelaide de Poitou+ b. c 945, d. bt 1004 - 1005 (1)
2 CONT
2 CONT Forrás:
2 CONT
2 CONT http://www.thepeerage.com/p10478.htm#i104772
2 CONT
2 CONT --------------------
2 CONT
2 CONT Married at age 10
2 CONT
2 CONT --------------------
2 CONT
2 CONT http://www.geneajourney.com/nrmndy.html
2 CONT
2 CONT Children of Rollo/Robert I of Normandy and Poppa of Bayeux were:
2 CONT
2 CONT •	William I of Normandy, Duke of Normandy, b abt 891.
2 CONT
2 CONT •	Adele/Gerloc of Normandy b abt 916, d 14 Oct 962. She md William I of Poitou, Count of Poitou, 935, son of Ebles Mancer, Count of Poitou, and Emliane.
2 CONT
2 CONT William I of Normandy [b], Duke of Normandy, "Long Sword", b abt 891, of Normandy, d 17 Dec 942, Normandy. He md [1] Sprota abt 922, [2] Luitgarde de Vermandois abt 935.
2 CONT
2 CONT Child of William I of Normandy and Sprota was:
2 CONT
2 CONT --------------------
