2 CONT Adele Hrólfsdóttir de Normandie (c.897 - 962)
2 CONT
2 CONT Her original name was Geirlaug or Gerloc, but she was baptised in Rouen as Adela (or Adèle) in 912. She was the sister of Duke William Long sword.
2 CONT
2 CONT In 935, she married William or Guillaume Towhead, the future count of Poitou and duke of Aquitaine. She gave him two children before dying on 14 October 962: 
2 CONT
2 CONT * William IV of Aquitaine 
2 CONT
2 CONT * Adelaide of Aquitaine, wife of Hugh Capet
2 CONT
2 CONT She adopted the name ADELA when baptized. "Guillelmi comitis, Adeleidis comitisse" subscribed a charter recording a donation to Cluny dated [963][69]. Lothaire King of France granted her 14 Oct 962 the right to dispose of extensiv
2 CONC e property in Poitiers, la Cour de Faye, this grant effectively putting an end to the long dispute between her husband and the family of Hugues "Capet". She used the property to found the Monastery of Sainte-Trinité[70]. 
2 CONT --------------------
2 CONT Gerloc (or Geirlaug), baptised in Rouen as Adela (or Adèle) in 912, was the daughter of Rollo, first duke of Normandy, and his wife, Poppa. She was the sister of Duke William Longsword.  In 935, she married William Towhead, the fu
2 CONC ture count of Poitou and duke of Aquitaine. They had two children together before she died on 14 October 962: William IV of Aquitaine Adelaide of Aquitaine, wife of Hugh Capet 
