2 CONT From Darryl Lundy's Peerage page on Hedwig von Sachsen (Forrás / Source):
2 CONT
2 CONT http://www.thepeerage.com/p398.htm#i3973
2 CONT
2 CONT Hedwig von Sachsen
2 CONT
2 CONT F, #3973, b. before 922, d. after 965
2 CONT
2 CONT Last Edited=19 Jun 2005
2 CONT
2 CONT Hedwig von Sachsen was born before 922. She was the daughter of Heinrich I von Sachsen, Holy Roman Emperor and Mathilda von Ringelheim. (1) 
2 CONT
2 CONT (Ben M. Angel notes: Heinrich was actually the last German ruler not to be titled Holy Roman Emperor. He did carry the title King of Germany, though.)
2 CONT
2 CONT She married Hugues of Neustria, Comte de Paris, son of Robert I, Roi de France, before 14 September 938. (1) 
2 CONT
2 CONT She died after 965, on a 10 May.
2 CONT
2 CONT Hedwig von Sachsen was also known as Hatwide.1
2 CONT
2 CONT Children of Hedwig von Sachsen and Hugues of Neustria, Comte de Paris
2 CONT
2 CONT -1. Hugues de Paris, Roi de France+ b. c 938, d. 24 Oct 996
2 CONT
2 CONT -2. Emma de Paris b. a 942, d. 19 Mar 968
2 CONT
2 CONT Citations
2 CONT
2 CONT [S45] Marcellus Donald R. von Redlich, Pedigrees of Some of the Emperor Charlemagne's Descendants, volume I (1941; reprint, Baltimore, Maryland, U.S.A.: Genealogical Publishing Company, 2002), page 63. Hereinafter cited as Pedigre
2 CONC es of Emperor Charlemagne, I.
2 CONT
2 CONT --------------------
2 CONT
2 CONT Era irmã de Otto I(Imperador do Sacro Império Romano). Que planejou um casamento dela com Hugues le Grand.
2 CONT
2 CONT --------------------
2 CONT
2 CONT From the Foundation for Medieval Genealogy page on France Capetian Kings:
2 CONT
2 CONT http://fmg.ac/Projects/MedLands/CAPET.htm#Huguesdied956A
2 CONT
2 CONT Hugues Le Grand married thirdly ([9 May/14 Sep] 937) HEDWIG of Germany, daughter of HEINRICH I King of Germany & his second wife Mathilde [Immedinger] ([922]-9 Jan [958 or after 965]).  
2 CONT
2 CONT "Hugues abbé de Saint-Martin" donated "son alleu de Lachy…dans le comté de Meaux", inherited from "comte Aledramnus", to Tours Saint-Martin by charter dated 14 Sep 937 which names "sa femme Havis"[96].  
2 CONT
2 CONT Rodulfus Glauber names "sororem [=Otto] Haduidem" as wife of "Hugo dux Francorum cognomento Magnus"[97].  Flodoard refers to "sororem Othonis regis Transfhenensis, filiam Heinrici" as the wife of "Hugo princeps, filius Roberti", w
2 CONC ithout naming her, recording their marriage in 938[98].  Flodoard also refers to "relicta Hugonis" as "amita Lotharius rex"[99].  
2 CONT
2 CONT The necrology of the abbey of Saint-Denis records the death "V Id Jan" of "Hadhuidis comitissa"[100].  
2 CONT
2 CONT Duke Hugues & his third wife had four children:
2 CONT
2 CONT 1. Hugues (b. c.940, d. 24 October 996 at Villa Les Juifs, near Prasville, Eure-et-Loire, buried Eglise de l'Abbaye Royale de St-Denis, First King of France) 
2 CONT
2 CONT 2. Emma (b. c.943, d. after 18 March 968, married as first wife Richard I Sans Peur Comte de Normandie) 
2 CONT
2 CONT 3. Otton (Eudes, b. c.945, d. 23 February 965, buried St-Germain d'Auxerre, installed by Lothaire as Duke of Burgundy) 
2 CONT
2 CONT 4. Eudes (Odo, b. c.948, d. 15 October 1002 at Chateau de Poilly-sur-Saone, buried Auxerre, adopted the name of Henri when becoming Duke of Burgundy, apparently different from previous brother)
2 CONT
2 CONT References:
2 CONT
2 CONT [96] Tours Saint-Martin LVIII, p. 95. 
2 CONT
2 CONT [97] Rodulfi Glabri, Historiarum I.4, MGH SS VII, p. 54. 
2 CONT
2 CONT [98] Flodoard 938, MGH SS III, p. 385. 
2 CONT
2 CONT [99] Flodoard 957, MGH SS III, p. 404. 
2 CONT
2 CONT [100] Obituaires de Sens Tome I.1, Abbaye de Saint-Denis, p. 307. 
2 CONT
