2 CONT
2 CONT Hugues of Neustria, Comte de Paris was born circa 895. He was the son of Robert I, Roi de France. (1) 
2 CONT
2 CONT He married, firstly, Eadhilda (?), daughter of Eadweard I, King of Wessex and Ælflæd (?), between 926 and 927. (2) 
2 CONT
2 CONT He married, thirdly, Hedwig von Sachsen, daughter of Heinrich I von Sachsen, Holy Roman Emperor and Mathilda von Ringelheim, before 14 September 938. (1) 
2 CONT
2 CONT He died on 9 June 956.
2 CONT
2 CONT Hugues of Neustria, Comte de Paris also went by the nick-name of Hugues 'the Great'. (1) 
2 CONT
2 CONT He gained the title of Comte de Paris. He gained the title of Duc de France.
