2 CONT 1 NAME Guillaume (William) Duke Of/NORMANDY/
2 CONT
2 CONT According to Stuart--Royalty for Commoners 1-3 & Weis Ancestral Roots 4-10
2 CONT
2 CONT Guillaume I "Long Sword" Duke of Normandy
2 CONT
2 CONT    Sources: A. Roots 121E; RC 166; Norr, p60; Coe; Guizot; Pfafman; AF;
2 CONT Kraentzler 1156, 1194, 1443, 1453; Davis; Ashley.
2 CONT    William Longsword (Longaspatha), second Duke of Normandy, 917-943, andDuke
2 CONT of Aquitaine. He captured Britanny, Cotentin, the Channel Islands and the
2 CONT Avranchin, annexing them to his kingdom. He was slain by Arnulf ofFlanders.
2 CONT    RC: William I "Longsword," Duke of Normandy; murdered 17 Dec. 943
2 CONT in France.
2 CONT    K: Guilaume I Longue Epee, Duke of Normandy.
2 CONT    Roots: William I, "Longsword," born ca. 930, probably Rouen. Succeededto
2 CONT Duchy of Normandy about 927. In about 930 the Bretons rebelled. Hesubdued
2 CONT them, taking Brittany, the Channel Islands, Contentin and the Averanchin.
2 CONT Killed in a treacherous ambush 17 Dec. 942 by servants of Theobald ofBlois and
2 CONT Arnulf of Flanders.
2 CONT    Norr: William Longsword (Guillaume Longue-espee); son of Poppa; 2ndduke,
2 CONT 927-942; murdered.
2 CONT    Ashley: William "Longsword", Count of Normandy.
2 CONT    Davis: William I Longsword, ruled Normandy 931-942
2 CONT
2 CONT The vast majority of the information presented is obtained from online sources.  While I believe it to be accurate, caution must be taken to always be careful of its validity.
2 CONT Please do contact me if you find errors or have questions.
2 CONT
2 CONT OCCU 2nd Duke of Normandy...
2 CONT SOUR GWALTNEY.ANC (Compuserve);
2 CONT Royalty for Commoners, Roderick W. Stuart, p. 124 says c900;
2 CONT HAWKINS.GED says ABT 900 & place;members.aol.com/sargen3 says ABT 893 & place
2 CONT SOUR Royalty for Commoners, Roderick W. Stuart, p. 124 says 17 Dec 943;
2 CONT HAWKINS.GED says 17 Dec 943;
2 CONT The Conquest of England, Eric Linklater, p. 28 says 17 Dec 942
2 CONT SOUR Americans of Royal Descent, Charles H. Browning, p. 408;
2 CONT Royalty for Commoners, Roderick W. Stuart, p. 124
2 CONT William the Longsword - Americans of Royal Descent, Charles H. Browning, p. 25
2 CONT William Longue-epee - p. 30; Longespada - COMYN4.TAF (Compuserve Roots), p. 5;
2 CONT COMYNI.GED shows mother as Gisela de France. NORM.TAF shows Poppa.  I suspect
2 CONT these are the same people and one of the parents is incorrect - NLP; Guillaume
2 CONT "Longaspada" de Normandie - COMYNI.GED (Compuserve);The Norman Conquest also
2 CONT gives his mother as Poppa - NLP;GWALTNEY.ANC (Compuserve) gives Gisela - NLP
2 CONT WILLIAM I, son of ROLLO the DANE and POPPA DE BAYEUX: Before he added the Cotentin or Cherbourg, peninsula to his domain, he may have had to suppress a Breton rising there, and then a revolt of
2 CONT  recalcitrant Danes.  It is possible that he invited new 
2 CONT Danish settlers to the Cotentin. He is said to have been a just and vigorous man, and in 942 he was murdered, at Picquigny on the Somme, by order of Arnulf of Flanders, who had forced a quarrel on
2 CONT  him in consequence of personal insult or some dispute 
2 CONT about an
2 CONT intervening property - The Conquest of England, Eric Linklater, p. 28
2 CONT Aceded 932 - http://gendex.com/users/daver/rigney/D0002/G0000093.html#I1245
