2 CONT Guillaume I "Long Sword" Duke of Normandy
2 CONT
2 CONT    Sources: A. Roots 121E; RC 166; Norr, p60; Coe; Guizot; Pfafman; AF;
2 CONT Kraentzler 1156, 1194, 1443, 1453; Davis; Ashley.
2 CONT    William Longsword (Longaspatha), second Duke of Normandy, 917-943, andDuke
2 CONT of Aquitaine. He captured Britanny, Cotentin, the Channel Islands and the
2 CONT Avranchin, annexing them to his kingdom. He was slain by Arnulf ofFlanders.
2 CONT    RC: William I "Longsword," Duke of Normandy; murdered 17 Dec. 943
2 CONT in France.
2 CONT    K: Guilaume I Longue Epee, Duke of Normandy.
2 CONT    Roots: William I, "Longsword," born ca. 930, probably Rouen. Succeededto
2 CONT Duchy of Normandy about 927. In about 930 the Bretons rebelled. Hesubdued
2 CONT them, taking Brittany, the Channel Islands, Contentin and the Averanchin.
2 CONT Killed in a treacherous ambush 17 Dec. 942 by servants of Theobald ofBlois and
2 CONT Arnulf of Flanders.
2 CONT    Norr: William Longsword (Guillaume Longue-espee); son of Poppa; 2ndduke,
2 CONT 927-942; murdered.
2 CONT    Ashley: William "Longsword", Count of Normandy.
2 CONT    Davis: William I Longsword, ruled Normandy 931-942
2 CONT
2 CONT The vast majority of the information presented is obtained from online sources.  While I believe it to be accurate, caution must be taken to always be careful of its validity.
2 CONT Please do contact me if you find errors or have questions.
