1 NOTE BIOGRAPHY: William the Longsword's "Danish wife," called a Breton concubine by Flodoard.
1 NOTE --Other Fields
2 CONT
2 CONT Ref Number: 408
1 NOTE RESEARCH NOTES:
2 CONT Dutchess of Normandy, concubine
1 NOTE _P_CCINFO 1-20792
1 NOTE Also known as Adela.
1 NOTE She was a Breton concubine captured in war and bound to William by a Danish marriage. After William died, Sprota became the wife of Esperleng, a wealthy miller; Rodulf of Ivry was their son and Richard's half-brother.
1 NOTE !Source: THE RUFUS PARKS PEDIGREE by Brian J.L. Berry
2 CONT !Information: page 59                 Chart: page  55
2 CONT
2 CONT !Page 59 ---
2 CONT
2 CONT See notes of William I Longsword,
2 CONT
2 CONT !Availability: The libraries of Ken, Karen, Kristen, Kevin, Brian, Amy, Adam and FAL
