2 CONT Original individual @P2689360840@ (@MS_NHFETTERLYFAMIL0@) merged with @P2689280809@ (@MS_NHFETTERLYFAMIL0@)
1 NOTE OR "ADELA"; NOT WIFE, MISTRESS
1 NOTE A noble lady who married Duke William "a la Danoise". {Burke's Peerage} [GADD.GED]
2 CONT
2 CONT Also have birth as ca 911 in Bretagne, Brittany, France. [Betz Homepage http://info.lu.farmingdale.edu/~betzja/gene]
1 NOTE 33rd great grandmother
1 NOTE _P_CCINFO 1-20792
2 CONT Sources: A. Roots 121E; RC 166; Coe; AF; Kraentzler 1156, 1194, 1443,1453; Pfafman; Norr, p60.
2 CONT RC: Sprote de Bretagne "Danish Wife," a Breton captive.
2 CONT Roots: Sprota (Danish wife), a Breton.
2 CONT Coe: Esposita.
2 CONT Pfafman: Espriota (Sprota, Adela) of Senlis, a Breton.
2 CONT Norr: Sprota (Espriota), mistress; married about 932 under paganrites.
2 CONT
2 CONT According to Stuart--Royalty for Commoners 1-3 & Weis Ancestral Roots 4-10
2 CONT
2 CONT Ancestral File Number:<AFN> 9HMF-3L
2 CONT !"Royal Ancestors" by Michel Call, 1989, Chart # 11504, # 11546.
2 CONT _UID16FC0A6236EA844FA5CAA08CFE3367ED91A5
1 NOTE SOURCE NOTES:
2 CONT Bu852 http://uts.cc.utexas.edu/~churchh/edw3chrt.html
1 NOTE Sprota was a Breton concubine captured in war and bound to William by a Danish marriage. After William died, Sprota became the wife of Esperleng, a wealthy miller.
1 NOTE From a genealogical website (http://sbaldw.home.mindspring.com/hproject/prov/sprot000.htm)
2 CONT
2 CONT Wife or concubine of Guillaume (William) "Longsword" (of Normandy), 10th century.
2 CONT
2 CONT Called a Breton concubine by Flodoard [s.a. 943: "Rex Ludowicus filio ipsius Willelmi, nato de concubina Britanna, terram Nortmannorum dedit; ..." (clearly referring to Richard), MGH SS 3, 389, van Houts (2000), 47], she was first
2 CONC  given a name by William of Jumièges [GND iii, 2 (vol. 1, 78-9)], who, writing in the second half of the eleventh century, stated that she was bound to William by the Danish custom ("... Danico more iuncta, nomine Sprota ..."). Al
2 CONC though the name "Sprota" gives us a convenient name to refer to the mother of Richard I, the unusual form of the name and the lateness of the source (more than 100 years later) make it uncertain that her name has been correctly re
2 CONC ported
1 NOTE 	1  NAME Sprote /De Bourgogne/
2 CONT 	2  GIVN Sprote
2 CONT 	2  SURN De Bourgogne
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT 1  NAME Sporta /De Senlis/ 1  BIRT 2  DATE ABT. 911 2  PLAC Bretagne, France 1  DEAT 2  DATE 946
1 NOTE Sprota was also known as Adele of Senlis. Her parents were Herbert I Count of Vermandois and Bertha (Beatrice) de Morvois, Countess of Vermandoi Her great great great great Grandfather was Charlemagne, the first Emperor of the Hol
2 CONC y Roman Empire
