2 NOTE https://www.tourismeloiret.com/en/diffusio/visits/vestiges-de-la-collegiale-saint-georges-pithiviers_TFOPCUCEN045V502SDX
3 CONT
3 CONT DESCRIPTIVE
3 CONT The collegiate church was established in the Roman camp which became a feudal castle in the 10th century. It dominates the valley of the Oeuf. Its bell tower, wrongly called "the keep". Only small fragments of the collegiate churc
3 CONC h of St George remain today: an imposing tower stands in the corner of the town hall, two small Romanesque bays, a Gothic nave and a Romanesque crypt, of which only a tiny part has been exhumed. The collegiate church was founded a
3 CONC t the beginning of the 11th century and a Romanesque church with a crypt was then built. It was burnt down in 1217 and a gothic church followed. The canons were attacked by the Protestants and withdrew to the southern side of the 
3 CONC Gothic church. The collegiate church was dissolved in 1791.
