2 CONT HEDWIGE [Avoie] de France ([1003]-5 Jun after 1063).  Rodolfus Glaber records that "Rainaldus…Landrici comitis filius" married a daughter of King Robert[194].  
2 CONT
2 CONT The Chronici Hugonis Floriacensis names "Adelaidem…Rainaldi comitis Nivernensis uxorem" as the daughter of King Robert and his wife Constance[195].  The Historia Nivernensium Comitum records that the wife of "Renaldum" was "sorori
2 CONC  Regis Roberti, filii Hugonis Capitonis"[196].  
2 CONT
2 CONT The Annales Vizeliacenses also specifies that Renaud's wife was the sister not daughter of King Robert II[197].  However, this is chronologically unlikely given that King Robert and his known sisters were born in the 970s, more th
2 CONC an twenty years before the earliest possible date of birth of Comte Renaud.  
2 CONT
2 CONT Her marriage was agreed by her father as part of his alliance with Landry Comte de Nevers after capturing Auxerre, which the king gave to his daughter as dowry[198].  
2 CONT
2 CONT "Rainaldus comes Nivernensis" donated property "Belmontis" to Cluny, for the souls of "…uxoris mee Advise…" by charter dated to [1028/40][199].  She founded the abbeys of Crisenon and Issenon.  
2 CONT
2 CONT m (1006, soon after 25 Jan 1016) RENAUD de Nevers, son of LANDRY Comte de Nevers & his wife Mathilde de Bourgogne-Comté (-killed in battle Sainte-Vertu, Yonne 29 May 1040, bur Auxerre, Saint-Germain).  
2 CONT
2 CONT He succeeded his father in 1028 as RENAUD I Comte de Nevers.  He was killed in battle against Robert I Duke of Burgundy, his brother-in-law.  
2 CONT
2 CONT From the Foundation for Medieval Genealogy page on Burgundy Duchy Nobility:
2 CONT
2 CONT http://fmg.ac/Projects/MedLands/BURGUNDIAN%20NOBILITY.htm#RenaudINeversdied1040A
2 CONT
2 CONT Renaud I married (soon after 25 Jan 1016) HEDWIGE [Avoie] de France, daughter of ROBERT II "le Pieux" King of France & his third wife Constance d'Arles [Provence] ([1003]-5 Jun after 1063).   
2 CONT
2 CONT Comte Renaud & his wife had [five] children:  
2 CONT
2 CONT 1. Guillaume I de Nevers (d. 20 June 1098, buried at Nevers, St-Etienne, succeeded as Comte de Nevers)
2 CONT
2 CONT 2. Henri de Nevers
2 CONT
2 CONT 3. Guy de Nevers (d. January 26, Unknown year)
2 CONT
2 CONT 4. Robert "Le Bourguignon" de Nevers (d. after 1098, became Seigneur de Sable by his first wife, Seigneur de Craon)
2 CONT
2 CONT 5. Adelaide (married Geoffroy II, Sire de Semur)
2 CONT
2 CONT From the Wikipedia page for Adela of France, Countess of Nevers:
2 CONT
2 CONT http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Adela_of_France,_Countess_of_Nevers
2 CONT
2 CONT Adele of France (ca. 1003-1063), was the daughter of Robert II of France and Constance of Arles. She married Renauld I, Count of Nevers 1000-1040 on 25 Jan. 1016, having issue who would inherit both Nevers and Auxerre.
2 CONT
2 CONT From the Wikipedia page of Renaud I, Count of Nevers:
2 CONT
2 CONT http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Renaud_I_of_Nevers
2 CONT
2 CONT Marriage
2 CONT
2 CONT He married Hedwig (or Advisa) of France on Jan 25, 1016, daughter of Robert II, King of France and Constance of Arles.
2 CONT
2 CONT Children
2 CONT
2 CONT 1. William I of Nevers (c.1030-1083/1097)
2 CONT
2 CONT 2. Henry of Nevers (-1067)
2 CONT
2 CONT 3. Guy of Nevers (-1067)
2 CONT
2 CONT 4. Robert of Nevers Baron of Craon (c.1035-1098)
2 CONT
2 CONT 5. Adelaide of Nevers
2 CONT
2 CONT --------------------
2 CONT
2 CONT Hedwige (Avoie) de France 
2 CONT
2 CONT daughter of Robert II & Constance d'Arles
2 CONT
2 CONT b abt 1003 d 5 Jun after 1063
2 CONT
2 CONT married Renaud I Comte de Nevers
2 CONT
2 CONT Children:
2 CONT
2 CONT Guillame I Comte de Nevers
2 CONT
2 CONT Henri de Nevers
2 CONT
2 CONT Guy de Nevers
2 CONT
2 CONT Robert de Nevers
2 CONT
2 CONT and possibly Adelaide
2 CONT
2 CONT http://fmg.ac/Projects/MedLands/CAPET.htm#HedwigeAvoiediedafter1063
2 CONT
2 CONT --------------------
2 CONT
2 CONT Hedwig of France
2 CONT
2 CONT From Wikipedia, the free encyclopedia
2 CONT
2 CONT Hedwig of France (c. 970- after 1013), also called Avoise, Hadevide or Haltude, was Countess of Mons. She was the daughter of Hugh Capet, the first King of France, and Adelaide of Aquitaine.
2 CONT
2 CONT [edit]Family
2 CONT
2 CONT In 996 Hedwig married Rainier IV of Hainaut (947-1013). They had three children:
2 CONT
2 CONT Reginar V, Count of Mons. Married Mathilde of Verdun, daughter of Herman, Count of Brabant.
2 CONT
2 CONT Lambert of Mons
2 CONT
2 CONT Beatrix, who married Ebles I, Count of Rheims and Roucy, and Archbishop of Rheims.
2 CONT
2 CONT Following the death of her first husband, Hedwig re-married to Hugh de Dagsbourg. She died after 1013.
2 CONT
2 CONT Hedwig (Edith) Princess of France 1 2 3
