2 CONT
2 CONT Fulk I (or Fulco) of Anjou, "said Rufus was the first Count of Anjou from 930 to 942, having been first Viscount d'Angers (before 898-930) and Tours (898-909), and Count of Nantes (909-919). It is the family Ingelgeriens and son o
2 CONC f Viscount Ingelger and perhaps Aelendis.
2 CONT
2 CONT It is mentioned for the first time in a charter of April 886, and then as Viscount in another charter dated 29 September 898, signed by Viscount Hardrada Tours. Another 909 charter also says the Vicomte de Tours. In 909, following
2 CONC  the death of Alain le Grand, the Viscount of Tours is provided Thibaud the Old and he received the county of Nantes, in charge of fighting against the Normans and Bretons. Nantes is taken by the Normans in 914, and Fulk waives it
2 CONC s rights to the county of Nantes in 919. He retained the title of count, but the title was finally recognized in 930, when his overlord Hugh the Great described him as such in one of his charters. He spent most of his life fightin
2 CONC g the Vikings.
2 CONT
2 CONT He married Roscille, daughter of Garnier (Warnerius), Lord of Loches, and Tescende, and had:
2 CONT
2 CONT Ingelger died before 929 and probably killed in 927 during an engagement against the Vikings.
2 CONT
2 CONT Gui (Widdoes), canon of St. Martin de Tours, then bishop of Soissons of 937 to 973
2 CONT
2 CONT Fulk II the Good, Count of Anjou.
2 CONT
2 CONT Roscille of Anjou, married Alain Barbetorte II, Duke of Brittany. They have a daughter Gerberga Nantes.
2 CONT
2 CONT He is cited with his son Fulk II the last time in August 941. A charter of 942 mentions a May Fulk Count of Anjou, not as we know it is Fulk Fulk I or II. Given the fact that I Fulk began his career to 886, he probably died shortl
2 CONC y after 941.
2 CONT
2 CONT Fulk le Roux is quoted in "The Chronicle the exploits of the Counts of Anjou," text written from 1100 to 1140 by a monk Angevin, at the request of the Rechin Fulk.
2 CONT
2 CONT Preceded by Fulk I of Anjou Followed by
2 CONT
2 CONT Ingelger Vicomte d'Angers,
2 CONT
2 CONT then Count of Anjou Fulk II the Good
2 CONT
2 CONT Hardrada Vicomte de Tours Thibaud the Old
2 CONT
2 CONT Alain le Grand Count of Nantes and Ottar Hroald, vikings
2 CONT
