2 CONT (Wiki)
2 CONT
2 CONT Gerberga of Saxony (also Gerberga of France) (c. 913 – 5 May 968/9 or 984?) was a member of the Ottonian dynasty and a descendant of Charlemagne. Her first husband was Gilbert, Duke of Lorraine. Her second husband was Louis IV of 
2 CONC France. Contemporary sources describe her as a highly educated, intelligent and forceful political player.
2 CONT
2 CONT Gerberga was born c.913. She was the oldest daughter of Henry the Fowler, King of Germany, and his second wife, Matilda. Her older brother was Otto I of Germany.
2 CONT
2 CONT First marriage[edit]
2 CONT
2 CONT In 928, Gerberga married her first husband, Gilbert, Duke of Lorraine.[1] They had four children: Alberade of Lorraine b. about 929. Married Renaud (originally as Ragenold), a Viking chieftain who became the Count of Roucy Henry, 
2 CONC Duke of Lorraine b. about 932 Gerberge of Lorraine b. about 935. Married Adalbert I of Vermandois. Wiltrude, b. about 937.
2 CONT
2 CONT Jocundus, a Lotharingia chronicler writing in the 1070s, recorded that Gerberga was the driving force behind Gilbert's decision to support her younger brother Henry when he rebelled against her older brother Otto I c.936.[2] Gisel
2 CONC bert was defeated by Otto I in 939 at the Battle of Andernach and, while trying to escape, drowned in the Rhine.
2 CONT
2 CONT --------------------
