2 CONT In 947, Taksony lead a raid to Italy till Apulia, and King Berengar II of Italy had to buy the peace by paying a large amount of money to him and his followers. He might have taken part in the Battle of Lechfeld (Hungarian: augsbu
2 CONC rgi csata) where King Otto I of Germany won a decisive victory over the Magyars. After the defeat the Magyars stopped their raids (kalandozások) in Western Europe, but they began to pillage the Byzantine Empire.
2 CONT
2 CONT Taksony became the Grand Prince of the Magyars just or shortly after the Battle of Lechfeld, but his authority must have been only nominal over some regions of the Carpathian Basin inhabited by the Magyars. During his rule a large
2 CONC  number of Pechenegs and Khalyzians immigrated to the territory of the future Hungary.
2 CONT
2 CONT In 963, Pope John XII ordained the first Roman Catholic missionary bishop, Zacheus for the Magyars, but he probably never visited them.
2 CONT
2 CONT Taksony arranged the marriage of his son Géza of Hungary to Sarolt, the daughter of Gyula of Transylvania.
