1 NOTE {geni:about_me} ==Skoglar Toste:==
2 CONT Viking leader from [https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/V%C3%A4sterg%C3%B6tland Vastergotland]
2 CONT
2 CONT ==Project MedLands, Sweden Kings==
2 CONT
2 CONT '''KINGS of SWEDEN 1060-[1111] (FAMILY of STENKIL)'''
2 CONT
2 CONT Skoglar" TOSTE, son of ---.  In Svithjod.  Snorre records that Harald "Grenske" was welcomed in Svithjod by "Toste…often in battle…therefore called Skoglar-Toste" and lived five years with him[68]. 
2 CONT m ---.  
2 CONT
2 CONT The name of Toste's wife is not known. 
2 CONT
2 CONT Toste & his wife had two children: 
2 CONT * 1.         '''ULF'''.  According to Snorre[69], he was the brother of Sigrid "Storråda/the Haughty".  m ---.  The name of Ulf's wife is not known.  
2 CONT
2 CONT '''ULF & his wife had one child:'''
2 CONT
2 CONT * a)         RAGNVALD Ulfsson .  Snorre names "Earl Ragnvald, Ulf's son" when recording his [first] marriage[70].  Jarl in Västergötland.  Snorre records that Ragnvald accompanied Ingegerd to Russia and was installed as Earl of La
2 CONC doga[71].  '''married  firstly INGEBORG Trygvesdatter, daughter of TRYGVE Olavsson of Norway & his wife Åstrid Eiriksdatter.''' Snorre records the marriage of Ingebjorg, Trygve's daughter, King Olaf's sister and Earl Ragnvald, Ulf
2 CONC 's son"[72].   '''married  secondly [as her first husband,] ASTRID Njalsdotter, daughter of NJAL & his wife.'''  The primary source which confirms her parentage and two marriages has not yet been identified.  [She married secondly
2 CONC  as his second wife, Emund Slemme den Gamle/the Old King of Sweden.  Her supposed second marriage to Ragnvald may be nothing more than a guess based on Adam of Bremen recording that nepos eius [=rex Sueonum Emund] Stinkel succeede
2 CONC d on the death of Emund[73].]  
2 CONT
2 CONT '''Jarl Ragnvald & his first wife had two children:'''
2 CONT
2 CONT >>>>* i)          '''ULF''' Snorre names "Earl Ulf and Earl Eilif" as the sons of Ragnvald & his wife[74]. 
2 CONT >>>>* ii)         '''EILIF''  names "Earl Ulf and Earl Eilif" as the sons of Ragnvald & his wife[75]. 
2 CONT
2 CONT '''Jarl Ragnvald & his second wife had one child:'''
2 CONT
2 CONT >>>>* iii)       ''' STENKIL Ragnvaldson''' (-1066).  The primary source which confirms his parentage has not yet been identified.  He succeeded [his stepfather] in 1060 as STENKIL King of Sweden.   
2 CONT
2 CONT * 2.         '''SIGRID "Storråda/the Haughty'''.  Snorre names Sigrid as daughter of "Skoglar" Toste and refers to her '''marriage to "the Swedish king, Eirik the Victorious'''  Saxo Grammaticus names "Syritha" as mother of "Erici
2 CONC  filius Olavus"[77].  The Fagrskinna names Sigrid, mother of King Olof, as daughter of Skoglar-Tosta[78].  Morkinskinna names "Sigridr en stórráda" as mother of “the lady Ástrídr…sister of two kings, Knútr the Great and Óláfr the 
2 CONC Swede” who married “Jarl Úlfr sprakaleggr”[79].  '''married firstly ([before 985]) ERIK "Segersäll/the Victorious" King of Sweden, son of [EMUND Erikson King of Sweden]''' (-Uppsala [994/95]). '''married secondly ([1000]) as his s
2 CONC econd wife, SVEND I "Tveskæg/Forkbeard" King of Denmark, son of HARALD I "Blåtand/Bluetooth" King of Denmark & his first wife Gunhild''' ([960]-Gainsborough 3 Feb 1014, bur in England, later removed to Roskilde).   
2 CONT
2 CONT '''Source''' Project MedLands, Sweden Kings - https://fmg.ac/Projects/MedLands/SWEDEN.htm#IngeIdied1111
2 CONT
2 CONT ==Entries:==
2 CONT Skoglar Toste resembles an Icelandic fairy tale tradition, a powerful magnate of the Vikings sprung from the soil of Vastergotland (West Gothland). Skoglar (Skauglar) is mentioned by Saxo and Odd Snorresson, etc.
2 CONT
2 CONT During the 900s, he was a wealthy magnate with substantial holdings in both Vastergotland and [https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/V%C3%A4rmland Varmland], from which sources he was able to live in the castle Aranas. The name Skauglar c
2 CONC omes from the Valkyries, and it is said that Skagul accompanies him personally on his Viking trips in order to constantly make sure that he won.
2 CONT
2 CONT A rune stone in the outer forecourt of Toste says that he was probably the first Viking to demand "danegeld" from England, in 970 (21 years before Edward the Unready). Danegeld was the silver that the English paid in order to esca
2 CONC pe Viking ravages, a form of extortion. The revenue from this allowed Toste to buy large tracts of land in Vadsbo county, Narke, and Varmland.
2 CONT
2 CONT Parts of these lands are recorded in Valdemar's yearbook from 1231. The book still identified a farm named Sigrid Levete, which indicates land by which his daughter Sigrid was assigned to live by. In 1231, there was yet farms held
2 CONC  by 8 descendants of Toste.
2 CONT
2 CONT Skoglar Toste or Skoglar Tosti (there are several variations) was a chieftain from the Swedish province of West Götaland. According to Snorri Sturluson, he was the father of Sigrid the Haughty. For some time he gave refuge to Hara
2 CONC ld Grenske, who later came back to woo Sigrid, only to be killed by her for his persistence. Toste is mentioned in several sagas, such as Heimskringla, and is said to have been the first to demand danegeld, in 970. Toste's great-g
2 CONC randson Stenkil became the King of Sweden in 1060.
2 CONT
2 CONT (Norwegian Wikipedia says that his names, Skagul, Skauglar, or Skogul, are linguistic variations in Old Norse, all of which means "Battle". Skagul Toste, or "Fighter Toste, was thus a hard and stubborn man, which may confirm that 
2 CONC he may have been the same Toste who ravaged England and one of the first to require gold in order to spare the English destruction, as early as 970 - Ben notes this is 21 years before Edward the Unready made the first really big p
2 CONC ayment.)
2 CONT
2 CONT According to Snorri Sturluson, he was the father of Sigrid the Haughty (OUR ANCESTOR). For some time he gave refuge to Harald Grenske (father of King Olav Haraldsson), who later came back to woo Sigrid, only to be killed by her fo
2 CONC r his persistence. (Norwegian Wikipedia says that she killed also his large entourage, which included Tore from Bjarkoy, father of Tore Hund, after they were rendered helpless by drink. Sigrid carried this out to teach everyone no
2 CONC t to believe that she would marry anyone.)
2 CONT
2 CONT Toste is mentioned in several sagas, such as Heimskringla, and is said to have been the first to demand danegeld (payment to not ravage), in 970. 
2 CONT
2 CONT Toste's great-grandson Stenkil became the King of Sweden in 1060.
2 CONT
2 CONT His name skoglar, skauglar or skagul is due to his experience in battle (skagul is one of the many names for battle in Old Norse).
2 CONT
2 CONT ==Children according to the sagas==
2 CONT
2 CONT 1.Ulf Tostesson jarl.
2 CONT
2 CONT 2.Sigrid the Haughty, queen of Sweden.
2 CONT
2 CONT ==Sources:==
2 CONT
2 CONT # Royal Genealogical Data, Hull, England
2 CONT # Ancestral Roots of Certain American Colonists Who Came to America Before 1700 by Frederick Lewis Weis, Lines: 241-5, 243A-20
2 CONT # From the Swedish-language of http://historiska-personer.nu/  [https://cse.google.com/cse?cx=012201696175632605838:dbj7sli6rda&q=skoglar-toste&oq=Skog&gs_l=partner-generic.1.0.0.12900.14403.0.16642.4.3.0.1.1.0.196.314.2j1.3.0.gsn
2 CONC os%2Cn%3D13...0.1460j809454j5..1ac.1.25.partner-generic..1.3.119.VFca7b4n9F8 Historiska Personer i Sverige och Norden - Skoglar Toste]
2 CONT
2 CONT * http://www.espell.se/saga/p86f2cb4e.html
2 CONT * http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Skagul_Toste
2 CONT *http://fmg.ac/Projects/MedLands/SWEDEN.htm
2 CONT
2 CONT ===Runestone===
2 CONT At Vallentuna, near Stockholm, the runestone of Orkesta ([https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Orkesta_Runestones U 344]) says:
2 CONT
2 CONT in ulfr hafir onklati * Þru kialtakat Þit uas fursta Þis tursti * Þa ---Þurktil * Þa kalt knutr
2 CONT
2 CONT Translation: "But Ulf has taken three danegelds in England. The first one was with Toste, the second one with Thorkel and the third one with Canute the Great".
2 CONT
2 CONT From the Foundation for Medieval Genealogy page on Sweden (Chapter 2):
2 CONT * http://fmg.ac/Projects/MedLands/SWEDEN.htm
2 CONT
2 CONT "Skoglar" TOSTE, son of ---.  In Svithjod.  Snorre records that Harald "Grenske" was welcomed in Svithjod by "Toste…often in battle…therefore called Skoglar-Toste" and lived five years with him.  
2 CONT
2 CONT m ---.  The name of Toste's wife is not known.  
2 CONT
2 CONT Toste & his wife had two children:  
2 CONT * Ulf (married to unknown, father of Ragnvald Ulfsson)
2 CONT * Sigrid "Storrada, or The Haughty" (married firstly Erik The Victorious, King of Sweden, secondly to Svend I "Forkbeard" King of Denmark)
2 CONT
