2 CONT
2 CONT '''ROTBALD''' [I], son of --- (-[949]).  His parentage is not known. ''It has been speculated that he was the son of [https://www.geni.com/people/Boson-d-Arles-margrave-of-Tuscany/6000000007043482057 Boso Marchese of Tuscany], for
2 CONC  onomastic reasons, but that Boso is not known to have had any sons[149].  In any case, Boso was a reasonably common name in the area at that time.''  <br/>
2 CONT Rotbald supported [https://www.geni.com/people/Louis-III-the-Blind-Holy-Roman-Emperor/6000000002205613665 King Louis III "the Blind"'s] campaign in Italy in 900 and his efforts to be crowned emperor in Feb 901. 
2 CONT
2 CONT '''m''' ---.  The wife of Rotbald is not known.  ''It has been speculated, for onomastic reasons only, that she was --- d'Aquitaine, daughter of [https://www.geni.com/people/Guillaume-I-the-Pious-Count-of-Auvergne-Duke-of-Aquitain
2 CONC e/6000000000571768859 Guillaume "le Pieux" Duke of Aquitaine] & his wife [https://www.geni.com/people/Engelberge-de-Provence/6000000000571768870 Engelberga de Provence], but there appears to be no other basis for this suggestion[1
2 CONC 50].  ''
2 CONT
2 CONT Rotbald & his wife had two children: 
2 CONT #       BOSON (-after Oct [965/67].   .. ...
2 CONT #       GUILLAUME [I] (-after Mar 965). .. ...
2 CONT
