2 CONT OCCU 1st Duke of Normandy,876.
2 CONT SOUR GWALTNEY.ANC (Compuserve) says 847; www.gendex.com  says ABT 846; Royalty for
2 CONT Commoners, Roderick W. Stuart, p. 123 says c870; members.aol.com/sargen3 says
2 CONT ABT 854, Maer; misc.traveller.com/genealogy/gedhtml/kmilburn say 845;
2 CONT SOUR Americans of Royal Descent, p. 25, 30;COMYN4.TAF,p6;ROYAL.THD say 932;
2 CONT COMYNI.GED (Compuserve) says ABT 933,NORM.TAF (Compuserve) (says 933);
2 CONT GWALTNEY.ANC 508044998 says d. 931;Royalty for Commoners p. 123 says 927-932
2 CONT SOUR www.gendex.com
2 CONT SOUR Americans of Royal Descent, Charles H. Browning
2 CONT Royalty for Commoners, Roderick W. Stuart, p. 123
2 CONT COMYNI.GED (Compuserve)
2 CONT PAGE 409
2 CONT Founder of the royal House of Normandy and England, 1st Duke of Normandy, 912
2 CONT Americans of Royal Descent, Charles H. Browning, p. 25; Hralfr Gongen Rollo -
2 CONT COMYN4.TAF (Compuserve Roots), p. 6; Gonge Rolf (Marching Rolf) "Rollo the
2 CONT Dane", 1st Duke of Normandy - NORM.TAF (Compuserve); Established the duchy
2 CONT of Normandy, a Viking - The Conquest of England, Eric Linklater, p. 7
2 CONT ROLLO THE DANE, son of ROGNVALD THE RICH and RAGNHILD NEFIA, settled in Normandy and traced his descent through eleven generation from a king called Fornjot who ruled in Finland.  His alleged
2 CONT  ancestors-or most of them- are mythical creatures, but the 
2 CONT tale of their exploits is, quite clearly, a fabulous recital of the discovery and exploration of Norway; and from such an ancestry an appetite for discovery, a zest for exploration, certainly
2 CONT  survived to animate the viking age - The Conquest of 
2 CONT England, Eric
2 CONT Linklater, p. 12
2 CONT Younger son, was a great viking.  He grew so tall that no horse could carry him-but probably the Norwegian horses were no bigger than an Iceland pony to-day-and because he had to go upon his own feet
2 CONT  he was known as Marching Rolf [Gongu-hrolfr].  He 
2 CONT offended king Harald Fairhair by harrying and
2 CONT committing what was called a 'strand-slaying' in the great gulf of south Oslo, and was outlawed.  He followed a customary viking path to the Hebrides, and remained their long enough to beget a
2 CONT  daughter who later married a Scots kinglet.  Rolf may have 
2 CONT adventured in Ireland, England and the valley of the Loire, but Icelandic annals say firmly that he won his place in Normandy in 898; and if that is true he must have spent thirteen years in
2 CONT  establishing the power that Charles the Simple confirmed in 
2 CONT 911.  He served a lively apprenticeship to war, and a distinguished father must, in the beginning, have helped him to enlist followers whom his own success in arms would later multiply. - The
2 CONT  Conquest of England, Eric Linklater, p. 24
2 CONT Count of Rouen - WIVES.TXT (Compuserve)
2 CONT Rollo (Rollon, Ranger Rolf), Count of Rouen; conquered Normandy; Popa was his 2nd wife - Royalty for Commoners, Roderick W. Stuart, p. 123-124
2 CONT Rolf became known as Robert or Rollo in Normandy. I have shown them as father and son but this is really a way of showing how his attribution changed. AKA Rolf Wend-a-foot Acceded 911  -
2 CONT  http://gendex.com/users/daver/rigney/D0001/G0000001.html#I1257
2 CONT
