2 CONT DATE 911
1 NOTE Rollo was the Frankish-Latin name taken by Hrolf Ganger (Rolf the Walker, because he was too big for any horse to carry him) He was also called Robert. His father was the 1st Earl of the Orkneys and Rollo was the 2nd son, and left
2 CONC  home to find landttle not to plunder. He made a treaty with the French King Charles the Simple that, for being given land around Rouen, he would convert to Christianity and defend the Seine River from other raiding Vikings. This 
2 CONC is today's upper Normandy and he pase Duchy of Normandy to his son, William Longsword. He was a direct ancestor of William the Conqueror and a direct ancestor of Elizabeth II
1 NOTE  Randy Wilson, Overview Chart of Lineal Ancestors of King Edward
2 CONT of England and Philippa of Hainault.
2 CONT
2 CONT B.S. Bachrach 1993, Fulk Nerra, the Neo-Roman Consul, 987-1040,
2 CONT Genealogy 10. Rollo, Count of Rouen, died 933.
2 CONT
2 CONT First Duke of Normandy.
2 CONT
2 CONT Index to Royal Genealogical Data, University of Hull WEB database,
2 CONT 1995. Became Duke 911. Originally Rolf the Ganger, he became known
2 CONT as Robert or Rollo in Normandy.
2 CONT
2 CONT Rollo = Rolf the Ganger = Rollo-Gange-Rolf = Gamego Rolf = Roll =
2 CONT Rou = G'ngu-Hr~lfr = Rolof the Walker = Hrolf the Ganger. He is
2 CONT reputedly to have been so large that he could not ride a horse, but
2 CONT had to walk, i.e. gang afoot. Apparently, Rollo was one of the
2 CONT northern raiders who seized land held by Charles the Simple (879-
2 CONT 929). By the Treaty of St. Clair-sur-Epte, Rollo paid homage to
2 CONT Charles in 911. After an initial period of peace and
2 CONT acculturization, the northerners again began to expand their
2 CONT territories.
2 CONT
2 CONT Parentage based on the Orkneying Saga of the late 12th century.
2 CONT Norman sources say Rollo was of Danish origin. The identification of
2 CONT Hrolf with Rollo as above may be suspect. Cf. Stewart Baldwin,
2 CONT soc.genealogy.medieval, 21 March 1998.
2 CONT
2 CONT Tom Aiken, 15 July 1997, soc.genealogy.medieval. Robert (Rollo) I,
2 CONT ks. Normandii, 846-931.
2 CONT
2 CONT Todd A. Farmerie, post to soc.genealogy.medieval, 8 January 1999.
2 CONT Circa 870 - circa 930. Rollo may or may not be the son of Ragnwald
2 CONT Eysteinsson.
2 CONT
2 CONT LDS Ancestral File, 4 November 2001. Of Maer, Nord-Trondelag,
2 CONT Norway. Died circa 891.
1 NOTE In the year 0911 Rollo laid siege to Chartres, but was repulsedby the forces of Charles III. However, the King saw theopportunity to achieve an accordance with the Vikings and hearranged a meeting with Rollo at St. Clair-sur-Epte 
2 CONC (betweenParis and Rouen). A stained glass window in the chapel that wasthe site of the meeting commemorates the treaty struck at themeeting. Rollo was granted Normandy as a Dukedom and the titleCount of Rouen in return for his all
2 CONC egiance to Charles III.Rollo kept this bargain and was later baptised as a Christian.
2 CONT Rollo's Vikings melded into the local culture fairly rapidly,taking local wives and concubines so that their children grew upspeaking the Frankish language. In time, most traces of the oldViking ways of Scandinavia and the Danelaw
2 CONC  of Englanddisappeared from Normandy.
2 CONT Also Rolf "the Walker", because, being so tall, he preferred togo afoot rather than ride the little Norwegian horses.
2 CONT Second wife: Gisele, Duchess of Normandy, b. abt 0895 inNormandy, France; d. 0919 (Dsp?); married: bef 0915.
2 CONT Conquered Normandy in 0912.
