2 CONT (Wiki)
2 CONT
2 CONT Saint Mathilda (or Matilda, c. 895 – 14 March 968) was the wife of King Henry I of Germany, the first ruler of the Saxon Ottonian (or Liudolfing) dynasty, thereby Duchess (consort) of Saxony from 912 and Queen (consort) of Germany
2 CONC  (East Francia) from 919 until her husband's death in 936. Their eldest son Otto succeeded his father as King of Germany (East Francia) and years later was crowned Holy Roman Emperor in 962, thus ending the vacancy of this office 
2 CONC begun in 924 with the death of Holy Roman Emperor Berengar I of Italy. Matilda lived to see the imperial crown restored under her son. Matilda's surname refers to Ringelheim, where her comital (of or relating to a count or earl) I
2 CONC mmedinger relatives established a convent about 940.
2 CONT --------------------
2 CONT from http://wc.rootsweb.ancestry.com/cgi-bin/igm.cgi?op=GET&db=janrobison&id=I48477
2 CONT
2 CONT >Second wife of Henry the Fowler. RC 338 says born about 900, which would be rather young (9) for a normal marriage age. It adds, "Mathilda's birthdate would seem to imply that she was the daughter of Gisela (of Lorraine ) , but t
2 CONC his is not certain." K. calls her Mathilde von Sachsen.
2 CONT
2 CONT >Her feast day is 14th March
2 CONT
2 CONT ----
2 CONT
2 CONT '''MATHILDE ([896]-Quedlinburg 14 Mar 968, bur Quedlinburg Stiftskirche) Lay Abbess of Nivelles'''
2 CONT d/o THEODERIC (-8 Nov 917) & REGINLIND [Reinhild]
2 CONT x  (Wallhausen 909) HEINRICH I "der Vogelsteller/the Fowler" King of Germany 
2 CONT
2 CONT https://fmg.ac/Projects/MedLands/SAXONY.htm#AmalradaMEberhard
2 CONT ----
2 CONT
2 CONT THEODERIC (-8 Nov 917).  Widukind names "Thiadrici" as father of Queen Mathilde, specifying that the family was "stirpis magni ducis Widukindi"[47].  The father of Queen Mathilde is named "Thietricus" in the Vita Mathildis Reginæ[
2 CONC 48].  m REGINLIND [Reinhild], daughter of --- (-11 May ----).  The wife of Theoderich is named "Reinhildam, Danorum Fresonumque germine procreatam" in the Vita Mathildis Reginæ[49].  According to Europäische Stammtafeln[50], she w
2 CONC as Reinhild, daughter of Gotfrid the Dane & his wife Gisela [Carolingian], which is presumably a guess based on this description in the Vita Mathildis.  However, the chronology is not ideal.  Regino records the marriage in 882 of 
2 CONC "Gisla filia Hlotharii" and "rex Godofridus Nordmannorum"[51].  If this couple's daughter was the mother of Queen Mathilde, the latter's estimated birth date (see below) would need to be pushed forward by several years, which make
2 CONC s the chronology for her known descendants tight.  A better fit may be Reginlind, [sister of Bovo Bishop of Chalons, daughter of ---].  The known sister of Bishop Bovo was Frederuna, wife of Charles III "le Simple" King of the Fra
2 CONC nks.  The hypothesis that there was another sister married to Theoderic would explain (1) the name Frederuna being transmitted to Regenhild's daughter, and (2) Berenger Bishop of Cambrai, recorded elsewhere as nepos of Queen Frede
2 CONC runa, being described as "…Ottonis imperatoris proxime consanguineus" in the Gesta Episcoporum Cameracensium[52].  If this is correct, the reference to Reginlind being "Danorum Fresonumque germine procreatam" has not been explaine
2 CONC d.  A list of names in the Libri Confraternitatum Sancti Galli sets out (in order) "Thieterich, Reginhilt, *, Oto, Amalrat, Perectheid, Friderun, Pia", immediately after a list of family members of Heinrich I King of Germany and h
2 CONC is wife, which no doubt refers to the latter's parents and sisters, "Oto" being the only person not so far identified[53].  The list is undated but was presumably written during the period [929/36] as King Heinrich's son-in-law Du
2 CONC ke Giselbert is included (married in [928/29]) but not his son-in-law Hugues Duc des Francs (married in 937).  The necrology of Merseburg records the death "11 May" of "Reinhild mater regine Mahtildis"[54].  Theoderic & his wife h
2 CONC ad seven children: 
2 CONT
2 CONT iv)        MATHILDE ([896]-Quedlinburg 14 Mar 968, bur Quedlinburg Stiftskirche).  Widukind names "Mahthilda" as wife of King Heinrich, also naming her father and three brothers[58].  Thietmar names Mathilde as daughter of "Dietri
2 CONC ch and Reinhild" when recording her marriage to Heinrich, and specifies that she was "a descendant of the lineage of King Widukind"[59].  Her alleged descent from Widukind is also referred to in the Vita Mahthildis[60].  Thietmar 
2 CONC records that Quedlinburg was bestowed on Mathilde as part of her dower 16 Sep 929[61], and that she established the convent there thirty days after the death of her husband[62].  Lay Abbess of Nivelles.  The necrology of Fulda rec
2 CONC ords the death "968 II Id Mar" of "Mahthild regina"[63].  m (Wallhausen 909) as his second wife, HEINRICH Graf, son of OTTO "der Erlauchte" Graf im Südthüringau & his wife Hedwig [Babenberg] ([876]-Memleben 2 Jul 936, bur Quedlinb
2 CONC urg Stiftskirche).  He was elected as HEINRICH I "der Vogelsteller/the Fowler" King of Germany at Fritzlar 6 May 919. 
2 CONT
2 CONT https://fmg.ac/Projects/MedLands/SAXONY.htm#AmalradaMEberhard
