1 NOTE Matilda of Ringelheim (born in 892,died 14 May 968 ) was the wife of Henry I the Fowler , emperor of the Holy Roman Empire , whom she married in 909 . Their son, Otto, succeeded his father as Otto I the Great .
2 CONT Matilda founded many religious  institutions including the Abbey of Quedlinburg . She was later canonized .
1 NOTE St. Mathilda was the daughter of the Westphalian count Dietrich and his wife Reinhild, and her biographers traced her ancestry back to the famed Saxon hero, Blessed Widukind (c. 730 - 807). 
