2 CONT In those fighting , HEINRICH had recognized the importance of a place that had long played a role as a border festival against the Sorbs. It was Merseburg that was in the early stages of urban development and whose "old castle" be
2 CONC longed to Count Erwin . In the mighty belt, the goods of the Liudolfing house moved from the Harz to S-Thuringia, westwards to Eichsfeld and Hersfeld Abbey, from the Elbe to Werra and Fulda. There was only one major gap in this mo
2 CONC ve: on that Saalebogen, as crowning and dominating the country was Merseburg. From here, the''' count Erwin den Hasgau''' and den , who had probably been tested and perhaps fallen in the border fightGau Friesenfeld (Frisonenfeld) 
2 CONC managed.''' His daughters were two daughters; one of them, Hatheburg , married but''' '''widowed again''', the other unknown by name and fate. The Church had focused on the rich and politically significant inheritance; under her i
2 CONC nfluence, Hatheburg probably took the veil.
