2 CONT   NAME Heinrich I "The Fowler" King Of The /GERMANS/
1 NOTE _P_CCINFO 2-2438
1 NOTE Original individual @P3960083042@ (@MS_TREE2.GED0_15GM2@) merged with @P3960083320@ (@MS_TREE2.GED0_15GM2@)
1 NOTE _P_CCINFO 2-2438
1 NOTE The first of the Saxon line of German kings. In 912 Henri succeeded his 
2 CONT father as duke of Saxony. Following the death of Conrad I, king of 
2 CONT Germany, in 918, Henri was chosen king by the Franconian and Saxon nobles. 
2 CONT Bavaria, Swabia, and Lotharingia refused to acknowledge him at first, and 
2 CONT it was not until 925 that he managed to win recognition from all the 
2 CONT German states. In 926 Henri secured a nine-year truce from warfare with 
2 CONT the Magyars. During that period he transformed many of the small towns of 
2 CONT Germany into fortified cities with trained troops of mounted warriors. His 
2 CONT military preparations were successfully tested in a war against the Wends 
2 CONT in 929. When the Magyars invaded Thuringia in 933, Henri repulsed them 
2 CONT decisively. He defeated the Danes in the following year and seized 
2 CONT territory from them. Henri was the first to create a united Germany, and, 
2 CONT although he never received the imperial crown, he is generally recognized 
2 CONT as one of the Holy Roman emperors. He was succeeded by his son, Otto.
1 NOTE GJ
1 NOTE GJ=Gary Jacobson www.garyjacobson.org/ahnentafel.html 
1 NOTE KNOWN AS "AUCEPS""THE FOWLER"; DUKE OF SAXONY; EMPORER OF GERMANY 912-926;
2 CONT EMPORER OF THE WEST 919-936
1 NOTE 33 great grandfather,and also the Duke of Saxony
1 NOTE Emperor of Germany or King of Saxons 912-936.
1 NOTE The first of the Saxon line of German kings. In 912 Henri succeededhis father as duke of Saxony. Following the death of Conrad I, king ofGermany, in 918, Henri was chosen king by the Franconian and Saxonnobles. Bavaria, Swabia, an
2 CONC d Lotharingia refused to acknowledge him atfirst, and it was not until 925 that he managed to win recognitionfrom all the German states. In 926 Henri secured a nine-year trucefrom warfare with the Magyars. During that period he tr
2 CONC ansformed manyof the small towns of Germany into fortified cities with trainedtroops of mounted warriors. His military preparations weresuccessfully tested in a war against the Wends in 929. When theMagyars invaded Thuringia in 93
2 CONC 3, Henri repulsed them decisively. Hedefeated the Danes in the following year and seized territory fromthem. Henri was the first to create a united Germany, and, although henever received the imperial crown, he is generally recogn
2 CONC ized as oneof the Holy Roman emperors. He was succeeded by his son, Otto.
1 NOTE Henrik I av Sachsen, også kalt Henrik I Fuglefangeren, tysk: Heinrich der Finkler eller Heinrich der Vogler (født 876, død 2. juli 936), var konge av Tyskland i perioden 919-936. Enkelte kilder omtaler ham som keiser. Han var Sac
2 CONC hsens første konge innen ?det ottonske dynasti?, da han var sønn til hertug Otto av Sachsen.
2 CONT
2 CONT Henrik var gift med Matilda av Ringelheim, datter av hertug Teodebert av Westfalen.
2 CONT
2 CONT Han ble konge etter sin onkel Konrad I etter at han på sin dødsseng overtalte han sin bror, markgreve Eberhard av Franken, om å tilby kronen til Henrik som var en av hans hovedmotstandere. Grunnen var at han så på Henrik som d
2 CONC en eneste prinsen som var i stand til å holde kongedømmet sammen mot de interne stridighetene blant hertugene og mot de pågående invasjonene til madjarene. Eberhard og den øvrige frankiske adelen aksepterte Konrads råd, og Hen
2 CONC rik ble valgt til konge som Henrik I i 919 ved Fritzlar.
2 CONT
2 CONT Henrik invaderte de nordiske områdene, hvor danskene hadde beseiret friserne og gjorde i følge munken og historikeren Widukind av Corvey i sin bok Rex gestae Saxonicae den danske konen til vasall under Henrik. Han inntok også om
2 CONC råder som hadde tilhørt venderne etter at disse hadde angrepet Tyskland sammen med danskene. Videre erobret han Slesvig i 934.
2 CONT
2 CONT Han erobret videre hertugdømmet Bayern og kongedømmet Lorraine og ga disse som arveland til sine barn.
2 CONT
2 CONT Da han døde av slag i sitt palass i Memleben var alle de tyske stammene samlet til et rike og Henrik blir derfor ansett som den første tyske kongen og den som la grunnlaget for Det tysk-romerske riket. Dette ble fullført av hans s
2 CONC ønn Otto.
2 CONT
2 CONT Barn
2 CONT Keiser Otto I, født 912, død 973 
2 CONT Gerberga av Sachsen, født 913, død 5. mai 984, gift med hertug Gilbert av Lorraine, deretter Ludvig IV av Frankrike 
2 CONT Henrik I av Bayern, født 919, død 955 
2 CONT Hedvig av Sachsen, født 922, gift med Hugo den store, hertug av Franken og de var foreldre til Hugo Capet 
2 CONT Bruno, erkebiskop av Köln, født 925, død 965 
1 NOTE Source: The Rufus Parks Pedigree by Brian J.L. Berry.  Chart: pages  55 & 56
2 CONT Page 54:
2 CONT 5b.	Henry the Fowler, 867-2 July 936, so called because he was hawking in the Hartz Mountians when he was notified of his election by the nobles to succeed Conrad I as emperor 919.  He succeeded his father as Duke of Saxony 864.  
2 CONC He was often at war over disputed lands as well as with plundering Magyars.  He mar. (2) Mechtilde, dau. of Dietrich, count of Ringelheim.  Henry d. in his palace at Memleben [and] was bur. at Quedlinburg.
2 CONT
2 CONT Page 58:
2 CONT 9.	Henry I the Fowler 876-2 July 936; Duke of Saxony, emperor; mar. (2) Mechtilde, dau. of Dietrich, Count of Ringelheim.
2 CONT
2 CONT !Availability: The libraries of Ken, Karen, Kristen, Kevin, Brian, Amy, Adam and FAL
2 CONT
2 CONT Source: "Ancestral Roots of Sixty Colonists" by Frederick Lewis Weis.
2 CONT Page121 line (141-18):
2 CONT 18.	Henry I, the fowler, b. 876, d. Memleben, 2 Jul. 936, Duke of Saxony, King of the Saxons 912-936; m. (2) Mechtilde, dau. of Count Dietrich of Ringelheim.  (CCN 495).
