2 CONT
2 CONT ===Biography
2 CONT
2 CONT -https://fmg.ac/Projects/MedLands/CENTRAL%20FRANCE.htm#ThibautIdied975
2 CONT
2 CONT 2.        ''' HUGUES de Blois''' ([946/47]-2 Jan 986, bur Marmoutier).  His parentage is confirmed by his mother’s [980] charter cited above.  Bijard suggests his birth “circa 946/47”[78], which is a reasonable suggestion.  "Hugon
2 CONC is archiepiscopi filii Theobaldi comitis" subscribed the charter dated 950 [presumably misdated] under which Ragnfred Bishop of Chartres donated property to Chartres Saint-Père[79].  Archbishop of Bourges 969.  The Annales Masciac
2 CONC enses record the ordination in 969 of “Ugo in...sede Biturigensium...archiepiscopus”[80].  "Ledgardis" donated property to "Sancti Petri Carnotensis ecclesiam", for the souls of "senioris mei…comitis Tedbaldi…patris mei Heirberti,
2 CONC  Trecassini comitis", with the consent of "archipresule…Hugone et…comite Odone, filiis meis", by charter dated 5 Feb 978, signed by "…Emma comitissa Pictavæ urbis…"[81].  "Hugonis ducis, Odonis comitis, Hugonis sanctæ Bituricensis
2 CONC  archipræsulis, Letgardis comitissæ, Bertæ comitissæ, Gauzfridi vicecomitis…" subscribed the charter dated 985 under which "Robertus" donated property to "Sancti Petri Carnotensis", on the advice of "Odonem, simul cum sua matre Le
2 CONC dgarde, pariterque dominam meam Bertam, ipsius æque coniugem"[82].  The necrology of Chartres Cathedral records the death “IV Non Jan” of “Hugo Bituricensis archiepiscopus et canonicus Sanctæ Mariæ”[83].  The necrology of Saint-Pè
2 CONC re-en-Vallée records the death "IV Non Jan" of "Hugo Bituricensis archiepiscopus filius comitisse Legardis", recording that they jointly donated "Gesiacum…predia"[84].  “Odo comes” restored “villam...Culturas” to Marmoutier, for t
2 CONC he souls of “...domini Hugonis archiepiscopi, cujus ibi corpus...jacet”, by charter dated to [986], subscribed by “Berte comitissæ uxoris eius, majoris filii eius Teutboldi, filii eius Odonis adhuc in cunabulo”[85]. 
2 CONT
2 CONT ----
2 CONT
2 CONT https://fr.wikipedia.org/wiki/Hugues_de_Blois
2 CONT
2 CONT Hugues de Blois, died in 985/986, was a French prelate in the 19th century, archbishop of Bourges.
2 CONT
2 CONT Hugues is the second son of Count [https://www.geni.com/people/Theobald-I-the-Trickster-count-of-Blois/6000000003243439507 Thibaud I of Blois] and Liutgarde of Vermandois, and brother of Eudes I of Blois. He succeeded his uncle Ri
2 CONC chard as Archbishop of Bourges in 969.
2 CONT
2 CONT The eldest of the siblings, also named Thibaud, died around 960-962, while a difficult war took place with Normandy, ranging from Évrecin to Brittany[1], via the southern confines of the Orne. Hugues being destined for an ecclesia
2 CONC stical career, it is the youngest Eudes I who will inherit the count titles and profits. Nevertheless, before his accession to the seat of Bourges, Hugues de Blois will have other secular or clerical offices, especially those atta
2 CONC ched to the abbey of Coulombs before the end of the 950s[2]. This same source suggests that he would be the first of the Hugos to be a castellan of Nogent. What would make him the agnatic ancestor or even the father of 
2 CONT
2 CONT *Roger I of Blois,
2 CONT *  Hugues de Beauvais and 
2 CONT * Héloïse de Pithiviers[3]. 
2 CONT
2 CONT The cognatic contribution passing through a daughter of Roger II of Laon[4].
2 CONT
2 CONT One of the few acts of his ministry dates from 983, where he seized the Saint-Sulpice Chapel of Jalvardan, which seems to depend on either the parish of Plaimpied-Givaudins or that of Lazenay.
2 CONT
2 CONT ----
2 CONT
2 CONT https://de.wikipedia.org/wiki/Hugues_de_Beauvais
2 CONT
2 CONT Hugues de Beauvais (* before 970; † before May 1008) was a French aristocrat of the Middle Ages, who was Count of the Kingdom after 991 and until his death.
2 CONT
2 CONT Hugues de Beauvais is probably a member of the family of the Counts of Blois, a grandson[1][2] of Theobald I († 975) and a son of the Archbishop of Bourges Hugues de Blois († 985/986); his other, cognatic origins, which were hinte
2 CONC d at by Christian Settipani[3] and Jean-Noël Mathieu[4], associate him with the family of the Counts of Laon.
2 CONT
2 CONT Hugues de Beauvais was the oldest of three siblings,[2] the other two were Roger de Blois, Bishop of Beauvais, and Héloïse de Pithiviers.
2 CONT
2 CONT His wife is not known, but studies by historian and archaeologist Adolphe de Dion[14] connect her with the region around Nogent-le-Roi and Épernon. Hugues de Beauvais had no descendants.
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT ----
2 CONT
2 CONT [https://fr.wikipedia.org/wiki/Héloïse_de_Pithiviers Héloïse of Pithiviers] at French Wikipedia
2 CONT
2 CONT Héloïse (or Helvide or Helvise) of Pithiviers (or Blois), lady of Pithiviers, was born between 965 and 970 and died before 1025.
2 CONT
2 CONT She is the sister of Roger de Blois, bishop of Beauvais in 999-1022 and probably of the Palatine Count Hugues de Beauvais. 
2 CONT
2 CONT Historians[1],[2] have demonstrated several times that she cannot be the daughter of [https://www.geni.com/people/Odo-I-count-of-Blois/6000000002043186469 Count Eudes I of Blois] and [https://www.geni.com/people/Berthe-de-Bourgogn
2 CONC e-reine-consort-de-France/6000000009756433107 Berthe of Burgundy] [3].
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT -----------
2 CONT
2 CONT Reste d'actualité une hypothèse reprenant un manuscrit de l'abbé d'Espagnac[4], où le père de [https://www.geni.com/people/Roger-de-Blois-1st-comte-%C3%A9v%C3%AAque-de-Beauvais/6000000223153030851?through=6000000223152842883 Roger
2 CONC ] serait '''Hugues de Blois''', archevêque de Bourges, fils de [https://www.geni.com/people/Theobald-I-the-Trickster-count-of-Blois/6000000003243439507 Thibaud le Tricheur], ce qui permet de préserver le lien agnatique avec la Mai
2 CONC son de Blois (plus tard de Blois-Champagne) ; il serait alors le neveu du comte Eudes Ier de Blois et le cousin germain d'Eudes II[5],[6]. On verrait de surcroît en Roger et sa sœur Héloïse des enfants d'Helvise, une fille de Roge
2 CONC r II, comte de Laon et de Bolenois. Les noms Roger et Helvise/Helvide/Héloïse se retrouvent chez les comtes de Laon) : il y aurait donc un lien cognatique avec cette dernière famille. Par les recoupements qu'on vient d'évoquer, il
2 CONC  serait donc bien le frère[6] du comte palatin Hugues de Beauvais.
2 CONT
2 CONT * https://fr.wikipedia.org/wiki/Roger_Ier_de_Blois#Famille
2 CONT
2 CONT One hypothesis remains relevant, based on a manuscript by Abbot d'Espagnac,[4] which suggests that Roger's father was Hugh of Blois, Archbishop of Bourges, son of Theobald the Trickster. This would preserve the agnatic link with t
2 CONC he House of Blois (later Blois-Champagne); he would then be the nephew of Count Odo I of Blois and the first cousin of Odo II.[5],[6]  Furthermore, Roger and his sister Heloise would be considered children of Helvise, a daughter o
2 CONC f Roger II, Count of Laon and Bolenois. The names Roger and Helvise/Helvide/Heloise are found among the Counts of Laon, thus establishing a cognatic link with that family. Based on the connections mentioned above, he would therefo
2 CONC re indeed be the brother[6] of the Count Palatine Hugh of Beauvais.
2 CONT
2 CONT
