1 NOTE 55449052. Grev Rainer III RAINERSON Hainaut was born in 920. He was a Greve between 932 and 973 in Hainaut. He died in 973. He was married to Adele N.NSDTR
2 CONT
2 CONT 55449112. Grev Reginar III REGINARSON av Hennegau(7494) was born about 920.(7495) He died in 973.(7496) He was a Greve in Hennegau. (7497) Han ble satt i mann i 958 He was married to Adele N.NSDTR.
1 NOTE Reginar III (c. 920-973) was Count of Hainaut from 940 to 958
2 CONT
2 CONT He was born in Brabant as the son of Reginar II, Count of Hainaut.
2 CONT
2 CONT Together with his brother Rodolphe, he took part in the rebellion of his uncle Gilbert, Duke of Lorraine. When Gilbert was killed in 939, Regnier had to pledge fealty to King Otto the Great.
2 CONT
2 CONT He then allied himself with King Louis IV of France, but King Otto sent duke Hermann of Swabia to quell the rebels in 944.
2 CONT
2 CONT Otto appointed Conrad the Red as duke of Lotharingia, who tried to diminish the power of Reginar. However, when Conrad rose against Otto, Reginar supported him. In an anarchic situation, Reginar appropriated the dowry of Queen Ger
2 CONC berge, Otto's sister and mother of the French king, and also church property.
2 CONT
2 CONT In 953, Bruno, Archbishop of Cologne, who had also been appointed duke of Lotharingia, restored order and defeated Reginar.
2 CONT
2 CONT As Reginar refused to submit, he was exiled to Bohemia, where he died.
2 CONT
2 CONT Family
2 CONT He fathered two sons:
2 CONT Reginar IV, Count of Mons 
2 CONT Lambert I of Leuven 
