2 CONT Walter de St. Martin is also spelled Gautier de St. Martin. The family of Warren derived its name from the fief of Varenne in St-Aubin-le-Cauf, arrondissement of Dieppe, and descends from Gautier de St-Martin. {-per "Falaise Roll,
2 CONC " M.J.Crispin (1938), p. 52} 
2 CONT
2 CONT {W.H.Turton, "The Plantagenet Ancestry" (Balt.:Gen.Pub.Co.,1968),p.112, gives Hugh, Bishop of Coutances (d.1020) as father of Ralph de Warren.}
2 CONT =<nowiki>--------------------</nowiki>=
2 CONT Gautier was also called Walter.
2 CONT =<nowiki>-------------------------</nowiki>=
2 CONT Note from Curator: Various trees have Gautier as the son of Roger 'The Old' de Loudun Tours & Ulmes; Ralph de Garenne; Nicholas de de BOCQUEVILLE; Grandaughter De Blue Tooth; NN. de Sauqueville; and Miss de Bosqueville CLARE. I ha
2 CONC ve removed these connections since I have found no evidence to support any of them. 
2 CONT
2 CONT The only evidence I have found indicates that Gautier was a descendant of Roger de Bacqueville, son of Nicholas de Bacqueville. Here is what [http://fmg.ac/Projects/MedLands/NORMAN%20NOBILITY.htm#RogerBaquevilleMnieceGunnora Charl
2 CONC es Cawley] writes about him: <Guillaume de Jumièges records that a second niece of Gunnora, mistress of Richard I Comte [de Normandie], married "Roger de Bacqueville, dont l´un des descendans a eu pour fils Guillaume Martel et Gau
2 CONC tier de Saint-Martin"> (source: WJ VIII.37, p. 304.)
2 CONT --------------------
