1 NOTE {geni:about_me} Ben M. Angel notes: There is no primary or secondary source backing given for Garnier having lived 844-929. Would welcome seeing some source or explanation for the dates other than it appearing on someone else's fa
2 CONC mily tree profile (particularly one that has nothing to support the information asserted).
2 CONT ---------------------
2 CONT Unattributed basic information (no sources cited):
2 CONT
2 CONT Garnier, Seigneur De Loches [De Villentrois]-3620 [Parents] was born about 844 in Of, Loches, , France.  He died about 929.
2 CONT
2 CONT Other marriages:
2 CONT
2 CONT Loches, Mrs. Garnier
2 CONT
2 CONT He had the following children:
2 CONT
2 CONT F 	i 	Roscille De Loches [Countess Of Anj-4148 was born about 874. She died about 940. 
2 CONT --------------------
2 CONT From the Foundation for Medieval Genealogy page on Carolingian Nobility: http://fmg.ac/Projects/MedLands/FRANKISH%20NOBILITY.htm#RoscilleMFoulquesIAnjou
2 CONT
2 CONT G.      FAMILY of ADALHARD [COMTE de LOCHES] Two brothers, parents not known: 
2 CONT
2 CONT 1.  ADALHARD .  m ---.  The name of Adalhard's wife is not known.  Adalhard & his wife had two children: 
2 CONT ---
2 CONT a)  GARNIER .  
2 CONT
2 CONT The Gesta Consulum Andegavensium names "Guarnerius…filius Adalaudi, illius scilicet Carolus Calvus Lochas dedit… [et] Ambasium"[197].  
2 CONT
2 CONT m TESCENDA, daughter of ---.  
2 CONT
2 CONT "Falco comes Andecavorum iuvenis" names "uxor mea Roscila et filii mei Guido et Fulco" in a donation of property "pro anima Ingelgerii patris mei et iterum Ingelgerii filii mei et Vuarnerii soceri mei et uxoris suæ Tescendæ" by ch
2 CONC arter dated 929[198].  "Fulco Andecavorum comes abbas quoque Sancti Albini Sanctique Lizinii necnon et uxor mea Roscilla et filii mei Widdo ac Fulco" donated property to Saint-Aubin d'Angers for the souls of "…Warnerio socro meo e
2 CONC t uxore sua Tescenda" by charter dated to [929/30][199].  
2 CONT
2 CONT Garnier & his wife had one child: 
2 CONT
2 CONT i)  ROSCILLE ([870]-).   The Gesta Consulum Andegavensium records the marriage of Comte Foulques and "de pago Turonico…Roscillam, Warnerii filiam", specifying that "Warnerius…filius Adalaudi" had three castles "in Turonico…Lochas 
2 CONC atque Villentrasti et Haia" which Foulques later acquired[200].   m (before 5 Jul 905) FOULQUES, son of INGELGER Comte [d'Anjou] & his wife Adelais --- ([888]-[941/42]).   He succeeded in 909 as Vicomte de Tours et d'Anjou.  He wa
2 CONC s installed as Comte d'Anjou in 929 by Raoul King of France. 
2 CONT ---
2 CONT b)  ADALHARD .  The Gestis Consulum Andegavensium names "Adalaudo Episcopo filio suo [Adalaudi]"[201].  Bishop. 
2 CONT
2 CONT 2. RAYMOND (-after [before 5 Jul 905]).  
2 CONT
2 CONT References:
2 CONT
2 CONT [197] Marchegay, P. and Salmon, A. (eds.) (1856) Chroniques d´Anjou (Paris), Gestis Consulum Andegavensium, p. 65.  [198] Urseau, C. (ed.) (1908) Cartulaire noir de la cathédrale d'Angers (Paris, Angers) 33, p. 74.  [199] Broussil
2 CONC lon, B. de (ed.) (1903) Cartulaire de l'abbaye de Saint-Aubin d'Angers (Paris), 177, p. 203.  [200] Gestis Consulum Andegavensium, Chroniques d'Anjou, p. 65.  [201] Gestis Consulum Andegavensium, RHGF IX, p. 30. 
2 CONT --------------------
