1 OCCU Senhora de Amboise, Countess Adelaide Rescinse De Gatinais of AMBROISE, Aelinde was a nickname, it seems.
1 NOTE {geni:about_me} http://genealogics.org/getperson.php?personID=I00020232&tree=LEO
2 CONT
2 CONT http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Adelais_of_Amboise
2 CONT
2 CONT --------------------
2 CONT
2 CONT From the Foundation for Medieval Genealogy page on Franksih Nobility (covering her birth family): http://fmg.ac/Projects/MedLands/FRANKISH%20NOBILITY.htm#AdelaisMIngelger
2 CONT
2 CONT Q.      FAMILY of HUGUES [DUKE of BURGUNDY]
2 CONT
2 CONT 1.  HUGUES .  m ---.  
2 CONT
2 CONT The name of Hugues's wife is not known.  Hugues & his wife had two children: 
2 CONT
2 CONT a)  HUGUES .  
2 CONT
2 CONT The Gestis Consulum Andegavensium names "Hugo Dux Burgundiæ, filius alterius Hugonis" was "ex parte matris suæ [Fulco] consanguineus"[547].  [Duke of Burgundy].  This is the only reference so far identified to a duke of Burgundy i
2 CONC n the late 9th century and should presumably therefore be treated with caution. 
2 CONT
2 CONT b) PETRONILLA .  
2 CONT
2 CONT The Gesta Consulum Andegavensium records the marriage of "Tertullus nobilem dux" and "ducis Burgundiæ filiam nomine Petronillam"[548].  The Chronico Turonensi names "Ingelgerius comes Andergavensis" as "nepos Hugonis Ducis Burgund
2 CONC iæ"[549].
2 CONT
2 CONT m TERTULLUS, son of TORQUATIUS & his wife ---. 
2 CONT
2 CONT The precise relationship between the following family sub-group and Hugues [Duke of Burgundy] (their "propinquus", see below) has not been identified.  The issue is complicated by the fact that Ingelger, husband of Adelais, was th
2 CONC e son of Petronilla and Tertullus (see above).  This suggests that the relationship (if there was one) may have been a remote one, maybe indirectly through one of the wives of Hugues or his father. 
2 CONT
2 CONT 1.         ---.  m ---.  One child: 
2 CONT
2 CONT a)  ADELAIS .  
2 CONT
2 CONT The Historia Comitum Andegavorum records that Ingelgerius married "Rursus Adelardus et Raymo ambo germani fratres, Turonensium et Andegavensium pontifices, neptem suam Aelindis" and that her dowry consisted of "alodiis suis…Ambazi
2 CONC o, Busenciaco et Castellione"[550].  
2 CONT
2 CONT The Gesta Consulum Andegavorum records that Ingelger married "Landonensis castri sive Gastinensis pagi consul nomine Gaufredus…filiam unicam…Adelam", and thereby inherited "Landonensi castro" as she was her father's heir as he had
2 CONC  no surviving male issue[551], but this text may confuse Ingelger's wife with the first wife of Comte Foulques II "le Bon", Gerberge de Gâtinais.  
2 CONT
2 CONT The Gesta Consulum Andegavorum records that, after the death of her husband, Adelais was unjustly accused of adultery by a group of nobles led by "Guntrannus parens Ingelgerii" but later exonerated[552].  
2 CONT
2 CONT m INGELGER Comte [d'Anjou], son of TERTULLUS & his wife Petronilla of Burgundy (-[888], bur Châteauneuf église Saint-Martin).   
2 CONT
2 CONT 2.         ADALHARD .   "Karolus…imperator augustus" confirmed a donation by "Hugo…propinquus noster" of property "villam Apiarias in pago Aurelianensi" to "episcopo Adalaldo archiepiscopo simulque Rainoni episcopo, fratri eiusdem
2 CONC " at the request of "Odo comes" by charter dated 27 Oct 886[553].   Bishop of Tours. 
2 CONT
2 CONT 3.  RAINO .  Bishop of Angers. 
2 CONT
2 CONT References:
2 CONT
2 CONT [547] Gestis Consulum Andegavensium, RHGF IX, p. 29.  [548] Gestis Consulum Andegavensium, Chroniques d'Anjou, p. 36, footnote 3 noting that 2 mss record her as "consanguinea" not "filia".  [549] Chronico Turonensi, RHGF IX, p. 47
2 CONC .  [550] Historia Comitum Andegavorum, Chroniques d'Anjou, p. 320.  [551] Chronica de Gesta Consulum Andegavorum, Chroniques d'Anjou, pp. 40-1.  [552] Chronica de Gesta Consulum Andegavorum, Chroniques d'Anjou, pp. 41-4.  [553] An
2 CONC gers 14, p. 34. 
2 CONT
2 CONT ---------------------
2 CONT
2 CONT From the Foundation for Medieval Genealogy page on Anjou (covering her married family): http://fmg.ac/Projects/MedLands/ANJOU,%20MAINE.htm#_Toc256354719
2 CONT
2 CONT INGELGER, son of [TERTULLUS & his wife Petronilla of Burgundy] (-[888], bur Châteauneuf, église Saint-Martin).  
2 CONT
2 CONT Foulque I "le Roux" Comte d´Anjou names "Ingelgerio genitore meo…" in a charter dated to [929/30][34].  
2 CONT
2 CONT There is doubt whether the other references to Ingelger which follow accurately reflect the historical reality of his life.  The Gesta Consulum Andegavorum names "Ingelgerius" as son of "Tertullus nobilem dux" & his wife[35].  The
2 CONC  Gesta Consulum Andegavorum names "Ingelgerius…iuvenis filius Tortulfi"[36].  The Chronico Turonensi names "Ingelgerius comes Andergavensis" as "nepos Hugonis Ducis Burgundiæ"[37]. 
2 CONT
2 CONT Charles II "le Chauve" King of the West Franks gave him "a piece of a fief in the castle of Landonense".  
2 CONT
2 CONT He was installed as viscount of the city of Orléans by Louis II "le Bègue" King of the West Franks, and appointed royal representative at Tours.  The Historia Comitum Andegavorum records that Louis II "le Bègue" King of the West F
2 CONC ranks, therefore dated to [877/79], granted "dimidium Andegavis comitatum" to "Ingelgerius"[38].  
2 CONT
2 CONT The Gesta Consulum Andegavorum records that Ingelger died from "focositatem, phthisim et hydropisim"[39].  The Gesta Consulum Andegavorum records the burial of "Ingelgerius" at "ecclesia beati Martini Castrinovi"[40]. 
2 CONT
2 CONT m ADELAIS, niece of ADALHARD Bishop of Tours and of RAINO Bishop of Angers, daughter of ---.  
2 CONT
2 CONT The Historia Comitum Andegavorum records that Ingelgerius married "Rursus Adelardus et Raymo ambo germani fratres, Turonensium et Andegavensium pontifices, neptem suam Aelindis" and that her dowry consisted of "alodiis suis…Ambazi
2 CONC o, Busenciaco et Castellione"[41].  The Gesta Consulum Andegavorum records that Ingelger married "Landonensis castri sive Gastinensis pagi consul nomine Gaufredus…filiam unicam…Adelam", and thereby inherited "Landonensi castro" as
2 CONC  she was her father's heir as he had no surviving male issue[42], but this text may confuse Ingelger's wife with the first wife of Comte Foulques II "le Bon" (see below).
2 CONT
2 CONT The Gesta Consulum Andegavorum records that, after the death of her husband, she was unjustly accused of adultery by a group of nobles led by "Guntrannus parens Ingelgerii" but later exonerated[43]. 
2 CONT
2 CONT Comte Ingelger & his wife had one son:
2 CONT
2 CONT 1.  FOULQUES ([888]-[Aug 941/942], bur Châteauneuf, église Saint-Martin).  
2 CONT
2 CONT The Gesta Consulum Andegavorum names "Ingelgerius…filius eius Fulco cognominatus Rufus"[44].  Comte de Nantes 908-919.  Vicomte de Tours et d'Anjou.  "Domni Fulconis Andecavorum comitis, Tedbaldi Turonorum vicecomitis" subscribed 
2 CONC the charter dated 30 Oct 909 under which the testamentary executors of "domni Gauzuini" donated property to Saint-Martin de Tours[45].  
2 CONT
2 CONT He was installed as FOULQUES I "le Roux" Comte d'Anjou in 929 by Raoul King of France.  
2 CONT
2 CONT His lay abbacies are noted in the charter dated to [929/30] under which "Fulco Andecavorum comes abbas quoque Sancti Albini Sanctique Lizinii necnon et uxor mea Roscilla et filii mei Widdo ac Fulco" donated property to Saint-Aubin
2 CONC  d'Angers for the souls of "Ingelgerio genitore meo atque Ingelgerio filio meo necnon…Warnerio socro meo et uxore sua Tescenda"[46].  
2 CONT
2 CONT The Gesta Consulum Andegavorum records the burial of "Fulco Rufus" at "ecclesia beati Martini iuxta patrem suum"[47].  "Domni Fulconis et filii ipsius…quoque Fulconis" are named as a present in a charter dated Aug 941 which record
2 CONC s a lawsuit concerning land claimed by "sacerdos Sancti Martini…Tesmunnus"[48].  
2 CONT
2 CONT m (before 5 Jul 905) ROSCILLE [de Loches], daughter of GARNIER Seigneur de Loches, Villentrasti et Haia & his wife Tescenda --- ([870]-).  
2 CONT
2 CONT The Gesta Consulum Andegavorum records the marriage of Comte Foulques and "de pago Turonico…Roscillam, Warnerii filiam", specifying that "Warnerius…filius Adalaudi" had three castles "in Turonico…Lochas atque Villentrasti et Haia"
2 CONC  which Foulques later acquired[49].  "Falco comes Andecavorum iuvenis" names "uxor mea Roscila et filii mei Guido et Fulco" in a donation of property "pro anima Ingelgerii patris mei et iterum Ingelgerii filii mei et Vuarnerii soc
2 CONC eri mei et uxoris suæ Tescendæ" by charter dated 929[50].  "Fulco Andecavorum comes abbas quoque Sancti Albini Sanctique Lizinii necnon et uxor mea Roscilla et filii mei Widdo ac Fulco" donated property to Saint-Aubin d'Angers for
2 CONC  the souls of "Ingelgerio genitore meo atque Ingelgerio filio meo necnon…Warnerio socro meo et uxore sua Tescenda" by charter dated to [929/30][51].  
2 CONT
2 CONT Comte Foulques I & his wife had five children.
2 CONT
2 CONT ---
2 CONT
2 CONT FOULQUES d'Anjou, son of FOULQUES I "le Roux" Comte d'Anjou & his wife Roscille de "Loches" ([920]-11 Nov 958) who succeeded his father in 942 as FOULQUES II "le Bon" Comte d'Anjou m firstly (937) GERBERGE, daughter of --- (-befor
2 CONC e 952).  
2 CONT
2 CONT "Gaufridus…Andecavorum comes" names "patris mei Fulconis, matris quoque meæ Gerbergæ" in his charter dated 19 Jun 966[62].  
2 CONT
2 CONT Maurice Chaume suggested that she was Gerberge, daughter of Geoffroy Vicomte d'Orléans [Comte de Gâtinais], based on onomastic reasons only to explain the use of the name Geoffroy in the family of the Comtes d'Anjou[63]. 
2 CONT
2 CONT References:
