2 CONT Ingelger (Ingelerus) was the first Count d'Anjou, the title granted to him in 9th Century. It is generally believed his parents were Tertullus and Petronilla. He was born in Renne. He inherited his father's land about 877. He was 
2 CONC closely associated with Louis II and Louis III of France. He married Adelais in Orleans. He was buried in the church of Saint-Martin at Châteauneuf-sur-Sarthe. He was succeeded by his son Fulk the Red. This is a summary from the s
2 CONC ources below.
2 CONT
2 CONT --added by Maria Edmonds-Zediker, Curator, 10/5/10 http://fmg.ac/Projects/MedLands/ANJOU,%20MAINE.htm The creation of the "march" of Anjou is probably dated to the early 860s, as a measure to control the Bretons.
2 CONT
2 CONT INGELGER (-[888], bur Châteauneuf, église Saint-Martin). The Gesta Consulum Andegavorum names "Ingelgerius" as son of "Tertullus nobilem dux" & his wife. Tertullus is no more convincing than Tortulfus as the name of a figure in no
2 CONC rth-west France during the mid-9th century. As is the case with his supposed father, it is possible that Tertullus was not a historical person. m PETRONILLA, daughter of --- Duke of Burgundy & his wife ---. The Gesta Consulum Ande
2 CONC gavorum records the marriage of "Tertullus nobilem dux" and "ducis Burgundiæ filiam nomine Petronillam. Thus the supposition that Tertullus and Petronilla
2 CONT
2 CONT Charles II "le Chauve" King of the West Franks gave him "a piece of a fief in the castle of Landonense". He was installed as viscount of the city of Orléans by Louis II "le Bègue" King of the West Franks, and appointed royal repre
2 CONC sentative at Tours. The Gesta Consulum Andegavorum records the burial of "Ingelgerius" at "ecclesia beati Martini Castrinovi"
2 CONT
2 CONT m ADELAIS, niece of ADALHARD Bishop of Tours and of RAINO Bishop of Angers, daughter of ---. The Historia Comitum Andegavorum records that Ingelgerius married "Rursus Adelardus et Raymo ambo germani fratres, Turonensium et Andegav
2 CONC ensium pontifices, neptem suam Aelindis" and that her dowry consisted of "alodiis suis…Ambazio, Busenciaco et Castellione"
2 CONT
