1 NOTE {geni:about_me} '''Lietgardis de Troyes.''' There are several hypotheses about the wife of Héribert de Vermandois. See Christian Settipani, ''La prehistoire des Capetiens 481-987: Premiere Partie'', p. 222 n. 218, and Tableau 8. S
2 CONC ettipani tentatively suggests Heribert's wife was '''Lietgardis of Troyes'''. K. F. Werner in ''Die Nachkommen Karls des Grossen'' at V.3 in his Tafel does not identify anyone as Heribert's wife (nor in his discussion of Heribert 
2 CONC in his "Untersuchungen zur Fruehzeit des franzoesischen Fuerstentums (9.-10. Jahrhundert): V." in ''Welt als Geschichte'' 20 (1960) pp. 93-100). Cf. [http://fmg.ac/Projects/MedLands/NORTHERN%20FRANCE.htm#HeribertIdied900907 Medlan
2 CONC ds].
2 CONT
2 CONT --------------------
2 CONT The wife of Héribert de Vermandois is unknown.''' She is listed as Bertha, daughter of [http://www.geni.com/people/Widerich-de-Morvois/6000000000334385426 Guerri de Morvois] in a 12th-century chronicle from Waulsort abbey, that dr
2 CONC ew on epic literature to aggrandize its founder's lineage (Peter Stewart in [http://groups.google.com/group/soc.genealogy.medieval/browse_thread/thread/7592d8e8043d36/9926bf2582418831?hl=en&lnk=gst&q=bertha+morvois#9926bf258241883
2 CONC 1 soc.genealogy.medieval], June 28, 2004).
2 CONT
2 CONT She is listed as Beatrice of Morvois, the daughter of Guerri I, count of Morvois, and Eve of Rousillon in the unreliable Roderick W. Stuart, ''Royalty for Commoners'' (2d ed., 1992), page 194, citing *The Journal of the Society of
2 CONC  Genealogists* (London, 1911- ) and G. Andrews Moriarty as authorities. 
2 CONT
2 CONT There are several hypotheses about the wife of Héribert de Vermandois. See Christian Settipani, ''La prehistoire des Capetiens 481-987: Premiere Partie'', p.222 n.218, and Tableau 8. Settipani tentatively suggests Heribert's wife 
2 CONC was Lietgardis of Troyes. K. F. Werner in ''Die Nachkommen Karls des Grossen'' at V.3 in his Tafel does not identify anyone as Heribert's wife (nor in his discussion of Heribert in his "Untersuchungen zur Fruehzeit des franzoesisc
2 CONC hen Fuerstentums (9.-10. Jahrhundert): V." in ''Welt als Geschichte'' 20 (1960) pp.93-100). Cf. [http://fmg.ac/Projects/MedLands/NORTHERN%20FRANCE.htm#HeribertIdied900907 Medlands].
2 CONT
2 CONT Bertha's parents have been variously suggested as:
2 CONT
2 CONT # [http://www.geni.com/people/Robert-IV-le-Fort-Marquis-de-Neustrie/6000000006036670007 Rutpert IV of Womgau] and [http://www.geni.com/people/Ad%C3%A9la%C3%AFs-A%C3%A9lis-de-Tours/6000000012468581950 Adelaide de Tours], OR 
2 CONT
2 CONT # [http://www.geni.com/people/Widerich-de-Morvois/6000000000334385426 Guerri I de Morvois] and [http://www.geni.com/people/Eve-d-Auxerre/6000000004148992439 Eve d'Auxerre], OR 
2 CONT
2 CONT # [http://www.geni.com/people/Widerich-de-Morvois/6000000000334385426 Guerri I de Morvois] and an unknown woman, OR
2 CONT
2 CONT # [http://www.geni.com/people/Conrad-I-le-Vieux-Comte-d-Auxerre/4932952221030036762 Conrad d'Auxerre] and [http://www.geni.com/people/Ad%C3%A9la%C3%AFs-A%C3%A9lis-de-Tours/6000000012468581950 Adélais de Tours].
2 CONT
2 CONT --------------------
2 CONT
2 CONT Name given by the Foundation for Medieval Genealogy: http://fmg.ac/Projects/MedLands/NORTHERN%20FRANCE.htm#HeribertIdied900907
2 CONT
2 CONT HERIBERT [I], son of PEPIN [Carolingian] Seigneur de Péronne et de St Quentin, Comte near Paris ([848/850]-murdered [900/6 Nov 907]) m [LIETGARDIS], daughter of --- (-27 May <nowiki>----</nowiki>).  
2 CONT
2 CONT The name of the wife of Comte Héribert is not known.  However, a "Comtesse Liedgardis", different from the daughter of Comte Héribert [II], is named who could have been his wife[1275].  If this is correct, the necrology of Reims w
2 CONC hich records the death "VI Kal Jun" of "Letgardis comitissa"[1276], may refer to the same person[1277].  
2 CONT
2 CONT According to the Histoire de Guise, Albert Comte de Vermandois constructed the abbey of Saint-Michel at Rochefort in 945 "d'accord avec la comtesse Hérésinde sa femme", while in 947 Hérésinde founded the nearby Benedictine convent
2 CONC  of Bucilly[1278].  The source assumes that this refers to Albert Comte de Vermandois, but his supposed marriage to Hérésinde is not mentioned by Settipani[1279].  
2 CONT
2 CONT According to the introduction to the Cartulaire de l'abbaye de Bucilly, Bucilly was founded by "Gerberge, femme d'Albert I Comte de Vermandois" although it notes that "certains auteurs ont voulu faire remonter [sa foundation] à la
2 CONC  libéralité de Hersinde femme d'Herbert Comte de Vermandois morte en 901"[1280].  
2 CONT
2 CONT No other reference has been found to Hérésinde being the wife of Comte Héribert ]I]. 
2 CONT
2 CONT Comte Héribert [I] & his wife had four children:
2 CONT
2 CONT 1. HERIBERT [II] ([880]-23 Feb 943, bur Saint Quentin).  None of the sources so far consulted states explicitly that Heribert [II] and his sister Beatrix were the children of Heribert [I] but this looks probable.  He succeeded his
2 CONC  father in [900/907] as Comte de Meaux, de Soissons et de Vermandois.
2 CONT
2 CONT 2.  BEATRIX de Vermandois ([880/83]-after 26 Mar 931).  None of the sources so far consulted state explicitly that Heribert [II] and his sister Beatrix were the children of Heribert [I] but this looks probable.  Her birth date ran
2 CONC ge is estimated from her eldest daughter giving birth to her own first child in [915]. m ([897]) as his second wife, ROBERT Marquis en Neustrie, son of ROBERT “le Fort” Marquis en Neustrie & his wife --- ([860]-killed in battle ne
2 CONC ar Soissons 15 Jun 923).  Comte de Paris 898.  He was elected 22 Jun 922 as ROBERT I King of France. 
2 CONT
2 CONT 3. [daughter [ADELA]. Jackman suggests[1285] that the wife of Graf Gebhard [Konradiner] was the daughter of Héribert [I] Comte de Vermandois, although this appears supported only by onomastic indications.  The name of Graf Gebhard
2 CONC 's wife is not given explicitly in the sources.  However, an "Adela" is named in a name-list in the Reichenau memorial book dated [926/32] which appears to include members of the Konradiner family, Jackman suggesting that she is w
2 CONC ell placed in the list to be Graf Gebhard's wife[1286], although this is not the only possible interpretation of the text.  m GEBHARD Graf im Ufgau, son of EBERHARD Graf in der Ortenau [Konradiner] & his wife Wiltrud --- (-after 1
2 CONC 5 Jan 947).] 
2 CONT
2 CONT 4. [daughter [CUNIGUNDIS] ([890/900]-after 943). The Vermandois origin of Graf Udo's wife is suggested by the fact that Flodoard refers to the wife of "Uddone [frater Hermanno]" as amita of "Hugo [de Vermandois Archbishop of Reims
2 CONC ]"[1287].  The name of Graf Udo's wife is not given explicitly in the sources.  However, a "Cunegundis" is named in a name-list in the Reichenau memorial book dated [926/32] which appears to include members of the Konradiner famil
2 CONC y, Jackman suggesting that she is well placed in the list to be Graf Gebhard's wife[1288], although this is not the only possible interpretation of the text.  Her birth date range is estimated from her estimated marriage date. m (
2 CONC [915]) UDO Graf in der Wetterau, son of GEBHARD Graf in der Wetterau [Konradiner] & his wife Hidda --- (-12 Dec 949).]
2 CONT
