2 CONT *[577] Nécrologe du Mans, p. 329. 
2 CONT
2 CONT ---
2 CONT
2 CONT From the Foundation for Medieval Genealogy page on Northern France (covering his married life):
2 CONT
2 CONT http://fmg.ac/Projects/MedLands/NORTHERN%20FRANCE.htm#HeribertIdied900907
2 CONT
2 CONT HERIBERT [I], son of PEPIN [Carolingian] Seigneur de Péronne et de St Quentin, Comte near Paris ([848/850]-murdered [900/6 Nov 907]).  
2 CONT
2 CONT Regino names (in order) "Bernardum, Pippinum et Heribertum" as the three children of "Pippinum", specifying that Héribert killed "Rodulfum comitem filium Balduini comitis"[1400].  "Heribertus, Bernhardi frater" is named in the Vit
2 CONC a Hludowicis Imperatoris[1401].  
2 CONT
2 CONT He was at the court of Emperor Charles II “le Chauve” in 877.  
2 CONT
2 CONT *Comte de Soissons 886/898.  
2 CONT *Abbé de St Crépin.  
2 CONT *Comte de Meaux et de Madrie 888/889[1402].  
2 CONT *He became Comte de Vermandois in 896.  
2 CONT
2 CONT The Annales Vedastini record that "Rodulfus comes" disrupted the peace in 896 and took the property of "Heribertus et Erkingerus", that "Odo rex" besieged "castrum sancti Quintini et Peronam" and expelled Raoul's supporters, and t
2 CONC hat Héribert killed Raoul[1403].  
2 CONT
2 CONT Comte Héribert opposed Eudes King of France, but was reconciled with the king in 897, an event which may have been confirmed by the marriage of Héribert's daughter to the king's nephew Robert[1404].  
2 CONT
2 CONT Baudouin II Count of Flanders attacked Vermandois, was driven out by 900 but reconquered it and killed Héribert [I] Comte de Vermandois in revenge for his brother's death[1405]. 
2 CONT
2 CONT m [LIETGARDIS], daughter of --- (-27 May <nowiki>----</nowiki>).  
2 CONT *The name of the wife of Comte Héribert is not known.  However, a "Comtesse Liedgardis", different from the daughter of Comte Héribert [II], is named who could have been his wife[1406].  If this is correct, the necrology of Reims 
2 CONC which records the death "VI Kal Jun" of "Letgardis comitissa"[1407], may refer to the same person[1408].  
2 CONT *According to the Histoire de Guise, Albert Comte de Vermandois constructed the abbey of Saint-Michel at Rochefort in 945 "d'accord avec la comtesse Hérésinde sa femme", while in 947 Hérésinde founded the nearby Benedictine conven
2 CONC t of Bucilly[1409].  The source assumes that this refers to Albert Comte de Vermandois, but his supposed marriage to Hérésinde is not mentioned by Settipani[1410].  
2 CONT *According to the introduction to the Cartulaire de l'abbaye de Bucilly, Bucilly was founded by "Gerberge, femme d'Albert I Comte de Vermandois" although it notes that "certains auteurs ont voulu faire remonter [sa foundation] à l
2 CONC a libéralité de Hersinde femme d'Herbert Comte de Vermandois morte en 901"[1411].  No other reference has been found to Hérésinde being the wife of Comte Héribert ]I]. 
2 CONT
2 CONT Comte Héribert [I] & his wife had four children:
2 CONT
2 CONT 1.  HERIBERT [II] ([880]-23 Feb 943, bur Saint Quentin).  
2 CONT *None of the sources so far consulted states explicitly that Heribert [II] and his sister Beatrix were the children of Heribert [I] but this looks probable.  
2 CONT *He succeeded his father in [900/907] as Comte de Meaux, de Soissons et de Vermandois.   
2 CONT
2 CONT 2.  BEATRIX de Vermandois ([880/83]-after 26 Mar 931).  
2 CONT *None of the sources so far consulted state explicitly that Heribert [II] and his sister Beatrix were the children of Heribert [I] but this looks probable.  
2 CONT *Her birth date range is estimated from her eldest daughter giving birth to her own first child in [915].  
2 CONT *The Historia Francorum Senonensis records that "sororem Herberti" was the wife of "Robertus princeps" who rebelled against Charles III "le Simple" King of France[1412].  Guillaume de Jumièges records that Duke Robert's wife was t
2 CONC he sister of Héribert, and that the couple had a son named Hugues[1413].  
2 CONT *The marriage may have been arranged to confirm her father's reconciliation with Eudes King of France, who was her husband's uncle[1414].  Werner suggests [897] as the date of the marriage, on the assumption that it followed the p
2 CONC olitical reconciliation between Béatrix's father and Robert's uncle[1415].  
2 CONT *As discussed in relation to Robert's first marriage in the document CAPET, there is a possibility that Robert's first wife was still alive in 907, which would of course mean that Béatrix's marriage took place after that date.  
2 CONT *m ([897]) as his second wife, ROBERT Marquis en Neustrie, son of ROBERT “le Fort” Marquis en Neustrie & his wife --- ([860]-killed in battle near Soissons 15 Jun 923).  Comte de Paris 898.  He was elected 22 Jun 922 as ROBERT I K
2 CONC ing of France. 
2 CONT
2 CONT 3.  [daughter [ADELA] .  
2 CONT *Jackman suggests[1416] that the wife of Graf Gebhard [Konradiner] was the daughter of Héribert [I] Comte de Vermandois, although this appears supported only by onomastic indications.  The name of Graf Gebhard's wife is not given 
2 CONC explicitly in the sources.  However, an "Adela" is named in a name-list in the Reichenau memorial book dated [926/32] which appears to include members of the Konradiner family, Jackman suggesting that she is well placed in the lis
2 CONC t to be Graf Gebhard's wife[1417], although this is not the only possible interpretation of the text.  
2 CONT *m GEBHARD Graf im Ufgau, son of EBERHARD Graf in der Ortenau [Konradiner] & his wife Wiltrud --- (-after 15 Jan 947).] 
2 CONT
2 CONT 4. [daughter [CUNIGUNDIS] ([890/900]-after 943).  
2 CONT *The Vermandois origin of Graf Udo's wife is suggested by the fact that Flodoard refers to the wife of "Uddone [frater Hermanno]" as amita of "Hugo [de Vermandois Archbishop of Reims]"[1418].  The name of Graf Udo's wife is not gi
2 CONC ven explicitly in the sources.  However, a "Cunegundis" is named in a name-list in the Reichenau memorial book dated [926/32] which appears to include members of the Konradiner family, Jackman suggesting that she is well placed in
2 CONC  the list to be Graf Gebhard's wife[1419], although this is not the only possible interpretation of the text.  
2 CONT *Her birth date range is estimated from her estimated marriage date.  
2 CONT *m ([915]) UDO Graf in der Wetterau, son of GEBHARD Graf in der Wetterau [Konradiner] & his wife Hidda --- (-12 Dec 949).]
2 CONT
