1 NOTE {geni:about_me} '''HELGAUD, Abbé de Saint-Riquier. ?Comte de Montreuil''' 
2 CONT s/o NN (-c 866)
2 CONT x NN
2 CONT *HERLUIN (-killed in battle 13 Jul 945) Comte de Montreuil
2 CONT *HERARD Seigneur du château de Ham (Picardie)
2 CONT *LAMBERT (-killed in battle, tryimg to avenge his brother > 945)
2 CONT
2 CONT https://fmg.ac/Projects/MedLands/nfraamp.htm#_Toc127521366
2 CONT ----
2 CONT
2 CONT 1.         HELGAUD, son of --- (-[866]).  Abbé de Saint-Riquier.  The Chronique de Saint Riquier records that "le comte Helgaud" succeeded "Rodolphe…du sang imperial" as lay abbot of Saint-Riquier and that he was succeeded by "Gue
2 CONC lfon…du sang royal"[681].  "Rodolphe" is identified with Rudolf Comte de Sens, brother of Empress Judith, who died in 866, and "Guelfon" as Rudolf's son.  This casts doubt on the chronology of this passage as, if the relationship 
2 CONC between Rudolf and Welf is correctly identified, it is likely that the son succeeded the father as lay abbot as such a post was often hereditary.  same person as…?  HELGAUD (-after 879).  Flodoard records "terra filiorum Balduini,
2 CONC  Rodulfi quoque de Gangeio atque Hilgaudi" in 925[682].  Comte de Montreuil 877-879.  It is probable that Helgaud, abbé de Saint-Riquier, and his son Herluin are in fact the same people as Helgaud Comte de Montreuil 877-79 and his
2 CONC  son Herluin who died in 945, and that the Chronique de Saint-Riquier is inaccurate in its chronology relating to the supposedly earlier father and son of these names.  m ---.  The name of Helgaud's wife is not known.  
2 CONT
2 CONT a)         HERLUIN (-killed in battle 13 Jul 945).  Flodoard names "Monasteriolum castellum Erluini filii Hilgaudi comitis" when recording that Montreuil was besieged by "Heribertus et Hugo"[683].  The Chronique de Saint Riquier n
2 CONC ames "Herluin…comte" as son of "le comte Helgaud" lay abbot of Saint-Riquier[684].  As noted above, it is possible that Helgaud and his son Herluin are in fact the same people as Helgaud Comte de Montreuil 877-79 and his son Herlu
2 CONC in who died in 945 (see below), and that the Chronique de Saint-Riquier is inaccurate in its chronology relating to the supposedly earlier father and son of these names.  Comte de Montreuil.  Arnoul Count of Flanders captured Mont
2 CONC reuil in 939: Flodoard records in 939 that “comes Arnulfus” captured “castellum Erluini...Monasteriolum” and that he sent “uxorem ipsius Erluini...cum filiis” across the sea “ad Alstanum regem”[685].  Guillaume of Jumièges records
2 CONC  that “Arnulfus Flandrensis comes” captured "castrum...Monasteriolum" from “comiti...Herluino”, who sought help from “Normanniæ dominum” who recaptured the castle for Herluin[686].  Comte d'Amiens 944/45.  He was killed fighting t
2 CONC he Normans.  The Liber Modernorum Regum Francorum records the death of "Herluinus Monasterioli castro comes" fighting "Aygroldo regi Danorum"[687].  Guillaume de Jumièges records that “Herluini” was killed on the orders of “Haigro
2 CONC ldo regi Danorum”[688].  m firstly (divorced before 927) ---.  The primary source which confirms her marriage has not been identified.  m secondly (before 927) --- (-after 939).  Flodoard records in 939 that “comes Arnulfus” captu
2 CONC red “castellum Erluini...Monasteriolum” and that he sent “uxorem ipsius Erluini...cum filiis” across the sea “ad Alstanum regem”[689]. 
2 CONT
2 CONT b)         ERARD .  Flodoard names "Ebrardum fratrem Erluini" when recording that his castle of Ham was captured in 932 by "Heribertus comes"[693].  Seigneur du château de Ham (Picardie). 
2 CONT
2 CONT c)         LAMBERT (-killed in battle after 945).  Guillaume de Jumièges records that “Lambertus frater eius” was killed trying to avenge the death of “Herluini”[694]. 
2 CONT
2 CONT https://fmg.ac/Projects/MedLands/nfraamp.htm#_Toc127521366
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT ----
