2 CONT >>i)          '''[https://www.geni.com/people/Ranulf-II-duc-d-Aquitaine/6000000006129390166?through=6000000003097891610 RAINULF] ([845/50]-after Jul 892).  The primary source which confirms his parentage has not yet been identifie
2 CONC d.  The Chronicle of Adémar de Chabannes specifies that "Ramnulfus…comes Pictaviensis" was "consanguineus…Willelmi…comitis Arvernis"[280].  The Chronico Richardi Pictavensis also states that "Ramnulfus consanguineus erat Willelmi 
2 CONC Pii Aquitanorum Ducis et Arveniæ Comitis"[281].  The relationship between Rainulf and Duke Guillaume has not yet been traced.  After the death of Rainulf's father in 866, he and his brothers were deprived of their inheritance. It 
2 CONC appears that no-one was at that time installed as Comte de Poitou, the county being administered by Louis King of Aquitaine, son of Charles II "le Chauve" King of the Franks[282].  He appears to have been finally installed as RAIN
2 CONC ULF II Comte de Poitou in [878], judging by his heading the list of confirmants of his brother's Apr 878 donation to the church of Saint-Hilaire de Poitiers[283].   After the death of Louis II "le Bègue" King of the West Franks, C
2 CONC omte Rainulf had custody of the late king's youngest son Charles, who later succeeded as Charles III "le Simple" King of the West Franks[284].  After the deposition of Emperor Karl III in Nov 887, Comte Rainulf claimed the success
2 CONC ion to the kingdom of Aquitaine and supported the candidature of Guy of Spoleto as King of the Franks[285].  He was appointed Duke of Aquitaine in 888.  Regino names "Ramnulfum et fratrem eius Gozbertum et Ebulonem abbatum de sanc
2 CONC to Dionysio" when recording their battle against "Waltgerius comes" in Jul 892[286].  The Chronicle of Saint-Maxence records the death in 890 of "Ramnulfus comes Pictavinus"[287], but the year is incorrect if Regino correctly name
2 CONC s Rainulf in Jul 892.  m [ERMENGARDE, daughter of ---] (-1 Jul after 890).  The name of the wife of Comte Rainulf II is not known with certainty.  "Gauzberto comite, Ramnulfus comes, Ermengarde…" subscribed the charter dated Apr 8
2 CONC 78 under which "Gauzbertus comes" donated property "in pago Santonico…in villa…Dorodonno" to the church of Saint-Hilaire de Poitiers[288].  Richard suggests that Ermengarde must have been the wife of one of the named counts becaus
2 CONC e of the order of the signatures[289].  Richard rejects the hypothesis that Adda "coniunx Ramnulf", whose tomb was discovered at Saint-Hilaire de Poitiers, was the wife of Comte Rainulf II[290].  Mistress (1): ---.  The name of Co
2 CONC mte Rainulf's mistress is not known'''.  
2 CONT
2 CONT >>Comte Rainulf II & his wife had [one child]: 
2 CONT
2 CONT >>>(a)       [RAINULF [III] (-[901]).  Rainulf is shown in Europäische Stammtafeln[291] as the legitimate son of Comte Rainulf II but the primary source on which this is based has not yet been identified.  He is not named by Besly
2 CONC [292], nor by Richard[293].  Both authors state that Eble was the only child of Comte Rainulf II.] 
2 CONT
