1 NOTE {geni:about_me} http://finnholbek.dk/genealogy/getperson.php?personID=I27397&tree=2
2 CONT
2 CONT From the Foundation for Medieval Genealogy page on Saxony:
2 CONT
2 CONT http://fmg.ac/Projects/MedLands/SAXONY.htm#OttoErlauchtedied912
2 CONT
2 CONT OTTO "der Erlauchte", son of Graf LIUDOLF & his wife Oda [Billung] (-30 Nov 912, bur Gandersheim Stiftskirche).  
2 CONT
2 CONT The Annalista Saxo records "Otto" as "filius Liudolfi ducis"[142].  "Hludowicus…rex" granted immunities to Kloster Gandersheim, naming "Brun et Otto nostri fideles comites…[et] Liutolf genitor eorum…[et]…Gerbirg soror eorundem com
2 CONC itum" by charter dated 26 Jan 877[143].  Graf im Südthüringau.  "Hludowicus…rex" donated property "Tennisteti et Heriki in pago Suththuringa in comitatu Ottonis" to Kloster Gandersheim by charter dated 26 Jan 877[144].  "Rihdahc" 
2 CONC denoted property to Kloster St Maria an der Rosel, in the castle of Coblenz, by undated charter, placed in the compilation with other charters dated [981/89], subscribed by "domini Ottonis Liutolfi filius…"[145].  
2 CONT
2 CONT Graf im Eichsfeld.  Emperor Arnulf confirmed an exchange including property "in pago Eichesfelden in comitatu Ottonis" between the abbot of Fulda and "Chunrado comite" on the intervention of "Ottonis…marchionis" by charter dated 2
2 CONC 8 Jan 897[146].  
2 CONT
2 CONT Lay Abbot of Hersfeld 908.  He was chosen to succeed Ludwig "das Kind" [Carolingian] as king of Germany in 911, but declined on the grounds of his advanced age and recommended the election of Konrad ex-Duke of the Franconians[147]
2 CONC .  
2 CONT
2 CONT "Chuonradus…rex" confirmed privileges to Kloster Murbach by charter dated 12 Mar 913 with the consent of "fidelium nostrorum Hathonis, Salomonis, Thiodolfi, Hildini, Einhardi, Erchangarii, Chuonradi, Hugonis, Ottonis, Heinrici, Bo
2 CONC pponis, Udalrici, Eberhardi"[148].  
2 CONT
2 CONT Thietmar records the death of Otto on 30 Nov but does not give the year[149].  The necrology of Merseburg records the death "30 Nov" of "Oddo comes pater Heinrici regis Saxonum"[150].  
2 CONT
2 CONT m HEDWIG [Hathui], daughter of HEINRICH dux [Babenberg] & his wife Engeltrudis --- ([850/55]-24 Dec 903). 
2 CONT
2 CONT Mistress (1): ---.  The name of Otto's mistress is not known.  
2 CONT
2 CONT Graf Otto & his wife had [seven] children:
2 CONT
2 CONT 1.  [daughter ([865/70][154]-).  
2 CONT *"Wundilgartam Henrici regis de filia neptim" is named in the Chronicle of St Gall, which also names her husband[155].  The commentary in the printed text interprets this as "granddaughter of Heinrich I King of Germany", but this 
2 CONC is chronologically impossible assuming that the approximate death date of Wundelgart's husband is correct.  If there is any truth in the text, it is more likely that Wundelgart was the niece of King Heinrich by his sister, althoug
2 CONC h this is far from certain considering the broad range of interpretation possible for the word "neptis".  However, the chronology is tight even for this interpretation, as shown by the estimated birth date range of this daughter, 
2 CONC which must mean that she was one of her parents' older children.  Another possibility is that she was illegitimate.  The same source in a later passage names "Ekkehardo…diacono et Purchardo puero post abate consobrinis suis"[156].
2 CONC   As Wundelgart was the mother of abbot Burkhard, this gives the essential clue about the name of this daughter's husband, who in the same source is named as the father of the sisters who were mothers of the younger Ekkehard and a
2 CONC bbot Burkhard.  
2 CONT *m as his first wife, EKKEHARD [I], son of ---.] 
2 CONT
2 CONT 2. THANKMAR (-before 30 Nov 912).  
2 CONT *"Thancmarus et Liudolfus", sons of Otto & Hathwiga, died before their father according to the Annalista Saxo, which implies they were older than their brother Heinrich who "ecce fratribus defunctis, tota hereditas in ipsum iam du
2 CONC cem derivatur"[157]. 
2 CONT
2 CONT 3. LIUDOLF (-before 30 Nov 912).  
2 CONT *"Thancmarus et Liudolfus", sons of Otto & Hathwiga, died before their father according to the Annalista Saxo, which implies they were older than their brother Heinrich who "ecce fratribus defunctis, tota hereditas in ipsum iam du
2 CONC cem derivatur"[158].  
2 CONT *m ---.  The name of Liudolf's wife is not known.  
2 CONT *Liudolf & his wife had one child.
2 CONT
2 CONT 4. HEINRICH ([876]-Memleben 2 Jul 936, bur Quedlinburg Stiftskirche).  
2 CONT *Thietmar records that Heinrich was "born of the noble lineage of Otto and Hadwig"[161].  According to the Annalista Saxo, he was son of the unnamed sister of Adalbert [Babenberg], with whom he and his brothers fought against the 
2 CONC Konradiner family, his complete parentage being recorded in a later passage[162].  
2 CONT *He was elected as HEINRICH I King of Germany at Fritzlar 6 May 919. 
2 CONT
2 CONT 5. ODA ([884][163]-[2 Jul] after 952).  
2 CONT *Regino records the marriage in 897 of "Ottonem comitem…filiam Odam" and King Zwentibold[164].  Regino records that "Gerhard comes" married "Odam uxorem Zuendiboldi regis" after killing her first husband in battle in 900[165].  "O
2 CONC tto…rex" confirmed the donation of property " in loco Dauindre…in pago…Hamalant in comitatu Vuigmanni" to St Moritz at Magdeburg by "nostra amita…Uota" by charter dated 30 Dec 952[166].  Jackman speculates[167] that Graf Eberhard 
2 CONC married Oda as her third husband, Oda von Sachsen, for onomastic reasons as the name of Eberhard's supposed daughter (her affiliation also being based only on his own separate onomastic hypothesis) was that of Oda's maternal grand
2 CONC mother.  This is an interesting theory but it accumulates one onomastic hypothesis on another and must be considered highly speculative.  
2 CONT *m firstly ([Worms] [27 Mar/13 Jun] 897) ZWENTIBOLD King of Lotharingia [Carolingian], illegitimate son of Emperor ARNULF King of Germany & his mistress --- ([870/71]-killed in battle 13 Aug 900, bur [Süsteren or Echternach]).  
2 CONT *m secondly (900) Graf GERHARD [Matfride], son of --- (-killed in battle 22 Jun 910).  
2 CONT *[m thirdly (after Jun 910) EBERHARD Graf im Oberlahngau Pfalzgraf, son of KONRAD Graf in der Wetterau und im Wormsgau [Konradiner] & his wife Glismod --- (-killed in battle near Andernach 23 Oct 939).] 
2 CONT
2 CONT 6. LIUTGARD [Dodica] (-21 Jan 923).  
2 CONT *Europäische Stammtafeln[168] names Liutgard as daughter of Otto & his wife, but the primary source which confirms this has not so far been identified.  
2 CONT *Abbess of Gandersheim 919/923.
2 CONT
2 CONT 7. [IRMINBURG (-before 936).  
2 CONT *Europäische Stammtafeln[169] names Irminburg as daughter of Otto & his wife, and records her marriage, but the primary source which confirms this has not so far been identified.  
2 CONT *m as his first wife, SIEGFRIED, son of THIETMAR [Ostmark] & his wife --- (-[3 Dec 936/941]).]
2 CONT
2 CONT Graf Otto had one illegitimate daughter by Mistress (1):
2 CONT
2 CONT 8. daughter.  932.  
2 CONT *Widukind names "sorore regis quæ nupserat Widoni Thuringo…ex concubina nata"[170].  
2 CONT *m WIDO, from Thuringia.
2 CONT
2 CONT References:
2 CONT
