2 CONT Robert "the Strong" Count of Anjou and Blois was the son of Rutpert III Count of Wormsgau and Waldrada of Orléans.1,2,3,4 His name was also spelt "Robert "le Fort"" in French.4 His name was also spelt Rutpert IV "der Tapfer" or "d
2 CONC er Starke" in German.1,4 Robert "the Strong" Count of Anjou and Blois was appointed in 852 as Lay Abbot of St. Martin de Marmoutier near Tours.4 In 858/859, he revolted against Charles the Bald, inviting Charles' brother Ludwig to
2 CONC  invade Neustria. After the brothers made peace, Robert was restored to favor and given the defense of Neustria against the Normans.5 About 864 Robert married second Adelaide of Alsace and Tours, daughter of Hugh "le Méfiant" Coun
2 CONC t of Tours and Aba.2,4 Robert "the Strong" Count of Anjou and Blois was killed in the Battle of Brissarthe against the Normans on Wednesday, 15 September 866. Sewell gives his death date as 25 July 866, while Moriarty (1953) gives
2 CONC  it as October 866.1,2,3,5,4 Children of Robert "the Strong" Count of Anjou and Blois and Adelaide of Alsace and Tours ◦Regilinda+2 ◦Odo or Eudes King of the Franks1,3,5,4 (856 - 898) ◦Robert I Duke of France+1,2,3,5,4 (866 - 15 J
2 CONC un 923)
2 CONT
