2 NOTE ROBERT of Anjou lived from 1276-1343 - He was the King of Naples; He was not the same person as Robert the Strong of Neustria who died in 866. 
2 NOTE Robert of Anjou (1276-1343)
3 CONT
3 CONT Robert was born around 1276, the third son of the future Charles II of Naples (then heir apparent) and his wife Mary of Hungary.[3] His father was the son of the incumbent King of Naples, Charles of Anjou, who had established an I
3 CONC talian realm a decade earlier in 1266. In 1282, the Angevin kingdom was shaken by the Sicilian Vespers, a revolt by the Sicilians against the rule of his grandfather Charles. The ensuing War of the Sicilian Vespers against the Sic
3 CONC ilian rebels widened when the crown of Crown of Aragon intervened in support of the Sicilians.
