2 CONC en who were laying waste the settlements nearthe Loire. A great victory over the Northmen in 865 was followed by theKing's grant to Robert of full control over Neustria early the next year;but he was killed in a skirmish against t
2 CONC he Northmen in September. Thememory of Robert's exploits brought great prestige to his family. Hissons, Eudes and Robert I, both became kings of West Francia (or France);and the Capetian kings (from 987) were his direct descendant
2 CONC s.
