1 NOTE Stewart Baldwin: 'Baldwin I 'Iron-arm' (Baudouin I 'Bras de Fer',
2 CONT Balduinu s Ferreorum-brachiorum) Count, before 862-879. [presumably count
2 CONT of Flanders, 870x5?-879]. Count Baldwin I, ancestor of the counts of
2 CONT Flanders, firs t appears in history in the year 862, when Judith, daughte
2 CONT r of king Charles the Bald, and successively widow of the t wo
2 CONT Anglo-Saxon kings Æthelwulf and Æthelbald, eloped with h im, with the
2 CONT assistance of Judith's brother Louis (later ki ng Louis II) [Annales
2 CONT Bertiniani, s.a. 862, MGH SS 1: 456]. Charles asked his bishops to
2 CONT anathemize Baldwi n and Judith, but he reconciled with them the next year
2 CONT a t the pope's request, when Baldwin and Judith were marrie d [Annales
2 CONT Bertiniani, s.a. 863, MGH SS 1: 462 (see below)]. The region over whic h
2 CONT Baldwin was then count is not identified in any ninth cen tury source,
2 CONT but it would seem that Ingelramn was still cou nt of Flanders at that
2 CONT time, having not yet been dispossess ed (see below under Ingelramn in the
2 CONT Commentary section). A ccording to Flodoard, writing in the next century,
2 CONT bishop H ungarius of Utrecht, during the time of Baldwin's excommuni
2 CONT cation, had warned the Norman Roric, then ruling at Doresta dt in Frisia,
2 CONT not to receive Baldwin [see Flodoard, Histori a Remensis Ecclesiae iii,
2 CONT 23, 26, MGH SS 13: 529, 541], whi ch would presumably place Baldwin's
2 CONT area of influence in th e same neighborhood. It seems likely that Baldwin
2 CONT became co unt of Flanders when count Ingelramn was dispossessed betwe en
2 CONT 870 and 875 (see below). In 871, he was sent by Charle s along with abbot
2 CONT Gauzlin to negotiate with Charles's rebe llious son Carolman [Annales
2 CONT Bertiniani, s.a. 871, MGH SS 1 : 491]. Dying in 879, he was followed by
2 CONT his son Baldwin II. The ep ithet of 'Iron-arm' usually attributed to him
2 CONT appears in th e work of Wimann (d.1192), who attributed the nickname to h
2 CONT is strength and audacity ['... Balduinus comes Flandrie, fi lius Odocri,
2 CONT vir audax et fortis, ita ut Ferreorum-brachior um vocaretur, ...' Wimann,
2 CONT Liber de possessionibus sancti V edasti, MGH SS 13: 711]. Two different
2 CONT manuscripts of the c ontemporary Annals of Saint-Vaast (Annales
2 CONT Vedastini) giv e him the epithets of Ferreus (Iron) and Bonus (the Good)
2 CONT [ 'Balduinus, Ferreus cognomine, comes moritur, sepeliturque in Sithiu
2 CONT monasterio .' MGH SS 1: 517; 'Balduinus comes, cognomine Bonus, moritu r,
2 CONT sepeliturque in Sithiu monasterio.' [Annales Vedastini , s.a. 879, MGH SS
2 CONT 2: 197]. Date of Birth: Unknown. Place of Birth: Unknown. Date of Death:
2 CONT 879. [Annales Vedastini (see above); Chronicon Vedastinum (see b elow);
2 CONT Annales Blandinensis (see below); the Annales Elnonenses mi nores (see
2 CONT below) give 878] Place of Death: Saint-Bertin? A marginal addition to
2 CONT chapter 88 of Folcwine's history sta tes that Baldwin died after having
2 CONT spent some time as a mon k at Saint-Bertin and that his body was buried
2 CONT at St. Berti n (Sithiu), but that his heart and intestines were remove d
2 CONT to St. Peter's in Ghent [MGH SS 13: 623]. This would expl ain the
2 CONT disagreement between Annales Vedastini and Annale s Blandinensis
2 CONT regarding his place of burial. Father: Uncertain. See the Commentary
2 CONT section below for a discussion of the po ssibility that his father was
2 CONT named Odoacer/Audacer. Mother: Unknown. Spouses: m. at Auxerre, 863
2 CONT (eloped 862), Judith, daughte r of Charles the Bald, king of the West
2 CONT Franks, emperor. ['..., et ad Autisiodorum civitatem usque pervenit; ibi
2 CONT fil iam suam Iudith, sicut domnus apostolicus eum petierat, con silio
2 CONT fidelium suorum Balduino, quem sequuta fuerat, legali ter coniugio
2 CONT sociari permisit.' (Translation: ... and he [C harles] arrived in the
2 CONT city of Auxerre; there, just as th e pope had requested, by the advice of
2 CONT his loyal men, he al lowed his daughter Judith to be legally joined in
2 CONT matrimon y with Baldwin, with whom she had run off.) Annales Bertini ani,
2 CONT s.a. 863, MGH SS 1: 462] Children: The contemporary Annals of Saint-Vaast
2 CONT state that Baldwin a nd Raoul were brothers ['Balduinus vero comes et
2 CONT Rodulfus f rater eius, ...' Annales Vedastini, s.a. 895, MGH SS 1: 529].
2 CONT Regino, writin g in the first decade of the tenth century, states that
2 CONT Rao ul (Rodulfus) was a son of Baldwin [I], and that Raoul's br other
2 CONT Baldwin [II] held Flanders. Writing between 951 and 9 59, Witger also
2 CONT states that Baldwin II was a son of Baldwi n I [Witgeri genealogia
2 CONT Arnulfi comitis, MGH SS 1: 303]. Baldwin II, d. 918, 'count' of Flanders,
2 CONT 879-918; m. Ælftru de, daughter of Ælfred ('the Great'), king of Wessex.
2 CONT Raoul, d. 17 June 896, count [of Cambrai?]. Raoul was killed in 896 in
2 CONT battle with count Heribert I (o f Vermandois) ['Rodulfus vero in ira
2 CONT commotus propter caste lla perdita, dum depraedari non cessit abbatiam
2 CONT sancti Quin tini, ab Heriberto occiditur in bello' Annales Vedastini, s
2 CONT .a. 896, MGH SS 1: 530; 2: 208; 'Rodulfus comes interficitu r 4. Kal.
2 CONT Iulii.' Annales Blandinensis, s.a. 896, MGH SS 5: 24; '... qui Heribertus
2 CONT R odulfum comitem, filium Balduini interfecit nostris tempori bus, et non
2 CONT multum post occisus est a Balduino, satellite B alduini, fratris Rodulfi,
2 CONT qui Balduinus hucusque in Flandri s ducatum tenet.' Regino, s.a. 818 (in
2 CONT a retrospective anna l written ca. 906, describing the family of Bernard,
2 CONT son o f Pepin of Italy), MGH SS 1: 567]. The region over which Ra oul was
2 CONT count does not appear in sources until the twelft h century
2 CONT [Vanderkindere (1902), 287]. Commentary The Legendary Ancestors of
2 CONT Baldwin of Flanders No source earlier than the eleventh century gives the
2 CONT paren tage of Baldwin I of Flanders. However, by the the late thi rteenth
2 CONT century, a more elaborate story had developed whic h provided Baldwin
2 CONT with three generations of ancestry bac k to a certain Lideric, who was
2 CONT then said to be the first ' forester' of Flanders, followed in the same
2 CONT position by hi s son Ingelramn, grandson Odoacer/Audacer, and
2 CONT great-grands on Baldwin, who then became the first count of Flanders. Fo
2 CONT rtunately, the surviving rescensions of the genealogies of the counts of
2 CONT F landers allow us to see some of the stages by which this le gendary
2 CONT scenario developed, and a careful examination of th ese shows us that
2 CONT even if Lideric existed (and this is no t certain), the alleged descent
2 CONT of Baldwin I from him can b e rejected. Much of the early development of
2 CONT the legend appears in th e various works edited under the collective
2 CONT title of Geneal ogiae Comitum Flandriae [MGH SS 9: 302-336, here
2 CONT abbreviate d Gen. Com. Fland.], a collection of nine items (identifie d
2 CONT here by Roman numerals I-IX) written by various authors o ver a period of
2 CONT several hundred years, having in common tha t they involve the genealogy
2 CONT or succession of the counts of Flanders. The two earliest parts, dating
2 CONT from th e tenth century, say nothing about the parentage of Baldwi n I
2 CONT [I. Witgeri genealogia Arnulfi comitis (pp. 302-4, als o an important
2 CONT source for later Carolingian genealogy); II . De Arnulfo comite (pp.
2 CONT 304)]. The claimed parentage of Baldwin I as a son of a certain Od
2 CONT acer/Audacer first appears in certain annals compiled in th e middle of
2 CONT the eleventh century. The Annales Elnonenses Mi nores have two entries
2 CONT giving this parentage, while the Ann ales Blandinenses not only have two
2 CONT similar entries for Bal dwin's parentage, but also mention Lideric and
2 CONT Ingelramn, b ut without any genealogical affiliation for the latter two.
2 CONT Annales Elnonenses Minores [MGH SS 5: 19] 862. Balduinus, O dacri filius,
2 CONT Caroli regis filiam, uxorem duxit, illa illu m sequente. 878. Balduinus,
2 CONT Odacri filius, obit. Annales Blandinensis [MGH SS 5: 23-4] 836. Lidricus
2 CONT comes o biit et Arlabeka sepelitur. 856. Herebertus tradidit sancto Petro
2 CONT res suas in Berenga , sub Inghelramno abbate vel comite. 862. Iudith
2 CONT secuta est Baldwinum Ferreum, filium Audacri. 875. Hludowicus, suadente
2 CONT Ingelramno abbate, regnum Karol i vastat. 879. Balduvinus, filius
2 CONT Audacri, obiit; Blandinio sepelitur. The Annales Formoselenses [MGH SS 5:
2 CONT 35] also have an (earl ier) obituary for Lideric ['817. Lidricus comes
2 CONT obiit, et H arlabecce sepelitur.'] and another for Baldwin with his par
2 CONT entage ['877. Balduvinus, filius Audacri, obiit. Carolus Ca lvus obiit,
2 CONT Blandinio sepelitur.' Note the obituary of Char les the Bald which has
2 CONT been carelessly inserted in the middle of the entry, otherwise c opied
2 CONT from Annales Blandinenses], but these two entries, ev idently copied
2 CONT carelessly from Annales Blandinenses, have n o independent authority. The
2 CONT Chronicon Vedastinum, an eleventh century compilation , also gives this
2 CONT parentage of Baldwin ['Balduinus, Audacr i filius, moritur et Sithiu
2 CONT sepelitur.' Chronicon Vedastinu m, s.a. 879, MGH SS 13: 709], adding the
2 CONT parentage to the i nformation taken from its evident source, the Annales
2 CONT Vedas tini (see above). Also, from the same source, we have an en try
2 CONT apparently making Baldwin the son of an eighth centur y man named Odacer
2 CONT ['... ubi Karolus rex Gramannum atque Od acrum, patrem Balduini comitis
2 CONT Flandrensium, misit.' Chroni con Vedastinum, s.a. 788, MGH SS 13: 705],
2 CONT who does in fac t appear in a similar contemporary annal, but without
2 CONT Baldwin as his son ['..., et fuerunt ib i missi domni Caroli regis
2 CONT Grahamannus et Audacrus cum aliq uibus Francis.' Annales Laurissenses,
2 CONT s.a. 788, MGH SS 1: 174]. It seems cl ear from the chronology that this
2 CONT Odoacer from 788 was no t Baldwin's father. Thus, it appears that the
2 CONT compiler of this chronicle at lea st thought that he knew the name of
2 CONT Baldwin's father, not o nly adding the parentage to Baldwin's obituary,
2 CONT but also id entifying a specific Odoacer as Baldwin's father in anothe r
2 CONT addition, evidently without noticing the chronological pr oblem. In
2 CONT Genealogia comitum Flandriae Bertiniana [Gen. Com. Fland . III, pp.
2 CONT 305-8], apparently composed under count Robert I I (1093-1111), the
2 CONT genealogy adds the names of Lideric an d Ingelramn, who had arleady
2 CONT appeared in Annales landinensi s without genealogical affiliation
2 CONT ['Lidricus Harlebeccensi s comes genuit ingelrannum. Ingelrannus genuit
2 CONT Audacrum. Au dacer genuit Balduinum Ferreum, qui duxit filiam Karoli Cal
2 CONT vi nomine Iudith.' MGH SS 9: 305]. While Lideric and Odoace r are not
2 CONT known to appear in the records prior to those men tioned above, Ingleramn
2 CONT appears as count of several regions, including Fl anders, in November 853
2 CONT [MGH Leg. 1: 426; see below]. The 8 75 entry in Annales Blandinensis
2 CONT corresponds to (and was pe rhaps derived from) an entry in the same year
2 CONT in Annales Be rtiniani, in which the Ingleramn in question was a camerari
2 CONT us et domesticus of Charles the Bald, but it is not clear t hat all of
2 CONT these references to a count or abbot Ingelramn a ll refer to the same
2 CONT individual (see below for more about I ngelramn). Indeed, the apparent
2 CONT overlap between Ingelramn and Baldwi n in these sources led some early
2 CONT scholars to assume that O doacer did not exist as a separate individual,
2 CONT and that Odo acer was a cognomen of Baldwin, who was then made to be a s
2 CONT on of Ingelramn [see the comments of Bethmann, MGH SS 9: 30 5, n. 6].
2 CONT However, such an explanation does not fit the evidence. I t is apparent
2 CONT that certain eleventh century authors though t that the father of Baldwin
2 CONT I was named Odoacer, about who m they provide no other information (not
2 CONT counting the unlik ely identification in the year 788 mentioned above),
2 CONT and th at even Annales Blandinensis, which shows knowledge of bot h
2 CONT Lideric and Ingelramn, did not show any awareness of a re lationship
2 CONT between them and Baldwin I, even providing a chr onology which weighs
2 CONT against such a link. Thus, the best ex planation is that the connection
2 CONT of Lideric and Ingelramn to the genealogy i s an eleventh century
2 CONT invention (perhaps involving some jum ping to conclusions from the
2 CONT entries in Annales Blandinensi s). As for the parentage of Baldwin I, it
2 CONT seems clear tha t by the eleventh century it was believed that his
2 CONT father' s name was Odoacer/Audacer, about whom they had little or n o
2 CONT information. Although the above comments are sufficient to reject the ap
2 CONT pearance of Lideric and Ingelramn in Baldwin's genealogy, i t is
2 CONT interesting to indicate some of the later embellishmen ts to the story.
2 CONT In the twelfth century, Lambert of Saint-O mer made some additions to the
2 CONT previous version [Lamberti g enealogia comitum Flandriae, Gen. Com.
2 CONT Fland. V, pp. 308-31 3], which set the year 792 as the beginning date of
2 CONT Lideric's rule, and stated that in that year, Lideric saw t hat Flanders
2 CONT was vacant, uncultivated, and well-wooded, an d occupied it ['Anno ab
2 CONT incarnatione Domini 792. Karolo Mag no regnante in Francia, Lidricus
2 CONT Harlebeccensis comes, vide ns Flandriam vacuam et incultam ac nemorosam,
2 CONT occupavit eam . Hic genuit Ingelramnum comitem ...' MGH SS 9: 309; and si
2 CONT milarly in Flandria Generosa (Gen. Com. Fland. VI, pp. 313- 334)]. The
2 CONT story that Baldwin's predecessors were 'foresters' of F landers comes
2 CONT from the chronicler John of Thielrode, writin g in 1294 [Iohannis de
2 CONT Thielrode genealogis comitum Flandriae (Gen. Com. Fland . VIII), MGH SS
2 CONT 9: 334-5; see also Iohannis de Thilrode Chronicon, MGH S S 25: 566-7,
2 CONT 574]: 'Tempore Balduini Flandria fit comitatus, et Balduinus prim us
2 CONT comes. Antecessores sui fuerunt forestarii Flandriae sub rege Fran cie,
2 CONT sicuti legimus in cronicis Francorum. Lidricus et Audacer impetrav erunt
2 CONT ab abbate Heinardo monasterii Sancti Bavonis licentiam venand i in silva
2 CONT que Heinarstriist nuncupatur, modo Loe dicitur, sub tali co nditione,
2 CONT quod de decimia bestia unam darent abbati et suis successor ibus.'
2 CONT (Translation: Flanders became a county in the time of Baldu inus, and
2 CONT Balduinus was the first count. His predecessors were forest ers under the
2 CONT king of France, just as we read in chronicles of the Fr anks. Lidricus
2 CONT and Audacer obtained license from Heinardus, abbo t of the monastery of
2 CONT St. Bavo, to hunt in the woods called Heinarst riist, now called Loe,
2 CONT subject to the condition that they give one-ten th of the beasts to the
2 CONT abbot and to his successors.) Here, Heinardus is the famous Einhard,
2 CONT biographer of Charle magne, who was abbot from 826 until his death in 844
2 CONT ['Anno 792 Lydric us comes Arlebeccensis comitatum Flandrie suscepit. ...
2 CONT Anno 826 Eyn ardus, capellanus Ludovici piisimi imperatoris, factus est
2 CONT abbas G andensis cenobii. ... Anno 844 Eynardus abbas Gandensis obiit,
2 CONT succe ssit Einkericus.' Annales S. Bavonis Gandensis, MGH SS 2: 187 (1
2 CONT 4th century)]. Note that if the license from Einhard is based o n
2 CONT reliable information, it would place Odoacer's activity in 844 or ea
2 CONT rlier, further undermining the claim that he was a son of Ingelram n. In
2 CONT the work of John of Ypres, writing in the fourteenth cen tury, we find an
2 CONT exotic origin for Lideric, whose activities are ext ended back to the
2 CONT time of Charles Martel, and who is provided with a w ife who is the
2 CONT daughter of Gerard de Roussillon, another figure of leg end [MGH SS 25:
2 CONT 764]: 'Dum Sarraceni sic ab Hispania venirent ad Eudonis mandatum , miles
2 CONT quidam iuvenis christianus de partibus Ulixbone seu Portuga llie, regia
2 CONT stirpe progenitus, Liedricus nomine, despectis parentibus , qui cum illis
2 CONT de patria ad legem perfidi transierant Machometi, a d Karolum Tuditem et
2 CONT Gerardum de Rossilione se contulit, ut sacri bap tismatis christianque
2 CONT fidei Deo pacta servaret, et sub Karolo milita ns, multa probitatis opera
2 CONT gessit. Et Karolo predicto carus effectu s est, sibi toto vite sue
2 CONT tempore servivit et filio suo Pupino post eu m regi. Cui postea Karolus
2 CONT Magnus terram Flandrie dedit. Ipse est a qu o Flandrie comites
2 CONT descenderunt. Ipse uxorem habuit filiam Gerardi d e Rossilione predicti,
2 CONT de qua genuit filium Ingelramnum, militem probu m et prudentem, suum
2 CONT Flandrie successorem.' (Translation [with c omments in brackets]: Thus,
2 CONT when the Saracens came from Spain to the c ommand of Eudes [of
2 CONT Aquitaine], a certain young Christian knight fro m the region of Lisbon,
2 CONT or Portugal, of royal descent, named Lideric, de spising his parents, who
2 CONT with those of their country had converted to t he faithless law of
2 CONT Mohammed, went to Charles Tudites [i.e., M artel] and Gerard de
2 CONT Roussillon, in order to receive the rite of bapti sm and to serve the
2 CONT Christian faith by agreement with God, and servin g as a soldier under
2 CONT Charles, performed much honest service. And h e became dear to the said
2 CONT Charles, and served him during his entir e career, and also his son
2 CONT Pepin, king after him. Afterward, Charlemagn e gave him the land of
2 CONT Flanders. He is the one from whom the counts o f Flanders descend. He
2 CONT [Lideric] married a daughter of the aforesaid G erard de Roussillon, by
2 CONT whom he had a son Ingelramn, an honest and p rudent knight, his successor
2 CONT in Flanders.) Later embellishments expanded the genealogy to include addi
2 CONT tional fictional generations before Lideric of Harlebeck, includin g a
2 CONT seventh century count Salvardus of Dijon. The story also gained a g iant
2 CONT named Rinardus, an earlier Lidricus le Buc, the first forester, h is
2 CONT successor Antonius, and so forth [see, e.g., MGH SS 9: 316] . Some of
2 CONT these more elaborate later inventions have been accepted b y some of the
2 CONT less critical genealogists of the Forester family, wh o have used the
2 CONT office of 'forester' supposedly held by Lideric to trac e members of the
2 CONT Forester family back through the counts of Flanders . Such claims have no
2 CONT historical basis. Thus, the existence of Lideric and Odoacer/Audacer
2 CONT remain s uncertain, but there is still the chance that the entries in
2 CONT Annales B landinensis are based on genuine information. If the name of
2 CONT Odoacer/Au dacer for the father of Baldwin I is correct, he is little
2 CONT more tha n a name, and the alleged genealogical connections Baldwin I to
2 CONT Lideric a nd Ingelramn can be clearly rejected. Falsely attributed
2 CONT great-grandfather (existence uncertain) : Lideric, said to have d. 836,
2 CONT buried at Harlebeck ['836. Lidricus co mes obiit et Arlabeka sepelitur.',
2 CONT Annales Blandinensis, MGH SS 5: 23 ], count [of Harlebeck, Genealogia
2 CONT comitum Flandriae Bertiniana, MG H SS 9: 305]. Falsely attributed
2 CONT grandfather: Ingelramn, living 875, evid ently d. before 883, count of
2 CONT Noyon, Vermandois, Artois, Courtrai, a nd Flanders, before 853-870x5,
2 CONT chamberlain of king Charles th e Bald, m. Friderada, who m. (2)
2 CONT Bernarius, d. 883; and m. (3) Hugues , son of king Lothair II. Count
2 CONT Engilramnus is indicated as having authority over the se five regions in
2 CONT a capitulary of emperor Lothair I and king Charl es the Bald in November
2 CONT 853 ['Imino episcopus, Adelardus abba, Waltcaud us, Odelricus, missi in
2 CONT Noviomiso, Vermendiso, Adertiso, Curtri ciso, Flandra, comitatibus
2 CONT Engilramni, et in comitatibus Waltcaud i.' MGH Leg. 1: 426]. He is
2 CONT referred to as abbot or count by an ent ry in Annales Blandinensis under
2 CONT the year 856 (not necessarily contemporary), recording the donation of
2 CONT land by a certai n Heribert, but he does not appear in the (possibly
2 CONT imcomplete) list o f abbots in Catalogus abbatus Blandinensium [MGH SS
2 CONT 13: 645]. He appear s also in a capitulary of Charles the Bald on 21
2 CONT March 858 [MGH Leg. 1 : 457], and Charles made a pact with his brother
2 CONT Louis (Ludwig) 'the Ge rman' in 864, he was named (along with Hincmar of
2 CONT Reims) as a guaran tor on the behalf of king Charles [Annales Fuldenses,
2 CONT MGH SS 1: 378] . In 868, he was sent with gifts to king Salomon of
2 CONT Brittany [Annales Be rtiniani, MGH SS 1: 480], and he acted as a
2 CONT guarantor again in 870 [c apitulary of a meeting of Charles and Louis, 6
2 CONT March 870, MGH Leg. 1 : 516]. In 875, having been deprived of his honors
2 CONT due to the influenc e of queen Richilde, he persuaded Louis to devastate
2 CONT the kingdom of Ch arles ['Hludovicus vero, persuadente Engelranno,
2 CONT quondam Caroli r egis camerario et domestico, suasione Richildis reginae
2 CONT ab honor ibus deiecto et a sua familiaritate abiecto, cum hoste et fili o
2 CONT aequivico suo Hludowico usque ad Attiniacum venit; ad quem obsistendu m
2 CONT primores regni Caroli iubente Richilde regina sacramento se confirma
2 CONT verunt; quod non attenderunt, sed ex sua parte regnum Caroli pessin
2 CONT dantes, hostili more devastaverunt.' Annales Bertiniani, s.a. 875 , MGH
2 CONT SS 1: 498; Annales Blandinenses, MGH SS 5: 23 (quoted above)]. The
2 CONT information on Ingelramn's wife and child comes from Regino 's chronicle
2 CONT for the year 883, which states that in that year , Hugues (son of king
2 CONT Lothair II) ordered a certain noble named Bern arius to be killed, and
2 CONT then married his widow. Regino also states tha t before being united to
2 CONT Bernarius, she had been married to the pote ns vir Ingelramn, by whom
2 CONT they had a daughter who was later marrie d to count Richwin ['Hoc etiam
2 CONT tempore idem Hugo [son of Lothair II] W icbertum comitem, qui ab ineunte
2 CONT aetate sibi faverat, interfecit; pa ucis dehinc interpositis diebus,
2 CONT Bernarium, nobilem virum sibique fidel issimum, dolo trucidari iussit,
2 CONT pulchritudine illius captus uxoris , quam absque momento sibi in
2 CONT matrimonium iungit. Vocabatur autem mulie r Friderada, quae antequam
2 CONT Bernario sociaretur, copulata fuerat Engilram no potenti viro, ex quo
2 CONT filiam peperit, quam postmodum Richwinus come s in coniugium accepit,
2 CONT quam etiam propter stuprum commissum ide m comes decollari iussit.'
2 CONT Regino, s.a. 883, MGH SS 1: 594]. Possible father (unproven, existence
2 CONT uncertain): Odoacer/Au dacer. While the lack of evidence predating the
2 CONT eleventh century s uggests caution, there are no strong reasons for
2 CONT rejecting the name , as there are with the alleged links to Ingelramn and
2 CONT Lideric. If th e name is correct, nothing further is known of him, except
2 CONT for the un certain possibility that there is something to the very late
2 CONT stor y mentioned above that Odoacer obtained hunting rights from abbot
2 CONT Einha rd (826-844). Falsely attributed daughter: Guinidilda, m. Guifred,
2 CONT coun t of Barcelona. Gesta comitum Barcinonensium (written about 1290)
2 CONT states th at Guifred impregnated a daughter (unnamed) of the count of
2 CONT Flanders ( also unnamed) and later married her [see RHF 9: 68]. Later
2 CONT autho rs have expanded the story to identify this girl with Guifred's kno
2 CONT wn wife Guinidilda, with the count of Flanders in question being va
2 CONT riously identified as Baldwin I [] or Baldwin II [Anselme 2: 714] . There
2 CONT is no good reason to accept this late source on this point.
2 CONT -----------------------------------------------------------
2 CONT --------------------- Bibliography Anselme = Père Anselme, Histoire
2 CONT généalogique et chronologi que de la maison royale de France, 9 vols
2 CONT (Paris, 1726-33). Gen. Com. Fland. = L. C. Bethmann, ed., Genealogiae
