2 CONT >'''LUITGARDIS''' (before 925-14 Nov after 985, bur Chartres, Abbaye de Saint-Père).  
2 CONT >Rodulfus Glauber refers to the wife of Comte Guillaume as "''sororem [Heribertum Trecorum comitem]''", specifying that she was childless by her first husband, when recording her second marriage to "''Tetbaldus''"[1318].  
2 CONT The ''Liber Modernorum Regum Francorum'' refers to the wife of "''Tetbaudi comitis''" as "s''orore Herberti Trecorum comitis''"[1319].  
2 CONT >"''Theobaldi comitis…Ledgardis comitisse''" subscribed the charter dated 950 under which Ragnfred Bishop of Chartres donated property to Chartres Saint-Père, although the relationship between the two is not specified[1320]. 
2 CONT >"''Ledgardis''" donated property to "''Sancti Petri Carnotensis  ecclesiam''", for the souls of "''senioris mei…comitis Tedbaldi…patris mei Heirberti, Trecassini comitis''", with the consent of ''"archipresule…Hugone et…comite Od
2 CONC one, filiis meis"'', by charter dated 5 Feb 978, signed by "…''Emma comitissa Pictavæ urbis''…"[1321].  
2 CONT >“''Ledgardis comitissa necnon Hugo episcopus et filius meus et item filius meus Odo comes''” donated property to Saint-Martin de Tours, for the souls of “''Theobaldi comitis quondam senioris mei…Richildis quondam sanctimonialis, 
2 CONC eiusque filii Richardi episcopi''” (referring to “''dicti comitis et fratris sui Theobaldi''”, in relation to Bishop Richard), by charter dated to [980][1322].  
2 CONT >"''Hugonis ducis, Odonis comitis, Hugonis sanctæ Bituricensis archipræsulis, Letgardis comitissæ, Bertæ comitissæ, Gauzfridi vicecomitis''…" subscribed the charter dated 985 under which "Robertus" donated property to "Sancti Petr
2 CONC i Carnotensis", on the advice of ''"Odonem, simul cum sua matre Ledgarde, pariterque dominam meam Bertam, ipsius æque coniugem''"[1323].  
2 CONT >The necrology of Chartres cathedral records the death "XVIII Kal Dec" of "Letgardis comitissa"[1324].  
2 CONT >'''m firstly''' ([940]) as his second wife, '''GUILLAUME I “Longuespée”''' Comte [de Normandie], son of ROBERT I [Rollo] Comte [de Normandie] & his [second] wife Poppa de Bayeux (-murdered Péquigny-sur-Somme 17 Dec 942, bur Rouen
2 CONC , cathédrale de Notre-Dame).  
2 CONT >>'''m secondly''' ([942/45]) '''THIBAUT [II] "le Tricheur" Comte de Blois''', son of THIBAUT [I] "l'Ancien" Comte de Blois, Vicomte de Tours & his first wife --- (-16 Jan [975/77]).  
2 CONT >>'''THIBAUT [II] de Blois''', son of THIBAUT [I] "l'Ancien" Vicomte de Tours & his first wife ---] ([910]-16 Jan [975/77]).  
2 CONT >>"''Le comte Thibault père de Thibault''" relinquished rights relating to "l''es terres de Vancé, de Joué, de Martigny et de Berthenay''" to Tours Saint-Martin and paid for his future burial in the abbey by charter dated to [944]
2 CONC [25].  
2 CONT >>“''Ledgardis comitissa necnon Hugo episcopus et filius meus et item filius meus Odo comes''” donated property to Saint-Martin de Tours, for the souls of “''Theobaldi comitis quondam senioris mei…Richildis quondam sanctimonialis,
2 CONC  eiusque filii Richardi episcopi''” (referring to “dicti comitis et fratris sui Theobaldi”, in relation to Bishop Richard), by charter dated to [980][26].  This confirms that Richildis was the mother of Richard and that Richard wa
2 CONC s the brother of Thibaut.  However, the absence of a phrase in the text such as “''matris sui''” linking “''Richildis''” to “''Theobaldi comitis''” suggests that she was not the mother of Richard´s brother Thibaut, and that theref
2 CONC ore the brothers were born from different marriages of the same father.  
2 CONT >>He succeeded [his father] in [942] as THIBAUT I "''le Tricheur''" Comte de Blois, Vicomte de Tours.  
2 CONT >>He dominated Brittany as guardian of his nephew Drogo, after the death of his brother-in-law Alain II Duke of Brittany in 952[27].  
2 CONT >>"''Domnus Tetbaldus comes Turonis''" withdrew his claims to a serf in favour of the monks of Saint-Martin de Tours by charter dated 957, signed by "d''omni Tetbaldi comitis, Tetbaldi filii ipsius…Alberici Aurelianensium vicecomi
2 CONC tis''…"[28].  
2 CONT >>"''Teutbaldi comitis, Teutbaldi junioris, Gausfredi comitis, Hugonis comitis Cenomannorum''…" subscribed the charter dated Sep 960 under which "''Aremburgis''" donated property to Saint-Florent de Saumur[29].  
2 CONT >>He gained control of the counties of Chartres and Châteaudun in [960], and became the vassal of Lothaire King of the West Franks in 963.  
2 CONT >>He was excommunicated by Odalric Archbishop of Reims in 964 for taking Coucy and other estates from the archbishopric[30].  
2 CONT >>Seigneur de Chino, de Saumur et de Beaugency.  
2 CONT >>He plotted against Richard I Comte [de Normandie], who defeated his forces in [955] after the French had captured Evreux[31].  
2 CONT >>A charter dated May 974 records a donation by "''comes Teutbaldus''" to Saint-Florent de Saumur[32]. 
2 CONT >'''m''' ([943/44]) as her second husband, '''LUITGARDIS de Vermandois''', widow of GUILLAUME I “''Longuespée''” Comte [de Normandie], daughter of HERIBERT [II] Comte de Vermandois [Carolingian] & his wife Adela [Capet] (before 92
2 CONC 5-14 Nov after 985, bur Chartres, Abbaye de Saint-Père). 
2 CONT >>Rodulfus Glauber refers to the wife of Comte Guillaume as "''sororem [Heribertum Trecorum comitem]''", specifying that she was childless by her first husband, when recording her second marriage to "Tetbaldus"[33].  
2 CONT >>The ''Liber Modernorum Regum Francorum'' refers to the wife of "''Tetbaudi comitis''" as "''sorore Herberti Trecorum comitis''"[34].  
