2 CONC ti Petri Carnotensis''", on the advice of "''Odonem, simul cum sua matre Ledgarde, pariterque dominam meam Bertam, ipsius æque coniugem''"[38].  
2 CONT >>The necrology of Chartres cathedral records the death "''XVIII Kal Dec''" of "''Letgardis comitissa''"[39]. 
2 CONT >>'''Comte Thibaut & his wife had five children:'''
2 CONT >>1.'''THIBAUT de Blois''' (-killed in battle [Sep 960/962]). 
2 CONT >>"''Domnus Tetbaldus comes Turonis''" withdrew his claims to a serf in favour of the monks of Saint-Martin de Tours by charter dated 957, signed by "''domni Tetbaldi comitis, Tetbaldi filii ipsius…Alberici Aurelianensium vicecomi
2 CONC tis''…"[40]. 
2 CONT >>"''Teutbaldi comitis, Teutbaldi junioris, Gausfredi comitis, Hugonis comitis Cenomannorum''…" subscribed the charter dated Sep 960 under which "''Aremburgis''" donated property to Saint-Florent de Saumur[41]. 
2 CONT >>2.'''HUGUES de Blois''' (-2 Jan 986).  "''Hugonis archiepiscopi filii Theobaldi comitis''" subscribed the charter dated 950 under which Ragnfred Bishop of Chartres donated property to Chartres Saint-Père[42].  
2 CONT >>The necrology of Saint-Père-en-Vallée records the death "''IV Non Jan''" of "''Hugo Bituricensis archiepiscopus filius comitisse Legardis''", recording that they jointly donated "''Gesiacum…predia''"[43].  
2 CONT >>Archbishop of Bourges 965-985.  
2 CONT "''Ledgardis''" donated property to "''Sancti Petri Carnotensis ecclesiam''", for the souls of "''senioris mei…comitis Tedbaldi…patris mei Heirberti, Trecassini comitis''", with the consent of "''archipresule…Hugone et…comite Odon
2 CONC e, filiis meis''", by charter dated 5 Feb 978, signed by "…''Emma comitissa Pictavæ urbis''…"[44].  
2 CONT >>"''Hugonis ducis, Odonis comitis, Hugonis sanctæ Bituricensis archipræsulis, Letgardis comitissæ, Bertæ comitissæ, Gauzfridi vicecomitis''…" subscribed the charter dated 985 under which "Robertus" donated property to ''"Sancti P
2 CONC etri Carnotensis''", on the advice of "''Odonem, simul cum sua matre Ledgarde, pariterque dominam meam Bertam, ipsius æque coniugem''"[45].  
2 CONT >>The necrology of Chartres Cathedral records the death “IV Non Jan” of “Hugo Bituricensis archiepiscopus et canonicus Sanctæ Mariæ”[46]. 
2 CONT >>3. '''EUDES de Blois''' (-Châteaudun [12 Feb/4 Jul][47] 995, bur Tours, Abbaye de Saint-Martin, Marmoutier). >>"''Odonis comitis filii Theobaldi comitis''" subscribed the charter dated 950 under which Ragnfred Bishop of Chartres
2 CONC  donated property to Chartres Saint-Père[48].  
2 CONT >>Rodulfus Glaber names "''Odo…filius Tetbaldi Carnotensis cognomento fallacis''", recording that he was "chief among the rebels…who rebelled against the king [Robert I] from positions that should have made them humble"[49].  
2 CONT >>Rodulfus Glauber names "''Odonem''" son of "''Tetbaldus [et] sororem [Heribertum Trecorum comitem]''"[50].  
2 CONT >>Ademar names "''Odonis Campanensis''" as brother of "''Emma''", mother of Guillaume Duke of Aquitaine[51].  
2 CONT >>Odalric Archbishop of Reims granted him Coucy after recovering it from Eudes's father[52].  
2 CONT >>He succeeded his father as EUDES I Comte de Blois, de Chartres, de Châteaudun, de Tours, de Beauvais et de Dreux.  
2 CONT >>"''Odo comes''…" signed a charter dated Feb 977 of Chartres Saint-Père[53].  
2 CONT >>"''Odoni comitis''…" signed a charter dated Oct 977 relating to Bourgeuil[54].  
2 CONT >>"''Ledgardis''" donated property to "''Sancti Petri Carnotensis ecclesiam''", for the souls of "''senioris mei…comitis Tedbaldi…patris mei Heirberti, Trecassini comitis''", with the consent of "''archipresule…Hugone et…comite Od
2 CONC one, filiis meis''", by charter dated 5 Feb 978, signed by "…''Emma comitissa Pictavæ urbis''…"[55].  
2 CONT >>Seigneur de Chinon et de Saumur.  "Odo comes" restored "''villam…Culturas''" to the abbey of Marmoutier by charter dated 3 May 983, signed by "''Berte comitisse uxoris eius, majoris filii eius Teutboldi, minoris filii eius Odoni
2 CONC s adhuc in cunabulo quiescentis''"[56].  
2 CONT >>A letter of Gerbert dated 983 records that "''Heriberti Trecassini et Oddonis comitis filii Tedbaldi''" were enemies of "''Adelbero Remonis archiepiscopus''"[57], while a letter dated to mid-985 records that "''Ottonem, Heribert
2 CONC um"'' made peace with the archbishop[58].  
2 CONT >>A letter of Gerbert dated to [late 986/early 987] records that "''O et Heribertus comites''" were part of the council of Emma Queen of France[59].  
2 CONT >>It is assumed that "Oddonis/Ottonem/O" all refer to the same person.  Rodolfus Glaber records his place of burial when stating that his son Eudes II was buried next to his father[60].  
2 CONT >>'''m''' ([978/80]) '''as her first husband, BERTHE of Burgundy''', daughter of CONRAD I “le Pacifique” King of Burgundy [Welf] & his second wife Mathilde de France [Carolingian] ([964/965]-16 Jan after 1010).  
2 CONT >>The ''Liber Modernorum Regum Francorum'' names "''Berta filia Conradi regis Burgundiæ''" wife of "''Odone comite Carnotensium''"[61].  
2 CONT >>Rodulfus Glauber names "''Odo natus ex filia Chuonradi regis Austrasiorum, Berta nomine''"[62].  The date of her marriage is suggested by the charter dated 3 May 983 under which "Odo comes" restored "''villam…Culturas''" to the 
2 CONC abbey of Marmoutier, signed by "Berte comitisse uxoris eius, majoris filii eius Teutboldi, minoris filii eius Odonis adhuc in cunabulo quiescentis"[63].  
2 CONT >>"''Hugonis ducis, Odonis comitis, Hugonis sanctæ Bituricensis archipræsulis, Letgardis comitissæ, Bertæ comitissæ, Gauzfridi vicecomitis''…" subscribed the charter dated 985 under which "''Robertus''" donated property to "''Sanc
2 CONC ti Petri Carnotensis''", on the advice of "Odonem, simul cum sua matre Ledgarde, pariterque dominam meam Bertam, ipsius æque coniugem"[64].  
2 CONT >>A charter dated 996 records the confirmation by "''comitissæ Berthæ''" of the donation by "''Odo comes''" of property for the construction of the abbey of Bourgeuil, with the consent of "filiorum suorum Teobaldi…atque Odonis"[65
2 CONC ].  
2 CONT >>>She married secondly ([late 996/early 997], divorced [1003/05]) as his second wife, Robert II King of France.  Richer records that King Robert married "''Berta Odonis uxor''"[66].  
2 CONT >>>"''Bertæ reginæ, Odonis comitis filii eius''…" subscribed the charter dated 1004 under which "''Gislebertus prepositus''" recorded a donation[67].  
2 CONT >>>"''Odonis comitis, Ermengardis uxoris eius, Bertæ reginæ''…" subscribed the charter dated after 1005 under which "''comitem Odonem''" donated property "''in comitatu Dunensi…Boscus Medius''" to "''Sancti Petri''"[68].  
2 CONT >>>The necrology of Chartres cathedral records the death "''XVII Kal Feb''" of "''Berta mater Odonis comitis''"[69].  
2 CONT >>'''Comte Eudes I & his wife had [six] children:'''
2 CONT >>'''—a) [ROBERT de Blois''' (-[989/95]).  "''Odonis comitis, Rotberti filii eius, Tetbaldi filius eius, Odonis alterius filius, Hugonis vicecomitis Castridunensis, Raherii de Montigniaco''" subscribed the charter dated 989 under 
2 CONC which "Robert Vicomte de Blois" donated property to the abbey of Evron[70].  Lex suggests that this document was a 12th century falsification and that this supposed eldest son Robert did not exist[71].  This position is supported 
2 CONC by the charter dated 3 May 983 under which "Odo comes" restored "villam…Culturas" to the abbey of Marmoutier, signed by "Berte comitisse uxoris eius, majoris filii eius Teutboldi, minoris filii eius Odonis adhuc in cunabulo quiesc
2 CONC entis"[72].] 
2 CONT >>'''—b) THIBAUT de Blois''' ([979/81]-11 Jul 1004, bur Chartres Saint-Père).  "Odo comes" restored "villam…Culturas" to the abbey of Marmoutier by charter dated 3 May 983, signed by "Berte comitisse uxoris eius, majoris filii eiu
2 CONC s Teutboldi, minoris filii eius Odonis adhuc in cunabulo quiescentis"[73].  "Odonis comitis, Rotberti filii eius, Tetbaldi filius eius, Odonis alterius filius, Hugonis vicecomitis Castridunensis, Raherii de Montigniaco" subscribed
2 CONC  the charter dated 989 under which "Robert Vicomte de Blois" donated property to the abbey of Evron[74].  He succeeded his father in 995 as THIBAUT II Comte de Blois.  A charter dated 996 records the confirmation by "comitissæ Ber
2 CONC thæ" of the donation by "Odo comes" of property for the construction of the abbey of Bourgeuil, with the consent of "filiorum suorum Teobaldi…atque Odonis"[75].  He resigned in favour of his younger brother and became a priest.  A
2 CONC  charter dated to before 1024 records that "comes Tedbaldus" was buried "in capitulo Sancti Petri" at the feet of "fratris sui Teoderici"[76]. 
2 CONT >>'''—c) EUDES de Blois''' ([982/83]-15 Nov 1037).  "Odo comes" restored "villam…Culturas" to the abbey of Marmoutier by charter dated 3 May 983, signed by "Berte comitisse uxoris eius, majoris filii eius Teutboldi, minoris filii 
2 CONC eius Odonis adhuc in cunabulo quiescentis"[77].  He succeeded his brother as EUDES II Comte de Blois, de Chartres, de Châteaudun, de Tours, de Beauvais. 
2 CONT >>'''—d) AGNES de Blois'''  "La reine Berthe et ses enfants Thibaud, Eudes et Agnès" confirmed a donation to Bourgeuil by Emma Ctss de Poitiers dated Sep 1001[78].  A charter dated to before 1024 records that "Odonis comitis, Bert
2 CONC æ matris suæ, Agnetis filiæ ipsius" subscribed a charter dated to before 1024 recording a donation to Chartres Saint-Père "in capitulo Sancti Petri" at the feet of "fratris sui Teoderici"[79].  [A fragmentary chronicle of the duke
2 CONC s of Aquitaine records that "Wido…comes de Thoarcio, vicecomitis Ebles filius" married "Agnete" who brought him "terram…de Salmuriaco" from "Odone patre comite Turonensi"[80].  It should be noted that the genealogy of the vicomtes
2 CONC  de Thouars which is included in this document cannot be fitted into the family which has been reconstructed from other primary sources and is shown in the document AQUITAINE NOBILITY.  Its accuracy is therefore open to doubt.  m 
2 CONC GUY Vicomte de Thouars, son of EBLES Vicomte de Thouars & his wife Altrude de Limoges.] 
2 CONT >>'''—e) THIERRY de Blois''' (-[996/Sep 1101], bur Chartres Saint-Père).  A charter dated to before 1024 records that "comes Tedbaldus" was buried "in capitulo Sancti Petri" at the feet of "fratris sui Teoderici"[81]. 
2 CONT >>'''—f)  LANDRY de Blois''' (-after 27 Sep 1007).  A charter of Robert II King of France dated 1007 confirmed the properties of "ecclesia B. Mariæ Bellimontis…sita a castro Patris Martini" near Tours including the donation of "Li
2 CONC uziam" [Luzé] with the consent of "Odonis comitis et fratris sui Landrici"[82]. 
2 CONT >>4. '''EMMA de Blois''' ([953]-1 Aug, 1004 or later). 
2 CONT >>The Chronicle of Adémar de Chabannes records the marriage of "''Willelmum''" (son of "''Willelmo Capite stupæ''") and "''filiam Tetbaldi Campenensis…Emmam''"[83].  
2 CONT >>The Chronicle of Saint-Maxence names ''"filiam Tetbaudi Campanensis…Emmam sive Emelinam''" as the wife of "''Willelmu duce…Caput Stupæ…filium eius Willelmum''"[84].  
2 CONT >>She inherited property near Vernon in eastern Normandy from her mother which she gave to the abbey of Bourgueil in Aquitaine[85].  
2 CONT >>Her dowry in 968 was Chinon.  
2 CONT >>"''Vuillelmus dux Aquitanorum''" donated property to Saint-Jean d'Angély for the soul of "…''uxore mea Emma''…" by charter dated [971][86].  
2 CONT >>She fled Poitou between 976 and 988 because of the adulterous behaviour of her husband[87].  
2 CONT >>"''Ledgardis''" donated property to "''Sancti Petri Carnotensis ecclesiam''", for the souls of "''senioris mei…comitis Tedbaldi…patris mei Heirberti, Trecassini comitis''", with the consent of "''archipresule…Hugone et…comite Od
2 CONC one, filiis meis''", by charter dated 5 Feb 978, signed by "…''Emma comitissa Pictavæ urbis''…"[88].  
2 CONT >>"''Willelmus Aquitanorum comes et dux et uxor mea Hemma et filius noster equivocus Willelmus''" donated property to Saint-Maixent by charter dated Dec 992[89].  
2 CONT >>"''Emme matris eius''" subscribed the donation by "''Willelmus dux Aquitanorum''" of property to St Cyprien, Poitiers by charter dated [990/1004][90].  
2 CONT >>She confirmed her son's 27 Dec 1003 donation of Bretignolle to the Abbey of Bourgueil, but according to Richard she was still alive when her first grandson was born in 1004[91].  
2 CONT >>A necrology of Vendôme La Trinité records the death "''Kal Aug''" of "''Emma comitissa, Burgulii''"[92].  
2 CONT >>'''m''' ([968]) '''GUILLAUME IV "Fier-à-Bras" Duke of Aquitaine''' [GUILLAUME II Comte de Poitou], son of GUILLAUME III “Tête d'Etoupes” Duke of Aquitaine [GUILLAUME I Comte de Poitou] & his wife Adela [Gerloc] [de Normandie] ([
2 CONC 937]-Saint-Maixent 995 after May, bur Abbaye de Saint-Maixent).  
