2 CONT 2. HUGUES de Blois (-2 Jan 986). "Hugonis archiepiscopi filii Theobaldi comitis" subscribed the charter dated 950 under which Ragnfred Bishop of Chartres donated property to Chartres Saint-Père[42]. The necrology of Saint-Père-en-
2 CONC Vallée records the death "IV Non Jan" of "Hugo Bituricensis archiepiscopus filius comitisse Legardis", recording that they jointly donated "Gesiacum…predia"[43]. Archbishop of Bourges 965-985. "Ledgardis" donated property to "Sanc
2 CONC ti Petri Carnotensis ecclesiam", for the souls of "senioris mei…comitis Tedbaldi…patris mei Heirberti, Trecassini comitis", with the consent of "archipresule…Hugone et…comite Odone, filiis meis", by charter dated 5 Feb 978, signed
2 CONC  by "…Emma comitissa Pictavæ urbis…"[44]. "Hugonis ducis, Odonis comitis, Hugonis sanctæ Bituricensis archipræsulis, Letgardis comitissæ, Bertæ comitissæ, Gauzfridi vicecomitis…" subscribed the charter dated 985 under which "Rober
2 CONC tus" donated property to "Sancti Petri Carnotensis", on the advice of "Odonem, simul cum sua matre Ledgarde, pariterque dominam meam Bertam, ipsius æque coniugem"[45]. The necrology of Chartres Cathedral records the death “IV Non 
2 CONC Jan” of “Hugo Bituricensis archiepiscopus et canonicus Sanctæ Mariæ”[46]. 
