1 OCCU Count of Hainault, de Mons 957, de Mons, de Valenciennes, Châtelain de Valenciennes, Sieur d'Ostrevant, Count de Hainhault, Graf im Hennegau, Reginar III Graf of Hainault
1 NOTE {geni:about_me} '''Reginar II, Count of Hainaut''' @[http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Reginar_II,_Count_of_Hainaut '''en.Wikipedia''']
2 CONT
2 CONT Reginar (or Rainier) II (890–932) was Lotharingian magnate who was active from approximately 915 to 932. He was brother of Duke Gilbert of Lotharingia, who died at the Battle of Andernach in 939, and because his son and grandson c
2 CONC laimed it, he probably already personally held the fort of Mons in Hainaut as the seat of a county.
2 CONT
2 CONT He was the son of Reginar I Longneck, and this means his paternal grandmother was possibly a daughter of Charles the Bald and Ermentrude.
2 CONT
2 CONT Flodoard's Annals, reports under the year 924 that Reginar the brother of Duke Gilbert of Lotharingia already had a son who was given as a hostage during conflicts between several of the Lotharingian magnates of the time.[1]
2 CONT
2 CONT By 943 he was dead, because a charter made in favor of his widowed daughter was done partly in the name of atoning for his sins.[2]
2 CONT
2 CONT Reginar II had at least three children with Adelaide, daughter of Richard, Duke of Burgundy:
2 CONT
2 CONT >'''Issue'''
2 CONT >1. Reginar III, Count of Hainaut
2 CONT >2. Rodolphe, Count of the Maasgau;
2 CONT >3. Liéthard
2 CONT >4. A daughter who married to Nibelung, Count of Betuwe.
2 CONT
2 CONT Upon his death, Reginar was succeeded as Count of Hainaut by his son and namesake.
2 CONT
2 CONT >'''References'''
2 CONT >1. ''The annals of Flodoard of Reims'', 919-966, S. Fanning and David. S. Bachrach trans., in: Readings in medieval civilizations and cultures 9 (Peterborough etc. 2004) p.11. Also Latin edition available at dmgh.de, MGH SS 3, J.
2 CONC  Heller and G. Waitz, eds (Hannover 1881).
2 CONT >2. Vanderkindere, Léon, ‘A propos d´une charte de Baldéric d’Utrecht’, in:'' Académie royale de Belgique Bulletin de la Classe des Lettres et des Sciences Morales et Politiques'' (1900)
2 CONT ——————————————————————————————
2 CONT ====Medlands''' (''18 Aug 2022'') [https://fmg.ac/Projects/MedLands/HAINAUT.htm#ReginarIIdiedafter932A Hainaut].====
2 CONT >'''REGINAR [II]''', son of REGINAR [I] "Langhals/Longneck" Graf im Maasgau & his wife Alberade --- ([885/900]-932 or after).  The Annales Hanoniæ name "''Raginerus''" as son of "''Raginerus dictus Longi-colli''"[26].  Flodoard na
2 CONC mes "''Ragenarii, fratris ipsius Gisleberti''"[27].  
2 CONT >'''Charles III "le Simple"''' King of the West Franks restored Kloster Süsteren to the abbey of Prüm by charter dated 19 Jan 916 which names "''fidelium nostrorum…Widricus comes palatii, Richuuinus comes, Gislebertus, Matfridus, 
2 CONC Beringerius comites, Theodericus comes, Reinherus comes, Erleboldus''"[28]. 
2 CONT >'''A document dated 7 Nov 921''' recording a meeting between King Charles III "le Simple" and Heinrich I King of Germany names "''Matfredus, Erkengerus, Hagano, Boso, Waltkerus, Isaac, Ragenberus, Theodricus, Adalardus, Adelelmus
2 CONC ''" as representatives of the former[29].  It is not certain that "''Ragenberus''" refers to Reginar [II] Comte de Hainaut.  
2 CONT >'''Flodoard's Annals''' record that "''Berengarius''" captured "''Giselbertum''" and only freed him after receiving "''filiis Ragenarii fratris ipsius Gisleberti''" as hostages, after which Giselbert ravaged the lands of "''Beren
2 CONC garii, Ragenariique fratris sui et Isaac comitis''"[30]. 
2 CONT >'''The primary source''' which confirms that Reginar [II] was Comte de Hainaut has not yet been identified.  "''Otto…imperator augustus''" confirmed the donations to the convent of Nivelles by "''Regenarius comes''" of property "
2 CONC i''n pago Ardenna super fluvia Aisna in comitatu Waudricia in villa Villaro''" and by "''predicti Regenarii filius nomine Liechardus in pago Hasbanensi in villa Gingolonham''", by "''Rodolphus comes villa Lentlo''", by "''Hillinus
2 CONC …in villa…Gislebrertruoz…pro anima Gisloberti genitoris sui''", and by "''Robertus uxorque eius…Geua cum filio suo Regennario…in pago Hainau in villa…Hayna''" by charter dated 24 Jan 966[31].  This document presumably refers to Co
2 CONC mte Reginar [II], as his son Reginar [III] was living in exile at the date of the charter.  
2 CONT >.
2 CONT >'''Comte Reginar [II] & his wife had four children:'''
2 CONT >1. REGINAR [III] (920-973)....
2 CONT >2. RUDOLF (-after 24 Jan 966)....
2 CONT >3. LIETARD (-[before 944]). 
2 CONT >4. daughter....
2 CONT ——————————————————————————————
