1 NOTE From THE RUFUS PARKS PEDIGREE by Brian J.L. Berry, chart pg 55.
2 CONT
2 CONT Page 54:
2 CONT
2 CONT 6c.     Règnier II, 890-932, younger son, inherited the countship of Hainaut which remained in the male line of descendants, all named Règnier until Règnier V who d. 1035.  The second Règnier made his capital at Mons, still today 
2 CONC the provincial seat of Hainaut. but his principal residence was in the Castle of Hornu, six or seven miles distant.  He mar. Adèle (Adèlaide), dau. of Richard of Burgandy.
