1 NOTE {geni:about_me} -------------------- Adelaudus of Loches1
2 CONT
2 CONT b. circa 820
2 CONT
2 CONT Adelaudus of Loches was born circa 820. He was was given the castle at Loches by Charles the Bald, King of France. Family
2 CONT
2 CONT Child ?Garnier, seigneur de Loches+ b. 844
2 CONT
2 CONT Citations 1.[S193] Louis Halphen and René Poupardin, Counts of Anjou and Ambois http://homepages.rootsweb.ancestry.com/~cousin/html/p49.htm#i5736
2 CONT
2 CONT ----
2 CONT
2 CONT From the Foundation for Medieval Genealogy:
2 CONT
2 CONT http://fmg.ac/Projects/MedLands/FRANKISH%20NOBILITY.htm#_Toc371156049
2 CONT
2 CONT http://fmg.ac/Projects/MedLands/FRANKISH%20NOBILITY.htm#RoscilleMFoulquesIAnjou
2 CONT
2 CONT ADALHARD .
2 CONT
2 CONT m ---. The name of Adalhard's wife is not known.
2 CONT
2 CONT Adalhard & his wife had two children:
2 CONT
2 CONT 1. Garnier (married Tescenda)
2 CONT
2 CONT 2. Adalhard (became a Bishop)
2 CONT
2 CONT The French Wikipedia page on Loches, in its Medieval Period History section, gives further information on who Adalhard, or Alalande, was:
2 CONT
2 CONT http://fr.wikipedia.org/wiki/Loches
2 CONT
2 CONT En 840, Charles le Chauve nomme Alalande, un de ses lieutenants, gouverneur de Loches. Sa petite-fille Roscille se marie avec Foulque Ier d'Anjou, apportant notamment Loches en dot au comté d'Anjou (887).
2 CONT
2 CONT In English:
2 CONT
