2 CONT
2 CONT Chapter 11.  GRAVEN van MAASGAU (MASAU)
2 CONT
2 CONT Both banks of the Maas valley, from Maastricht to the county of Teisterbant and as far as the county of Tettuaria on the right bank, comprised two counties, Upper and Lower Maasgau (or Masau).  The division of Lotharingian territo
2 CONC ries agreed 8 Aug 870 between Ludwig II "der Deutsche" King of the East Franks and his half-brother Charles II "le Chauve" King of the West Franks allocated "…comitatum…Masau subterior…[et] Masau superior…" between King Ludwig Kin
2 CONC g Charles[1491].  Giselbert was installed as count in Maasgau, probably in the late 830s/early 840s, although no record has been found to indicate whether the county was still divided into two parts at that time and if so which of
2 CONC  the parts was ruled by Giselbert.  He was dispossessed briefly, between 846 and 849, after his dispute with Emperor Lothaire concerning his abduction of the emperor's daughter.  Giselbert was also appointed count in Darnau, ident
2 CONC ified in the area of Namur, before 863.  It is assumed that he retained his interests in Maasgau. 
2 CONT
2 CONT =<nowiki>---------------------------------</nowiki>=
2 CONT Giselbert Von Barnau Zu Maasgau Count Of Brabant
