2 CONT '''Pepin III, Count of Vermandois''' (also known as '''Pepin II, Count of Senlis'''; French: Pépin) (c. 846 – 893) was a Frankish noble; the Count of Senlis and Count of Vermandois (850 – 893); Lord of Valois (877 – 886),[1] and l
2 CONC ater Count of Valois (886 – 893). He was a son of Pepin, Count of Vermandois and Valois and thus a grandson of Bernard of Italy, who was himself a grandson of Charlemagne. The brothers of Pepin III were Herbert I, Count of Vermand
2 CONC ois and Bernard II, Count of Laon.
2 CONT
2 CONT Pepin III of Vermandois's wife's name and origin are unknown; their son was:
2 CONT *[https://www.geni.com/people/Pepin-III-count-of-Senlis/6000000202431421839 Pepin III of Senlis] (876 – 922), Count of Senlis.
2 CONT
