2 CONT PEPIN [I], son of BERNARD I King of Italy [Carolingian] & his wife Cunegundis --- ([815]-after 850).  Regino names "Pippinum" son of "Bernhardus filius Pippin rex Italiæ"[577].  Seigneur de Péronne et de Saint-Quentin[578].  Comte
2 CONC  near Paris after 834.  He supported Emperor Lothaire after the death of Emperor Louis I "le Pieux", despite having sworn allegiance to Charles II "le Chauve" King of the West Franks[579].  The Annales Bertiniani name "Ratholdus…e
2 CONC piscopus, Bonifacius comes, Pippinus consanguineus imperatoris" as supporters of Emperor Louis I in 834[580]. 
2 CONT
2 CONT m ---.   The name of Pépin's wife is not known.  Settipani suggests[581] that she was --- [du Vexin], daughter of THEODERIC, son of NIBELUNG Comte du Vexin, bearing in mind that Pépin's descendants inherited estates in the Vexin. 
2 CONT
2 CONT Comte Pépin & his wife had five children:
2 CONT
2 CONT 1.         BERNARD [I] ([845]-[before 893]).  Regino names (in order) "Bernardum, Pippinum et Heribertum" as the three children of "Pippinum"[582].  According to Italian authors[583], Bernard went to Italy and was the ancestor of 
2 CONC the Bernardhengi.  Settipani is sceptical about this, particularly as the names Pepin and Heribert are not found among the alleged descendants.  He suggests that comte Bernard may be the same Bernard recorded as one of the executo
2 CONC rs of Charles II "le Chauve" King of the West Franks in 877[584].  "Adelelm et Bernard comtes de la region du Laonnais" donated property to Sainte-Marie de Laon as executors of the testament of Charles II "le Chauve" King of the F
2 CONC ranks[585]. 
2 CONT
2 CONT 2.         PEPIN [II] ([845]-after 28 Jan 893]).  Regino names (in order) "Bernardum, Pippinum et Heribertum" as the three children of "Pippinum"[586].  At the court of Emperor Charles “le Chauve” in 877[587], thereafter Comte to 
2 CONC the north of Paris.  Emperor Karl III confirmed a grant of property including "villamque in Pipenensi comitatatu quæ Nogenlis dicitur" to the church of Grandval by charter dated 20 Sep 884[588].  Regino names "Folcone episcopo, He
2 CONC riberto et Pippino comitibus in Remorum civitate" when recording that they supported the accession of Charles III "le Simple" King of the West Franks in 892 in opposition to King Eudes, but does not specify the relationship betwee
2 CONC n Heribert and Pepin[589]. 
2 CONT
2 CONT 3.         HERIBERT ([850]-killed [900/6 Nov 907]).  Regino names (in order) "Bernardum, Pippinum et Heribertum" as the three children of "Pippinum", specifying that Heribert killed "Rodulfum comitem filium Balduini comitis"[590].
2 CONC   "Heribertus, Bernhardi frater" is named in the Vita Hludowicis Imperatoris[591].  Regino names "Folcone episcopo, Heriberto et Pippino comitibus in Remorum civitate" when recording that they supported the accession of Charles II
2 CONC I "le Simple" King of the West Franks in 892 in opposition to King Eudes, but does not specify the relationship between Heribert and Pepin[592].  Heribert became Comte de Vermandois in 896.     [Medlands]
2 CONT --------------------
2 CONT http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Pepin_of_Vermandois
2 CONT
2 CONT Pepin (818 - Unknown) was the first count of Vermandois, lord of Senlis, Péronne, and Saint Quentin. He was the son of King Bernard of Italy and Cunigunda. Pepin first appears in 834 as a count to the north of the Seine and then a
2 CONC ppears as same again in 840. In that year, he supported Lothair I against Louis the Pious. Pepin's wife is unknown, she has been spuriously called "Rothaide de Bobbio". His heir inherited much Nibelungid territory and so historian
2 CONC  K. F. Werner hypothesized a marriage to a daughter of Theodoric Nibelung. Their children were: Bernard (c. 844 – after 893), count of Laon Gerberge (born c. 854) Pepin (c. 846–893), count of Senlis and lord of Valois (877–893) He
2 CONC rbert I of Vermandois (c. 850–907) Beatrix (born c. 854) Mathilde (born c. 857) Adelaide (born c. 858) Cunigunda
2 CONT --------------------
2 CONT http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Berengar_II_of_Neustria
2 CONT --------------------
