2 CONT Birth: abt 842, Vermandois, Normandy, France Death: aft 28 Jan 893 Father: Count Pepin de Vermandois (817-892) Mother: Rothaide Misc. Notes
2 CONT
2 CONT Americans of Royal Descent* by Charles Browning, 7th edition, 1986. has, p. 2 (and elsewhere, with minor differences): " PEPIN DE SENLIS DE VALOIS, Count Berengarius, of Bretagne, father of: LADY POPPA DE VALOIS, who m. (his first
2 CONC  wife) Rollo the Dane." [If the above is true, then Pepin was the father of POPPE OF BAYEUX and was the same person as BERENGER, COUNT OF BAYEUX.] From K.Werner's Die Nachkommen der Karl der Grosse, in volume IV, Karl der Grosee, 
2 CONC ed W.Braunfels, 1965: Count in 877, he was present at Reims in 893 with [his brother] HERIBERT when CHARLES THE SIMPLE was crowned by Abp Fulk. [ed. comment by the poster of this information: Sometimes secondary sources call him C
2 CONC t of Valois, I don't know why.] References: [WallopFH],[RoyalAAF],[RFC]
2 CONT
2 CONT Spouses: (blank)
2 CONT
2 CONT Children:
2 CONT
2 CONT 1. Pepin II (~876->922) 2. Poppa (~872-932)
2 CONT ---
2 CONT
2 CONT (Ben M. Angel notes: Holmes' research appears to be based on secondary sources alone. The Medlands project speculates that his sister as being the mother of Poppa. The primary and secondary sources that are cited by FMG indicate t
2 CONC hat Pepin II, himself, was never married nor had children. The Valois reference probably comes from references to his father as being the Comte du Vexin as a result of marriage. The two counties appear to be frequently confused. T
2 CONC he Vexin originated as a county that governed the Gaulic Véliocasses tribe. The Valois was a county based at Vez. The two were united in 1077 under the Capetians. The confusion between the Vexin and the Valois appears to be perpet
2 CONC uated in part by English Wikipedia entries that, although list sources, are not particularly well-cited.)
