2 CONT He was deprived of the throne of Italy by Emperor Louis, the Debonaire, and received a part of Vermandois and the Seigneuries of St. Quentin and Peronne. --------------------
2 CONT
2 CONT Americans of Royal Descent* by Charles Browning, 7th edition, 1986. has, p. 2 (and elsewhere, with minor differences): " PEPIN DE SENLIS DE VALOIS, Count Berengarius, of Bretagne, father of: LADY POPPA DE VALOIS, who m. (his first
2 CONC  wife) Rollo the Dane." [If the above is true, then Pepin was the father of POPPE OF BAYEUX and was the same person as BERENGER, COUNT OF BAYEUX.] From K.Werner's Die Nachkommen der Karl der Grosse, in volume IV, Karl der Grosee, 
2 CONC ed W.Braunfels, 1965: Count in 877, he was present at Reims in 893 with [his brother] HERIBERT when CHARLES THE SIMPLE was crowned by Abp Fulk. [ed. comment by the poster of this information: Sometimes secondary sources call him C
2 CONC t of Valois, I don't know why.]
2 CONT
2 CONT From http://www.rpi.edu/~holmes/Hobbies/Genealogy/ps04/ps04_233.htm
2 CONT
2 CONT [There appears to be a missing generation, probably Pepin I, Ct. of Senlis and Valois, d. ca. 893, between Pepin II and Pepin, Ct. of Vermandois. Cf. W.H.Turton, "The Plantagenet Ancestry" (Balt.:Gen.Pub.Co.,1968),p.112.]
2 CONT
2 CONT References: [RoyalAAF],[PlantagenetA]PlantagenetA] -------------------- PEPIN [I], son of BERNARD I King of Italy [Carolingian] & his wife Cunegundis --- ([815]-after 850). Regino names "Pippinum" son of "Bernhardus filius Pippin 
2 CONC rex Italiæ"[577]. Seigneur de Péronne et de Saint-Quentin[578]. Comte near Paris after 834. He supported Emperor Lothaire after the death of Emperor Louis I "le Pieux", despite having sworn allegiance to Charles II "le Chauve" Kin
2 CONC g of the West Franks[579]. The Annales Bertiniani name "Ratholdus…episcopus, Bonifacius comes, Pippinus consanguineus imperatoris" as supporters of Emperor Louis I in 834[580].
2 CONT
2 CONT m ---. The name of Pépin's wife is not known. Settipani suggests[581] that she was --- [du Vexin], daughter of THEODERIC, son of NIBELUNG Comte du Vexin, bearing in mind that Pépin's descendants inherited estates in the Vexin.
2 CONT
2 CONT Comte Pépin & his wife had five children:
2 CONT
2 CONT 1. BERNARD [I] ([845]-[before 893]). Regino names (in order) "Bernardum, Pippinum et Heribertum" as the three children of "Pippinum"[582]. According to Italian authors[583], Bernard went to Italy and was the ancestor of the Bernar
2 CONC dhengi. Settipani is sceptical about this, particularly as the names Pepin and Heribert are not found among the alleged descendants. He suggests that comte Bernard may be the same Bernard recorded as one of the executors of Charle
2 CONC s II "le Chauve" King of the West Franks in 877[584]. "Adelelm et Bernard comtes de la region du Laonnais" donated property to Sainte-Marie de Laon as executors of the testament of Charles II "le Chauve" King of the Franks[585].
2 CONT
2 CONT 2. PEPIN [II] ([845]-after 28 Jan 893]). Regino names (in order) "Bernardum, Pippinum et Heribertum" as the three children of "Pippinum"[586]. At the court of Emperor Charles “le Chauve” in 877[587], thereafter Comte to the north 
2 CONC of Paris. Emperor Karl III confirmed a grant of property including "villamque in Pipenensi comitatatu quæ Nogenlis dicitur" to the church of Grandval by charter dated 20 Sep 884[588]. Regino names "Folcone episcopo, Heriberto et P
2 CONC ippino comitibus in Remorum civitate" when recording that they supported the accession of Charles III "le Simple" King of the West Franks in 892 in opposition to King Eudes, but does not specify the relationship between Heribert a
2 CONC nd Pepin[589].
2 CONT
2 CONT 3. HERIBERT ([850]-killed [900/6 Nov 907]). Regino names (in order) "Bernardum, Pippinum et Heribertum" as the three children of "Pippinum", specifying that Heribert killed "Rodulfum comitem filium Balduini comitis"[590]. "Heriber
2 CONC tus, Bernhardi frater" is named in the Vita Hludowicis Imperatoris[591]. Regino names "Folcone episcopo, Heriberto et Pippino comitibus in Remorum civitate" when recording that they supported the accession of Charles III "le Simpl
2 CONC e" King of the West Franks in 892 in opposition to King Eudes, but does not specify the relationship between Heribert and Pepin[592]. Heribert became Comte de Vermandois in 896. [Medlands] -------------------- http://en.wikipedia.
2 CONC org/wiki/Pepin_of_Vermandois
2 CONT
2 CONT Pepin (818 - Unknown) was the first count of Vermandois, lord of Senlis, Péronne, and Saint Quentin. He was the son of King Bernard of Italy and Cunigunda. Pepin first appears in 834 as a count to the north of the Seine and then a
2 CONC ppears as same again in 840. In that year, he supported Lothair I against Louis the Pious. Pepin's wife is unknown, she has been spuriously called "Rothaide de Bobbio". His heir inherited much Nibelungid territory and so historian
2 CONC  K. F. Werner hypothesized a marriage to a daughter of Theodoric Nibelung. Their children were: Bernard (c. 844 – after 893), count of Laon Gerberge (born c. 854) Pepin (c. 846–893), count of Senlis and lord of Valois (877–893) He
2 CONC rbert I of Vermandois (c. 850–907) Beatrix (born c. 854) Mathilde (born c. 857) Adelaide (born c. 858) Cunigunda -------------------- http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Berengar_II_of_Neustria -------------------- Count Berenguer de Bay
2 CONC eux 1 was born 2 in 848 in Bayeux, Bretagne, France. He died 3 before 930 in France. He married 4 Lady Cunégonde de Rennes before 872.
2 CONT
2 CONT [Notes] Lady Cunégonde de Rennes [Parents] 1, 2 was born 3 in 860 in Rennes, Bretagne, France. She married 4 Count Berenguer de Bayeux before 872. Cunégonde was born in France.
