2 CONT The Magyars were a nomadic tribe who plundered Europe in late 9th/early 10th centuries
2 CONT
2 CONT One Ügyek; m.Emese, dau.of Pr Önedbelia of Dentümoger; they had a son:
2 CONT
2 CONT Álmos, *820, +Transylvania ca 895,
2 CONT had a son: Árpád, Prince of Hungary, +907; he settled in what is now Hungary in about 900, though they continued to ravage western Europe til their defeat by Emperor Otto I in 955.
2 CONT
2 CONT He had issue:
2 CONT *A1. Liüntika (Levente), Pr of Hungary ?, living 895 
2 CONT *A2. Tarkatzus (Tarhos) his son: B1. Teveli; his son: Tormás (Termatzus), lived in Byzantium, +k.a. VIII.955; his son: D1. Koppány, Duke in Somogy, +k.a.997/8 
2 CONT *A3. Jelekh (Üllő) "the Epicure" 
2 CONT *A4. Jutotzas (Jutas); his son: B1. Falitzi (Fajsz), Prince of Hungary (948-955), +ca 955 and B2. Tas, living 950 
2 CONT *A5. Zaltas (Zoltán), Prince of Hungary (907-948); his son: 
2 CONT **B1. Taksony, Prince of Hungary (955-ca 972), *ca 905, +ca 972 Taksony had two sons 
2 CONT ***C1. Géza, Great Prince of Hungary (ca 972-997), *ca 945, +1.2.997 and 
2 CONT ***C2. Mihály (Michael), Duke between March and Gran, +ca 978/before 997 and more Descendants
