2 CONT
2 CONT    3. ^ The Byzantine De administrando imperio says around 950: Prior to this Árpád, the Magyars did never have another ruling prince ('archont') and since then up to today the ruling prince of Hungary has been from that family. H
2 CONC owever, his father was probably proclaimed Grand Prince around 855.
2 CONT
2 CONT    4. ^ http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Constantine_VII_Porphyrogenetos
2 CONT
2 CONT    5. ^ It is remarkable that Árpád was never mentioned by contemporary Western sources, which strengthens the idea that he was the spiritual ruler of the Magyars.
2 CONT
2 CONT    6. ^ Some scholars consider Kende to be the name of a person.
