2 CONT '''Bernard II Plantevelue Comte d'Auvergne''' 1
2 CONT
2 CONT Alias: '''Bernard Comte d'Autun'''
2 CONT
2 CONT Born: 22 MAR 840/41 in Uzes, Languedoc, France 2
2 CONT
2 CONT Died: 886 in Autun, Saone-et-Loire, Bourgogne, France 1
2 CONT
2 CONT Father: '''Bernard I Count of Autun, Margrave Septimania''' b: BEF 804 in Autun, Saone-et-Loire, Bourgogne, France 
2 CONT
2 CONT Mother: '''Dhuoda of Gascony, Countess of Agen & Septimania''' b: ABT 804 in Gascony, France
2 CONT
2 CONT Marriage 1 '''Ermengarde d'Auvergne''' b: 845 in Chalons-sur-Marne, Marne, Champagne, France
2 CONT
2 CONT Children:
2 CONT
2 CONT * William "Le Pieux" Duke of Aquitaine b: ABT 863 in Toulouse, Haute-Garonne, Midi-Pyrenees, France
2 CONT * Ava (Aba) d'Auvergne, Abbess of Sauxillanges b: 865 in Auvergne, France
2 CONT * Adelaide d'Auvergne b: 867 in Auvergne, France
2 CONT * Raculfe de Macon b: ABT 870 in Macon, Saone-et-Loire, Bourgogne, France
2 CONT
2 CONT ==Notes [JW]==
2 CONT
2 CONT Bernard was Count of Aquitaine and the Auvergne, Marquis of Gothie, Count of Autun, Count of Rodez.
2 CONT
2 CONT Turton has Bernard's parents as Bernard d'Auvergne & Luitgard, who are actually parents of his wife Ermengarde.
2 CONT
2 CONT =<nowiki>----------------------</nowiki>=
2 CONT
2 CONT The following is a post-em by Curt Hofemann, curt_hofemann@yahoo.com:
2 CONT
2 CONT ID: I01374 Bernard II Plantevelue Comte d'Auvergne
2 CONT
2 CONT Bernard was Count of Aquitaine and the Auvergne, Marquis of Gothie, Count of Autun, Count of Rodez.
2 CONT
2 CONT As far as Count of Aquitaine, Ronald F. Malan in _The Genealogist_ vol. xi in an article titled: "The Ancestry of Dhouda, Duchess of Septamani" did state this. To my knowledge, Aquitaine in this period was a duchy not a county, th
2 CONC e duke being Charles III son of Charles II king of Franks, HRE (grandson of Charlemagne). Note: I do not know if there was a "County of Aquitaine" within the duchy, but in this period of the beginnings of titles & meanings of same
2 CONC , I’d think it doubtful.
2 CONT
2 CONT As to where the sources of the titles you give: 
2 CONT
2 CONT Bernard Plantevelue Count of Auvergne [Ref: Bouchard, ES III:731, Dillange, Keats-Rohan Family Trees p247, Nat Taylor 23 May 1997, Nat Taylor-Sant Wm p205-223] 
2 CONT
2 CONT Count of Autun, Count of Auvergne and Rovergue, 872: Marquis of Toulouse [Ref: Moriarty p215]
2 CONT
2 CONT Barnard Hairyfoot, Count of Auvergne; styled Duke by 898 [Ref: McBride2] Note: considering that he died in 885/6… 
2 CONT
2 CONT Marquis of Gothie; Count of Autun, Count of Rodez [Ref: CP II:731, Keats-Rohan Family Trees p211-267]
2 CONT
2 CONT Dillange = Michael Dillange, Les comtes de Poitou, ducs d'Aquitaine (778-1204), Geste Editions, Geste Editions, 1996.
2 CONT
2 CONT Regards,
2 CONT
2 CONT Curt
2 CONT
2 CONT Sources:
2 CONT
2 CONT Title: The Plantagenet Ancestry, by William Henry Turton, 1968
2 CONT
2 CONT Page: 6
2 CONT
2 CONT Title: Newsgroup: soc.genealogy.medieval, at groups - google.com
2 CONT
2 CONT Page: Alan B Wilson, 12 Jun 1998
2 CONT --------------------
2 CONT Aka: Count of Anvergne.
2 CONT --------------------
2 CONT Chapter 4.    DUKES of AQUITAINE 909-927 (FAMILY of BERNARD "Plantevelue")
2 CONT http://fmg.ac/Projects/MedLands/AQUITAINE.htm#BernardPlanteveluedied885 
2 CONT
2 CONT '''BERNARD "Plantevelue" ''', son of BERNARD Marquis of Septimania & his wife Doda --- (Uzès 22 Mar 841-[20 Jun 885/16 Aug 886], maybe 6 Jan 886).  The Manual of Dhuoda records the birth "XI Kal Apr", in the year following the dea
2 CONC th of Emperor Louis, at "Uzecia urbes" of the second child [Bernard] of Doda and her husband Bernard[130].  The Annales Bertiniani name "rex markiones Bernardum scilicet Tolosæ et iterum Bernardum Gothiæ, itemque Bernardum alium" 
2 CONC in 868[131], this being Bernard Marquis of Gothia, although the date of his appointment has not so far been traced.  Lay Abbot of Brioude 857/68.  Comte d'Autun 864/69, deposed.  "Bernardus comes et uxor eius Ermengardis" donated 
2 CONC property "ecclesiam…in villa…Viciaco…et in villa Lubiriaco…et in villa…Dignaciaco…in…patria Arvernica in vicaria Randanensi" to Saint-Julien de Brioude by charter dated 10 Mar [867][132].  Comte de Rodez/Rouergue 864/74.  Comte d'
2 CONC Auvergne after 872.  The Annales Bertiniani name "Bernardum Arvenicum comitem" in 877[133].  "Petrus" donated property "in pago Arvernico in comitatu Brivatensi in vicaria Nonatensi..." to Saint-Julien de Brioude for the souls of 
2 CONC "Bernardi...comitis necnon...Bernardi comitis eiusque conjugis Inmengardis...comitissa, horumque prolis" by charter dated Jan "anno secundo regnante rege Francorum Carolo"[134].  "Bernardus…comes et uxor mea Hermengardis" donated 
2 CONC property "in pago Rutenico, in vicaria Severiacense…villa…Bautone" to the abbey of Conques by charter dated 21 Jul 882[135].  "Bernardus comes et uxor mea Hermengardis" donated property to Conques abbey by charter dated 21 Jul 883
2 CONC [136].  He obtained the county of Mâcon during the wars between the Carolingians and the Bosonids[137].  The 13th century obituary of the Eglise primatiale de Lyon records the death "VIII Id Jan" of "Bernardus comes"[138], althoug
2 CONC h it is not certain that this relates to the same person. 
2 CONT
2 CONT '''m''' ERMENGARDE, daughter of [BERNARD Comte [d'Auvergne] & his wife Liegardis ---] (-after 21 Jul 883).  Ermengarde is shown in Europäische Stammtafeln as the daughter of Bernard and his wife Liegardis[139].  The primary source
2 CONC  on which this information is based has not yet been identified.  It is possible that it results from the charter dated Jan "anno secundo regnante rege Francorum Carolo" under which "Petrus" donated property "in pago Arvernico in 
2 CONC comitatu Brivatensi in vicaria Nonatensi..." to Saint-Julien de Brioude for the souls of "Bernardi...comitis necnon...Bernardi comitis eiusque conjugis Inmengardis...comitissa, horumque prolis"[140].  The document does not specify
2 CONC  any family relationship between the first-named Comte Bernard and the second or his wife Ermengarde.  If such a family relationship existed, one of the possibilities is that Ermengarde was the daughter of the first Bernard.  "Ber
2 CONC nardus comes et uxor eius Ermengardis" donated property "ecclesiam…in villa…Viciaco…et in villa Lubiriaco…et in villa…Dignaciaco…in…patria Arvernica in vicaria Randanensi" to Saint-Julien de Brioude by charter dated 10 Mar [867][1
2 CONC 41].  "Bernardus comes et uxor mea Hermengardis" donated property to Conques abbey by charter dated 21 Jul 883[142].  "Bernardus…comes et uxor mea Hermengardis" donated property "in pago Rutenico, in vicaria Severiacense…villa…Bau
2 CONC tone" to the abbey of Conques by charter dated 21 Jul 882[143].  "Princeps et marchio Willelmus" donated property to the church of Holy Trinity "pro…animæ patris mei Bernardi et matris meæ Ermengardis…" by charter dated Nov 916[14
2 CONC 4].  Her parents are shown in Europäische Stammtafeln[145] but the primary source on which this is based has not yet been identified. 
2 CONT
2 CONT   Comte Bernard & his wife had four children:
2 CONT
2 CONT #    GUILLAUME ([860/65]-6 Jul 918, bur Abbaye de Brioude, Haute-Loire).
2 CONT #    WARIN (-[before 918]). 
2 CONT #         AVA (-before [913]).  
2 CONT #  4.         ADALINDA .
2 CONT
2 CONT --------------------
2 CONT Bernard Plantapilosa or Bernard II of Auvergne (22 March 841 – 886[1]), or Plantevelue, son of Bernard of Septimania and Dhuoda, was the Count of Auvergne (as Bernard II) from 872 to his death. The Emperor Charles the Fat granted 
2 CONC him the title of Margrave of Aquitaine in 885.
2 CONT
2 CONT His mother's Liber Manualis mentions that he was born at Uzès in the year following the death of Louis the Pious. He was appointed Margrave of Septimania (or Gothia) before 868. He was the lay abbot of Brioude between 857 and 868 
2 CONC and Count of Autun and from 864 to 869. He was deposed before 876 and replaced by Bernard of Gothia in that year. He returned to favour under Charles the Fat. In the war against Boso of Provence, he obtained the county of Mâcon.
2 CONT
2 CONT https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Bernard_Plantapilosa
2 CONT
2 CONT https://fmg.ac/Projects/MedLands/AQUITAINE.htm#BernardPlanteveluedied885
2 CONT
2 CONT ----
2 CONT
2 CONT From https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Bernard_Plantapilosa
2 CONT
2 CONT Bernard Plantapilosa or Bernard II of Auvergne (22 March 841 – 886[1]), or Plantevelue, son of Bernard of Septimania and Dhuoda, was the Count of Auvergne (as Bernard II) from 872 to his death. The Emperor Charles the Fat granted 
2 CONC him the title of Margrave of Aquitaine in 885.
2 CONT
2 CONT Family He married Ermengard, daughter of Bernard I of Auvergne (or perhaps of Guerin I). 
2 CONT
2 CONT They had at least two children:
2 CONT *William I of Aquitaine
2 CONT *Adelinda, who married Acfred I of Carcassonne
2 CONT
2 CONT Plantapilosa is often claimed to mean "Hairyfeet" or "Hairypaws".[2] This is based on the Latin meaning "sole of foot" of planta.
