2 CONT -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
2 CONT
2 CONT Rolf Nevja (Nese) var odelsbonde. Han levde 820. Han hadde datteren Hild Rolvsdatter. 
2 CONT
2 CONT Nefja eller Nevja er ikke et slektsnavn, men et tilnavn Rolv hadde. Betydninger er "nese" og hadde trolig å gjøre med skatteinnkreving (pr. nese).
2 CONT
2 CONT Fornavnet er opprinnelig Hrólfr eller Hrólf (avhengig av grammatisk form), på moderne norsk Rolf eller Rolv. 
2 CONT
2 CONT Fra Snorre Sturlason: Harald Hårfagres saga:
2 CONT
2 CONT «24. Ragnvald Mørejarl var den kjæreste venn kong Harald hadde, og kongen satte ham høyt. Ragnvald jarl var gift med Hild, datter til Rolv Nevja (Nese); deres sønner var Rolv og Tore. ...» 1)
2 CONT
2 CONT 1) Snorre Sturlasson: Harald Hårfagres saga, avsnitt 24. 
2 CONT
2 CONT Mogens Bugge: Våre forfedre, nr. 282. 
2 CONT
2 CONT Bent og Vidar Billing Hansen: Rosensverdslektens forfedre, side 76. 
2 CONT
2 CONT http://www.tore-nygaard.com/middelalder/2708.htm
2 CONT
2 CONT ---------------------
2 CONT
2 CONT '''Original text from''' http://lind.no/nor/splitt.asp?lang=no&emne=&person=&list=&vis=s_ie_harald_harfagre:
2 CONT
2 CONT "25. Göngu-Hrólfur útlægur ger: Rögnvaldur Mærajarl var hinn mesti ástvin Haralds konungs og konungur virti hann mikils. Rögnvaldur átti Hildi dóttur Hrólfs nefju. Synir þeirra voru þeir Hrólfur og Þórir."
2 CONT
2 CONT "25. Gongu-Hrólfur exiled; Rögnvaldur Earl of Mæra was the greatest lover of King Harald and the king held him in high esteem. Rögnvaldur married Hildi, daughter of Hrólfur's nephew. Their sons were Hrólfur and Þórir."
2 CONT
2 CONT --------------------
2 CONT
2 CONT '''Hrolf* NEFJA'''
2 CONT
2 CONT BIRTH: ABT 0826, Norway
2 CONT DEATH: ABT 0847, Norway 
2 CONT
2 CONT MARRIAGE: 0804, Maer,Nord Trondelag,Norway 
2 CONT +Rognhild* HROLFSDATTER 
2 CONT
2 CONT --------------------
2 CONT
2 CONT '''Levde fra 845 til 886.''' 
2 CONT
2 CONT Hild (Ragnhild) reiste til kong Harald Hårfagre for å be om nåde for sin sønn, Gange-Rolv, da han av kongen ca. 886 var lyst fredløs over hele Norge på grunn av strandhugg i Viken, men Gange-Rolv måtte forlate landet.
2 CONT
2 CONT Fra Snorre Sturlasson: Harald Hårfagres saga: «24. Ragnvald Mørejarl var den kjæreste venn kong Harald hadde, og kongen satte ham høyt, Ragnvald jarl var gift med Hild, datter til Rolv Nevja (Nese); deres sønner var Rolv og Tore.
2 CONT  ...
2 CONT Rolv var en stor viking; Han var så svær av vekst at ingen hest kunne bære ham, derfor gikk han til fots overalt. Han ble kalt Gange-Rolv. Han herjet ofte i Austerveg. En sommer han kom østfra til Viken fra vikingtog, hogg han str
2 CONC andhogg der. Kong Harald var i Viken; han ble alvorlig sint, da han fikk høre om dette, for han hadde strengt forbudt å rane innenlands. Kongen lyste på tinget at han gjorde Rolv fredløs i Norge. Da Hild, Rolvs mor, fikk vite dett
2 CONC e, dro hun til kongen på ba om fred for Rolv, men kongen var så sint at det nyttet henne ikke å be. Da kvat Hild dette:
2 CONT
2 CONT >Du vraker Nevjas navne, driver som varg av landet
2 CONT >bønders kjekke helbror; hvorfor så bister, herre?
2 CONT >farlig å vise ulvhug mot slik en ulv, høvding;
2 CONT >han blir ikke god mot fyrstens flokk om til skogs han renner».
2 CONT §
2 CONT '''Lived from 845 to 886.'''
2 CONT
2 CONT Hild (Ragnhild) traveled to King Harald Fairhair to ask for mercy for her son, Gange-Rolv, when the king had declared him an outlaw throughout Norway around 886 because of beaching in Viken, but Gange-Rolf had to leave the country
2 CONC .
2 CONT
2 CONT From Snorri Sturlasson: Harald Fairhair's saga: "24. Ragnvald Earl of Møre was the dearest friend that King Harald had, and the king held him in high esteem. Earl Ragnvald was married to Hild, daughter of Rolf Nevja (Nose); their 
2 CONC sons were Rolf and Tore.
2 CONT
2 CONT Rolf was a great Viking; He was so large in stature that no horse could carry him, so he went everywhere on foot. He was called Gange-Rolf. He often ravaged Austerveg. One summer he came from the east to Viken from a Viking raid, 
2 CONC he cut down the beach there. King Harald was in Viken; he was seriously angry when he heard about this, because he had strictly forbidden robbing within the country. The king announced at the Thing that he was making Rolv an outla
2 CONC w in Norway. When Hild, Rolf's mother, heard this, she went to the king to ask for peace for Rolv, but the king was so angry that it was no use for her to ask. Then Hild said this:
2 CONT
2 CONT >You are destroying Nevja's name, driving like a wolf from the land
2 CONT >the handsome full brother of the farmers; why so fierce, lord?
2 CONT >It is dangerous to show wolfishness against such a wolf, chieftain;
2 CONT >he will not be good to the prince's flock if he runs into the forest".
2 CONT
2 CONT '''———————————————————————————'''
2 CONT ====Heimskringla.no/wiki: [https://heimskringla.no/wiki/Haralds_saga_hins_h%C3%A1rfagra '''''Haralds saga hins hárfagra''''']:—
2 CONT
2 CONT '''24.''' Gönguhrólfr gerr útlœgr.'''
2 CONT
2 CONT “Rögnvaldr Mœrajarl var hinn mesti ástvin Haralds konungs, ok konungr virði hann mikils. Rögnvaldr jarl átti Hildi, dóttur Hrólfs nefju, synir þeirra váru þeir Hrólfr ok Þórir. Rögnvaldr jarl átti ok friðlusonu 3, hét einn Hallaðr
2 CONC , annar Einarr, þriði Hrollaugr. Þeir váru rosknir, þá er hinir skírbornu brœðr þeirra váru börn. Hrólfr var víkingr mikill; hann var svá mikill maðr vexti, at engi hestr mátti bera hann, ok gékk hann hvargi sem hann fór; hann var
2 CONC  kallaðr Gönguhrólfr. Hann herjaði mjök í Austrvegu. Á einu sumri er hann kom or víkingu austan í Víkina, þá hjó hann þar strandhögg. Haraldr konungr var í Víkinni; hann varð mjök reiðr, þá er hann spurði þetta, því at hann hafði 
2 CONC mikit bann á lagt at ræna innanlands. Konungr lýsti því á þingi, at hann gerði Hrólf útlaga af Noregi. En er þat spurði Hildr, móðir hans, þá fór hon á fund konungs ok bað friðar Hrólfi. Konungr var svá reiðr, at henni týði ekki a
2 CONC t biðja. Þá kvað Hildr þetta:
2 CONT
2 CONT >Hafnit nefju nafna! 
2 CONT >Nú rekit gand or landi 
2 CONT >horskan hölda barma; 
2 CONT >hví bellit því stillir? 
2 CONT >Ilt er við úlf at ylfask 
2 CONT >Yggs valbríkar slíkan; 
2 CONT >muna við hilmis hjarðir 
2 CONT >hœgr, ef hann renn til skógar.
2 CONT
2 CONT “Gönguhrólfr fór síðan vestr um haf til Suðreyja, ok þaðan fór hann vestr í Valland ok herjaði þar ok eignaðist jarlsríki mikit ok bygði þar mjök Norðmönnum, ok er þar síðan kallat Norðmandí. Son Gönguhrólfs var Vilhjálmr, faðir R
2 CONC íkarðar, föður annars Ríkarðar, föður Roðberts löngum spaða, föður Vilhjálms bastarðs Englakonungs; frá honum eru síðan komnir Englakonungar allir. Af Hrólfs ætt eru ok komnir jarlar í Norðmandí. 
2 CONT
2 CONT ”Ragnhildr dróttning hin ríka lifði síðan 3 vetr, er hon kom í Noreg. En eptir dauða hennar fór Eiríkr, son þeirra Haralds konungs til fóstrs í Fjörðu til Þóris hersis Hróaldssonar, ok fœddist hann þar upp.”
2 CONT
2 CONT ====Translated eBook: Passage Above
2 CONT >'''Sturlason, Snorri. (c.1225) 2009.''' ''Heimskringla, or The Chronicle of the Kings Of Norway''. Translated by Douglas B. Killings and David Widger. Salt Lake City, Utah, USA: Project Gutenberg. [https://www.gutenberg.org/files
2 CONC /598/598-h/598-h.htm#link2H_4_0036 Gutenberg.org/files]:—
2 CONT
2 CONT 24. ROLF GANGER DRIVEN INTO BANISHMENT. 
2 CONT
2 CONT Earl Ragnvald was King Harald's dearest friend, and the king had the greatest regard for him. He was married to Hild, a daughter of Rolf Nefia, and their sons were Rolf and Thorer. Earl Ragnvald had also three sons by concubines,—
2 CONC the one called Hallad, the second Einar, the third Hrollaug; and all three were grown men when their brothers born in marriage were still children Rolf became a great Viking, and was of so stout a growth that no horse could carry 
2 CONC him, and wheresoever he went he must go on foot; and therefore he was called Rolf Ganger. He plundered much in the East sea. One summer, as he was coming from the eastward on a Viking’s expedition to the coast of Viken, he landed 
2 CONC there and made a cattle foray. As King Harald happened, just at that time, to be in Viken, he heard of it, and was in a great rage; for he had forbid, by the greatest punishment, the plundering within the bounds of the country. Th
2 CONC e king assembled a Thing, and had Rolf declared an outlaw over all Norway. When Rolf's mother, Hild heard of it she hastened to the king, and entreated peace for Rolf; but the king was so enraged that here entreaty was of no avail
2 CONC . Then Hild spake these lines:— 
2 CONT
2 CONT >"Think'st thou, King Harald, in thy anger,
2 CONT >To drive away my brave Rolf Ganger
2 CONT >Like a mad wolf, from out the land?
2 CONT >Why, Harald, raise thy mighty hand?
2 CONT >Why banish Nefia's gallant name-son,
2 CONT >The brother of brave udal-men?
2 CONT >Why is thy cruelty so fell?
2 CONT >Bethink thee, monarch, it is ill
2 CONT >With such a wolf at wolf to play,
2 CONT >Who, driven to the wild woods away
2 CONT >May make the king's best deer his prey."
2 CONT
2 CONT Rolf Ganger went afterwards over sea to the West to the Hebrides, or Sudreys; and at last farther west to Valland, where he plundered and subdued for himself a great earldom, which he peopled with Northmen, from which that land is
2 CONC  called Normandy. Rolf Ganger's son was William, father to Richard, and grandfather to another Richard, who was the father of Robert Longspear, and grandfather of William the Bastard, from whom all the following English kings are 
2 CONC descended. From Rolf Ganger also are descended the earls in Normandy. Queen Ragnhild the Mighty lived three years after she came to Norway; and, after her death, her son and King Harald's was taken to the herse Thorer Hroaldson, a
2 CONC nd Eirik was fostered by him. 
2 CONT
2 CONT '''———————————————————————————'''
2 CONT ====Heimskringla.no/wiki: [https://heimskringla.no/wiki/Landn%C3%A1mab%C3%B3k_-_Fj%C3%B3r%C3%B0i_hluti Landnámabók, Fjórði hluti], 8. Kapituli. (tr., Settlement Book, Pt. 4, Ch. 8)
2 CONT Þorsteinn leggr, sonr Bjarnar blátannar, fór ór Suðreyjum til Íslands ok nam lönd öll fyrir norðan Horn til Jökulsár í Lóni ok bjó í Böðvarsholti þrjá vetr, en seldi síðan löndin ok fór aftr í Suðreyjar. 
2 CONT >Thorsteinn Leggr, son of Bjorn Bluetooth, went from the South Islands to Iceland and took all the lands north of Horn to Jökulsá in Lón and lived in Böðvarsholt for three winters, but then sold the lands and went back to the Sout
2 CONC h Islands.
2 CONT Rögnvaldr jarl á Mæri, sonr Eysteins glumru Ívarssonar Upplendingajarls, Hálfdanarsonar ins gamla, Rögnvaldr átti Ragnhildi, dóttur Hrólfs nefju. Þeira sonr var Ívarr, er fell í Suðreyjum með Haraldi konungi inum hárfagra. Annarr 
2 CONC var Göngu-Hrólfr, er vann Norðmandí. Frá honum eru Rúðujarlar komnir ok Englakonungar. Þriði var Þórir jarl þegjandi, er átti Álöfu árbót, dóttur Haralds konungs hárfagra, ok var þeira dóttir Bergljót, móðir Hákonar jarls ins ríka
2 CONC . 
2 CONT >Earl Rögnvaldr of Mæri, son of Eysteinn glumru, son of Earl Ivar, son of Earl Hálfdan the Old, Rögnvaldr married Ragnhild, daughter of Hrólfr's nephew. Their son was Ivarr, who fell in the South Islands with King Harald the Fair-
2 CONC haired. Another was Göngu-Hrólfr, who conquered Nordmandi. From him came the Earls of Rúð and the Kings of the Angles. The third was Earl Þórir the Silent, who married Álöfa Árbót, daughter of King Harald the Fair-haired, and thei
2 CONC r daughter was Bergljót, mother of Earl Hákon the Strong.
2 CONT Rögnvaldr jarl átti frillusonu þrjá. Hét einn Hrollaugr, annarr Einarr, þriði Hallaðr. Sá veltist ór jarlsdómi í Orkneyjum. 
2 CONT >Earl Rögnvald had three concubines. One was named Hrollaugr, another Einarr, the third Hallaðr. He was overthrown from the earldom in Orkney.
2 CONT Ok er Rögnvaldr jarl frá þat, þá kallaði hann saman sonu sína ok spurði, hverr þeira þá vildi til eyjanna, en Þórir bað hann sjá fyrir um sína för. Jarlinn kvað honum vel fara, en kvað hann þar skyldu ríki taka eftir sinn dag. 
2 CONT >And when Earl Rögnvaldr had left, he called his sons together and asked which of them wanted to go to the islands, and Thorir asked him to make arrangements for his journey. The earl said that he would go well, but said that he w
2 CONC ould take the kingdom there after his day.
2 CONT Þá gekk Hrólfr fram ok bauð sik til farar. Rögnvaldr kvað honum vel hent fyrir sakar afls ok hreysti, en kveðst ætla, at meiri ofsi væri í skapi hans en hann mætti þegar at löndum setjast. 
2 CONT >Then Hrolf stepped forward and offered to go. Rögnvaldr said he was well suited for the task because of his strength and bravery, but said he thought there was more anger in his temper than he could immediately settle down on lan
2 CONC d.
2 CONT Þá gekk Hrollaugr fram ok spurði, ef hann vildi, at hann færi. Rögnvaldr kvað hann ekki mundu jarl verða. "Hefir þú þat skap, er engi styrjöld fylgir. Munu vegir þínir liggja til Íslands. Muntu þar göfugr þykkja á því landi ok ver
2 CONC ða kynsæll, en engi eru hér forlög þín." 
2 CONT >Then Hrollaugr stepped forward and asked if he wanted to go. Rögnvaldr said he would not become an earl. "You have the disposition that no war follows. Your ways will lie to Iceland. You will think noble there in that land and be
2 CONC  sexually attractive, but there are no provisions for you here."
2 CONT Þá gekk Einarr fram ok mælti: "Láttu mik fara til Orkneyja. Ek mun þér því heita, er þér mun bezt þykkja, at ek mun aldri aftr koma þér í augsýn." 
2 CONT >Then Einar stepped forward and said: "Let me go to Orkney. I will promise you whatever you think best, that I will never come into your sight again."
2 CONT Jarlinn svarar: "Vel þykkir mér, at þú farir brott, en lítils er mér ván at þér, því at móðurætt þín er öll þrælborin." 
2 CONT >The earl answers: "It seems good to me that you are leaving, but I have little hope for you, for your mother's family is all slave-born."
2 CONT Eftir þat fór Einarr vestr ok lagði undir sik eyjarnar, sem segir í sögu hans. 
2 CONT >After that, Einar went west and subdued the islands, as is told in his story.
2 CONT Hrollaugr fór þá til Haralds konungs ok var með honum um hríð, því at þeir feðgar kómu eigi skapi saman eftir þetta.
2 CONT >Hrollaugr then went to King Harald and stayed with him for a while, because the father and son did not get along after this.
2 CONT
2 CONT ----
