2 CONT --------------------------------
2 CONT
2 CONT The German Wikipedia page on "Stift Herford" seems to indicate that her granddaughter was brought to be raised at her convent (the oldest in Germany) on her initiative:
2 CONT
2 CONT http://de.wikipedia.org/wiki/Stift_Herford
2 CONT
2 CONT In der Zeit der Äbtissin Mathilde I. wurde hier deren Enkelin Mathilde erzogen, die 909 durch Vermittlung ihrer Großmutter den Sachsenherzog und späteren König Heinrich I. heiratete. In den Jahren 919 bis 924 wurde Herford durch d
2 CONC ie Ungarn zerstört, aber bereits 927 wieder aufgebaut. Zur Erinnerung an ihren 936 verstorbenen Gatten gründete die in Herford erzogene Königin Mathilde im gleichen Jahr ein Frauenstift in Quedlinburg.
2 CONT
2 CONT In English:
2 CONT
2 CONT During the time of Abbess Mathilde I, her granddaughter Mathilde was brought here through her intermediation, and later the girl married Heinrich I, Duke of Saxony and later King. Between 919 and 924, Herford was destroyed by the 
2 CONC Magyars, but by 927 was rebuilt. In the memory of her late husband, the Herford-educated Mathilde established in 936 the Convent of Quedlinburg.
2 CONT --------------------
2 CONT Äbtissin des Klosters Herford 
2 CONT
2 CONT =SOurces=
2 CONT
2 CONT [https://humanmen.wordpress.com/2017/03/14/mathilde-von-ringelheim/ Mathilde of Ringelheim]
2 CONT Published on March 14, 2017 from atomic orbital
2 CONT
2 CONT ----
2 CONT https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Herford
2 CONT
2 CONT Herford, Germany
2 CONT
2 CONT The town was founded in 789 by Charlemagne in order to guard a ford crossing the narrow Werre river. A century later, Matilda, daughter of Theudebert, duke of Saxony, grew up in the abbey of Herford; she was a descendant of the Sa
2 CONC xon leader Widukind. In Herford she met Henry the Fowler, who later became king of Germany. 
2 CONT
