2 CONT
2 CONT {Encyclopaedia Britannica, 1956 Ed., 20:33 states:} Ludolph (Liudolf) was appointed about 850 by King Louis "the German" as margrave to defend the `Limes Saxoniae' (a narrow strip of land on the eastern frontier) against the Slavs
2 CONC . Ludolph vigorously fought the Slavs and extended the frontier and his own influence. {-This source states he died in 866.} He was succeeded by his son Bruno who was killed fighting the Normans in 880; the second son, Otto the Il
2 CONC lustrious, then succeeded and was recognized Duke of Saxony by King Conrad I.
