2 CONT Ben M. Angel's summary:
2 CONT
2 CONT Relationships:
2 CONT
2 CONT Known Parents: Graf Brunhart von Engern/Angaria (Mittelalter Genealogie), all other information unknown or unconfirmed (spouse unknown)
2 CONT
2 CONT Siblings: Unknown
2 CONT
2 CONT Spouse: Oda von Sachsen (daughter of a Billung prince and Aeda), c.805-913
2 CONT
2 CONT Children:
2 CONT
2 CONT 1. Bruno von Sachsen (d. 880) died crossing a flooded river or in battle during an expedition against the Danes. 2. Otto "der Erlauchte" von Sachsen (d. 912), Graf im Südthüringau, Graf im Eichsfeld (888), Lay Abbot of Hersfield (
2 CONC 908), husband of Hedwig/Hathui. 3. Thankmar, Abbot of Corvey (877/879) 4. Liutgard, wife of Ludwig III der Jungere, King of the East Franks (876-911), King of Bavaria (879-911), King of Lotharingia/Lorraine (880-911). 5 Enda, wife
2 CONC  of Unknown 6. Hathmod (840-874), first Abbess of Gandersheim (852/856-874) 7. Gerberga (d. 896/897), second Abbess of Gandersheim (874-896/897) 8. Christina (d. 919/920), third Abbess of Gandersheim (897) One unnamed daughter and
2 CONC  three unnamed sons, died young. Basic information and justifications:
2 CONT
2 CONT Birth: circa 805 (English and German Wikipedia, Genealogie Mittelalter says 805/820) - location unknown, but most likely in the historic province of Engern/Angaria (present Niedersachsen), Stammesherzogtum Sachsen (Duchy of Saxony
2 CONC ), Eastern Franconia
2 CONT
2 CONT Wedding: c820/835 - location unknown
2 CONT
2 CONT Death: 11 March 866 (FMG) - location unknown
2 CONT
2 CONT Burial: First Kloster Gandersheim in Brunshausen (Bad Gandersheim), Landkreis Northeim, Niedersachsen
2 CONT
2 CONT Alternate names: Ludolf
2 CONT
2 CONT Occupation: Dux Orientalium Saxonum, Graf von Sachsen (844-866)
