2 CONT
2 CONT Three brothers, parents not known, although the primary source which confirms this relationship has not so far been identified.
2 CONT
2 CONT It is assumed that the brothers were related to Bruno (d. after 775) and his son Ekbert (d. after 834, husband of Ida). If this is correct, from a chronological point of view they may have been brothers of Ekbert. It is also possi
2 CONC ble that the relationship was through Ekbert's (unknown) mother.
2 CONT
2 CONT 1. BRUNO .
2 CONT
2 CONT Brun was named as father of Liudolf in the early 13th century Gandersheimer Reimchronik[103], but no earlier source has so far been identified which confirms the relationship. m ---. The name of Bruno's wife is not known. Bruno & 
2 CONC his wife had one child:
2 CONT
2 CONT a) LIUDOLF (-11 Mar 866, bur Brunshausen). Graf.
