2 CONT From Mark H. Holmes' personal family research:
2 CONT
2 CONT http://www.rpi.edu/~holmes/Hobbies/Genealogy/ps08/ps08_313.htm
2 CONT
2 CONT {Encyclopaedia Britannica, 1956 Ed., 20:33 states:} Ludolph (Liudolf) was appointed about 850 by King Louis "the German" as margrave to defend the Limes Saxoniae' (a narrow strip of land on the eastern frontier) against the Slavs.
2 CONC  Ludolph vigorously fought the Slavs and extended the frontier and his own influence. {-This source states he died in 866.} He was succeeded by his son Bruno who was killed fighting the Normans in 880; the second son, Otto the Ill
2 CONC ustrious, then succeeded and was recognized Duke of Saxony by King Conrad I.
2 CONT
2 CONT References: [AR7],[Weis1]
