1 NOTE _P_CCINFO 2-2438
1 NOTE BIOGRAPHY
2 CONT Daughter of Count Billung and his wife Aeda, Oda was born about 805 or 806. She married Liudolf, a count in Saxony, about the year 836 and they had eleven or twelve children. Oda died on 17 May 913, aged 107, and was buried in the
2 CONC  Abbey of Gandersheim, which had been founded by her husband in 852.
2 CONT
2 CONT In the tenth century, more than half a century after Oda's death, Oda's descendant Gerberga, who was Abbess of Gandersheim, recorded some family details. Hrotsvita, a nun at Gandersheim, wrote a poem _Carmen de primordiis coenobii
2 CONC  Gandersheimensis_ that stated that Oda died aged 107 in 913. Hrotsvita also named Oda's parents as the ruler (or prince) Billung and Aeda ('fila Bilungi cuiusdam principis almi atque bonae famae generosae scilicet Aeda').
1 NOTE Ancestral File Number:<AFN> FLH2-GW
2 CONT
2 CONT Oda was the daughter of a Frankish prince named Billung and his wifeAeda. Oda died on 17 May 913, supposedly at the age of 107.
1 NOTE [De La Pole.FTW]
2 CONT
2 CONT Sources: RC 92, 301; AF; Ancestral Roots.   Dates from AF, which had note that she was 107 when she died.
