2 CONT The Annales Bertiniani record the marriage in 842 of "Ermendrud neptem Adalardi comitis" and "Karolus" at "Carisiacum palatium"[242].  Nithard names "Hirmentrude, daughter of Odo and Ingiltrud" as wife of Charles[243].  She was cr
2 CONC owned in Aug 866 at Saint-Médard de Soissons.  After she was separated from her husband, she retired to a monastery.  The Annales Bertiniani record the death "869 II Non Oct in monasterio Sancti Dyonisii" of "Hyrmentrudem uxorem s
2 CONC uam [=Karoli]" and her burial at Saint-Denis[244].  The Obituaire de Notre-Dame de Paris records the death "Non Oct" of "Irmentrudis regina uxor Caroli"[245].  The necrology of the abbey of Saint-Denis records the death "Non Oct" 
2 CONC of "Hirmentrudis regina"[246]. 
