2 CONT Ermentrude of Orléans (also Hirmentrude or Irmintrud) (September 27, 823 – October 6, 869) was Queen of Franks by her marriage to Charles the Bald, Holy Roman Emperor and King of West Francia. 
2 CONT
2 CONT She was the daughter of Odo, Count of Orleans and his wife, Engeltrude.
2 CONT
2 CONT She and Charles married in 842. 
2 CONT
2 CONT Their children were:
2 CONT * Judith (844–870), married firstly with Ethelwulf of Wessex, secondly with Ethelbald of Wessex (her stepson) and thirdly with Baldwin I of Flanders
2 CONT * Louis the Stammerer (846–879)
2 CONT * Charles the Child (847–866)
2 CONT * Lothar (848–865), monk in 861, became Abbot of Saint-Germain
2 CONT * Carloman (849–876)
2 CONT * Rotrud (852–912), a nun, Abbess of Saint-Radegunde
2 CONT * Ermentrud (854–877), a nun, Abbess of Hasnon. 
2 CONT * Hildegard (born 856, died young)
2 CONT * Gisela (857–874)
2 CONT
2 CONT Ermentrude had a gift for embroidery and an interest in religious foundations. Her husband gave her the Abbey of Chelles. She separated from her husband after he executed her rebellious brother William in 866, and retreated to the
2 CONC  life of a nunnery. Ermentrude was buried in the Basilique Saint-Denis, Paris, France.
2 CONT --------------------
2 CONT Ermentrude d'Orléans (ou Hermentrude), (825-869), fille de Eudes d'Orléans (ou Vodon d'Orléans) et d'Engeltrude de Fézensac, descendante de Charles Martel[réf. nécessaire], elle épousa Charles II le Chauve en 846 à Quierzy-sur-Ois
2 CONC e, et fut couronnée à Saint-Médard de Soissons. Son mariage ne fut pas heureux car le roi vouait une passion à sa concubine Richilde d'Ardennes, sœur de Boson de Provence, duc de la Bourgogne-Cisjurane.
2 CONT
2 CONT Ermentrude, séparée de Charles en 867, mais non répudiée, se retire à l'abbaye de Hasnon, près de Valenciennes, où elle meurt le 6 octobre 869 à l'âge de 44 ans. Après sa mort, le roi Charles le Chauve épousera sa concubine Richil
2 CONC de d'Ardennes, en 870.
2 CONT
2 CONT --------------------
2 CONT
2 CONT http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Ermentrude_of_Orl%C3%A9ans
2 CONT
