2 CONT Ermentrude of Orléans (27 September 823 – 6 October 869) was Queen of Franks by her marriage to Charles the Bald, Holy Roman Emperor and King of West Francia. She was the daughter of Odo, Count of Orleans and his wife, Engeltrude.
2 CONT
2 CONT She and Charles married in 842. Their children were:
2 CONT
2 CONT     * Judith of Flanders, consort of Æthelwulf of Wessex, Æthelbald of Wessex, and Baldwin I, Count of Flanders
2 CONT     * Louis the Stammerer (846–879)
2 CONT     * Charles the Child (847–866)
2 CONT     * Lothar (848–865), monk in 861, became Abbot of Saint-Germain
2 CONT     * Carloman, son of Charles the Bald (849–876)
2 CONT     * Rotrud (852–912), a nun
2 CONT     * Ermentrud (854–877), a nun
2 CONT     * Hildegard (born 856, died ?)
2 CONT     * Gisela (857–874)
2 CONT
2 CONT Ermentrude had a gift for embroidery and an interest in religious foundations. Her husband gave her the Abbey of Chelles. She separated from her husband after he executed her rebellious brother William in 866, and retreated to the
2 CONC  life of a nunnery. Ermentrude was buried in the Basilique Saint-Denis, Paris, France.
2 CONT --------------------
