2 CONT Ermentrude of Orléans (also Hirmentrude or Irmintrud) (September 27, 823 – October 6, 869) was Queen of Franks by her marriage to Charles the Bald, Holy Roman Emperor and King of West Francia. She was the daughter of Odo, Count of
2 CONC  Orleans and his wife, Engeltrude. She and Charles married in 842. Their children were: Judith (844–870), married firstly with Ethelwulf of Wessex, secondly with Ethelbald of Wessex (her stepson) and thirdly with Baldwin I of Flan
2 CONC ders Louis the Stammerer (846–879) Charles the Child (847–866) Lothar (848–865), monk in 861, became Abbot of Saint-Germain Carloman (849–876) Rotrud (852–912), a nun, Abbess of Saint-Radegunde Ermentrud (854–877), a nun, Abbess o
2 CONC f Hasnon Hildegard (born 856, died young) Gisela (857–874) Ermentrude had a gift for embroidery and an interest in religious foundations. Her husband gave her the Abbey of Chelles. She separated from her husband after he executed 
2 CONC her rebellious brother William in 866, and retreated to the life of a nunnery. Ermentrude was buried in the Basilique Saint-Denis, Paris, France.
2 CONT
