2 CONT >10.      [https://www.geni.com/people/Rothilde-of-the-Franks/6000000001744908320?through=6000000005588616059 ROTHILDIS] ([871]-22 Mar 929).  Charles III "le Simple" King of the West Franks confirmed donations of property "in comi
2 CONC tatu quoque Cœnomannico" made by "Hugo comes et mater sua Rothildis", at the request of "genitrix nostra Adeleidis et…comes Hugo consanguineus, necnon et…comes Ecfridus" by charter dated 1 Nov 900[277].  The charter dated 929 subs
2 CONC cribed by "Hugonis comitis filii Rotgerii comitis" suggests that Rothildis must have been the wife of Roger[278].  Flodoard names "Rothildis, amitæ suæ [regis Karoli], socrus autem Hugonis" when recording that the king deprived he
2 CONC r of "abbatiam…Golam" [Chelles] in favour of his favourite Haganon, the context dictating that "Hugonis" was "Hugo filius Rotberti"[279].  As the paternal aunt of King Charles III, chronology determines that she must have been the
2 CONC  daughter of her father's second marriage, although no source has so far been identified which states this to be the case.  She acquired the monasteries of Chelles, and Notre-Dame and Saint-Jean at Laon.  She retreated to Chelles 
2 CONC in 922 but was deprived of the monastery by her nephew Charles III "le Simple" King of the West Franks in favour of his favourite Haganon, an event which led to the rebellion of Robert Marquis en Neustrie who was the father of Rot
2 CONC hildis's son-in-law (Hugues, later "le Grand" Duc des Francs)[280].  Her death is dated to late 928/early 929 as Flodoard names "Rothildis…nuper defunctæ" when recording that "Heribertus et Hugo comites" (specifying that "Hugo" wa
2 CONC s "gener ipsius Rothildis") attacked "Bosonem Rodulfi regis frater" in 929 over the property of Rothildis[281].  This is also the only source so far identified from which her marriage is deduced.  The necrology of the abbey of Sai
2 CONC nt-Germain-des-Prés records the death "XI Kal Apr" of "Rothildis abbatisse et monache filia regis magni Karoli"[282].  The necrology of the abbey of Saint-Denis records the death "XI Kal Mar" of "Rotildis abbatissa"[283].  These e
2 CONC ntries could refer alternatively to Rothildis, daughter of Emperor Charlemagne, but it is more likely that the former entry would have referred to her father as "imperator" if that was the case.  m ([890]) ROTGER [Roger] Comte, ne
2 CONC phew of [HUGUES Comte de Bourges], son of --- (-before I Nov 900).  Comte du Maine 897. 
2 CONT
2 CONT >11.      [https://www.geni.com/people/Drogo/6000000001299392110?through=6000000005588616059 DROGO] ([872/73]-[873/74], bur Abbaye de Saint-Amand, Flanders).  The Chronico Floriacensi records the birth and death of "de Caroli Caro
2 CONC lus…rex…Pippinus…simulque Drogo"[284].  Twin with Pépin.
2 CONT
2 CONT >12.      [https://www.geni.com/people/Pippin/6000000002187857781?through=6000000005588616059 PEPIN ]([872/73]-[873/74], bur Abbaye de Saint-Amand, Flanders).  The Chronico Floriacensi records the birth and death of "de Caroli Car
2 CONC olus…rex…Pippinus…simulque Drogo"[285].  Twin with Drogo. 
2 CONT
2 CONT >13.      [https://www.geni.com/people/NN/6000000000234722752?through=6000000005588616059 son] (23 Mar 875-soon after).  The Annales Bertiniani record that in 875 "Richildis uxor eius [=Karoli]" gave birth to a child "noctu ante q
2 CONC uartam feriam paschæ" which died immediately after being baptised[286]. 
2 CONT
2 CONT >14.      [https://www.geni.com/people/Charles/6000000002908958963?through=6000000005588616059 CHARLES] (10 Oct 876-877 before 7 Apr, bur église de l'abbaye royale de Saint-Denis).  The Annales Bertiniani record the death in early
2 CONC  877 of "filius eius [=Karoli]…Karolus" and his burial at Saint-Denis[287]. 
2 CONT
