2 CONT >>'''[https://www.geni.com/people/Charles-II-the-Bald-Western-Emperor/6000000005588616059?through=6000000000904661585 CHARLES II]''' (Frankfurt-am-Main 13 Jun 823-Avrieux or Brides-les-Bains, Savoie 6 Oct 877, bur Nantua Abbey, tr
2 CONC ansferred to église de l'abbaye royale de Saint-Denis).  The Annales S. Benigni Divisionensis record the birth of "Karolus filius Ludowici" in Frankfurt "Idus Iun 824".  Thegan's Vita Hludowici Imperatoris names Charles as son of 
2 CONC his father by his second wife. Under the division of Imperial territories by the Treaty of Verdun 11 Aug 843, he became CHARLES II “le Chauve” King of the West Franks. http://fmg.ac/Projects/MedLands/CAROLINGIANS.htm#LouisIEmperor
2 CONC Bhttp://fmg.ac/Projects/MedLands/CAROLINGIANS.htm#LouisIEmperorB
