2 CONT Marriages and children
2 CONT
2 CONT Charles married Ermentrude, daughter of Odo I, Count of Orléans, in 842. She died in 869. In 870, Charles married Richilde of Provence, who was descended from a noble family of Lorraine.
2 CONT
2 CONT With Ermentrude:
2 CONT *1. Judith (844–870), married firstly with Ethelwulf of Wessex, secondly with Ethelbald of Wessex (her stepson) and thirdly with Baldwin I of Flanders
2 CONT *2. Louis the Stammerer (846–879)
2 CONT *3. Charles the Child (847–866)
2 CONT *4. Lothar (848–865), monk in 861, became Abbot of Saint-Germain
2 CONT *5. Carloman (849–876)
2 CONT *6. Rotrud (852–912), a nun, Abbess of Saint-Radegunde
2 CONT *7. Ermentrud (854–877), a nun, Abbess of Hasnon
2 CONT *8. Hildegard (born 856, died young)
2 CONT *9. Gisela (857–874)
2 CONT
2 CONT With Richilde:
2 CONT *1. Rothild (871–929), married firstly with Hugues, Count of Bourges and secondly with Roger, Count of Maine
2 CONT *2. Drogo (872–873)
2 CONT *3. Pippin (873–874)
2 CONT *4. a son (born and died 875)
2 CONT *5. Charles (876–877)
2 CONT
