2 CONT
2 CONT Charles II "the Bald" King of France was born on 13 June 828 in Frankford-on-Main, Germany. Sewell gives his birth date as 13 June 823.[4],[2],[3] He was the son of Louis I "the Fair" Emperor of the West and Judith of Bavaria.[1],
2 CONC [2],[3],[4] 
2 CONT
2 CONT Charles II "the Bald" King of France was crowned King of West Franks in 840.[4] 
2 CONT
2 CONT On 14 December 842 Charles married Ermentrude of Orléans, daughter of Eudes unknown Count of Orléans and Engeltrude.[4],[2],[3],[5] 
2 CONT
2 CONT By the Treaty of Verdun in 843, the Carolingian Empire was divided into three kingdoms, with Charles the Bald receiving the West Frankish Kingdom, Lothar receiving the Kingdom of Lothar, and Louis the German receiving the East Fra
2 CONC nkish Kingdom.[3] 
2 CONT
2 CONT Charles II "the Bald" King of France was crowned King of Burgundy in 869.[2] 
2 CONT
2 CONT On 25 November 870 Charles married Richardis of Metz, daughter of Budwine Count of Italy and Metz and Richilde of Arles.[2],[3] 
2 CONT
2 CONT Charles II "the Bald" King of France was crowned King of Italy in 875.[2] 
2 CONT
2 CONT He was crowned Emperor of the West in 25 December 875.[4],[2] 
2 CONT
2 CONT He died on Wednesday, 6 October 877 in Brides-les-Bains, Near Mt. Cenis in the Alps, at age 49 years, 3 months and 23 days.[4],[2],[3] He was buried in St. Denis, France.[2] 
2 CONT
