1 OCCU Vicomte de Blois ( 906), Vicomte de Tours ( 908), Comte de Blois & Tours (~940), Comte de Chartres, Vicomte de Tours, perhaps Count of Bourges, comte d Blois, Vicount of Troyes
1 NOTE {geni:about_me} http://fr.wikipedia.org/wiki/Thibaud_l%27Ancien
2 CONT
2 CONT http://fmg.ac/Projects/MedLands/CENTRAL%20FRANCE.htm#ThibautIdied975
2 CONT
2 CONT Thibaud dit l'Ancien (né en 890 - mort en 943), vicomte de Blois en 906, vicomte de Tours en 908, puis comte de Tours et comte de Blois vers 940.
2 CONT
2 CONT Il serait de haute extraction franco-bourguignonne et arrivé sur les bords de la Loire inférieure au début du Xe siècle. Il est le fondateur de la dynastie des Thibaldiens.
2 CONT
2 CONT Il épousa Richilde de Bourges, connue aussi sous le nom de Richilde du Maine (v.890-† ap.942), fille de Hugues (v.862-892), comte de Bourges et de Rothilde (v.871-v.928), fille de Charles le Chauve et de Richilde d'Ardennes. Veuve
2 CONC  d'Hugues de Bourges, Rothilde épousa en secondes noces Roger, comte du Maine.
2 CONT
2 CONT Richilde de Bourges eut pour sœur Rohaut, la première épouse d'Hugues le Grand.
2 CONT
2 CONT Avec Richilde, Thibaud eut trois enfants :
2 CONT
2 CONT     * Thibaud le Tricheur qui lui succéda dans ses « honneurs »
2 CONT
2 CONT     * Richard (†969), archevêque de Bourges
2 CONT
2 CONT     * une fille peut-être prénommée Adélaïde, mariée en premières noces au duc Alain Barbetote de Bretagne, en secondes noces au comte Foulque II le Bon d'Anjou, mort en 958.
2 CONT
2 CONT Bibliographie 
2 CONT
2 CONT     * Pierre Riché, Les Carolingiens, une famille qui fit l'Europe, Hachette, coll. « Pluriel », Paris, 1983 (réimpr. 1997), 490 p. (ISBN 2-01-278851-3) 
2 CONT
2 CONT     * Jean-Charles Volkmann, Bien Connaître les généalogies des rois de France (ISBN 2-87747-208-6 )
2 CONT
2 CONT     * Michel Mourre, Le petit Mourre. Dictionnaire d'Histoire universelle (ISBN 978-2-04-732194-2)
2 CONT
2 CONT     * Jean Gouget - Thierry Le Hête, Les comtes de Blois et de Champagne et leur descendance agnatique
2 CONT
2 CONT -----------------------------------
2 CONT
2 CONT THIBAUT [Tetbald] [I] "l'Ancien", son of --- (-[944], bur Tours Saint-Martin).  The Chronicle of Alberic de Trois-Fontaines records that "Hastingo" sold "civitate Carnoto" to "Turonensi comiti Theobaldo" in 904[13].  Guillaume de 
2 CONC Jumièges describes how "le comte Thibaut" bought the town of Chartres from Hasting the Viking[14].  Vicomte de Tours.  "Domni Fulconis Andecavorum comitis, Tedbaldi Turonorum vicecomitis" subscribed the charter dated 30 Oct 909 un
2 CONC der which the testamentary executors of "domni Gauzuini" donated property to Saint-Martin de Tours[15].  "…Tetbaldi vicecomitis…" subscribed the charter of "Hugo rector abbatiæ sancti Martini" relating to Tours Saint-Martin dated 
2 CONC 931[16].  The identity of the husband of Richilde, and father of Thibaut [II] and Richard, is brought together by the charter dated to [944] under which "le comte Thibault père de Thibault" relinquished rights relating to "les ter
2 CONC res de Vancé, de Joué, de Martigny et de Berthenay" to Tours Saint-Martin and paid for his future burial in the abbey[17].  m firstly ---.  The primary source which confirms this first marriage has not yet been identified.  It is 
2 CONC likely that the only indication is provided by the charter, dated to [980], under which “Ledgardis comitissa necnon Hugo episcopus et filius meus et item filius meus Odo comes” donated property to Saint-Martin de Tours, for the so
2 CONC uls of “Theobaldi comitis quondam senioris mei…Richildis quondam sanctimonialis, eiusque filii Richardi episcopi” (referring to “dicti comitis et fratris sui Theobaldi”, in relation to Bishop Richard)[18].  This charter confirms t
2 CONC hat Richildis was the mother of Richard and that Richard was the brother of Thibaut [II].  However, the absence of a phrase in the text such as “matris sui” linking “Richildis” to “Theobaldi comitis” suggests that she was not the 
2 CONC mother of Richard´s brother Thibaut, and that therefore the brothers were born from different marriages of the same father.  m secondly RICHILDIS, daughter of ---.  Richildis is named as second wife of Thibaut in Europäische Stamm
2 CONC tafeln[19] but the primary source on which this is based has not yet been identified.  The charter, dated to [980], under which “Ledgardis comitissa necnon Hugo episcopus et filius meus et item filius meus Odo comes” donated prope
2 CONC rty to Saint-Martin de Tours, for the souls of “Theobaldi comitis quondam senioris mei…Richildis quondam sanctimonialis, eiusque filii Richardi episcopi” (referring to “dicti comitis et fratris sui Theobaldi”, in relation to Bisho
2 CONC p Richard)[20] confirms that Richildis was the mother of Richard and that Richard was the brother of Thibaut.  However, it provides no indication of the name of their father and therefore of Richildis´s husband.  Comte Thibaut & h
2 CONC is first wife had [one possible child]:
2 CONT
2 CONT a)         THIBAUT [II] ([910]-16 Jan [975/77]).  "Le comte Thibault père de Thibault" relinquished rights relating to "les terres de Vancé, de Joué, de Martigny et de Berthenay" to Tours Saint-Martin and paid for his future buria
2 CONC l in the abbey by charter dated to [944][21].  He succeeded [his father] in [944] as THIBAUT I "le Tricheur" Comte de Blois, Vicomte de Tours. 
2 CONT
2 CONT -        see below. 
2 CONT
2 CONT Comte Thibaut & his second wife had two children:
2 CONT
2 CONT b)         RICHARD (-969).  “Ledgardis comitissa necnon Hugo episcopus et filius meus et item filius meus Odo comes” donated property to Saint-Martin de Tours, for the souls of “Theobaldi comitis quondam senioris mei…Richildis quo
2 CONC ndam sanctimonialis, eiusque filii Richardi episcopi” (referring to “dicti comitis et fratris sui Theobaldi”, in relation to Bishop Richard), by charter dated to [980][22].  This confirms that Richildis was the mother of Richard a
2 CONC nd that Richard was the brother of Thibaut.  However, the absence of a phrase in the text such as “matris sui” linking “Richildis” to “Theobaldi comitis” suggests that she was not the mother of Richard´s brother Thibaut, and that 
2 CONC therefore the brothers were born from different marriages of the same father.  Archbishop of Bourges 956/57. 
