0 @N6000000008799853382@ NOTE [Jeremiah Brown.FTW]
1 CONT
1 CONT [from Ancestry.com 139798.GED]
1 CONT Robert de Bellomont, or Beaumont, came into England with William the Conqueror and contributed mainly to the Norman triumph at Hastings. This Robert inherited the Earldom of Mellent in Normandy from his mother, Adelina, daughter o
1 CONC f Waleran and sister of Hugh (who took the habit of a monk in the abbey of Bec), both Earls of Mellent. For his gallant services at Hastings he obtained sixty-four lordships in Warwickshire, sixteen in Leicester, seven in Wiltshir
1 CONC e, three in Northamptonshire, and one in Gloucestershire, in all ninety-one. He did not however arrive at the dignity of the English peerage before the reign of King Henry I, when that monarch created him Earl of Leicester. The mo
1 CONC de by which he attained this honor is thus stated by an ancient writer: "The city of Leicester had then four lords, viz., the King, the Bishop of Lincoln, Earl Simon, and Yvo, the son of Hugh de Grentmesnil. This Earl of Mellent, 
1 CONC by favor of the King, cunningly entered it on that side which belongs to Yvo (the governour thereof, as also Sheriff, and the King's farmer there), subjecting it wholly to himself, and by this means, being made an Earl in England,
1 CONC  exceeded all nobles of the realm in riches and power".
