0 @N6000000004270563079@ NOTE http://masseyfamgenealogy.tripod.com/a31.htm#i2327
1 CONT
1 CONT 1073741828. Roger De Beaumont Earl Of Meulan [Count Of Beaumont] , son of Humphrey De Harcourt De Vielles Sn De Beaumont and Aubrey De La Haie, was born in 1010-1022 of Pontaudemer, Normandy, France died on 29 Nov 1094 in Abbey DE
1 CONC  Pre'aux, Pontaudemer, Normandy, at age 84, and was buried in Abbey, Preaux, Normandy, France.
1 CONT
1 CONT     General Notes: ROGER DE BEAUMONT, SIRE DE PONTEAUDEMER (Humphrey de Veulles ..., Touroude ..., Torf), born about 1010, succeeded to the family estates in Normandy, as Sire du Ponteaudemer, Seigneur de Veulles, Pre'aux, Torvill
1 CONC e, and du Ponteaitorf, and Seigneur de Beaumont (or Bellomont), by which last name he came to be generally described. By his marriage he greatly increased the possessions and prestige of the family, and he rose to be one of the mo
1 CONC st powerful feudal noblemen of his age in Normandy. When William the Conqueror invaded England in 1066, Roger de Beaumont furnished sixty armed vessels for the fleet and was left in charge of the government of Normandy when the Co
1 CONC nqueror started on the expedition. He munificently endowed the Abbey of Pre'aux, of which late in life he became a monk; and dying in 1094 at advanced age, he was buried in this monastery at Ponteaudemer, Normandy. (P) He married 
1 CONC about 1040, ADELINE DE MEULLANT, daughter and eventually sole heiress of Waleran, Comte de Meullant, a great feudal nobleman of France. She died in 1081. (P) Children .... [see under their names]."
1 CONT     --- J Gardner Bartlett, *Newberry Genealogy*, Boston, 1914, p 4-5
1 CONT
1 CONT     Roger de BEAUMONT was born about 1010 in "of" Pont Audemer, N, France. IGI has abt 1022. So does Roderick W Stuart, *Royalty for Commoners*, 2nd edn, 1992, p 161 (lin 220) He died in 1094. OR: Roger de BELLOMONT
1 CONT     "The same thing is true of Beaumont [i.e., the name "may well be Norman or at
1 CONT     least French in origin".] There was a Roger de Beaumont recorded in the Domesday Book as holding Sturminster Marshal in Dorset, and this Roger certainly took his name from Beaumont in Normandy. From Roger descended the Counts 
1 CONC of Meulan, the old Earls of Leicester, and the old Earls of
1 CONT     Warwick."
1 CONT     --- Leslie Gilbert Pine, *They Came with the Conqueror, A study of the modern
1 CONT     descendants of the Normans", London (Evans Brothers Ltd) 1954, p 106-107
1 CONT     Alt Name: Robert De Beaumont Sn De Beaumont
1 CONT     Alt Birth: 1005-1011
1 CONT     Alt Name: Roger De Beaumont [Count Of Beaumont]
1 CONT     Seigneur of Beaumont, Pontaudemer, Brionne and Vatteville, Normandy. He built a castle at Beaumont-le-Roger, above Vieilles.
1 CONT
1 CONT     Apparently he was faithful to William the Conqueror during disturbances early in his reign, and was said to have defeated and slain Roger de Tosny. He was credited with having furnished 60 ships for the invason of England, but
1 CONC  in 1066 he remained in Normandy as advisor to the Duchess Maud.
1 CONT     Until 1082 he witnessed many charters of William the Conueror. In 1086 he was recorded as holding land in dorset and Gloucestershire, which later devolved to his grandson, Waleran, Count of Meulan. About 1088, he founded the c
1 CONC ollegiate church of the Holy Trinity at Beaumont-le-Roger for the canons of St. Frideswide of Oxford, and he was a benefactor of St. Pierre-de-Preaux and St. Wandrille. Shortly after 1090 he became a monk at the Abbey of Preaux.
1 CONT
1 CONT         Noted events in his life were:
1 CONT
1 CONT         1. Fact 1: No Issue.
1 CONT
1 CONT         2. Fact 1: Comte DE Beaumont. Sn DE Ponteaudemer.
1 CONT
1 CONT         3. Fact 2: Succeeded To The Family Estates In Normandy.
1 CONT
1 CONT         4. Fact 3: Sn DE Veulles, Pre'aux, Torville, & Du Ponteaitorf.
1 CONT
1 CONT         5. Fact 4: Rose To Be One Of The Most Powerful Feudal Noblemen Of His Age In Normandy.
1 CONT
1 CONT         6. Fact 5: Furnished 60 Armed Vessels For The Fleet Of The Conqueror.
1 CONT
1 CONT         7. Fact 6: Regent Of Normandy When The Conqueror Invaded England.
1 CONT
1 CONT         8. Fact 7: Munificently Endowed The Abbey Of Pre'aux, He Became A Monk There Late In Life.
1 CONT
1 CONT         9. Fact 8: Recorded In The Domesday Book As Holding Sturminster Marshal In Dorset.
1 CONT
1 CONT         10. Fact 9: Norman Companion With William The Conqueror.
1 CONT
1 CONT         11. Fact 10: Took His Name From Beaumont In Normandy.
1 CONT
1 CONT         12. Origin of Name of Beaumont: Beaumont Is A Place Name In Normandy, Near Eure.
1 CONT
1 CONT         13. Fact 11: Buried At Preaux, France.
1 CONT
1 CONT         14. Fact 12: Seigneur DE St. Lenfroy, DE Montfort, DE Brone, DE Sahus, & DE La Crax.
1 CONT
1 CONT         15. Fact 2: Sn DE Pont-Audemer, Vielles, Beaumont & Beaumontel.
1 CONT
1 CONT         16. Fact 3: Sn DE Pre'aux, Torville, Ponteautorf. 
1 CONT
1 CONT     Roger married Adeline De Meulan Cts De Meulan [Countess Of Meulan] in 1040 in Ponteaudemer, Normandy. 
1 CONT
1 CONT     Marriage Notes: By his marriage he greatly increased the possessions and prestige of the Beaumont family, and he rose to be one of the most powerful feudal noblemen of his age in Normandy.
1 CONT
1 CONT         Children from this marriage were:
1 CONT
1 CONT         536870914       i.  Sir Robert De Beaumont 1st Earl Leicester (born in 1060 Of, Pont Audemer, Brittany, France - died on 5 Jun 1118 in Leicestershire, England)
1 CONT                        ii.  Henry De Beaumont I Earl Of Warwick [Earl Of Warwick (born in 1065 Meulan, Normandy, France - died on 20 Jun 1119 in Ponteaudemer, Normandy, France)
1 CONT                       iii.  William De Beaumont (born about 1047 Of, Neubourg, Manche, France)
1 CONT                        iv.  Aubreye De Beaumont [Abbess] (born in 1049 Of Neubourg, Normandy - died in 1112)
