0 @N6000000003403249602@ NOTE [alfred_descendants10gen_fromrootsweb_bartont.FTW]
1 CONT
1 CONT "Lord of Lewes, Reigate and Caonningsburg, Lord of Bellencombre and Mortemer in Normandy; born before 1071; succeeded as second Earl of Surrey, June 24, 1089; patron of Lewes Priory; Knight before January, 1091; deprived of the ea
1 CONC rldom about October, 1101; restored 1102; Commander of third division of the King's army (Tinchebraye) September 26, 1106; second founder of Castleacre Priory; Commander in Kings's army (Bemule) August 20, 1119; Governor of Rouen 
1 CONC and the district of Caux, December, 1135; wittness to King Stepnen's second Charter of Liberties 1136. (YFT. pp. 91-92).
1 CONT William De Warenne, d. 11 May 1138, second Earl of Surrey, son of William de Warenne and Gundred. (CP IV 670 chart III, VII 520, 523-526, 737, X 351). Weis 50-24 2h.  Father of Gundred de Warenne, (and others) Countess of Warwick,
1 CONC  wid. of Roger de Newburg; m. (2) William de Lancaster I. (Weis 88-25).
