0 @N6000000001783594501@ NOTE He md Aubreye de la Haye abt 1000. She was b abt 984, d 1045.
1 CONT
1 CONT Seigneur of Vieilles and Pont-Audemer in Normandy, he was one of the followers of Robert I, Duke of Normandy, and appears as a witness in ducal charters among the great lords of Normandy. He founded two monasteries at Preux, namel
1 CONC y St. Pierre, for monks, before 1035, and St. Leger, for nuns, about 1040. He is said to have become a monk at St. Pierre-de Preux, where he was buried. He left three sons, Roger "de Bello Monte", Robert (to whom was given lands i
1 CONC n the Contentin, by Duke William), and William, as well as a daughter, Dunelme.
