0 @N6000000009304884784@ NOTE #Générale#inhumation : Saint-Denis 93
1 CONT
1 CONT #Générale#Sacré à Reims le 14 Mai 1027.
1 CONT Profession : Roi de France de 1031 à 1060.
1 CONT
1 CONT 14/5 51000.Reims
1 CONT Selon d'autres sources, marié le 29 Janvier 1044 ou en 1049.
1 CONT
1 CONT inhumation : Abbaye de Saint-Denis
1 CONT
1 CONT Roi de France (juillet 1031-août 1060).
1 CONT
1 CONT Il dut céder à son frère Robert le duché de Bourgogne (1032), lutter contre lamaison de Blois-Champagne, puis contre Guillaume le Conquérant, qui le vainquit.
1 CONT Il épousa  en secondes noces Anne, fille de Iaroslav, grand-duc de Kiev.
1 CONT
1 CONT Source : Le Petit Larousse (1993), page 1392.
1 CONT
1 CONT #Générale#Il est couronné roi de France en 1027.
0 @N6000000008799888113@ NOTE [Jeremiah Brown.FTW]
1 CONT
1 CONT [from Ancestry.com 139798.GED]
1 CONT King of France 1031-1060. He was the Duke of Burgundy 1015-1031. He is the least-known of all the Capetian Kings; no one wrote about him in his lifetime, and the destruction of the archives shortly after his time has left a huge b
1 CONC lank over this period. All that is known is that his mother, Constance, contested his right to the throne, which she wanted to go to Robert. This resulted in a war between the two brothers, of which little is known. Henry won it b
1 CONC y buying the support of his vassals, which cost him French Vexin and the total renunciation of the duchy of Burgundy in favor of his brother in 1034.
1 CONT Without the benefit of the coronation it is likely that Henry, who appears to have been a mediocre man, would have been brushed aside. But the anointing brought him respect and won time for concessions. Managing to remain in power
1 CONC  is after all a sign of stability, and despite the obscurity of his reign it saw a strengthening of the dynasty. He was crowned co-king with his father in 1026.
1 CONT The most interesting aspect of Henry's life was his attempt to bring about a Franco-Russian alliance by marriage to Anne of Kiev, daughter of Yaroslav and granddaughter of Vladimir I.
