0 @N6000000003949642284@ NOTE Gundred (daughter of Gherbod the Fleming), d. 27 May 1085; m. bef. 1077, William de Warenne, d. Lewes 24 June 1088, created 1st Earl of Surrey, son of Rudolf de Warenne and Beatrice. [Magna Charta Sureties]     He married, 1stly, 
1 CONC Gundred, sister of Gerbod the Fleming, EARL OF CHESTER, possibly daughter of Gerbod, hereditary advocate of the Abbey of St. Bertin at St. Omer. She died in child-birth, 27 May 1085, at Castle Acre, Norfolk, and was buried the cha
1 CONC pter-house at Lewes. [Complete Peerage XII/1:493-5, XIV:604 (transcribed by Dave Utzinger)]
1 CONT Note: I think that Gundred was daughter of Gerbod the Fleming, Earl of Chester. He was also advocate of the Abbey of St. Bertin of St. Omer (as CP itself indicated-see notes under Gherbod) . As far as I know there is only one Gerb
1 CONC od. MCS, which has later information than CP, certainly (at least the way I read it) seems to indicate so.  (per Jim Weber)
1 CONT Gundred, wife of William de Warrenne, may have been daughter of Gherbod
1 CONT the Fleming but she was definitely not a child of Maud of Flanders.  A forged charter known to William Dugdale in the 17th century was long believed to indicate that Gundred was actually a daughter of William the Conqueror and Mat
1 CONC ilda/Maud of Flanders.  Once that myth was exploded, however, and it was realized that Gundred might well have been Gherbod's child, another legend got in the way--that Matilda had been married to Gherbod before she married Willia
1 CONC m and that Gundred was the child of this early marriage.  Of course, none of this is true.  I believe the sources of the early disinformation are sorted out in CP under "Surrey," and if memory serves me aright at this hour of the 
1 CONC morning, David Douglas' *William the Conqueror* says something brief about the legends.
0 @N6000000007329696428@ NOTE Leutner, soc.med, Sept '95] Leaving aside the question of whether   the
1 CONT line  back from R. Warren is right (many appear to think it isn't), there
1 CONT is a major  earlier flaw with 'Princess Gundred,' who was not dau. of
1 CONT William   the CQ &  Matilda but of unknown parentage.  She was sister of
1 CONT Gerbod the   Fleming, Earl  of Chester.  If I recall, she was at some
1 CONT point  ward of William or   in some  sense 'stepdaughter.'
1 CONT [David Collyer <dcollyer@giant.bnc.au> 6-11-96] Now I know there has
1 CONT been a  lot of discussion on Gen-Medieval at different times regarding
1 CONT Gundred, wife  of William De WARENNE. While all seem to agree that she is
1 CONT NOT the   daughter of  William I (The Conqueror), I see that you have her
1 CONT as the daughter of   his son  William II (Rufus). My book, 'Britain's
1 CONT Royal Families' by Alison   WEIR, 1996,  says that William II did not
1 CONT marry, but had one illegitimate child   'Berstrand'  (? male/female). No
1 CONT mention of Gundred. When I turned to Gundred,   (Gundrada)  WEIR simply
1 CONT notes that there is no evidence that she was the daughter   of  either
1 CONT William I or Matilda of Flanders. I have her (from the Royal   Pedigrees,
1 CONT Uni. of Hull) as being the daughter of Gerbod St.OMER, Advocate of   St.
1 CONT Bertin.  Gundred d. 27 May 1085 at Castle Acre, Norfolk; bried, Chapter
1 CONT House,   Lewes,  Sussex.
