0 @N6000000001783359944@ NOTE One of the three known sisters of Gunnora, Duchess of Normandy, who was the wife of Richard I of Normandy, and grandmother of William the Conqueror.
0 @N6000000002248121896@ NOTE Notes
1 CONT Weis' "Ancestral Roots. . ." (184:1) calls her Duvelina, the sister of the 
1 CONT DUCHESS GUNNORA 
1 CONT In a posting to the soc.genealogy.medieval newsgroups on the Internet on 
1 CONT Tue, 10 Sep 1996, Todd A. Farmerie explained: 
1 CONT "Robert de Torigny, the only source we have for the existance of Osbern 
1 CONT de Bolbec, says that he married a sister of Gunnora, named Wevia. Some 
1 CONT copies appear to have dropped a couple of phrases, making it appear that 
1 CONT a different sister, Duvelina was mother, but this appears to be incorrect. 
1 CONT Well, . . . Gunnora (and hence Wevia) were sisters of yet another, (whose 
1 CONT name I forget) who was wife of the forester. In addition, they had a 
1 CONT brother, Herfast/Arfast who was of similar rank. We do not know who 
1 CONT their father was. Who was Osbern de Bolbec's wife and who were her 
1 CONT parents? Wevia, and no one knows."
0 @N6000000002248190825@ NOTE One of the three known sisters of Gunnora, Duchess of Normandy, who was the wife of Richard I of Normandy, and grandmother of William the Conqueror. To see a notional chart of her familial connections.
