0 @N6000000003949540323@ NOTE     From: Todd A. Farmerie (taf2 AT po.cwru.edu)
1 CONT     Subject: Robert de Torigny and the family of Gunnor, Duchess of Normandy
1 CONT     Newsgroups: soc.genealogy.medieval
1 CONT     Date: 1996/12/03
1 CONT     Wevia, the only other sister of Gunnor named by Torigny, married Osbern de Bolbec (who is otherwise unknown to history). They had at least two sons: Walter Giffard, ancestor of the English Giffard/Gifford families, and also, t
1 CONC hrough his daughter, of the Clare family; and Godfrey, whose son William de Arques had two daughters and co-heiresses.
1 CONT     Note; I have Wevia's son as Gozeline (or Godfrey) and grandfather of William de Arques.
0 @N6000000003949643314@ NOTE From: Todd A. Farmerie (taf2@po.cwru.edu)
1 CONT Subject: Robert de Torigny and the family of Gunnor, Duchess of Normandy 
1 CONT Newsgroups: soc.genealogy.medieval Date: 1996/12/03
1 CONT Duvelina, a second sister of Gunnor, married Turulf de Pont Audemer, son of a Norman founder Torf, and uncle of the first of the Harcourts. They had at least one son, Humphrey de Vielles, who in turn was father of Roger de Beaumon
1 CONC t, another Conquest-era baron.
0 @N6000000003949876759@ NOTE Gunnor had at least three sisters, of which the oldest appears to have been Senfria (Seinfreda), who was wife of the (unnamed) forester from the area of St. Vaast d'Equiqueville, and it was her charms which are said first to have 
1 CONC attracted the attentions Duke Richard I. She appears to have had at least one daughter, Joscelina, wife of Hugh de Montgomery. (Torigny makes Joscelina daughter of another sister, Wevia, but a contemporary of Torigny, in demonstra
1 CONC ting the genealogical impediment to a marriage of a bastard of Henry I to a Montgomery descendant specifically calls Joscelina's mother Senfria, and the inheritance by the Montgomerys of large holdings suggests that Joscelina was 
1 CONC a significant coheir to her parents, which does not match Wevia's family where two sons would be expected to acquire most of the family land.) Hugh de Montgomery and Joscelina had a son Roger, but contrary to Torigny's statements,
1 CONC  he was not the Conquest baron of that name, but instead his father. By a wife possibly named Emma, Roger had: Hugh; Roger (who married Mabel of Belleme and played a significant role in pre-Conquest Normandy); William (who murdere
1 CONC d cousin Osbern); Robert, and Gilbert.
0 @N6000000003051208598@ NOTE [Weis 157] sister of the Duchess Gunnora.
0 @N6000000004533948759@ NOTE Avelina, sister of Gundra, wife of Richard I, Duke of Normandy.[Burke's Peerage]
1 CONT
1 CONT -------------------
1 CONT
1 CONT The following is excerpted (full post is in notes under father) from apost to SGM, 3 Dec 1996, by Todd Farmerie:
1 CONT
1 CONT From: Todd A. Farmerie (taf2@po.cwru.edu)
1 CONT Subject: Robert de Torigny and the family of Gunnor, Duchess ofNormandy
1 CONT Newsgroups: soc.genealogy.medieval
1 CONT Date: 1996/12/03
1 CONT
1 CONT Wevia, the only other sister of Gunnor named by Torigny, marriedOsbern de Bolbec (who is otherwise unknown to history).  They had atleast two sons:  Walter Giffard, ancestor of the EnglishGiffard/Gifford families, and also, throug
1 CONC h his daughter, of the Clarefamily; and Godfrey, whose son William de Arques had two daughters andco-heiresses.
1 CONT
1 CONT Note; I have Wevia's son as Gozeline (or Godfrey) and grandfather ofWilliam de Arques.
0 @N6000000000337410759@ NOTE Weis, p. 157 - sister of the Duchess Gunnora.
