1 CONT the empire of his grandfather, Svyntoslav. By 1036, he had succeeded in
1 CONT making himself ruler of all Russia, with the Kievian state reaching its
1 CONT greatest power. This grand Duke of Kiev revised the first Russian law code,
1 CONT the Russkaya Pravda (Russian truth). His death in 1054 signaled the decline
1 CONT of Kiev. See "Sons of Yaraslav".
