1 CONT      Constance d'Arles was born circa 973. She was the daughter of Guillaume III Taillefer, Comte de Provence and Adelaide d'Anjou.1 She married Robert II, Roi de France, son of Hugues de Paris, Roi de France and Adelaide de Poito
1 CONC u, in 1003. She was also reported to have been married circa 1000. She died on 25 July 1032. 
1 CONT      Constance d'Arles was also known as Constance de Taillefer.2
1 CONT
1 CONT Children of Constance d'Arles and Robert II, Roi de France
1 CONT Hugues III, Roi de France b. 1007, d. c 1025
1 CONT Henri I, Roi de France+ b. Apr 1008, d. 4 Aug 10602
1 CONT Adela de France, Princesse de France+ b. 1009, d. 8 Jan 1079
1 CONT Robert I de Bourgogne, Duc de Bourgogne+ b. c 1011, d. 21 Mar 1076
1 CONT Citations
1 CONT 1. [S16] Jirí Louda and Michael MacLagan, Lines of Succession: Heraldry of the Royal Families of Europe, 2nd edition (London, U.K.: Little, Brown and Company, 1999), table 64. Hereinafter cited as Lines of Succession.
1 CONT 2. [S45] Marcellus Donald R. von Redlich, Pedigrees of Some of the Emperor Charlemagne's Descendants, volume I (1941; reprint, Baltimore, Maryland, U.S.A.: Genealogical Publishing Company, 2002), page 63. Hereinafter cited as Pedi
1 CONC grees of Emperor Charlemagne, I.
