1 CONC ertain Count William, she was an intriguing and amb itious woman, who made life miserable for her husband by encouraging h er sons to revolt against their father. She was the mother of his chil dren.  When her son Henry ascended t
1 CONC o the throne in 1027, she favored her younger son Robert and quickly moved in alliance with Eudes (Odo) II de Blois, to remove Henry in favor of her son Robert who was ultima tely pacified by being give the duchy of Burgundy which
1 CONC  stayed in his family well into the 1300's.  During the infighting over the successi0 on, she often acted to provoke and unhold Henry's brothers against him .
