0 @N6000000002187845040@ NOTE Guy I of Montlhéry
1 CONT From Wikipedia, the free encyclopedia
1 CONT
1 CONT Guy I (died 1095) was the second lord of Montlhéry. He was probably the son of Thibaud of Montmorency, but some sources say that his father was named Milo. Thibaud could instead be his grandfather.
1 CONT
1 CONT He married Hodierna of Gometz, daughter of William, lord of Gometz. They had seven children:
1 CONT
1 CONT Milo I the Great, lord of Monthléry 
1 CONT Melisende of Montlhéry, married Hugh I, count of Rethel, mother of Baldwin II of Jerusalem (died 1118) 
1 CONT Elizabeth of Montlhéry, married Joscelin, lord of Courtenay, mother of Joscelin I, Count of Edessa 
1 CONT Guy I the Red (died 1108), lord of Rochefort 
1 CONT Beatrice of Rochefort, married Anseau of Garlande (1069-1117) 
1 CONT Hodierna of Montlhéry, married Walter of Saint-Valéry 
1 CONT Alice of Montlhéry (1040-1097), married Hugh I, lord of Le Puiset (1035-1094) 
1 CONT Guy died in 1095, the same year Pope Urban II launched the First Crusade. Many of his descendants had illustrious careers in the Holy Land, through the Montlhéry, Courtenay, and Le Puiset branches of his family.
