0 @N6000000000945053954@ NOTE Greve av Provence 1008 - 1018. 
1 CONT Mogens Bugge angir i ?Våre forfedre? Vilhelm II som identisk med hans sønn(?) Vilhelm
1 CONT IV, at han er født ca. 980 (som sønnen), og at han var greve fra 992 til 1018. Bent og Vidar
1 CONT Billing Hansen angir i ?Rosensverdslektens forfedre? at han er født ca. 950.
1 CONT Han fylte klostrene i Montmajour og i Saint-Victor med gaver. Disse var meget
1 CONT populærte i hans land.
0 @N6000000000337421522@ NOTE Weis, p. 118;  138:  King of Burgundy
0 @N6000000000437048860@ NOTE Name Prefix:<NPFX> King Name Suffix:<NSFX> I/Ii, Of Burgundy "Le Pacifique"
0 @N6000000003300376001@ NOTE Conrad was King of the Two Bourgognes.
0 @N6000000000945044487@ NOTE Konrad ?den Fredelige? var konge av Burgund 937 - 993. 
1 CONT Han var første gang gift med Adele av England som døde i 963.
0 @N6000000000945065496@ NOTE Vilhelm var greve av Toulouse fra ca. 961 under sin mors, Garsindes, formynderskap. 
1 CONT Han delte med sin tremenning, Raimund II, grevskapene Rouergue, Quercy og
1 CONT Albigeois. Han var også greve av Auvergne, men overdro dette grevskap til Gui, vicomte av
1 CONT Clermont. Han ble stamfar til grevene St. Gille.
1 CONT I 981 bemektiger han seg klosteret Beaulieu i Nedre Limousin. I 988 nekter han å
1 CONT anerkjenne Hugo Capet som konge.
1 CONT Det synes som om han først var gift med en kvinne hvis navn er ukjent og som han
1 CONT forstøtte. Han var så gift ca. 975 med Arsinde, datter eller søster til greve Fulco Nera av Anjou.
1 CONT Med Emma fikk han halvdelen av Provence.
1 CONT Vilhelm døde i 1037 etter september, og ble begravet i St. Sernin i Toulouse, hvor hans
1 CONT grav enda finnes.
0 @N6000000000945078039@ NOTE Greve av Provence 992 -  1008. 
1 CONT Rothbold ble greve eller marquis av Provence sammen med sin bror, Wilhelm I, idet
1 CONT begge etterfulgte deres far, Boso II.
1 CONT Han var gift med Ermengard.
1 CONT Sammen med sin bror undertegner han et dokument i mai 961. I 992 undertegner han
1 CONT et dokument som ikke er underskrevet av Ermengarde. I 1004 var han tilstede på et møte i
1 CONT klosteret Psalmodi, hvor han undertegner.
1 CONT Et dokument fra 1005 angående en gave til klosteret S. Victor er undertegnet av ham,
1 CONT hans sønner og av Ermengarde. Hun nevnes etter hans sønner, noe som tyder på at hun ikke
1 CONT var deres mor.
1 CONT Etter 1008 hører man ikke mer fra ham.
0 @N6000000001783532345@ NOTE Basic Life Information
1 CONT
1 CONT William I of Provence
1 CONT
1 CONT William I (c. 950 - 993, after 29 August), called the Liberator, was Count of Provence from 968 to his abdication. In 975 or 979, he took the title of marchio or margrave. He is often considered the founder of the county of Proven
1 CONC ce. He and his elder brother Rotbold II, sons of Boso II of Arles, both carried the title of comes or count concurrently, but it is unknown if they were joint-counts of the whole of Provence or if the region was divided. His broth
1 CONC er never bore any other title than count so long as William lived, so the latter seems to have attained a certain supremacy.
1 CONT
1 CONT In 980, he was installed as Count of Arles. His sobriquet comes from his victories against the Saracens by which he liberated Provence from their threat, which had been constant since the establishment of a base at Fraxinet. At th
1 CONC e Battle of Tourtour in 973, with the assistance of the counts of the High Alps and the viscounts of Marseille and Fos, he definitively routed the Saracens, chasing them forever from Provence. He reorganised the region east of the
1 CONC  Rhône, which he conquered from the Saracens and which had been given him as a gift from King Conrad of Burgundy. Also by royal consent, he and his descendants controlled the fisc in Provence. With Isarn, Bishop of Grenoble, he re
1 CONC populated Dauphiné and settled an Italian count named Ugo Blavia near Fréjus in 970 in order to bring that land back to cultivation. For all this, he figures prominently in Ralph Glaber's chronicle with the title of dux and he app
1 CONC ears in a charter of 992 as pater patriae.
1 CONT
1 CONT He donated land to Cluny and retired to become a monk, dying at Avignon, where he was buried in the church of Saint-Croix at Sarrians. He was succeeded as margrave by his brother. His great principality began to diminish soon afte
1 CONC r his death as the castles of his vassals, which he had kept carefully under ducal control, soon became allods of their possessors.
1 CONT
1 CONT Marriages and Children
1 CONT
1 CONT He married 1st Arsenda, daughter of Arnold of Comminges and their son was:
1 CONT William II of Provence
1 CONT
1 CONT He married 2nd (against papal advice) in 984, Adelaide of Anjou, daughter of Fulk II of Anjou and Gerberga of Maine, and their daughter was:
1 CONT Constance of Arles (973 - 1034), married Robert II of France
1 CONT
1 CONT <http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/William_I_of_Provence>
