0 @N6000000001783248854@ NOTE Basic Life Information
1 CONT
1 CONT Adelaide of Anjou
1 CONT
1 CONT Adelaide (c. 947-1026), called the White, was the daughter of Fulk II of Anjou and Gerberga of Maine. She was therefore the sister of Geoffrey Greymantle.
1 CONT
1 CONT Marriages and Children
1 CONT
1 CONT She was married five times to some of France's most important noblemen.
1 CONT
1 CONT Her first marriage, probably before 960, was to Stephen, Viscount of Gévaudan. Her second marriage was to Raymond III, Count of Toulouse and Prince of Gothia, in 975. He died in 978.
1 CONT
1 CONT In 982, she married Louis, the young son of Lothair of France, and the two were jointly crowned Monarchs of Aquitaine on the same day at Brioude. The large difference in age between the spouses was cause for a quick divorce in 984
1 CONC .
1 CONT
1 CONT She fled then to Arles, where she contracted, against papal advice, a marriage with William I of Provence in 984. She gave him a daughter, Constance of Arles, who later married Robert II of France.
1 CONT
1 CONT Her final marriage was to Otto-William, Duke of Burgundy.
1 CONT
1 CONT <http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Adelais_of_Anjou>
