0 @N6000000000604979896@ NOTE Adelaide de Poitou (F) b. circa 945, d. between 1004 and 1005, #105197d. bt 1004 - 1005|p10520.htm#i105197|William I de Poitou, Duc d\\'Acquitaine|b. c 915d. 3 Apr 963|p10662.htm#i106618|Adele de Normandie|b. c 917d. a 14 Oct 962|
1 CONC p10478.htm#i104772|||||||Robert . o. N. Ragnvaldsson, 1st Duc de Normandie|b. 846d. 932|p10477.htm#i104767|Poppa o. N. de Valois||p10477.htm#i104766|');"Pedigree <JavaScript:pup('Adelaide de Poitou|b. c 945<BR> Last Edited=6 Apr 2
1 CONC 002
1 CONT Adelaide de Poitou was the daughter of William I de Poitou, Duc d'Acquitaine <p10662.htm> and Adele de Normandie <p10478.htm>.1,2 She was born circa 945. She married Hugues de Paris, Roi de France <p10311.htm>, son of Hugues of Ne
1 CONC ustria, Comte de Paris <p10519.htm> and Edhilda (?), circa 969. She died between 1004 and 1005.2
1 CONT Child of Adelaide de Poitou and Hugues de Paris, Roi de France <p10311.htm>:
1 CONT Robert II, Roi de France <p10310.htm>+ b. 27 Mar 972, d. 20 Jul 1031
1 CONT Citations
1 CONT [S106 <s3.htm>] Royal Genealogies Website (ROYAL92.GED), online <ftp://ftp.cac.psu.edu/genealogy/public_html/royal/index.html>. Hereinafter cited as Royal Genealogies Website.
1 CONT [S11 <s1.htm>] Alison Weir, Britain's Royal Family: A Complete Genealogy (London, U.K.: The Bodley Head, 1999), page 13. Hereinafter cited as Britain's Royal Family.
0 @N6000000001783309193@ NOTE Basic Life Information
1 CONT
1 CONT Adele or Adelaide of Aquitaine (or Adelaide of Poitiers) (c. 945 or 952 - 1004) was the daughter of William III, Duke of Aquitaine and Adele of Normandy, daughter of Rollo, Duke of Normandy.
1 CONT
1 CONT Marriage and Children
1 CONT
1 CONT Her father used her as security for a truce with Hugh Capet, whom she married in 970. In 987, after the death of Louis V, the last Carolingian king of France, Hugh was elected the new king with Adelaide as queen. They were proclai
1 CONC med at Noyon and blessed at Reims. They were the founders of the Capetian dynasty of France.
1 CONT
1 CONT Their children were:
1 CONT Hedwig, Countess of Mons (or Hadevide, or Avoise) (c. 969-after 1013), wife of Reginar IV, Count of Mons
1 CONT Robert II (972-1031), the future king of France. Crowned co-king 987 in order to consolidate the new dynasty
1 CONT Gisèle, Countess of Ponthieu(c. 970-1002), wife of Hugh I, Count of Ponthieu
1 CONT Adela, (c. 973-1063), wife of Renauld I, Count of Nevers
1 CONT
1 CONT <http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Adelaide_of_Aquitaine>
0 @N6000000001783309226@ NOTE Basic Life Information
1 CONT
1 CONT Adele or Adelaide of Aquitaine (or Adelaide of Poitiers) (c. 945 or 952 - 1004) was the daughter of William III, Duke of Aquitaine and Adele of Normandy, daughter of Rollo, Duke of Normandy.
1 CONT
1 CONT Marriage and Children
1 CONT
1 CONT Her father used her as security for a truce with Hugh Capet, whom she married in 970. In 987, after the death of Louis V, the last Carolingian king of France, Hugh was elected the new king with Adelaide as queen. They were proclai
1 CONC med at Noyon and blessed at Reims. They were the founders of the Capetian dynasty of France.
1 CONT
1 CONT Their children were:
1 CONT Hedwig, Countess of Mons (or Hadevide, or Avoise) (c. 969-after 1013), wife of Reginar IV, Count of Mons
1 CONT Robert II (972-1031), the future king of France. Crowned co-king 987 in order to consolidate the new dynasty
1 CONT Gisèle, Countess of Ponthieu(c. 970-1002), wife of Hugh I, Count of Ponthieu
1 CONT Adela, (c. 973-1063), wife of Renauld I, Count of Nevers
1 CONT
1 CONT <http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Adelaide_of_Aquitaine>
