1 CONT
1 CONT Her father used her as security for a truce with Hugh Capet, whom she married in 970. In 987, after the death of Louis V, the last Carolingian king of France, Hugh was elected the new king with Adelaide as queen. They were proclai
1 CONC med at Noyon and blessed at Reims. They were the founders of the Capetian dynasty of France.
1 CONT
1 CONT Their children were:
1 CONT Hedwig, Countess of Mons (or Hadevide, or Avoise) (c. 969-after 1013), wife of Reginar IV, Count of Mons
1 CONT Robert II (972-1031), the future king of France. Crowned co-king 987 in order to consolidate the new dynasty
1 CONT Gisèle, Countess of Ponthieu(c. 970-1002), wife of Hugh I, Count of Ponthieu
1 CONT Adela, (c. 973-1063), wife of Renauld I, Count of Nevers
1 CONT
1 CONT <http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Adelaide_of_Aquitaine>
