0 @N6000000003232551246@ NOTE Gunnora or Gunnor (c. 936–1031) was the wife and consort of Richard I of Normandy. Her parentage is unknown, earliest sources reporting solely that she was of Danish ancestry and naming siblings including brother Herefast de Crepo
1 CONC n who is sometimes erroneously given as her father.
1 CONT
1 CONT She was living with her sister Seinfreda, the wife of a local forester, when Richard passed by hunting. He is said to have approached Seinfreda with amorous intentions, but the lady rejected his advance, suggesting that her unmarr
1 CONC ied sister Gunnor might prove more receptive. They became lovers, Gunnor first acting as his mistress and eventually marrying him.
1 CONT
1 CONT They were parents to six children:
1 CONT
1 CONT     * Richard II "the Good", Duke of Normandy (966)
1 CONT     * Robert, Archbishop of Rouen, Count of Evreux, died 1037.
1 CONT     * Mauger, Earl of Corbeil, died after 1033; his alleged grandson (or perhaps great-grandson) was Robert Fitz Hamon, an important Anglo-Norman baron.
1 CONT     * Robert Danus, died between 985 and 989
1 CONT     * Emma of Normandy (c. 985-1052) wife of two kings of England.
1 CONT     * Maud of Normandy, wife of Odo II of Blois, Count of Blois, Champagne and Chartres
