0 @N6000000007329725376@ NOTE [Tom Bjornstad, <elcontob -at- telepost.no>] .. Gunnor is variation of
1 CONT Gunnvor..
1 CONT [R. Leutner, Soc.Medieval]  I would like to know if  there is a
1 CONT genealogical consensus, whether it is Icelandic, Norse, or English, as to
1 CONT the  parentage and siblings of  Gunnor / Gunnora, wife of Richard I, Duke
1 CONT of  Normandy.  Eleanor Searle,  Predatory Kinship and the Creation of
1 CONT Norman  Power, 840-1066 , a title that says it all (UCAl Press, 1988),
1 CONT does not name  Gunnor's parents for her own reasons, but we don't
1 CONT necessarily  have to buy  them; but here is her list of Gunnor(a) and
1 CONT siblings:
1 CONT GUNNOR=Richard I>ducal line (Normandy).  SISTER=Thorold of
1 CONT Pont-Audemer>Humphrey de Vielles>Beaumonts Warwick,  Leicester, etc.)
1 CONT SISTER=Osbern of Bolbec>Walter Giffard et al. (incl. Clare, earls of
1 CONT Hertford, Pembroke, etc.)
1 CONT HERFAST (brother)>Osbern=Emma (da. of Rodulf)>William fitz Osbern, earl
1 CONT of Hereford>lords of Breteuil, Ballon; and Bishop Osbern f. Osbern of
1 CONT Exeter.
1 CONT SIBLING>Gunnor's niece>Warenne, Earls of Surrey, and Mortimer, of
1 CONT Wigmore.  SISTER>Gunnor's niece=Roger of Montgomery>MONTGOMERY.
1 CONT SIBLING>Gunnor's niece=Keeper of Vernon.  SIBLING>Gunnor's niece=Vicomte
1 CONT of Rouen.  Who were the parents of this illustrious brood?  Is Gunnor's
1 CONT family wholly  fabulous, or can it be claimed in a genealogical way?  I
1 CONT can live without  her, but it would be nice to take on Thorold's and
1 CONT Osbern's wives and  whatever parentage they might share with Gunnor, and
1 CONT others might be happy  to  have clear title to these other siblings.
1 CONT Merged General Note:  Wurts, John S., Magna Charta: The Pedigrees  of the
1 CONT Barons, Philadelphia, PA: Brookfield Publishing Co, 1942.
1 CONT names: [Ref: Wurts p422]
1 CONT The parentage of Gunnor and her siblings is unknown.  While some sources
1 CONT call her father Herfastus, this was in fact the name of her brother.  She
1 CONT has also been claimed as daughter of the Danish royal family, but there
1 CONT is no evidence for this, and the context of her coming to the attention
1 CONT of Richard I and the family's subsequent rise to power militates against
1 CONT her being a royal daughter.  Douglas argued (in a 1944 English Historical
1 CONT Review article on the family of William Fitz Osbern), based on the
1 CONT donations of brother Arfast to the monastery of St. Pere, that the root
1 CONT of the family was in the Cotetin region of Normandy, but van Houts has
1 CONT suggested that the Cotetin land was granted to Arfast, rather than
1 CONT inherited by him.  Thus we are left with the more ambiguous statements of
1 CONT Torigny and others that she was a member of a Norman family of Danish
1 CONT origins.
1 CONT Person Source
0 @N6000000009304893649@ NOTE #Générale#D'origine norroise, concubine attitrée, épousée ensuite pour légitimer les enfants.
1 CONT Dudon en fait le portrait d'une très belle femme, très adroite et de grand esprit - L'ascendance de Gunnor, duchesse de Normandie, n'est pas établie historiquement (en particulier, l'ascendance royale danoise est tout à fait impro
1 CONC bable). Herfastus n'est pas le nom de son père, mais de son frère. La descendance des frère et soeurs de Gunnor qui figure ici est tirée de "Robert de Torigny and the family of Gunnor, Duchess of Normandy", par Todd A. Farmerie, S
1 CONC ociety of Medieval Genealogy (1996), article qui déclare résumer et harmoniser les travaux récents sur ce sujet. (Repris de Béatrice Serisey)
1 CONT
