0 @N6000000000337179375@ NOTE (Research):Richard I Encyclopædia Britannica Article    born c. 932 died 996   byname Richard The Fearless,  French Richard Sans Peur duke of Normandy (942-996), son of William I Longsword.   Louis IV of France took the boy-duke i
1 CONC nto his protective custody, apparently intent upon reuniting Normandy to the crown's domains; but in 945 Louis was captured by the Normans, and Richard was returned to his people. Richard withstood further Carolingian attempts to 
1 CONC subdue his duchy and, in 987, was instrumental in securing the French crown for his brother-in-law, the Robertian Hugh Capet.
