0 @N6000000002240813498@ NOTE In the history of the Dukes of Normandy, there is no information between 931
1 CONT and 942 as to the Dukes of Normandy. The 1st duke was Rollo, a direct
1 CONT ancestor of the rest, 860?-931?, the leader of a menacing band of Viking
1 CONT raiders. The Vikings set up their bases at the mouths of rivers. In 911 a
1 CONT large company of Vikings, under Rollo, accepted from King Charles the Simple
1 CONT  of France, the simple territory in the lower Seine Valley that became known
1 CONT as Normandy. Rollo, therefore, became the 1st Duke of Normandy. See Rollo.
0 @N6000000001354495758@ NOTE Richard I, byname RICHARD THE FEARLESS, French RICHARD SANS PEUR (b. c. 932--d. 996), duke of Normandy (942-996), son of William I Longsword.
1 CONT Louis IV of France took the boy-duke into his protective custody, apparently intent upon reuniting Normandy to the crown's domains; but in 945 Louis was captured by the Normans, and Richard was returned to hispeople. Richard withs
1 CONC tood further Carolingian attempts to subdue his duchy and, in 987, was instrumental in securing the French crown for his brother-in-law, the Robertian Hugh Capet
