0 @N6000000002187734921@ NOTE Adalbert I, Count of Vermandois
1 CONT From Wikipedia, the free encyclopedia
1 CONT
1 CONT Adalbert I of Vermandois (French: Albert I le Pieux, the Pious) (ca. 915/917 – 9 September 988), Count of Vermandois, was the son of Herbert II of Vermandois and Hildebrante of France.
1 CONT
1 CONT [edit] Family
1 CONT
1 CONT In 954 he married Gerberge of Lorraine (c.935-978), daughter of Giselbert, Duke of Lorraine, and Gerberga of Saxony.
1 CONT
1 CONT Their children were:
1 CONT
1 CONT     * Herbert III of Vermandois
1 CONT     * Eudes of Vermandois (c.956-983)
1 CONT     * Liudolfe de Noyon (c.957-986)
1 CONT     * Guy I of Vermandois, count of Soissons
1 CONT
1 CONT Preceded by
1 CONT Herbert II Count of Vermandois
1 CONT 943–988 Succeeded by
1 CONT Herbert III
