0 @N6000000001353851049@ NOTE Boso, French BOSON (d. Jan. 11, 887, Vienne [France]), king of lower Burgundy, or Provence (from 877).
1 CONT The son of Buvin (or Beuves), Count of Ardennes, Boso was given the governance of Lombardy (876) by his brother-in-law Charles II the Bald,king of the West Franks (France), and received the title of duke. During the minorities of 
1 CONC the West Frankish kings Louis III and Carloman, he demonstrated his ambition by convoking the bishops of Provence and having them proclaim him their king (Oct. 15, 879) and thereafter proceeded to expand his domains. The territory
1 CONC  over which he usurped royalauthority included not only Provence but many lands to the north, as far as Autun--an enlarged Burgundy.
1 CONT In succeeding years, especially 880-882, Boso lost many of the marginal northern lands to the French and German Carolingians, who were reestablishing their authority. He was succeeded by his son, Louis, who in901 became the empero
1 CONC r Louis III
