1 CONT Fulk II of Anjou, son of Fulk the Red, was count of Anjou from 941 to 958. He was often at war with the Bretons. He seems to have been a man of culture, a poet and an artist. In 958 he was succeeded by Geoffrey Greymantle.
1 CONT
1 CONT
1 CONT
1 CONT
1 CONT Preceded by:
1 CONT Fulk I Count of Anjou
1 CONT 941–958 Succeeded by:
1 CONT Geoffrey I 
1 CONT
1 CONT This biography of a French peer or noble is a stub. You can help Wikipedia by expanding it.
