0 @N6000000000337410092@ NOTE Weis, p. 128; 102:  Count of Poitou.
0 @N6000000000571069356@ NOTE William III (915 – 3 April 963), called Towhead (French: Tête d'étoupe, Latin: Caput Stupe) from the colour of his hair, was the Count of Poitou (as "William I") and Duke of Aquitaine from 935 to his death. He was also Count of Au
1 CONC vergne from 950.
1 CONT
1 CONT William was son of Ebalus Manzer and Emilienne. He was born in Poitiers. The royal chancery never recognised his ducal title, only calling him "count of the Duchy of Aquitaine" from 959 and "Duke of Aquitaine" only after 962.
1 CONT
1 CONT Shortly aftered the death of King Rudolph in 936, he was constrained to forfeit some land to Hugh the Great by Louis IV. He did it with grace, but his relationship with Hugh thenceforward deteriorated. In 950, Hugh was reconciled 
1 CONC with Louis and granted the duchies of Burgundy and Aquitaine. He tried to conquer Aquitaine with Louis's assistance, but William defeated them. Lothair, Louis's successor, feared the power of William. In August 955, he joined Hugh
1 CONC  to besiege Poitiers, which resisted successfully. William, however, gave battle and was routed.
1 CONT
1 CONT After the death of Hugh, his son Hugh Capet was named duke of Aquitaine, but he never tried to take up his fief, as William reconciled with Lothair.
1 CONT
1 CONT He was given the abbey of Saint-Hilaire-le-Grand, which remained in his house after his death. He also built a library in the palace of Poitiers. He married Gerloc (renamed Adele), daughter of Rollo of Normandy. They had at least 
1 CONC two children: Adelaide, who married Hugh Capet, and William, his successor in Aquitaine. William abdicated to the abbey of Saint-Cyprien in Poitiers and left the government to his son. 
0 @N6000000000945059428@ NOTE Vilhelm ?Stryhode? var greve av Poitou 935 - 963 (som Vilhelm I) og hertug av 
1 CONT Aquitania 951 - 963.
1 CONT Aquitaniaslekten var grever av Poitou ca. 800 til 1199, grever av Auvergne fra 839 til
1 CONT 928 og hertuger av Aquitania fra 893 til 1199. Deretter ble Aquitania en del av kongeriket
1 CONT England, men senere gjenerobret av Frankrike.
1 CONT Vilhelm fortsatte sine forfedres politikk. Vilhelm fikk grevskapet Auvergne og i 951
1 CONT titelen hertug av Guienne (Aquitanien), en titel som hans etterfølgere senere førte. Han
1 CONT forsvarte med hell Poitou mot Hugo ?den Store? og Lothar i 955.
1 CONT I 962 trakk han seg tilbake til klosteret St. Maxient og døde som munk der i 963.
