0 @N6000000002187580343@ NOTE Hedwige of Saxony
1 CONT From Wikipedia, the free encyclopedia.
1 CONT Jump to: navigation, search
1 CONT Hedwige of Saxony (c910-May 10, 965) was daughter, sister, and mother of kings. She was the daughter of Henry I the Fowler, and his wife Matilda of Ringelheim. After her brother Otto the Great came to power, an alliance and marria
1 CONC ge was arranged with Hugh the Great in 936. Her son, Hugh Capet, was crowned King of France in 987.
1 CONT
1 CONT   This biography of a member of a continental European royal house is a stub. You can help Wikipedia by expanding it. 
1 CONT
1 CONT This article on a member of the German nobility is a stub. You can help Wikipedia by expanding it.
