0 @N6000000005076775920@ NOTE Hugues of Neustria, Comte de Paris was born circa 895. He was the son of Robert I, Roi de France.1 He married, firstly, Eadhilda (?), daughter of Eadweard I, King of Wessex and Ælflæd (?), between 926 and 927.2 He married, thirdly
1 CONC , Hedwig von Sachsen, daughter of Heinrich I von Sachsen, Holy Roman Emperor and Mathilda von Ringelheim, before 14 September 938.1 He died on 9 June 956.
1 CONT      Hugues of Neustria, Comte de Paris also went by the nick-name of Hugues 'the Great'.1 He gained the title of Comte de Paris. He gained the title of Duc de France.
1 CONT Children of Hugues of Neustria, Comte de Paris and Hedwig von Sachsen
1 CONT Hugues de Paris, Roi de France+ b. c 938, d. 24 Oct 996
1 CONT Emma de Paris b. a 942, d. 19 Mar 968
1 CONT Citations
1 CONT [S45] Marcellus Donald R. von Redlich, Pedigrees of Some of the Emperor Charlemagne's Descendants, volume I (1941; reprint, Baltimore, Maryland, U.S.A.: Genealogical Publishing Company, 2002), page 63. Hereinafter cited as Pedigre
1 CONC es of Emperor Charlemagne, I.
1 CONT [S11] Alison Weir, Britain's Royal Family: A Complete Genealogy (London, U.K.: The Bodley Head, 1999), page 13. Hereinafter cited as Britain's Royal Family.
