0 @N6000000002322288417@ NOTE He was the progenitor of the Capetian kings of France and the brother-in-law
1 CONT of 3 kings: Rudolph of France, Athelstan of England, and Otto of Germany. He
1 CONT was the most powerful man in the kingdom of France (West Francia) during the
1 CONT reign of Louis IV and the early years of King Lothair. Possessing such vast
1 CONT territories, he could easily have assumed the crown on the death of Rudolf in
1 CONT 936, but he preferred working from behind the throne. He suggested the
1 CONT accession of Louis IV, son of the deposed Charles III the Simple.
