0 @N6000000002187576678@ NOTE William Longsword (died December 17, 942) was jarl (ruler) of Normandy.
1 CONT From Wikipedia, the free encyclopedia
1 CONT
1 CONT Little is known about his early years. He was born overseas in one of the many Viking territories before his father Rollo settled in northern France. William's mother was named Poppa; all that is known of her is that she was a Chr
1 CONC istian, and the daughter of a Count Berengar. According to the Planctus, he was baptized a Christian.
1 CONT
1 CONT William succeeded Rollo sometime around 928. It appears that he faced a rebellion early in his reign, from Normans who felt he had become too Frankified. The following years are obscure. In 939 William became involved in a war wit
1 CONC h Arnulf I of Flanders, which soon became intertwined with the other conflicts of the reign of Louis IV of France. He was killed by followers of Arnulf while at a meeting to settle their conflict. His son Richard I of Normandy suc
1 CONC ceeded him.
1 CONT
1 CONT [edit]
1 CONT External link
1 CONT Planctus for William Longsword 
1 CONT Preceded by:
1 CONT Rollo Duke of Normandy Succeeded by:
1 CONT Richard I 
1 CONT ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
1 CONT Duke of Normandy 932-942. According to some sources,William was born in 876. He was what might be termed *co-regent* with his father from about 925. William had a 2. wife, Liutgard, who, after his death, married Theobald, Count of
1 CONC  Blois and Chartres. From this marriage, a direct line of descent can be traced to King Stephen. He was murdered by the Flemings. Source: RoyaList, Dan Pomerleau, Leo van de Pas . 
