0 @N6000000002187855032@ NOTE Hedwig of France
1 CONT From Wikipedia, the free encyclopedia
1 CONT
1 CONT Hedwig of France
1 CONT Born c. 970
1 CONT Died after 1013
1 CONT Title Countess of Mons
1 CONT Spouse Rainier IV of Hainaut
1 CONT Parents Hugh Capet
1 CONT Adelaide of Aquitaine
1 CONT
1 CONT Hedwig of France (c. 970- after 1013), also called Avoise, Hadevide or Haltude, was Countess of Mons. She was the daughter of Hugh Capet, the first King of France, and Adelaide of Aquitaine.
1 CONT
1 CONT [edit] Family
1 CONT
1 CONT In 996 Hedwig married Rainier IV of Hainaut (947-1013). They had three children:
1 CONT
1 CONT     * Reginar V, Count of Mons. Married Mathilde of Verdun, daughter of Herman, Count of Brabant.
1 CONT     * Lambert of Mons
1 CONT     * Beatrix, who married Ebles I, Count of Rheims and Roucy, and Archbishop of Rheims.
1 CONT
1 CONT Following the death of her first husband, Hedwig re-married to Hugh de Dagsbourg. She died after 1013.
