0 @N6000000002187818659@ NOTE Reginar IV, Count of Mons
1 CONT From Wikipedia, the free encyclopedia
1 CONT
1 CONT Regnier IV, Count of Mons (c. 950-1013) was the son of Reginar III, Count of Hainaut. Lambert I of Leuven was his brother.
1 CONT
1 CONT [edit] History
1 CONT
1 CONT His father was Count of Hainaut until 958, but fell in disgrace with Otto I, Holy Roman Emperor and lost his County to Godfrey I, Duke of Lower Lorraine.
1 CONT
1 CONT He received the County of Mons in 973 but was replaced with Godfrey I, Count of Verdun in 974. He replaced Godfrey as Count of Mons in 998.
1 CONT
1 CONT [edit] Family
1 CONT
1 CONT Regnier IV married Hedwig, Countess of Mons, daughter of Hugh Capet, King of France, and Adelaide of Poitou.
1 CONT
1 CONT They had three children:
1 CONT
1 CONT     * Reginar V, Count of Mons. Married Mathilde of Verdun, daughter of Herman, Count of Brabant.
1 CONT     * Lambert of Mons
1 CONT     * Beatrix, who married Ebles I, Count of Rheims and Roucy, and Archbishop of Rheims.
1 CONT
1 CONT
1 CONT Preceded by
1 CONT Reginald Count of Mons
1 CONT 973–974 Succeeded by
1 CONT Godfrey I, Count of Verdun
1 CONT Preceded by
1 CONT Godfrey I, Count of Verdun Count of Mons
1 CONT 998–1013 Succeeded by
1 CONT Reginar V
