0 @N6000000001353983724@ NOTE Ivo, Count of Beaumont.
1 CONT Davis: The great families like the Beaumonts, Bohuns and Warennes emerged in
1 CONT the 11th century (page 27). "In England we are so used to the names of those
1 CONT families
1 CONT who came over with the Conqueror'--de Beaumont, de Montfort, de
1 CONT Montgomery and the like--that we tend to assume that at that date they were
1 CONT already ancient and well established in Normand. In fact they were nearly all
1 CONT new in the sense that whether they were immigrants, or like Roger de
1 CONT Montgomery, ex Northmannis Northmannus, it was only rarely that they had
1 CONT acquired lands from which they took their family name before the 1030s."
