0 @N6000000002187631867@ NOTE Fulk I of Anjou
1 CONT From Wikipedia, the free encyclopedia.
1 CONT
1 CONT Fulk I of Anjou, called the Red, was son of viscount Ingelger of Angers, and was the first count of Anjou from 898 to 941. He increased the territory of the viscounty of Angers and it became a county around 930. During his reign h
1 CONC e was permanently at war with the Normans and the Bretons. He occupied the county of Nantes in 907, but abandoned it to the Bretons in 919. He died around 941 and was succeeded by his son Fulk II.
1 CONT
1 CONT
1 CONT
1 CONT
1 CONT Preceded by:
1 CONT — Count of Anjou
1 CONT 898–941 Succeeded by:
1 CONT Fulk II 
1 CONT
1 CONT This biography of a French peer or noble is a stub. You can help Wikipedia by expanding it.
