0 @N6000000002188307382@ NOTE Gilbert, Duke of Burgundy
1 CONT From Wikipedia, the free encyclopedia
1 CONT
1 CONT Gilbert of Chalon or Giselbert (died April 8, 956) was duke of Burgundy between 952 and 956. He ruled Burgundy in the name of his wife, Ermengarde, sister of Hugh the Black, with whom he had two daughters: Adelais and Liutgarde. G
1 CONC ilbert never managed to maintain the independence of the duchy in the struggles for power of 10th century France. In 955, he became a vassal of Hugh the Great, count of Paris and was compelled to give his oldest daughter, Lieutgar
1 CONC d, to Hugh's son Odo of Paris.
1 CONT
1 CONT See also: Dukes of Burgundy family tree
1 CONT
1 CONT
1 CONT Preceded by
1 CONT Hugh Duke of Burgundy Succeeded by
1 CONT Odo
