0 @N6000000002738819461@ NOTE hertog van Lotharingen
0 @N6000000003949675297@ NOTE The beginning of the reign of Gilbert is not clear. Lotharingia belonged to West Francia (or France) from 910, when a dux Lotharingiae is first mentioned. This may have been Gilbert. The French king Charles III was deposed in 922 
1 CONC by Robert. Charles remained king in Lotharingia and tried to reconquer West Francia from there. He was imprisoned in 923.
1 CONT In 925, Gilbert swore fealty to King Henry the Fowler of Germany as duke of Lotharingia. Gilbert married Henry's daughter Gerberge by 930. For whatever reason, Gilbert rebelled when Henry died in 936 and changed allegiance to the 
1 CONC king of France, where the king had less authority. Gilbert managed to be practically independent for three years until he was defeated and killed by the army of king Otto I of Germany in 939 at the Battle of Andernach.
