1 CONT
1 CONT Herbert II died on 23 February 943 without having succeeded in building the principality of which he dreamed. His succession was reconciled by Hugh the Great, maternal uncle of his children. It took place in 946 and led to an equi
1 CONC table distribution between the sons of Herbert II: Herbert III, Robert, Albert, and Hugh (his other son Eudes died before 946). As for his girls, Adela was married to Arnulf I, count of Flanders, Luitgarde (widow of William Longsw
1 CONC ord) was married to Theobald I, count of Blois, the first lieutenant of Hugh. She brought to Theobald Provins and domains in the Mézerais.
1 CONT
1 CONT [edit] Family
1 CONT
1 CONT He was first married to Adela, and then to Hildebrante of France (895-931), daughter of Robert I of France.
1 CONT
1 CONT With Adela, he had 7 children:
1 CONT
1 CONT     * Adele of Vermandois (910-960), married 934 Count Arnulf I of Flanders, also a descendant of Charlemagne
1 CONT     * Eudes of Vermandois, Count of Amiens and of Vienne, (910-946)
1 CONT     * Herbert "the Elder", Count of Meaux and of Troyes (-993)
1 CONT     * Robert of Vermandois, Count of Meaux and Chalons (-968)
1 CONT     * Adalbert I, Count of Vermandois (915-987), married Gerberga of Lorraine, also a descendant of Charlemagne
1 CONT     * Luitgarde of Vermandois (ca 920-978), married 943 Theobald I of Blois
1 CONT     * Hugh of Vermandois (died 962), Archbishop of Reims
1 CONT
1 CONT [edit] External links
1 CONT
1 CONT     * Comtes de Vermandois
1 CONT
1 CONT Preceded by
1 CONT Herbert I Count of Vermandois
1 CONT 907–943 Succeeded by
1 CONT Adalbert I
