0 @N6000000003300509138@ NOTE There had already been Norwegian and Danish settlers in the area. King Ch arles "the Simple" of France made an effort to chase away the Vikings, bu t Rolf's men triumphed at Pont-de-l'Arche, then went on to raid Melun, wh ere the 
1 CONC French again tried to beat them off and lost. So the Vikings rule d the area from their seat at Rouen, and mostly turned to colonization in stead of pillaging. But Rolf looked beyond the Seine valley; he extende d his holdings acr
1 CONC oss the Risle, then the Orne, then took Bayeux in 900 , killing Count Béreanger who had held it; Rolf married the count's daugh ter Popa. And, finally, in 911, Charles "the Simple" recognized Rolf's ho ldings
