1 CONT
1 CONT  Rollo the Viking (855-931) brought his  Normans ( northmen, vikings)
1 CONT from                        Norway to the northwest of France. This is
1 CONT the Rollo, or Rollon in the French
1 CONT spelling, who in 911 at the church in St.  Clair sur Epte signed the
1 CONT treaty with King
1 CONT  Louis the Simple of France that created him hereditary Duke of the new
1 CONT Duchy of Normandy.
1 CONT
1 CONT  Some say that Rollo was the same as Ganger-Hrolf, or Rollo the
1 CONT Ganger, who was called that because he was so gangly, to be  specific,
1 CONT his legs were so long that when he rode a horse it  looked like he was
1 CONT walking; Ganger means Walker. However,   according to Peter
1 CONT Kurrild-Klitgaard, Ph.D., the early sources all         distinguish the
1 CONT two men.
