0 @N6000000003495155075@ NOTE
1 CONT Ebalus, Duc d'Aquitaine1 (M)
1 CONT d. 934, #141516
1 CONT Last Edited=13 Jul 2005
1 CONT
1 CONT      Ebalus, Duc d'Aquitaine died in 934.1 
1 CONT       Ebalus, Duc d'Aquitaine also went by the nick-name of Ebalus 'the Bastard'.1 He was a member of the House of Poitiers.1 He gained the title of Comte de Poitou in 890.1 He gained the title of Duc d'Aquitaine in 927.1
1 CONT
1 CONT Child of Ebalus, Duc d'Aquitaine
1 CONT Guillaume III, Duc d'Aquitaine+ b. c 915, d. 3 Apr 9631
1 CONT Citations
1 CONT 1. [S38] John Morby, Dynasties of the World: a chronological and genealogical handbook (Oxford, Oxfordshire, U.K.: Oxford University Press, 1989), page 81. Hereinafter cited as Dynasties of the World.
1 CONT
1 CONT Guillaume VI, Duc d'Aquitaine1 (M)
1 CONT d. 1038, #141517
1 CONT Pedigree
1 CONT Last Edited=13 Jul 2005
1 CONT
1 CONT      Guillaume VI, Duc d'Aquitaine was the son of Guillaume V, Duc d'Aquitaine and Agnes de Bourgogne.1 He died in 1038.1 
1 CONT       Guillaume VI, Duc d'Aquitaine also went by the nick-name of Guillaume 'le Gros' (or in English, 'the Fat').1 He was a member of the House of Poitiers.1 He succeeded to the title of Duc d'Aquitaine in 1030.1
1 CONT Citations
1 CONT 1. [S38] John Morby, Dynasties of the World: a chronological and genealogical handbook (Oxford, Oxfordshire, U.K.: Oxford University Press, 1989), page 81. Hereinafter cited as Dynasties of the World.
