0 @N6000000003219704755@ NOTE MATHILDE ([896]-Quedlinburg 14 Mar 968, bur Quedlinburg Stiftskirche).  Widukind names "Mahthilda" as wife of King Heinrich, also naming her father and three brothers[42].  Thietmar names Mathilde as daughter of "Dietrich and Rein
1 CONC hild" when recording her marriage to Heinrich, and specifies that she was "a descendant of the lineage of King Widukind"[43].  Her alleged descent from Widukind is also referred to in the Vita Mahthildis[44].  Quedlinburg was best
1 CONC owed on Mathilde as part of her dower 16 Sep 929[45].  She established the convent there thirty days after the death of her husband[46].  Lay Abbess of Nivelles.  The necrology of Fulda records the death "968 II Id Mar" of "Mahthi
1 CONC ld regina"[47].  m (Wallhausen 909) as his second wife, HEINRICH Graf, son of OTTO "dem Erlauchten" Graf im Südthüringau & Hedwig [Babenberg] ([876]-Memleben 2 Jul 936, bur Quedlinburg Stiftskirche).  He was elected as HEINRICH I 
1 CONC "der Vogelsteller/the Fowler" King of Germany at Fritzlar 6 May 919.
1 CONT
