0 @N6000000001503830673@ NOTE
1 CONT Weis" "Ancestral Roots. . ." (48:18). Born posthumously 866, Count of
1 CONT Poitiers, Count of Paris, Marquis of Neustria, King of West Franks
1 CONT (France); m.(1) Aelis; m.(2) BEATRIX, as I have shown here. Also
1 CONT mentioned (50:18), (53:18), (101:18), (136:18).
1 CONT
1 CONT Nat Taylor posted the following to the soc.genealogy.medieval
1 CONT newsgroups on 4 Nov 1995 :
1 CONT "It would seem that it was Robert's first wife, Adele, not Beatrix, who
1 CONT was Hildebrante's mother. This was a double marriage alliance
1 CONT concluded between King Robert and Herbert II of Vermandois; Robert was
1 CONT married to Beatrice "in or by the late 890's" (Andrew W. Lewis, _Royal
1 CONT Succession in Capetian France (Harvard, 1981), p. 11); Herbert II had
1 CONT married Robert's daughter by 907 (ibid.). This double alliance
1 CONT strengthened the relationship of the two houses; the Vermandois counts
1 CONT had previously supported the Carolingians (Charles the Simple) against
1 CONT king Odo; but in 922 Vermandois supported Robert's succesful bid for the
1 CONT throne. See also Jean Dunbabbin, _France in the Making, 843-1180
1 CONT (Oxford, 1985), p. 95.
1 CONT Robert's first wife was as much a daughter of Louis the Pious as I am.
1 CONT She would have had to be at least 26 years Robert's senior, and to have
1 CONT borne children while over 50. Stuart's sources as mentioned do not
1 CONT inspire confidence, but this is hardly a surprise (sorry, Moriarty)."
1 CONT
1 CONT -SSMD
