1 CONT
1 CONT Robert's military success greatly enhanced his prestige, and dissensionbetween him and the King became undisguised. When Charles III imprudentlyoffered preferment exclusively to lords from Lorraine, the Neustrianlords, led by Robe
1 CONC rt, broke into open revolt. They elected Robert king atReims in June 922. In a battle near Soissons a year later, Charles's armywas routed, but Robert was killed.
1 CONT
