1 CONT OCCU Rutpert IV ...
1 CONT SOUR HAWKINS.GED says 825; members.aol.com/sargen3 says ABT 820, France;
1 CONT misc.traveller.com/genealogy/gedhtml/kmilburn says 820;
1 CONT gendex.com/users/daver/rigney/D0001 says 820
1 CONT SOUR Royalty for Commoners, Roderick W. Stuart,p5 says slain 15 Sept or 25 Aug 866;
1 CONT The Conquest of England, Eric Linklater, p. 21 says 866;
1 CONT ROYAL.THD (Compuserve) & gendex.com/users/daver/rigney/D0001 says 866
1 CONT SOUR Royalty for Commoners, Roderick W. Stuart, p. 126, 164;
1 CONT gendex.com/users/daver/rigney/D0001;
1 CONT Count of Paris - COMYNI.GED (Compuserve); Charles the Bald in 861 gave the
1 CONT important military command of Paris to Robert, count of Tours, called Robert
1 CONT the Strong.  Robert, who fought stoutly against the Norse invaders was killed
1 CONT in battle - The Conquest of England, Eric Linklater, p. 15
1 CONT For the dispute on the parentage of Robert, see
1 CONT ROBERT LE FORT, son of Rutpert III and Waldrada: THE PARENTAGE OF ROBERT THE STRONG  [EXCERPTED FROM: G.A. Moriarty's PLANTAGENET ANCESTRY; all material in double-quotes is a direct quote from him.]
1 CONT "The question of the parentage of Robert the Strong, Marquis of Anjou, is not fully as yet settled and the erudits are not in accord.
1 CONT "According to Richaer, who wrote more than 100 years after the time of Robert the Strong, who first occurs in 852, was the son of Witichin, as given on p.9 ante.  Witichin = "Young Gui."  In a very
1 CONT  doubtful charter he is styled "son of Robert."
1 CONT "J. Depoin ("Les origines de Robert le Fort," REVUE HISTORIQUES, 1908; J. Calmette, "La famille de Saint-Guilhem et l'ascendance de Robert le Fort," ANNLES DES MIDI, 1928) and Chaume ("Robert le Fort
1 CONT  et ses ultaches bourguignonnes" in RECHERCHES
1 CONT D'HISTOIRE [Dijon, 1947]) consider Robert to have been the son of Witichin.  The view at present most in favor, that he was the son of Robert (probably the Robert who was Missus in Touraine in 825,
1 CONT  cf. Boretius, CAPITULARIA, I, p.308), is maintained by
1 CONT K. Glockman in "Lorsch und Lothringen, Robertiner und Capetinger" (ZEITSCHRIFT FUR GESICHTE DES OBERSHEINNS, vol. 50 [1936], p.301-54), and perhaps by the distinguished French erudit, L. Levillain
1 CONT  (in "Essai sur le Comte Eudes, fils de Harduin et
1 CONT Guerinbourg," LE MOYEN AGE, 1937).  This second view appears in Winkhaus's
1 CONT AHNER KARL DEM GROSSEN UND WIDUKIND, and is given on p. 211 ante.
1 CONT "It is, I submit, quite certain that the Robertins originated in the Wormgau and all the erudits are in agreement that the mother of Robert the Strong was a sister of Eudes, Count of Orleans (d. 854)
1 CONT  and of William, Constable of Blois (d. 834) (cf.
1 CONT p.216 ante).  (See J. Dhoudt, ETUDES SUR LA NAISSANCE DES
1 CONT PRINCIPANTES TERRITORIALES EN FRANCE [1948], pp.93, 323-24)."
1 CONT - ROBERT.TXT (Compuserve)
1 CONT Rutpert IV "the Strong," Count of Paris, Tours and Wormsgau, Marquis of Anjou, Blois, Auxerre, and Nevers, Lay Abbot of Tours, 836-866 - Royalty for Commoner, Roderick W. Stuart, p. 126
1 CONT Count of Paris, Wormgau, Anjou, Blois, Tours, Auxerre, and Nevers - p. 164
1 CONT http://members.aol.com/sargen2/g0000015.htm#I2510 gives parents as Witithin (b. ABT 795, Saxony, Germany) and Geva (b. ABT 799, Jutland, Germany) - NPH
1 CONT Robert I, Count of Paris; Marquis in Neustria - p. 191
1 CONT Duke of Nuestria - http://gendex. com/users/daver/rigney/D0001/G0000056.html#I1367
1 CONT http://www.rootsweb.com/~gumby/cgi-bin/igmget.cgi/n=Winch?I12052 gives parents as Within and Geva- nph
1 CONT
