0 @N6000000003219699442@ NOTE Count of Poitiers, Count of Paris, Marquis of Neustria, King of the West Franks.Robert inherited vast estates from his brother Eudes, King of the West Franks, when Eudes died in 898. However, Robert did not claim the throne, inste
1 CONC ad he ruled as Duke of the Franks and he acknowledged Charles III "The Simple" (who had ruled jointly with Eudes) as the King of France. However, Charles' was not a successful ruler and finally Robert led a rebellion against him. 
1 CONC In 922, Robert drove Charles into Lorraine and Charles was deposed as King.A year later, Robert and Charles met again in battle at Soissons; Robert was killed on June 15, 923 and Charles was imprisoned for the remaining six years 
1 CONC of his life. Robert's son-in-law, Raoul/Rudolph of Burgundy was elected by the nobles to be the next King of France.
1 CONT
1 CONT I do not have verification on all information that you have downloaded.  Please feel free to contact me @ promise_me_tomorrow@yahoo.com for errors/corrections/ or any additional information, especially if you are willing to share 
1 CONC information
