0 @N6000000003219709100@ NOTE Of Beauvoisie, Picardie, Seigneur de Creil.
1 CONT  When Duke Richard I of Normandy was 12 years old he was living in the castle of Laon as the ward of Louis IV, King of France. Yves de Creil, according to Norman historians, betrayed a plot to murder Richard to Osmund, the Duke's 
1 CONC tutor and squire.
1 CONT Osmund had Richard feign illness and carried him out in a russet cloak, fleeing to the castle of Coucy, held by Bernard, Count of Senlis.
1 CONT The "Ecclesiastical History" of Orderic Vitalis mentions an "Ivo de Credolio regis balistarius" [literally, royal crossbow-man, but more likely officer in charge of the royal siege train of catapults, ballista, and trebuchet], cir
1 CONC ca 945. He married Geile de Ponthieu (912-965). In politics the family were Robertians, followers of the Dukes of France who would become Kings of France after the final fall of the Merovingians.
1 CONT
1 CONT I do not have verification on all information that you have downloaded.  Please feel free to contact me @ promise_me_tomorrow@yahoo.com for errors/corrections/ or any additional information, especially if you are willing to share 
1 CONC information
