1 CONC e most ancient and famous of the early French noble houses, and is descended in direct male line from the Emperor Charlemagne. The records of the counts go back to Herbert, grandson of Bernard of Italy. From 1045 to 1083, the coun
1 CONC ts possessed also the Valois.In 1102, Raoul de Vermandois was the reigning count. Hugh the Great, Earl of Vermandois, was one of the leaders of the First Crusade and died at Tarsus in Cilicia in 1102.
