0 @N6000000001783594320@ NOTE Herbert I of Vermandois (ca. 848/850 - 907), Count of Vermandois, lord of Senlis, of Peronne and of Saint Quentin, was the son of Pepin of Vermandois.
1 CONT
1 CONT He is a Fourth Generation Descendant of Charlemagne. (http://www.answers.com/topic/herbert-i-count-of-vermandois)
1 CONT
1 CONT Vermandois (vermäNdwä') , region, N France, now in Somme and Aisne depts. The region is largely agricultural (wheat, beets) but has some industry (metallurgy, textiles, rubber) located principally at Saint-Quentin, the former capi
1 CONC tal. Vermandois became an earldom under Charlemagne (9th cent.), and its lords were among the most powerful in N France. The region was annexed to the French crown (c.1200), ceded to Burgundy (1435), recovered by Louis XI (1477), 
1 CONC and incorporated into the province of Picardy. (http://www.answers.com/topic/vermandois)
