0 @N6000000003319675985@ NOTE
1 CONT WFT 6064
0 @N6000000007329688296@ NOTE Kilde: Weis, Frederick Lewis, Ancestral   Roots  of Sixty Colonists, 6th
1 CONT Edition, Baltimore: Genealogical Publishing   Co,  1988.
1 CONT Kilde: date: first marriage of Robert I [Ref:  Weis AR #48].  //
1 CONT [ Alan Bond Wilson, <abwilson -at- uclink2.berkeley.edu> 1026   Alvarado
1 CONT Road, Berleley, CA  94705-1548, (510) 848-6867]:
1 CONT I note that Winkhaus (p. 56) indicates that Hildebrande is the   daughter
1 CONT of  Robert I and Beatrix, whose parentage is unknown; and Moriarty (p. 9)
1 CONT indicates that Hildebrande may possibly be the daughter of Robert and
1 CONT his  second wife, Beatrice.
1 CONT Weis (line 48) indicates that Liegarde (Hildebrante) is daughter of
1 CONT Robert  I and his first wife, Aelis; Robert's second wife, Beatrix, is
1 CONT the  daughter of Herbert I, Count of Vermandois.  Stuart (line 169) also
1 CONT indicates that Hildebrante is daughter of Robert's first wife Adele
1 CONT (Aenis) and that Robert's second wife, Beatrice, is daughter of   Herbert
1 CONT I,  Count of Vermandois (line 134).
1 CONT In Europaische Stammtafeln (ii, 10) Hildebrante (Liegarde), wife of
1 CONT Heribert II, Count of Vermandois, is listed as daughter of Robert's
1 CONT first  wife, Aelis; Robert's second wife, Beatrix de Vermandois is mother
1 CONT of  Hugues le Grand.
1 CONT ***Elsewhere (line 259) Stuart lists Adele (Adelaide), wife of Robert
1 CONT I,  as daughter of Louis I, King of France, and Ermengarde of Hesbaye.
1 CONT Stuart  provides three references to line 259.  One of them, Moriarty
1 CONT (pp. 6   & 9)  does not mention Adele (Aelis/Aenis/Adelaide); I have not
1 CONT tracked   down the  other two references.
1 CONT It would seem that it was Robert's first wife, Adele (or something   like
1 CONT that), not Beatrix, who was Hildebrante's mother, but the critical
1 CONT connection between this Adele and Robert I relies on Stuart's line   259
1 CONT which I have not independently  confirmed.  //
1 CONT ***  [Nat Taylor, <ntaylor -at- fas.harvard.edu>]   '..Robert's first
1 CONT wife  (Adele) was as much a daughter of Louis the Pious as I am. She
1 CONT would   have  had to be at least 26 years Robert's senior, and to have
1 CONT borne   children  while over 50. Sruart's sources as mentioned do not
1 CONT inspire   confidence..'
