1 CONT Ryurik of Novgorod, Grand Duke of Kiev, ruled 862-879. Ryurik was probably a Danish Viking. He was succeeded by his nephew Oleg, who was, like Ryurik, a semi-legendary personage, who freed the Eastern Slavs from the rule of the Kh
1 CONC azars, a powerful Turkik stock. Oleg concluded a treaty with the Byzantine Empire and ruled 879-912.
