0 @N6000000009304907740@ NOTE #Générale##Générale#s:ds02.153 ; Auréjac
0 @N6000000003051286098@ NOTE [Wikipedia, "Zoltán of Hungary", retrieved 19 Oct 07]
1 CONT Zoltán, also known as Zolta and Zaltas, was a ruler of Hungary in the early 10th century. He was probably the son of Árpád and the father of Taksony and possibly Jutas. The early 13th century chronicle Gesta Hungarorum names Zolta
1 CONC  as the son and successor of Árpád. Although he ruled Hungary from 907 to 946, his leadership meant much less than with previous leaders, as during his time, tribal leaders had most of the powers. Latest researches questioned his 
1 CONC position as a ruler and prefer other sons of Árpád.
1 CONT
1 CONT In this era, the raids of Hungarians were common in much of Europe.
