0 @N6000000000437066178@ NOTE Name Prefix:<NPFX> Duchess
0 @N6000000008630617211@ NOTE Stammtafeln says she is the daughter of Henry, Margrave of Mark (d886).
1 CONT
1 CONT Current consensus (as summarised by E.Hlawitschka, in Rheinische
1 CONT Vierteljarhrblatter, 1974, p141ff) is that she was a daughter ofMargrave Henry who died at paris against the Normans 28.8.886 (he alsooften appears with other titles: Duke of the Austrasians, is one ofthem). Her mother was accordi
1 CONC ng to the same author) was probably agrand-daughter of St.Ida (d.c.820) and the Saxon Count Egbert (flor.809-11).
1 CONT
1 CONT I can only refer back to the same article: there was a family inSaxony
1 CONT at this time who historians call the Egbertiner or Cobbonen aftertheir
1 CONT most distinguished members. The details about Ida and Egbert's family
1 CONT come from two sources: her Life (written 980/3) and the Translatio
1 CONT S.Pusinnae (c.860/77). St.Ida was the founder of Herford, a convent
1 CONT in Saxony. Her Life calls Egbert duke of all saxony between the Rhine
1 CONT and the weser appointed by Charlemagne. A count Egbert appears in
1 CONT the Royal frankish annals in 809 and 811 concerned with the boundary
1 CONT between Saxony and the Denmark. Their children included Warin
1 CONT abbot of Corvey 826-56, and Count Cobbo the Elder (d. fl 845), and
1 CONT Addila abbess of Herford. This family continued to be important in
1 CONT Saxony in the 10th century.
1 CONT
1 CONT Ida is said to be the daughter of a Frankish count (though Hlawitschkatries to make her a daughter of Carloman I d.771, wrongly I think). AsEgbert of Wessex became king in 802 (?), it would seem unlikely thathe could have two diff
1 CONC erent careers in two different countries, at thesame time. Unless the ASC date 802 is wrong.
1 CONT
1 CONT Matt
1 CONT
1 CONT PS: the Egbertiner are also mentioned in an article in English (about
1 CONT the revolt of the Stellinga in Saxony c.840-43), in Speculum 70, 1995,p488.
1 CONT Speculum is an American journal on Medieval History.
1 CONT
1 CONT Dutch "Winkler Prins" encyclopedia says Henry was via his mother a
1 CONT grandson of Louis the German (who was a grandson of Charlemagne). The
1 CONT sources of this article are:
1 CONT - Jahrbc8her des deutschen Reichs unter Kn2ig Heinrich, by G. Waitz(1885,
1 CONT 1963)
1 CONT - Kn2ig Heinrich I, by Fr. Ld8tke (1936)
1 CONT - Geschichte der schsischen Kaiserzeit, by R. Holzmann (1941, 1953)
1 CONT - Kn2ig Heinrich I, by W. Mohr (1950)
1 CONT - Von den Karolingern zu den Staufern, by J. Haller (1958)
1 CONT - Die Mark Brandenburg, by J. Schultze (1961)
1 CONT - Heinrich I, Sd8west- und Westpolitik, by H. Bt8tner (1964)
1 CONT "Von den Karolingern zu den Staufern" is the source of thegenealogical information in the article.
