0 @N6000000001503791620@ NOTE His ancestry is a matter of hot dispute. The only nearly contemporary
1 CONT source on the matter is Richer, who stated in the 10th century that
1 CONT Robert's father was "Witichin".
1 CONT
1 CONT The genealogy from the "Dictionary of Royal Lineage" has Robert's father
1 CONT Theotbert, Count of Autun (RIN 3461).
1 CONT
1 CONT Weis' "Ancestral Roots . . .", which reflects a more recent opinion has his
1 CONT pedigree as I've shown it here. (48:17), (181:6), calls him Rutpert IV,
1 CONT Count in Wormgau; of Anjou, Blois, Tours, Auxerre, and Nevers; killed 15
1 CONT Sep 866.
1 CONT
1 CONT Richard Borthwick posted to the
1 CONT soc.genealogy.medieval newsgroup on 23 Oct 1996 (in part):
1 CONT Subject: Re: Ancestors of the Capetiens
1 CONT The matter was one of great debate but quite some time ago. The
1 CONT crucial study was done by K Glockner "Lorsch und Lothringen" in
1 CONT *Zeitschrift fur die Geschichte des Oberrheins*, 89, 1936/37, 301-54.
1 CONT The identification of Rutpert IV count in the Oberrheingau with Robert
1 CONT count of Paris is now considered most likely. Robert like many other
1 CONT Lotharingian nobles entered the service of Charles the Bald in 852
1 CONT following territorial squabbles between Charles and his brothers. You
1 CONT may find an article by K F Werner helpful: "Noble Families in
1 CONT Charlemagne's Kingdom" in a collection of papers entitled *The Medieval
1 CONT Nobility* edited and translated by Timothy Reuter (1979), 172 f.
1 CONT
1 CONT Fransisco Antonio Doria posted to the
1 CONT soc.genealogy.medieval newsgroup on 12 Jul 1998 (in part):
1 CONT Subject: Re: Who did Herbert I de Vermandois Marry?
1 CONT
1 CONT Recently (1989) Luiz de Mello Vaz de Sampayo suggested in a well-argued
1 CONT paper that Richer's "Witichinus" hypothesis (Witichinus as father of Robert
1 CONT le Fort) may stand on solid ground. He takes Witichinus as Wittchen -
1 CONT Little Witus, or better as Witus (Guido) the Young. He still plugs the
1 CONT whole family into Gloeckner's Robertini but from a side branch. Some
1 CONT reasonable onomastics support his claim. (Raizes & Trofeus, no. 2.)
1 CONT
1 CONT -Stevens/Southworth Medieval Database
1 CONT -http://www.gendex.com/users/jast/
