1 CONT RESEARCH NOTES:Count in Wormgau, of Tours, and of Paris [Ref: ES I.2 #200A] Count and Marquis of Newstria [Ref: Settipani Capet #11] Count of Wormgau, Paris, Anjou, and Blois [Ref: Weis AR7 #181] Count in Wormgau; of Anjou, Blois,
1 CONC  Tours, Auxerre, Nevers [Ref: Weis AR7 #48] Marquis of Neustria [Ref: CMH p358] Duke of France and Count of Anjou [Ref: Redlich CharlemagneDesc p63]
1 CONT  Richer is the only chronicler who gives the name of the father of Robert the Strong, i.e. Witichin, a German.  There is ample evidence that RObert and his brother Eudes were the maternal nephews of Count Eudes of Orleans and his 
1 CONC brother William the Constable, Count of Blois[Ref: Moriarty Plantagenet p215]
1 CONT  852-66: Count and Marquis of Newstria [Ref: Settipani Capet #11]
