0 @N6000000002187818670@ NOTE Reginar II, Count of Hainaut
1 CONT From Wikipedia, the free encyclopedia
1 CONT
1 CONT Reginar II (890-932) was Count of Hainaut from 915 until 932.
1 CONT
1 CONT [edit] History
1 CONT
1 CONT He was the son of Reginar, Duke of Lorraine and Hersent of France. His mother possibly was a daughter of Charles the Bald and Ermentrude.
1 CONT
1 CONT [edit] Family
1 CONT
1 CONT Reginar II married Adelaide of Burgundy, daughter of Richard, Duke of Burgundy and Adelaide of Auxerre, with whom he fathered Reginar III, Count of Hainaut.
1 CONT Preceded by
1 CONT Reginar I Count of Hainaut
1 CONT 915–932 Succeeded by
1 CONT Reginar III
