0 @N6000000007329697173@ NOTE [Aardy R. DeVarque, Feudalism: Serf & Turf]  Pat Boren wrote: >OK,   last
1 CONT one.  I can't find any corroberating documentation for this line, so   I
1 CONT appreciate help with it.
1 CONT I can corroborate the start of this line; I originally got the line
1 CONT from a  friend who got it from EuroStamm, and have since found it
1 CONT elsewhere.   (Now  that I just checked my notes, I see that it was also
1 CONT posted here not   so  long ago in a post which traced Heribert IV of
1 CONT Vermandois back to  Charlie.)
1 CONT >1.  Pepin (great-grandson of Charlemagne), seigneur of St. Quentin   and
1 CONT Peronne.
1 CONT Count of Senlis, Peronne, & St. Quentin, the son of Bernard (D. of
1 CONT Milan,  & K. of Italy; natural son of Pepin, K. of Italy, son of Charlie)
1 CONT &  Kunigunde.
1 CONT >2.  Pepin de Senlis de Valois, Count Berengarious of Brittany, Count
1 CONT of  Bayeaux.
1 CONT and brother of Herbet I, Count of Vermandois, Soisson, Meaux, and
1 CONT Merezais, Seigneur of Senlis, Peronne, and St. Quentin.  I would   guess
1 CONT that Herbert was the elder brother, as he got their father's titles.   I
1 CONT have a problem with that 'Count Berengarious' title; there were way   too
1 CONT many 'Berenger, Count of X's' running around during that time (and
1 CONT usually  latinized to 'Berengarius') for me to be comfortable with this.
1 CONT It   sounds  like two people got merged into one.
1 CONT >3.  Pepin II, count of Senlis. >4.  Bernhard, count of Senlis. >5.
1 CONT Adela  of Senlis = Gauthier II, count of Vexintamiens. >6.  Raoul II,
1 CONT count   of  Vexin = Adele of Breteuil (dau Hildouin, count of Breteuil
1 CONT and his   wife  Emmeline Chartres). >7.  Raoul III, the Great, count of
1 CONT Valois &   Vexin =  Adela of Bar-sur-Aube. >8.  Adela of Vexin = Heribert
1 CONT IV count of  Vermandois.
1 CONT Here's what the 11th ed. of the Enc. Brittanica has to say on the
1 CONT subject:  'Valois, Counts & Dukes of. ...From the 10th to the 12th
1 CONT century it   was  owned by the counts of Vermandois and of Vexin; but on
1 CONT the death of  Eleanor, sister and heiress oif Raoul V (d. 1167), it was
1 CONT united to   the  crown by King Philip Augustus. ...'.  'Vermandois.  A
1 CONT French   countship  composed originally of the two burgraviates
1 CONT (ch^atellenies) of St.   Quentin  (Aisne) and Peronne (Somme).  Herbert
1 CONT I., the earliest of its   hereditary  counts, was descended in direct
1 CONT male line from the emperor   Charlemagne,  and was killed in 902 by an
1 CONT assassin in the pay of Baldwin II., count   of  Flanders.  His son,
1 CONT Herbert II (902-943), a man absolutely devoid of  scruples, [sorry, had
1 CONT to include that comment. :)] ...In 1077 the   last  male of the first
1 CONT house of Vermandois, Herbert IV., received the  countship of Valois in
1 CONT right of his wife.  He died soon afterwards,  leaving his inheritance to
1 CONT his daughter, Adela, ...' Not really a   'smoking  gun',  but it does
1 CONT point towards the correctness of what you have.//
1 CONT [Anders Berg - anders.berg - at - pi.se - Stockholm, SWEDEN]: Alan
1 CONT Wilson <abwilson -at- uclink2.berkeley.edu> wrote:
1 CONT 'C.  SENLIS and VEXIN. 1.  Pepin of Peronne Count (817/818 - 892). 2.
1 CONT Pepin I de SENLIS Count (Circa 846 - 893). 3.  Pepin II de SENLIS   Count
1 CONT (Circa 876 - After 922). 4.  Bernard de SENLIS (Circa 918 - ). 5.   Adele
1 CONT de SENLIS (Circa 944 - ) & Gautier II de Vexin Count (Circa 944 -
1 CONT 1027).  6.  Raoul II of Vexin Count (Circa 980 - After 1030) & Adele de
1 CONT Bretuil  (Circa 980 - ). 7.  Raoul III 'the Great' (Circa 1010 - 8 Sep
1 CONT 1074) &  Adele de Bar-sur-Aube (Circa 1012 - 1043). 8.  Adela de Valois
1 CONT (Vexin)  (Before 1043 - ) & Herbert IV de  ERMANDOIS Comte (Circa 1032 -
1 CONT 1080/1096). Call often extends lines through uncertain links.  (Many
1 CONT lines  run to Adam.)  In this third line, immediately above, no
1 CONT parentage is assigned to Adele, generation 5, by Weis (Ancestral   Roots,
1 CONT line 250); Moriarty (Plantagenet Ancestry, pp. 135 & 229); and even
1 CONT Stuart  (Royalty for Commoners, line 268). But Turton (Plantagenet
1 CONT Ancestry,   p.  112) carries the  line through Adela's father, Bernardos,
1 CONT Count of Senlis, the Pepins,   and  on to Bernard of Italy, Pepin of
1 CONT Italy, and Charlemagne.  Turton, I   know,  has been caught out in quite
1 CONT a few errors.'
1 CONT Brandenburg (1935) mentions two children of Pippin, 'Graf' probably of
1 CONT Senlis (*845, + after 28 Jan 893): - Pippin II & Bernhard,  but, in   his
1 CONT notes, he finds the sources unsatisfactory. The new Brandenburg   edition
1 CONT (1995) refers to a work by K.F. Werner from 1967 ( Die Nachkommen   Karls
1 CONT des Grossen bis um das Jahr 1000 ). Werner dismisses Pippin II as an
1 CONT invention by later genealogists and cancels him out. No descendants   of
1 CONT either Pippin II or his brother Bernhard are listed in any of the
1 CONT editions  of Brandenburg. So, it is fair to say, the descent from
1 CONT Charlemagne   to  Adele (generation 5 above) is very dubious indeed.//
