0 @N6000000001354417270@ NOTE Sources: A. Roots 121E, 143A; RC 44, 166; Kraentzler 1453, 1593, 1609, 1645;
1 CONT AF; The Dukes of Normandy and Their Origins; Pfafman; History of the Vikings;
1 CONT Russell.
1 CONT RC:Eistein Ivarsson, Jarl of Hedemarken (of the Uplands), ca 830.
1 CONT Roots: Eystein Glumra, Jarl of the Upplands, ca. 830, said to have fathered
1 CONT two known children: Swanhild and Ragnvald I.
1 CONT K. calls him Eystein Ivarsson, aka Euslin "Ghimrice/Ghemvice" of Schleswig.
1 CONT K: Eystein "Glumra" Ivarsson, Count of Maere (More). Jarl of the Uplanders
1 CONT in Norway.
1 CONT Russell: Eisten Glumru of Vors, A.D. 870. Names Rogvald as a son, butnot
1 CONT son Malahue and daughter Swanhild. Names instead Sigurd, Jarl of the Orkneys,
1 CONT andd Huldrich, ancestor of Raoul de Toeny.
1 CONT Eystein Glumra was the Earl of Moera (various spellings for this) in Norway
1 CONT and Jarl of Orkney and Shetland.
1 CONT According to both the Heimskringla Saga and the Orkneyinga Saga, Eystein
1 CONT Glumra was the father of Rognvald. The Orkneyinga Saga says Eystein Glumra's
1 CONT earliest forebear was Fornjot, King of Finland and Kvenland. Fornjot's
1 CONT great-great-grandson was Thorri, or Fhorri, who had two sons, Norr and Gorr,
1 CONT who emigrated westward. Norr took the mainland called Norway and Gorrtook the
1 CONT islands. Gorr's son Heiti was the father of Sveithi (Sveide), the SeaKing,
1 CONT who died about 760. Sveithi's son, Halfdan the Old, who died in 800, was the
1 CONT father of Ivar, Earl of the Uplands. And Ivar, in turn, was the father of
1 CONT Eystein Glumra.
1 CONT RC 44 calls this man Eistein Ivarsson, son of Ivar, who was son of Halfdan
1 CONT the Old. So it follows the Sagas for three generations.
1 CONT There was no written language during this period, and the Norse sagas
1 CONT provided oral histories, much like those Alex Haley, author of "Roots,"
1 CONT found in Africa.
