0 @N6000000002187631538@ NOTE Ranulf I of Aquitaine
1 CONT From Wikipedia, the free encyclopedia
1 CONT
1 CONT Ranulf I (also Ramnulf, Rannulf, and Ranulph; 820 – 866) was a Count of Poitiers (from 835) and Duke of Aquitaine (from 852). He is considered a possible son of Gerard, Count of Auvergne, and Hildegard (or Matilda), daughter of Lo
1 CONC uis the Pious and Ermengard. Few details are known about Ranulf I, except that he died in 866 in Aquitaine from wounds received in the Battle of Brissarthe against the Vikings (in which Robert the Strong also died). Ranulf I, is t
1 CONC he 32nd Great-Grandfather to Queen Elizabeth II
1 CONT [edit] Marriage and issue
1 CONT
1 CONT He married Bilichild of Maine and they had the following:
1 CONT
1 CONT     * Ranulf II, who inherited Poitou and later acquired Aquitaine.
1 CONT
1 CONT [edit] See also
1 CONT
1 CONT     * Ramnulfids
1 CONT     * Dukes of Aquitaine family tree
1 CONT
1 CONT
1 CONT Preceded by
1 CONT — Duke of Aquitaine
1 CONT 852 – 866 Succeeded by
1 CONT Louis the Stammerer (as King)
1 CONT Preceded by
1 CONT Bernard I Count of Poitiers
1 CONT 835 – 866 Succeeded by
1 CONT Ranulf II
