0 @N6000000000269747020@ NOTE Ermentrude Of Orleans (also Hirmentrude, Irmintrud, 27 September 823 \endash  6 October 869) was a Frankish noblewoman. Daughter of Odo, Count of Orleans and Engeltrude, she married Charles the Bald, King of France in 842. She was
1 CONC  a gifted embroiderer and was interested in religious foundations. Charles gave her the abbey of Chelles. She separated from her husband after he executed her rebellous brother, retreated to the life of a nunnery.
1 CONT
1 CONT Her known children include Judith, Louis the Stammerer, and Charles of Aquitaine.
