0 @N6000000002188305462@ NOTE Charles of Provence
1 CONT From Wikipedia, the free encyclopedia
1 CONT
1 CONT Charles of Provence (845 – 24 January 863) was the Carolingian King of Provence from 855 until his early death in 863.
1 CONT
1 CONT Charles was the youngest son of Holy Roman Emperor Lothair I and Ermengarde of Tours.
1 CONT
1 CONT His father divided his realm of the Middle Franks (Lotharingia) between his three sons: the eldest, Louis, received Italy and the emperorship; Lothair II received Lotharingia (modern Lorraine and the Low Countries); and the younge
1 CONC st, Charles, received Upper and Lower Burgundy (Arles and Provence).
1 CONT
1 CONT Charles was only a child when his father died; accordingly, the governance of his realm was undertaken by his tutor, Count Gerard II of Vienne, whose wife was a sister-in-law of Emperor Lothar I. Gerard was a vigorous regent, defe
1 CONC nding the kingdom from the Northmen, who raided up the Rhone as far as Valence. In 860, he ejected them from the Rhone delta.
1 CONT
1 CONT Charles' uncle, Charles the Bald of West Francia, attempted to intervene in Provence in 861. After receiving an appeal for intervention from the Count of Arles, he invaded Provence, but only reached Macon, being restrained by Hinc
1 CONC mar of Rheims.
1 CONT
1 CONT Charles of Provence never ruled his realm in anything more but name. It was Gerard, rather than he, who in 858 arranged that should he die without children, Provence would revert to Charles' brother Lothair II. When Charles died, 
1 CONC however, his other brother Emperor Louis II also claimed Provence, and the realm was divided between the two (Lothair received the bishoprics of Lyon, Vienne and Grenoble, to be governed by Gerard; Louis II received Arles, Aix and
1 CONC  Embrun).
1 CONT Charles of Provence
1 CONT Carolingian Dynasty
1 CONT Born: 845 Died: January 863
1 CONT Regnal titles
1 CONT Preceded by
1 CONT Emperor Lothar I
1 CONT as King of Middle Francia King of Provence
1 CONT 23 September 855 – January 863 Succeeded by
1 CONT Kingdom divided between Emperor Louis II
1 CONT and Lothair II of Lotharingia
